window.FWN_NECROPOLIS_IMMORTAL_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_NECROPOLIS_IMMORTAL_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":2301,"title":"Chapter 2301: Chapter 2199.2: Emptying the Nation’s Coffers","paragraphs":["Chapter 2199.2: Emptying the Nation’s Coffers","“Come back home with me, Uncle Wu. You can hardly absolve yourself from blame when people discovery the robbery and will be dragged into the mess,” Lu Yun said to Wu Wei when he stowed the sword pagoda.","The man recomposed himself upon seeing his young master put the spatial treasure away. “That is just as well. There are too many powerhouses in the palace right now and I might be exposed if I stay here.”","It wasn’t that he was afraid of death, but that plans of a hundred years might be exposed if someone detected his presence.","A yellow haze rose from Lu Yun’s body and enveloped the two. They vanished from view, leaving just as quickly as Lu Yun had arrived with none the wiser. The young man was much more confident after obtaining the contents of the nation’s vaults. He had more than one hundred million paramount rank spirit stones on him at the moment, which was sufficient to deploy the forge’s might.","......","The second day, the Yuwen Clan.","The Yuwen Clan was now Darklake’s foremost clan. Although its trading company had been smashed in, they’d already announced that they would punish the Lu Clan for the transgression.","A tense atmosphere descended over the capital as everyone knew tumultuous times were creeping into the city. This would shuffle the members of the ruling echelon.","BOOM!","Yuwen cultivators awoke from a night of cultivation when a loud noise sounded from their front door. Someone had kicked it open and reduced it to a pile of shards.","“Get out here, Yuwen trash!” Lu Yun shouted as he planted himself in the doorway.","“What kind of cretin dares cause trouble at the Yuwen Clan!” A dignified voice responded from the depths of the complex, followed by the aura of a soul projection cultivator.","“You’re only showing part of yourself!” Golden light sparkled in Lu Yun’s eye; he picked out a skinny elder quietly meditating on a seat cushion in an unremarkable house located in the backyard. The elder’s aura was as deep and unfathomable as the sea—it was the true immortal in residence at the Yuwens’.","However, given that the heavenly book was yet to become entirely ineffective, the true immortal could not act as he wishedl since he was metaphorically hobbled. Regardless, his consciousness was locked onto Lu Yun and scanning the young man like it was a pair of physical eyes. He wanted to glean everything possible about the Lu young master.","Lu Yun had only been seventh level qi refinement a year ago, but advanced rapidly during this time to mid nascent soul. This kind of cultivation speed was incredible! Not even the greatest genius could cross three major cultivation stages within a year and have perfectly solid foundations to show for it.","Lu Yun wasn’t bothering to hide anything at this point—both sides showed their hands. They’d completed their preparations and accomplished what they should’ve done before this meeting. This was Lu Yun’s first official clash with the Origin Sect.","He couldn’t be bothered to exchange further words and punched forward, leaving a massive shadow of a fist in the void.","Bam!","A soul projection powerhouse hidden elsewhere was thrown out of hiding.","“An old fart of the Yuwen Clan?” The young man indifferently picked the elder up like he grasped a chick.","Dumbfounded, the elder hadn’t anticipated that he wouldn’t last even one move before being captured. Regardless, he remained composed. As strong as the Lu young master was, was he stronger than an immortal?","“Heh heh, don’t you know that death is coming for you Lus?” leered the soul projection elder.","Crunch!","Lu Yun still couldn’t be bothered with words and crushed the man’s neck, forcing out the elder’s nascent soul. He threw it into the sword pagoda for safekeeping. Tian Shanhe alone was insufficient to look after the Lu herb garden. The man needed a few more nascent soul helpers.","Yuwen cultivators streamed in from all parts of the residence.","“How dare you kill our people in our home, Lu Yun?! Do you want the Lus to go extinct?!” Current patriarch Yuwen Yang twitched when he saw the elder’s corpse.","“Hahaha!! This young master is here to have some fun killing today!” Lu Yun emitted a long peal of laughter and abruptly summoned Immortals Forbidden into his hand. Wrapping himself with rays of sword light, he rushed the Yuwen cultivators.","“DIE!!” The two remaining soul projection cultivators of the family quickly answered in kind and threw their treasures at the young man.","The initial and mid soul projection opponents were nothing to Lu Yun. He twisted in the air while crimson sword light flared, smashing the two paramount rank treasures to pieces.","A cultivator’s treasure was closely connected to their heart and mind, so the two soul projection heavyweights immediately spat out blood. They swiftly disintegrated into a bloody mist, leaving their nascent souls for Lu Yun to connect.","The Eighteen Cerulean Sword Dragons then howled through the area as Lu Yun twisted eighteen times in the air. The illustrious Yuwen Clan’s main hall swiftly turned into a pile of rubble while more than one hundred Yuwen cultivators died.","Lu Yun was no soft-hearted character. He’d come to kill, so why should he show mercy to an opponent who’d become his nemsis?","The grand complex turned into the slaughter fields within the blink of an eye. While the Yuwen Clan had long taken note of Lu Yun and made their preparations accordingly, they hadn’t thought that Lu Yun would come so quickly and act so decisively. They weren’t given a single chance to breathe!","Yuwen Zhi died yesterday. The Yuwen, Zhao, and Yu alliance was also defused yesterday. And today, Lu Yun was on their doorstep!","The young man ignored the true immortal hiding in the Yuwen background. He rushed into the heart of their compound with just himself and his sword.","Rumble!","Lu Yun hacked through the Yuwen defensive formation the moment it rose, breaking into the ground to enter a secret room.","Yu Shuai and Zhao Chenguang barely looked human. Their cultivation was restricted and all of their bones and meridians broken. They’d plainly been tortured and interrogated before this.","The two young masters had advanced with stunning speed, and while they kept low profiles, they could not hoodwink soul projection powerhouses. When those heavyweights returned to the capital, Yu Shuai and Zhao Chenguang were immediately exposed.","“I’ve caused you guys massive trouble this time.” Lu Yun took out two pills from his storage and shoved them into his friends’ mouths. Their bones and meridians reformed amid a series of pops and crackles.","“Not at all, we’re brothers!” Yu Shuai breathed out with relief. “If it wasn’t for you, we’d never form a golden core with our potential.”","“Don’t show any mercy to these Yuwen bastards!” Zhao Chenguang snarled. “But we didn’t give you up either. We didn’t reveal anything about what you gave us!”","Lu Yun smiled. “It wouldn’t have mattered if you did. Those things were tailor-made for you guys so even if other people took them, they wouldn’t be of any use.","“Alright, let’s go.” Lu Yun got to his feet. “There will be no more Yuwens in this world after today.”","“Good!” Savage glee dawned on Yu Shuai and Zhao Chenguang’s faces. They were rascals at heart and took revenge for every slight. How would they not seek vengeance after being tortured so badly?","“Heh heh heh heh heh, I’m afraid you won’t see the end of the Yuwens, if that even happens.” A cold sneer echoed through the air as the secret room quaked. Terrifying energy of heaven descended to crush the inhabitants.","“A seventh rank formation!” Lu Yun raised a brow. Now this was unexpected, but wholly unsurprising.","Rumble!","A void of hazy gray replaced the secret room vanished. Seventh rank formations were high level formations. The five elements were complete within this one and formed their own internal space.","Killing intent abounded inside, the dangers within were more pronounced than the ninth rank Nineheavens Brahman Formation. One single soul projection cultivator had directed the latter formation, whereas a dozen soul projection and a soul separation heavyweight powered the one they were caught in. It was naturally much stronger.","Thirty percent of this seventh rank formation was already brought to bear. On the other hand, less than one percent of the Nineheavens Brahman Formation had been in play that day.","“Lu Yun, you brat. Just the likes of you wish to destroy my clan?! The ones who came before were just Ling idiots and discardable Yuwen pawns. The clan’s strength is completely undiminished!","“We knew you'd come to save these two pieces of filth, so we set up a trap ahead of time!” As foreboding as the speaker’s tone was, he was hardly speaking the truth. Lu Yun had already killed quite a number of important Yuwen family members and even slain their previous patriarch.","The young man had come too quickly and caught them off guard."]},{"number":2302,"title":"Chapter 2302: Chapter 2200.1: Slaying An Immortal","paragraphs":["Chapter 2200.1: Slaying An Immortal","Whoosh whoosh whoosh!","Innumerable tiny rays of sword light formed as soon as the unknown speaker finished and shot at the trio. So this was a seventh rank sword formation!","Lu Yun sent Yu Shuai and Zhao Chenguang into the sword pagoda with a wave of his hand.","“A seventh rank sword formation? Show this young master how strong this formation of yours is!” Lu Yun no longer had any concerns after moving his friends to safety. He threw his head back with a howl and raised gusts of crimson sword qi.","He set foot into the void and shifted nine times in quick succession, leaving nine faint shadows in the air. Each of them lingered for a few moments before a crimson sword dragon darted out of it.","Eighteen Cerulean Sword Dragons!","Lu Yun deployed this move through the Nine Forms of the Cloud Dragon!","He didn’t hold back and sent nine out three-hundred-meter long crimson dragons. They threaded through the air, simultaneously twisting nine times in unison and forming the one hundred and sixty-two momentum of the Cerulean Sword Dragons. As each momentum ripped into the seventh rank formation, it elicited earth-shaking vibrations.","Pfft!","Of the thirteen cultivators in the air, the twelve soul projection uniformly spat out blood. One of them yelled with astonishment, “How is this possible?? Each of his attacks perfectly strike an eye of the formation! Is he also a formation grandmaster?”","Rumble!","The nine sword dragons came together as one and rammed a certain part of the array. It happened to be where an initial soul projection cultivator stood. He suffered full recoil from the formation and fell from his position. With his true origin in disarray, his energy was swiftly devoured by the assembly.","The cultivator withered away at a speed visible to the naked eye until even his nascent soul flew apart into dust. With his death, pressure mounted on the other twelve eyes of the formation. The entire assembly teetered on the edge of losing control.","“What a bunch of idiots. Are twelve soul projection and one soul separation expert enough to keep thirty percent of this kind of formation under control?” Lu Yun found things much easier with one formation eye destroyed. He could reveal himself now, but incredible wounds crisscrossed his body when he came into view. His clothes were tattered like he was a beggar, but he roared with laughter.","The formation of talismans that Terra Demon had set up was active. Lu Yun used himself as bait to draw the true immortal’s attention and deployed his methods at full force in preparation for this moment.","The Eighteen Cerulean Sword Dragons were a premier technique that the Mindful Potentate used to dominate the world of immortals. The Nine Forms of the Cloud Dragon was also Slaughterless’ ultimate move from eight thousand years ago. Both of these immediately caught the immortal’s eye. Thus, he didn’t pay particular attention to the formation activating in the void.","In the next moment, the entire Yuwen residence vanished from Dark City. It relocated to the air over Tiger Suppression Pass in the west of the empire.","Crraaaaaack!","The complex spontaneously disassembled, leaving nearly one thousand Yuwen descendants standing blankly in the sky. Those who didn’t react in time fell straight to the ground.","The complex’s geographical shift dismantled the seventh rank formation, thereby freeing Lu Yun.","“So I fell for a brattish baby’s scheme!” The skinny true immortal shook his head, nary a flicker of emotion on his face. “But what can you do after moving me here?”","He looked around the surroundings, finding it devoid of people and qi. It was a good place to make his next move.","“The heavenly book can suppress you, but not kill you.” Terra Demon materialized next to Lu Yun.","“It’s you.” The true immortal wasn’t surprised by Terra Demon, as if he knew the man. “You’re a soul projection cultivator with nearly the battle strength of an empyrean immortal... Wait, you’ve ascended to soul separation? No wonder.”","Surprise finally creased the immortal’s face.","“Aouu!” came a long croon. The Yuwen, Ling, and royal soul projection powerhouses felt a tremendous suction force around them before they flew out uncontrollably and landed in a massive bloody mouth.","The jiao’s three hundred meter long body also appeared in the void.","“The scaled-dragon from Jade Ice Lake...” Gravity finally crept into the immortal’s expression. “An empyrean immortal scaled-dragon, a soul separation cultivator with nearly the battle strength of an immortal... Are these the trump cards you’ve brought to bear against me?”","A smile developed on the man’s face. “There is an undeniable chasm between empyrean and true immortality...”","“This old guy talks too much, do it!” Lu Yun sighed with irritation when the immortal looked like he had more to say.","Whoosh!","Terra Demon had been just waiting for the word. A strangely shaped longsword appeared in his hand and he rushed for the true immortal. Hot on his heels, the gray jiao twisted itself around and sent currents of gray air rising into the sky. Its energy confined the void around them, upon which it raised its foreclaws to grab the true immortal.","Bam!","The true immortal also made his move. A beam of orange immortal light shimmered over his body to defend against the two attacks. He howled, covering himself with orange light and manifesting two hammers in his hands. As skinny as he was, his weapons were extremely formidable. They were two bright yellow hammers running almost two meters across and first rank immortal weapons!","BOOM!","The hammers caught Terra Demon’s next slash and threw the latter back.","“Kill!” The immortal’s eyes were shot through with blood. His immortal light undulated wildly, like he was a demon himself. His hammers howled madly through the air in a domineering fashion.","“Aouuu!” Unable to react in time, the gray jiao took a blow to its body and flew backward, smashing a mountain to pieces upon collision.","“Hahahaha!!” the immortal roared with laughter. “Heaven Shaker!”","Humm!","Brilliant light emanated from the two hammers and crashed toward Terra Demon like two miniature mountains.","“This guy’s only a half step august immortal.” Terra Demon immediately understood the truth of the matter when he saw the immortal’s aura. Regardless, he still wouldn’t be concerned even if the opponent was an august immortal.","Terra Demon threw away his sword and raised bare hands to the sky.","BOOM!","The massive weapons slammed into Terra Demon and drove him underground. However, he charged back up the next second and threw himself at the hammers again. Even the gray jiao crawled up from the ground and continued in a forward charge.","......","“These two!” Lu Yun chuckled ruefully when he read Terra Demon and the jiao’s actions. He dismissed the Forge of Heaven and Earth that he already held. The young man could tell what they wanted to do.","Although they’d refined the Hongmeng Fruit and digested its medicinal effects, they hadn’t absorbed one iota of the meaning of being an immortal overlord. The true immortal’s strength was helping them temper and process the meaning accumulated in their bodies.","In other words, as fierce as the immortal seemed and in complete control, he was just helping Terra Demon and the gray jiao further their cultivation.","The one thousand kilometers of Tiger Suppression Pass were leveled to completely flat land. Thankfully, nothing lived here. Wu Zhen and the others training had been recalled to form a brand new Vermilion Bird troop with Lu Xuan. They were in the field executing a mission to eliminate remnants of the Yuwen family.","The gray jiao and Terra Demon were having a tough time as their opponent was a peak true immortal powerhouse. While his attacks helped them forge the profound meaning in their bodies, the blows were solid hits to their bodies. It took only a dozen breaths before they were covered in blood.","The immortal in white robes also gradually felt that something was amiss. The two in front of him seemed to be continuously throwing themselves at him, but made no moves to fight back. While they were drenched in blood, they were still very energetic.","“This is very strange!” A keen light flashed through his eyes when he subconsciously glanced at Lu Yun hiding far away. He vanished on the spot as he made for the young man.","Rumble!!","A gigantic bolt of lightning flashed through the air and crashed into the true immortal’s head, blasting him into the ground. Gray tribulation clouds had appeared over him at some point in time. They’d now accumulated enough power to release a massive roar of thunder and lightning."]},{"number":2303,"title":"Chapter 2303: Chapter 2200.2: Slaying An Immortal","paragraphs":["Chapter 2200.2: Slaying An Immortal","“Blast it, a thunder tribulation from the heavenly book!” howled the immortal as his white robes started to get singed. Any foreign immortal who visited the Jade Ruins Realm and engaged in a fight would be punished by the heavenly book. Offenders were sentenced to death by the treasure, so very few immortals were willing to come to worlds of cultivation.","However, the heavenly book’s hold over the Jade Ruins Realm had been infinitely diminished and was about to vanish. Its suppression of immortals at the moment was almost negligible, so the might it released was insufficient to kill a true immortal.","Despite that, its vast and unbounded power wasn’t something that an immortal could endure—despite being incredibly weakened. Thus, the immortal was blasted straight underground.","“What a pity.” Terra Demon and the gray jiao hovered over the immortal, slightly saddened looks appearing in their eyes. If they’d taken a few more blows, they might’ve fully refined the profound meaning accumulated in their body. Their chance was at an end since the tribulation had arrived.","Kaboom!","The immortal was blasted underground by another bolt of lightning as soon as he crawled out of the hole.","“Break!!” Orange light shifted over the immortal’s body as he stood up to the next bolt of lightning and threw out his hammers, aiming for the tribulation cloud.","Boom!","Terra Demon and the gray jiao’s attacks arrived just as the immortal beat back the cloud. Terra Demon didn’t bother with any weapons as energy from the environment was his best weapon. He shifted into a massive being three hundred meters tall, black light sparkling over his fist. He, too, punched the immortal into the ground, just as the thunder tribulation had just done.","The gray jiao expanded to three thousand meters long as well and spewed out black lightning, raining electricity down on the immortal stuck in the ground.","“AHHHHH!!! DIE!!” shrieked the immortal. He was now embedded in bedrock and could not move. The bright yellow hammers that were about to fly back to his hand were halted by a black tower, confiscated before they could erupt with power.","Whoosh whoosh whoosh!","The inert ray of sword qi in the center of the sword pagoda shifted to motion when the hammers entered the treasure. Rays of keen sword qi erupted, churning the hammers to pieces so that their core essence could be absorbed by the sword pagoda.","This subsequent development was entirely out of Lu Yun’s expectations, and he discovered a hint of spirit rippling across the ray of sword qi after it swallowed the other two treasures.","“That’s... the Sword of Heaven and Earth...” Lu Yun suddenly recognized the sword shadow. It was... very unfamiliar as it seemed to both be his and not be his. The sealed version of him seemed to have once refined and assimilated it, and then... he knew not what came after.","“Augh!” The immortal spat out a mouthful of pale-gold blood. “You, you destroyed my Goldflash Hammers! I, Lu Youya, will hunt you to the ends of the world for this!”","BOOM!","He bit through the tip of his tongue and spat out blood essence, breaking free from the attacks raining down on him and rushing up from the ground. The immortal was a far cry from his previously composed self.","His white robes were muddy, tattered, and barely keeping him covered. A neat bun of white hair now looked more like a bird’s nest; wisps of blue smoke rose from it. He dodged the next bolt of tribulation lightning and rapidly formed hand seals, then crossed his arms in front of his chest.","Hum hum hum hum hum!","Energy of heaven and earth surged to him from all directions while a massive shadow of a wolf’s head looked out behind him.","“Moun—tain Brea—ker!!” Terra Demon greeted the wolf’s head with solemnity. He immediately rushed to Lu Youya and erupted with terrifying power from his fist. The shadow of a massive mountain formed in the void and loomed over the immortal.","“Awooo!” The enormous wolf head seemed to come alive and opened wide, swallowing the power of Terra Demon’s punch.","“The Greedy Wolf Star of the Greedy Wolf Immortal King!” Lu Yun frowned tightly, never imagining that he’d see the ultimate move from the central immortal emperor’s Greedy Wolf Immortal King. He took out the Forge of Heaven and Earth and threw it at Lu Youya.","The forge rapidly ballooned in the void until it was three hundred meters tall. Shortly afterwards, a massive curtain of light erupted from the forge and enveloped the immortal within. One hundred million paramount spirit stones blazed inside, fully powering the Nineheavens Brahman Formation.","A ninth rank formation was able to bring its complete capabilities to bear when one hundred million spirit stones were consumed for it.","“Terra Demon, gray jiao, look after the formation!” Lu Yun shouted.","The Forge of Heaven and Earth could only activate the formation for a split second. One hundred million paramount stones could bring its full power to bear for only a few breaths. After that, the formation would return to the forge given the lack of further qi supporting it.","A ninth rank formation simply required too much energy. If it was one hundred million paramount spirit crystals on the other hand, that would power the formation without end. Currently, the ninth rank formation required cultivators to oversee it so that it could deploy the might it possessed.","The gray jiao and Terra Demon took control of the formation without hesitation. Their combined battle strength could severely injure and even triumph over the immortal, but they could not prevent him from escaping. Only the formation could trap someone of this caliber.","The gray jiao and Terra Demon were on par with true immortals. They easily maintained a ninth rank formation.","“Nineheavens Brahman Fire?!” Lu Youya gasped to see several hundred crimson dragons circling around him. The Greedy Wolf Star over his head also howled with agony.","Nineheavens Brahman Fire was one of the rare fires of the world. Though its ranking wasn’t high, it was extraordinarily terrifying. The Nineheavens Brahman Formation could summon said fire from the void and form Brahman dragons. Given enough time, this fire could refine even true immortals.","“It’d be worth it even if I have to spend ten years refining this immortal, but I don’t have that much time right now.” A jade-green bow rested in Lu Yun’s hand. When he pulled back on it and deployed the Connate Great Dao of the Five Elements in conjunction, connate wood energy rolled in from the east. It formed a jade-green arrow between bow and string.","Color drained from the young man’s face as all of the Hongmeng qi in his body was consumed by the bow when the connate word energy gathered.","Whoosh!","The bowstring released the second he was devoid of energy, sending the arrow of wood energy flying into the Nineheavens Brahman Formation like a meteor.","Pfft!","Lu Youya was pierced through.","The moment his enemy fell, Lu Yun sagged to the ground like a kite with its strings cut. What kind of treasure was the jade-green bow? It took all of his Hongmeng qi and the remaining goodwill in the Seal of the Multitude to fire it just once!","The skies and earth darkened when the arrow shot out, as if all of the killing intent beneath the heavens gathered on it. This arrow of connate wood energy was far superior to the one that Yuwen Zhuifeng had fired. Their difference was so great it was as if a firefly compared to the moon.","The arrow of light seemed both tangible and formless, wavering without a set trajectory. Its terrifying presence locked on to the immortal and a gaping hole split his chest in less than one thousandth of a breath. His heart and lungs were completely obliterated.","“AHHHH!!” Lu Youya howled at the sky, never imagining that he’d die in a low level world of cultivation, and in one of its low level cultivation empires at that!","He realized the moment the arrow pierced his body that there was no hope of survival.","BOOM!","Nine hundred and ninety-nine crimson dragons snarled in the Nineheavens Brahman Formation. Brahman fire roared with thunder, breaking through all of the immortals’ defensive treasures.","“I’m taking you down with me!!” Lu Youya screamed. His body exploded into an entity of orange energy that wrapped tightly around a golden nascent soul, cocooning it with protection. No matter how the dragons charged, they couldn’t break through the incredible depth of the power.","“He wants to detonate his immortal light to break the formation!” Terra Demon looked on solemnly. Immortal light was the core essence of an immortal that appeared when one reached immortality. It was a powerful weapon in itself."]},{"number":2304,"title":"Chapter 2304: Chapter 2201.1: Immortal Light","paragraphs":["Chapter 2201.1: Immortal Light","There were nine ranks to immortal light—red, orange, yellow, green, azure, blue, purple, black, and white. When immortals first obtained immortal light, they gained first rank red light. Immortal light didn’t progress with an immortal’s cultivation. It required continual infusion of rare and powerful treasures to raise its level.","The costs were high to enhance its level. Lu Youya had expended more treasures than he could count to raise his immortal light to orange.","The detonation of orange rank immortal light rivaled the self-detonation of the immortal soul. It would shake the ninth rank formation and unleash recoil on those overseeing it.","However, no recovery was possible after immortal light was destroyed. It was the core essence of an immortal and its absence meant that an immortal would never again advance in their cultivation. Those without their immortal light would also see their strength decrease by thirty percent, if not more.","Lu Yun sat cross-legged on the ground, not a flicker of change in his expression. He gripped a lower rank spirit crystal and swiftly recovered his Hongmeng qi. The energy within a lower rank spirit crystal was clean and pure, the equivalent of ten thousand upper rank spirit stones. Dense energy rapidly surged into his meridians.","Within his dantian, a pale-gold nascent soul sat over a hazy dao character. Two pale hands blurred through the hand seals for qi accumulation, drinking in the energy like a whale breathing water.","Finally, the pure energy transformed into streams of Hongmeng qi through the nascent soul’s conversion and entered the dantian. With Lu Yun’s body as the center, a massive vortex of qi developed as all energy within five kilometers surged to him.","......","Lu Yun sat calmly on the ground while he recovered his cultivation. Terra Demon and the gray jiao continuously infused the Ninheavens Brahman Formation with their qi, directing it to barrage Lu Youya so the immortal wouldn’t have a chance to self detonate.","Hummm!","A resonance arose within the formation as Lu Youya’s immortal light completely devoured his body. Yellow radiance began shimmering over the orange immortal light, a light that built to lightning the greater the immortal light expanded. In contrast, Lu Youya’s nascent soul shrank swiftly—he was sacrificing his nascent soul to forcefully raise his immortal light’s rank!","“This guy’s crazy! His soul has a chance of reincarnating if immortal light continues to protect it, but he’s feeding it to his immortal light and then detonating it! He’ll be scattered to the four winds then!” Terra Demon quirked his lips with disbelief.","When Lu Yun saw the immortal’s nascent soul begin to diminish, he quickly retracted the floating Forge of Heaven and Earth and stowed the Nineheavens Brahman Formation. He looked back to find that Terra Demon and the gray jiao were already gone.","Meanwhile, Lu Youya’s jaw dropped inside the dome of orange-yellow immortal light. His opponents were suddenly gone, what was he to do now??","How deeply he regretted his actions! If he’d known that these two would be so shameless and run off, he would simply scare them a little. There was no need to detonate his immortal light to ensure mutual destruction!","And that ninth rank formation that seemed retractable at will, what kind of situation was this?! When were ninth rank formations portable??","While Lu Youya goggled at his circumstances, the immortal light erupted and swallowed the last of his nascent soul. An exceedingly rare yellow immortal light illuminated the scene.","However, he lost his courage at the last possible second, so the immortal light didn’t explode after devouring his nascent soul. It simply transformed into a ray of hazy light and fog that drifted to the ground.","Seated cross-legged on the ground, Lu Yun lifted his head to see the light floating down to him. He casually reached upward and grasped it in his hand. Having broken through to latter nascent soul, a rush of dense Hongmeng qi had surged out of his body in the moment of ascension and replenished the stores he’d used up.","His cultivation was several times stronger than mere moments ago.","“Those two faithless guys just left me here?” Lu Yun rolled his eyes and placed an Earthbending Talisman back in his ring. Although he grumbled, he would’ve been the first to run had Lu Youya truly detonated his immortal light. It’d just be the waste of an opportunity to breakthrough; his life was more important.","The yellow immortal light laid quietly in his hand, like it was tangible. Although it was light, there was form and weight to it. Only when immortal light combined with a nascent soul would it become pure light.","Whoosh whoosh!","Two figures flashed by—Terra Demon and the meter long jiao appeared in front of Lu Yun.","“Young master...” Terra Demon raised sheepishly.","“Never mind that.” Lu Yun waved him off and threw the sword light into the sword pagoda. It’d taken all that was Lu Youya—his body, nascent soul, storage ring, countless treasures and spirit stones, assorted pills and medicines to barely manage to raise it to yellow.","Lu Tianling was an awakened cultivator about to reach immortality. When he did, his immortal light would immediately ascend to the yellow rank if it devoured this. Immortals could also give their immortal light to others, but that immortal light would never advance again if they did so.","“To think that the Greedy Wolf Immortal King is still alive...” Lu Yun frowned faintly. This particular immortal king answered to the central immortal emperor. He’d once jointly suppressed the Mindful Potentate along with the Army Immortal King, Seven Kills Immortal King, and Fire Star Immortal King.","Legend had it that they died along with the Immortal Potentate, but that didn’t seem to be the case.","The Greedy Wolf Star was his ultimate move, a powerful combat art that walked the line between treasure and immortal method. It was one with a powerful suction force and protected by certain rules. Being the immortal king’s ultimate technique, only those who he willingly taught it to could learn it. Those who used it also required firm conviction in the immortal king.","In other words, only those with the immortal king’s approval could practice the combat art. Any other attempt would fail. That Lu Youya could deploy it meant that the immortal king still lived.","“Things are getting interesting.” Lu Yun’s lips curved upward. “No wonder his power lingers in the sword pagoda, but there is no sign of his body. I thought the sword pagoda swallowed it, but it seems that he’s still alive.”","“Young master, if the Greedy Wolf Immortal King is still alive... then what about the central immortal emperor...” Terra Demon asked worriedly.","The central immortal emperor was the only sovereign of the world of immortals. The immortal emperors of the other four directions were just subordinates to him. Only the central immortal emperor was the legitimate ruler of the world and its strongest.","“It’s best if he is, I can slap his face again.”","......","The enormous capital of Darklake Empire was as if an empty city these days. There was no one on the streets and not a single footstep darkening the storefronts of the prosperous outer quadrant.","The three great places of business—Ruyi Club, Rouge Pavilion, and Beast Colosseum were temporarily closed.","RUMBLE!!","Thunder roared in a certain part of the city as the Yuwen residence, one of the seven great clans of the capital, disappeared into thin air. Following that, multicolored curtains of light rose from the city’s foundations. One, two, three... twenty enormous curtains of light intersected in the air, coming together as a mammoth array that enclosed the city.","Figures in white appeared like ghosts when the formation assembled. They traversed the streets, giving rise to a faint scent of blood and gore. Soundlessly, wordlessly, families of varying sizes, pre-identified storefronts, and certain hidden strongholds were thoroughly uprooted.","......","A deathly silence reigned in the palace. Situ Jie sat high on the dais, a proud look of complete assurance on his face. Generations of the empire’s ancestors stood behind him. Even the empire’s founding father, soul projection Situ Lei, had returned to Dark City.","“Do you know your crimes, Situ Yun?!” Situ Jie suddenly thundered at the quiet young man off to the side.","“Might I ask royal brother what crime have I committed?” Situ Yun stood in an assembly of royal princes, not bothering to look at Situ Jie.","“What crime?” Situ Jie sneered. “You colluded with Tianlong Empire to subvert Darklake! The evidence is at hand, what more do you have to say for yourself?!”","He threw a jade slip to the ground.","Situ Yun was his biggest obstacle to assuming the throne. He was only one step away from that dragon seat, so he needed to eliminate this age-old rival.","Situ Yun had built quite a force for himself at court, so a sizable disturbance ran through the crowd when the officials saw the jade slip that had been thrown to the ground. Tianlong Empire was Darklake’s archenemies, the two nations had been at war for a thousand years. It wasn't until twenty years ago, at the battle of Tiger Suppression Pass, that Tianlong finally bowed its head.","But in the twenty years since, Tianlong had recovered much of its strength, and so its ambitions grew again. If it wasn't for wariness of the Lu father and son, they would’ve come back to the battlefield long ago."]},{"number":2305,"title":"Chapter 2305: Chapter 2201.2: Immortal Light","paragraphs":["Chapter 2201.2: Immortal Light","“Evidence?” Situ Yun’s handsome face remained composed. He lifted his head slightly and looked at Situ Jie seated on the throne. “Even if there is evidence, it’s not up to you to judge. You, are not the emperor yet.”","Emperor Situ Wenxian had announced that Crown Prince Situ Jie would be regent while he was in seclusion. Despite acting as one, Situ Jie was not the emperor.","“Hahahaha!!” Situ Jie threw his head back with laughter. “If this emperor says you are guilty, then you are guilty! Men, arrest the traitor!” A cold light sparkled in his eyes.","Whoosh whoosh whoosh!","Three unfamiliar nascent soul cultivators flew into the hall. Their energy fluctuated powerfully as they walked toward Situ Yun.","Savagery flashed across Situ Jie’s face. Nascent soul cultivators were either patriarchs of Darklake clans or lords of their local fiefdoms. While Situ Jie was the crown prince, he didn’t dare show too much disrespect to nascent soul powerhouses.","Yet with the Darklake senior royals returning as nascent soul powerhouses, and even some soul projection heavyweights coming to help, Situ Jie felt adequately fortified for his ambitions to bloom. He was the one behind placing Situ Wenxian under house arrest.","A voice rang out when the three figures drew close to Situ Wenxian. “These three look quite unfamiliar. They’re not from Darklake Empire, are they?”","Bam!","The three figures stuttered before a strange surge of power flung them outside the hall.","Immensely taken aback, the crowd focused on the man leading the group of officials to the right of the dais. He wore black court robes and a tiny golden hairband in his topknot. Roughly forty years of age, the three strands of long hair flowing in the air imparted an ethereal demeanor.","True origin circulated within his upraised hand. He was the one who’d sent the three nascent soul powerhouses flying.","“Are you trying to mutiny, Lu Tianling?!” Situ Jie surged to his feet, fear flashing through his eyes. His confidence quickly returned when another thought occurred to him.","“This is the imperial palace of Darklake Empire. No outsiders are allowed to give offense here,” Lu Tianling responded coldly as he put his hand down.","“How dare you! These three are royal guards that this emperor has recruited!” Situ Jie insisted stiffly.","“Oh? Then why does this marshal not know of them?” Lu Tianling raised his head. “I lead all of the cultivators in the nation and any nascent soul powerhouse or above that joins Darklake does so with my approval. Why has this marshal never seen these three?”","“Lu Tianling, does this emperor need your approval to recruit cultivators?!” Situ Jie slapped his throne with fury.","“This emperor?” Lu Tianling snorted with laughter. “What kind of emperor are you?”","“He will be the emperor very shortly,” came another jarring interjection. An otherworldly elder with white hair swept into the hall.","“Forefather!” Situ Jie greeted with delight and walked down from the throne, respectfully welcoming the elder. He was the founding father of Darklake Empire—Situ Lei. Situ Lei was a legendary figure of two thousand years ago and now latter soul projection.","Those assembled traded confused glances, not understanding what was taking place. Seeing as Situ Lei’s portrait hung in the palace’s Hall of ancestors, everyone recognized him.","“You are Lu Tianling, the current strongest of the nation?” Situ Lei coolly addressed Lu Tianling.","“I am.” The Lu patriarch assessed the Darklake legendary figure, not thinking much of him. Two thousand years and still latter soul projection? What a trash among trash. If among Great Xia, those who were two thousand years old should’ve become immortal long ago.","Of course, Lu Tianling also understood that it likely had much to do with Dark Orchid that the founding father hadn’t broken through. Once Situ Lei ascended beyond soul projection, he would shake off their control.","Dark Orchid would never permit a cultivator from a vassal nation to become a soul separation powerhouse.","“You’ve got some nerve!” Situ Lei sneered. “The empire that I created with my bare hands is now controlled by vicious rats the likes of you. You manipulate the court, collude with the enemy, and scheme to overthrow the Situ royal clan. Now that I am here, you will not be permitted to be lawless anymore!”","Lu Tianling looked at Situ Lei with a strange expression and said something that baffled everyone gathered. “Did... your parents not tell you before you came that Lu Tianling is very dangerous, to not offend him if you can?”","“Eh...” Not only Situ Lei, but the officials around them were flabbergasted by Lu Tianling’s mystifying response.","“Buahaha!” Lu Xiaochi couldn’t resist a round of chuckles when he heard his foster father’s reply. Why did that sound like something Lu Yun would say? To think that his taciturn foster father would be affected by the kid!","Ai, I wonder how he’s faring at the Yuwen Clan. I wonder if he’s succeeded or not.","Lu Xiaochi was ill at ease. Despite everything being under control, the Yuwens seemed to have gained a powerful backer as well. As heaven-defying as Lu Yun was, he was just a nascent soul cultivator. If anything happened to him, it would be more of a loss than a gain even if they managed to overcome the hardship at hand.","“Hmph! Is Lu Tianling supposed to be dangerous?” Situ Lei snorted, a ball of true origin flame burning over his palm. He slapped his palm at Lu Tianling’s forehead. If any other latter nascent soul cultivator was the target, they would be dead on the spot. However, it was the founding father of Darklake on one side and Lu Tianling on the other.","Shock rippled through the group of officials to see the legendary emperor attack their great war hero. Meanwhile, the Yuwen, Ling, and associates from assorted clans watched with schadenfreude. Lu Tianling was powerful? He was the greatest of Darklake? He was just a nascent soul cultivator. There was no hope of survival once a soul projection powerhouse made their move!","Bam!","Situ Lei’s blow connected solidly with Lu Tianling’s forehead, but the former was the one who froze instead. Situ Jie’s jaw dropped, and the assembly of officials reeled with surprise.","“Situ Lei, although you were the first emperor of Darklake Empire, don’t forget that you are a Dark Orchid citizen now. You are not of Darklake, so do you know the consequences of attacking an important subject in the imperial palace?!” Lu Tianling slowly lifted his head and regarded Situ Lei with a frosty glare.","“Y-you...” Situ Lei stammered with shock. He’d deployed his full strength with that blow—even latter soul projection cultivators would see their heads explode from the hit. Lu Tianling, however, remained completely unscathed.","In contrast, the Lu patriarch’s aura rose until he seemed as ponderous as a mountain.","Situ Lei and Situ Jie slowly backed away with incredulity.","“This cultivation... you are indeed guilty of high treason, Lu Tianling!” Situ Jie roared, trying to corral his mounting fear.","“High treason?” Lu Tianling snorted with laughter.","“You disappoint me too greatly, Situ Jie.” A majestic voice rang out as a middle-aged man clad in golden dragon robes walked in. A gold crown sat on his head; he walked with confidence and assurance.","“Greetings to Your Majesty!” The hall of officials rumbled with surprise. Meanwhile, the Yuwen and Ling Clans looked at each other with unpleasant expressions.","“R-royal father?” Situ Jie’s jaw dropped. Situ Wenxian had been confined by Dark Orchid’s powerhouses! What was he doing here?","The emperor’s aura was as boundless as the seas! Latter soul projection Situ Lei felt incredibly minuscule in front of the man. This was no latter nascent soul emperor! He was a heavyweight of unknown cultivation! At the very least, Situ Lei had never felt such a terrifying aura from Prince Sui of Dark Orchid.","“You, you...” Situ Lei’s face drained of color. Complicated emotions tinged primarily with fear flashed through his eyes as he looked at his descendant.","“Since the forefather has returned home, then do not go back. You can spend the rest of your days in Darklake and see how it rises over Jade Ruins Realm,” Situ Wenxian declared loftily. “As for this turncoat son... cripple his cultivation and throw him into the dungeons.”","......","Situ Wenxian’s sudden appearance and domineering methods completely shuffled the cards of Darklake’s court. Those hidden in the shadows with ulterior motives had all floated to the fore and were captured in one fell swoop.","Some princes, princesses, and brothers to emperor were also involved. All of them were crippled of their cultivation and thrown into the dungeons. Compared to the soundless assassinations in the capital, the cleansing of court was a much more bloody affair. Nearly thirty percent of the officials were executed on the spot. The Ling, Yuwen, and other small families that’d defected to Dark Orchid were completely exterminated.","An atmosphere of blood wreathed the capital. It was the final reckoning as the Lus and Situ Wenxian would all be doomed if the slightest hint went wrong.","Great Xia immortals would be completely unrestrained once the heavenly book’s power vanished. Lu Tianling could withstand external foes, but he could not defend against internal enemies.","The capital was surrounded by a massive formation that sealed the city within. All enemies were captured or executed on the spot. A massive spilling of blood occurred within the capital for an entire day."]},{"number":2306,"title":"Chapter 2306: Chapter 2202.1: Life Marches on the Heavens, Faith Collapses","paragraphs":["Chapter 2202.1: Life Marches on the Heavens, Faith Collapses","The purge of dissidents was complete when Lu Yun and the others returned to the capital. While the formation over the city was still active, Lu Yun was able to come and go at will since he was the one who’d secretly set it up.","Upon returning home, the gray jiao made for the seed storage zone within the secret vault while Terra Demon took time to adjust his condition. Although the battle had consumed a great deal of resources, they still gained much as both of them were able to fully refine the Hongmeng fruit and recover a bit more from their injuries.","Next time they met someone like Lu Youya, they wouldn’t need the aid of the Nineheavens Brahman Formation. Either Terra Demon or the gray jiao would easily kill such an immortal by themselves.","Lu Yun had broken through to latter nascent soul during the battle and saw his strength increase explosively once again. However, given what he was about to face next, mere latter nascent soul was just a tiny ripple in the vast sea—no matter how heaven-defying he was.","After the breakthrough, he found that something deep in his soul had been made whole again. This process was something that the past him had never experienced, whether in his three thousand lifetimes or the sealed memories. As such, such encounters were incredibly precious to him.","This was the rhythm that all living beings must endure throughout their development, as well as the trend of heavenly dao. It was something that he must understand.","......","“Young master, what should we do about the Ouyang Clan?” Terra Demon came to Lu Yun after a few days of rest and recovery.","“The Ouyang Clan...” Lu Yun mused for a while. “Leave them be for now, they’ll be useful when the time comes.”","Terra Demon nodded.","Ouyang Shengtian was now peak latter nascent soul. Although that wasn’t strong, he would be of vital importance at a critical time. His story about being a wandering immortal who’d possessed the former Ouyang genius? Lu Yun didn’t believe a word of it. He’d played along all this time and pretended to buy into what the Ouyang young master was spinning.","If a wandering immortal could possess another, why would he come to a lowly third rank world of cultivation?","It was far more likely that Ouyang Shengtian had devoured an unlucky wandering cultivator with the help of a powerhouse, thereby obtaining all of the wandering cultivator’s experience and memories. Ouyang Shengtian was still the same as he’d always been.","Lu Yun merely kept up the pretense and outwitted the would-be mastermind. The Ouyang Clan was likewise his tool. His core secrets had never been revealed to them—any that seemed like crucial details were just false intelligence.","He’d taken all of their spirit stones to cut them off at the knees. At the same time, he didn’t think that the Ouyang young master really had brought out all of his family’s spirit stones.","......","Another few days passed, leaving only ten days until the heavenly book’s power vanished from the realm. Lu Yun continued his preparations, reforging the Aureate Bird Cauldron into a lower dao rank treasure.","This was the highest level of treasure he could create at the moment. If word got out that a nascent soul cultivator could refine a lower draw rank treasure, even Great Xia would be up in arms about it.","Dao treasures were exceedingly hard to refine and a dao rank pill cauldron was rare even in Great Xia. If the nascent soul cultivator could manage the feat at his level of cultivation, then forging an immortal rank pill cauldron when he progressed wouldn’t be a difficult task!","Lu Yun threw the treasure to Terra Demon after raising its rank. The latter accepted it with a rueful smile. In the subsequent days, he trained Bloodbath, Lu Xiaochi, Gui Xie, and the others during the day while tirelessly refining pills and medicines at night.","His toils resulted in a successful refinement of a second Hongmeng Fruit within a short period of time. His immortal king nascent soul was further repaired and a hint of the profound meaning of immortal overlord appeared in his body.","Terra Demon was overjoyed, doubly overjoyed! Working for His Grace was always a matter of joy!","Lu Xuan, Wu Zhen, and the rest of the Vermilion Bird returned to the capital. This troop had been fully reformed, with Lu Xuan and Wu Zhen as its respective commander and vice commander. They were both latter nascent soul.","As Lu Xuan practiced the Sword of Slaughter Record, his cultivation had long exceeded the parameters of nascent soul. After a year of tempering, he could overcome even initial soul projection cultivators.","Meanwhile for Wu Zhen, although he was an ordinary latter nascent soul, he was sharp witted and thus served as the Vermilion Bird strategist. Many of his stratagems helped the troop defuse danger after danger.","The rest of the Vermilion Bird’s three hundred and sixty-five soldiers were all latter golden core. Dressed in red battle armor, they were covered in scars and injuries. Killing intent brimmed on their faces—a testament to their great experience.","......","The sparring grounds of the Lu residence.","“Only latter golden core?” Lu Yun frowned at the newly returned Vermilion Birds.","“Young master, there hasn’t been enough time. It is already an incredible feat that many brothers have progressed from foundation establishment to latter golden core.” Ever since Lu Xuan practiced the Sword of Slaughter Record, his aura strode toward perfection. Not only was there a lack of sinister killing intent around him, but his entire person was much more gentle than before.","Such was the highest level of slaughter—a blade hidden within a smile, killing without form.","“That’s not enough,” Lu Yun shook his head. “You cannot participate in what’s to come.”","The soldiers beneath didn’t say anything when they heard the young master’s announcement. Loyalty was deeply etched into their bones. No matter what Lu Yun said, they wouldn’t raise a word of protest. If it wasn’t for the young man, all of them would still be foundation establishment, or even mere qi refinement cultivators.","Apart from the city guards that initially made up the Vermilion Birds, the rest were impoverished citizens that Lu Yun had chosen out of the slums of the northern quadrant.","“Young master...” Lu Xuan was a personal follower since he’d always served Lu Yun. This time, however, he raised an objection. “Young master, the brothers have been training in Barren Mountain for more than a year so they can offer their services...”","“Offer their services?” Lu Yun shook his head. “In what’s to come, you lot don’t even have the right to be cannon fodder.”","That drew a reaction and the men lowered their heads.","“Any singular elite from grandpa’s Azure Dragon, White Tiger, and Black Tortoise troops can defeat all of the Vermilion Birds.”","The Lu Yun of old hadn’t understood, but the Lu Yun now was very much aware that the core contingent of Lu Tianling’s three secret armies were all soul separation powerhouses.","Lu Tianling bore great secrets. He hailed from Great Xia and had resided in Darklake Empire for two hundred years. If it wasn’t for Terra Demon detecting something slightly out of the ordinary, even Lu Yun wouldn’t know his grandpa’s full strength.","It was no easy feat to evade the Origin Sect’s dedicated hunt and retreat to a world of cultivation.","“But in the battlefield to come, these three troops do not have the right to be cannon fodder either,” Lu Yun sighed. “Terra Demon and I jointly suppressed a true immortal at Tiger Suppression Pass a few days ago. True immortals are the cannon fodder.”","Lu Xuan, Wu Zhen, and everyone assembled reeled with shock. The young master once reviled as trash, one who looked completely harmless, had killed a true immortal?","Even a soul separation cultivator was a lofty, inviolable being in their eyes, to say nothing of a true immortal. What kind of concept was a true immortal?!","“I say this not to boast about my feats,” Lu Yun chuckled at those gathered below. “I value your potential, not your lives. Dying now means nothing to me. I must have a trump card if I am to reign over the worlds, and that card is you.","“Therefore, my lowest requirement of you is golden immortal!”","Hidden in the shadows, Lu Tianling’s heart shook at this declaration. Golden immortal?!","That was the stuff of legends! It was a level that enabled one to be a titled marquis in Great Xia! That was what Lu Yun expected of them? Golden immortal?","Sharp gasps rang throughout the crowd, but a ball of fire also rose in their hearts. Hadn’t golden core once been a lofty, inviolable being to them? But now, many of them were latter golden core and about to break through to nascent soul.","That unfathomable chasm was easily crossed! So was the distant goal of golden immortal truly so impossible? Their young master had ascended from qi refinement to latter nascent soul in a year!","A wisp of... faith in Lu Yun rose from the Vermilion Birds. As faint as it was, Lu Yun could clearly sense it transmute into endless goodwill that surged into the Seal of the Multitude.","The empty seal began to fill with a strong current of goodwill. It wasn’t much, but it was unending. It would never cease so long as faith did not extinguish. Lu Yun also found that if he was willing, he could lend some of his abilities to those who believed in him.","“I see...” he murmured as he looked at the fervent soldiers beneath him."]},{"number":2307,"title":"Chapter 2307: Chapter 2202.2: Life Marches on the Heavens, Faith Collapses","paragraphs":["Chapter 2202.2: Life Marches on the Heavens, Faith Collapses","In a previous lifetime, when he was the High Lord of the Northern Sky, Lu Yun likewise oversaw a large group of immortals who believed in him. However, that faith had been completely useless. It could at most build a line of communication and enable him to bestow combat arts unto his followers for cultivation.","Yet with the Seal of the Multitude as the medium, Lu Yun could lend part of his combat arts to the soldiers. Of course, they were so weak on the soldiers that they were essentially negligible—it made no difference if the men used one or not.","But once Lu Yun became an immortal, then the combat arts he could lend would be formidable indeed. The more pious his followers’ faith was, the stronger the combat arts would be.","Goodwill transformed from faith seemed to have more uses than just enhancing cultivation. Even the strength of combat arts was enhanced. That meant to say that combat arts deployed through goodwill were several times more powerful than they usually were.","After reaching latter nascent soul, some of the secrets within the Nine Chapters of Dao and the Seal of the Multitude revealed themselves to Lu Yun.","This was just one kind of usage for goodwill. For the moment, he primarily used it to consolidate his cultivation of latter nascent soul. A certain enlightenment dawned at this time. When living beings practiced immortal dao, they believed in the heavenly dao!","Did the heavenly dao need to collect faith and maintain itself through belief?","He suddenly had an answer to something that’d puzzled him for quite some time—how the heavenly dao had broken.","When life marched on the heavens, their faith collapsed and so the heavenly dao broke.","Four hours later, Wu Zhen and Lu Xuan left the capital with some pills and other supplies. They vanished amid the vast world of cultivation. Lu Yun didn’t care when they came back since they wouldn’t be of any help in the short term.","......","Lu Yun relaxed on a reclining chair in his yard and leisurely drank tea. He took in the afternoon sun and teased Lan’er, prompting giggles out of her.","Bam!","His front door exploded into a pile of shards as Kong Mengqian rushed in, dressed in a black men’s outfit.","“Master master! I’ve successfully refined the first restriction on the bamboo!” Her cheeks were flushed red with excitement as she ran up to Lu Yun like she was presenting a treasure.","Lu Yun looked wordlessly at his front door. Why was his disciple the same as his grandfather? Couldn’t these noble beings lower themselves to gently push the door open?","Lu Tianling had kicked in more doors than could be counted, and ever since Kong Mengqian moved in, the doors of Lu Yun’s house were essentially swapped out everyday.","“So you’ve refined the first restriction?” He rose from the chair and calmly regarded the excited girl.","“Yep yep, I did it I did it!” Kong Mengqian’s blush was so bright that Lan’er covered her mouth as she giggled. The two girls were of similar age, so they became quick friends after Kong Mengqian moved in.","Lu Yun had also taken time to help Lan’er reach latter foundation establishment; she was only one step away from forming her core. She was gentle by nature and disliked conflict, so Lu Yun didn’t drill her like he did the Vermilion Birds. Otherwise, she would’ve coalesced her core long ago.","“And what have you gained from it?” Lu Yun cracked the Eye of Nullification open to scan the girl, noting that her true origin had taken on a hint of emerald from the bamboo.","“Gained?” Kong Mengqian blinked. All she had in mind was how to cook spirit cuisine like Lu Yun and the Nine Forms of the Cloud Dragon. Hence, she’d charged over as soon as she’d succeeded with the first restriction.","Lu Yun shook his head. While his disciple was latter soul separation and immensely strong, she was only fifteen years old at the end of the day. She lacked some tempering of the heart and mind.","Kong Mengqian frowned slightly and composed herself. She closed her eyes and scanned her body. Her master watched silently without saying a word.","“The Azure Emperor Chapter of Inception?” Kong Mengqian opened her eyes with astonishment.","“Oho, this method, is it?” Lu Yun responded with a smile.","“Um, this, ah...” She couldn’t understand why a new cultivation method had appeared in her mind after she refined that exceedingly ordinary bamboo. She fully understood the method after reading over its outline, but such high level cultivation methods couldn’t be found even in her home.","“This will be what you practice in the future and you can teach it to family if you wish, but they must join the sect first.” Lu Yun winked at the girl.","He was correct as he was able to practice the Nine Chapters of Dao because the heavenly dao had planted a dao mark in his body. In the same vein, those who wished to practice the Azure Emperor Chapter of Inception needed to refine the stick of bamboo first.","However, since Sky had gifted the bamboo to Kong Mengqian, that meant only those who obtained the recognition of the heavenly dao would be able to refine it.","“No!” Kong Mengqian shook her head as fast as she could. “Those people looked down on me when I was at home, saying that I was derelict in duty and focused on irrelevant business, that I impeded my proper cultivation! Now that I have this method, I’m going to reach a certain proficiency first before I go back and slap their faces!”","Kong Mengqian waved her fists in front of Lu Yun.","“Besides... can I teach this to others even if I wanted to?” She looked at Lu Yun with a strange expression, having seen hints of something after refining the bamboo.","“You can’t, it can only be done with the sect’s approval,” he cackled in response. “So practice well! Your future is limitless after obtaining me as your master.”","“Master...” Kong Mengqian pouted. “You said that you’d teach me something if I refined one of the restrictions.”","“This is a jade slip for the Nine Forms of the Cloud Dragon. Go back and practice it.” Lu Yun took out a jade slip from his storage ring and tossed it to the girl. Delighted, she quickly caught it and scanned it with her consciousness.","“As for the method to cook spirit cuisine, that requires the accumulation of various experience. Focus on cultivation for now. When your level is high enough, I will teach you how to cook spirit cuisine such that you can draw multiple inferences from one fact,” Lu Yun chuckled.","“Okay!” Kong Mengqian nodded emphatically and left the yard, hugging the jade slip to herself. Only now did she feel that Lu Yun was her master. He was hardly an ordinary person if he could easily give away heaven-defying methods like the Azure Emperor Chapter of Inception! Additionally, she’d asked around regarding the Lu young master after settling in at the Lu residence.","He’d been a seventh level qi refinement prodigal one year ago, but was now latter nascent soul. It’d only been a year!","It would be an astonishing feat even where she was from, not to mention that this had taken place in a low level cultivation world with sparse qi. It was akin to a tale from mythology! To many, the worlds of cultivation were nothing more than discarded worlds.","Lu Yun sighed when Kong Mengqian left, then directed the servants to find a new door and repair his house’s front doors.","......","Time passed day by day; Terra Demon noticed the rules hovering over his head gradually lessening until they fully vanished. The second they did, he fully retracted the strength that he used to cut through the heavenly book’s power. It took only a few moments for his strength to rise by another thirty percent.","“Is it finally gone?” murmured Lu Yun as he looked at the sky.","“The Origin Sect must have noticed that I killed their true immortal, how will they respond?”","The sect wouldn’t dare act too openly since Great Xia’s laws were still in place. A mere Marquis Origin was not the final authority in the immortal dynasty, nor would the chief law enforcer of Great Xia permit the sect to act as wantonly as it would in the worlds of cultivation.","Therefore, the sect would find an excuse to take action.","“Brother Lu, those from Dark Orchid are here.” Ouyang Shengtian rushed to the Lu residence as soon as the heavenly book’s power vanished.","“Oh?” Lu Yun raised an eyebrow.","Ouyang brothers Ouyang Shengmu and Ouyang Shenghe had reached initial nascent soul. Meanwhile, Ouyang Shengxiang had broken through the constraints of a connate fragrance constitution and advanced rapidly after establishing her foundation. She was now latter nascent soul.","A connate fragrance constitution was a rare and precious constitution even in Great Xia, but the holder’s cultivation speed prior to foundation establishment was much too slow. With Ouyang Shengtian claiming to be possessed by a wandering immortal, it didn’t appear out of the ordinary that the Ouyang siblings progressed so rapidly.","“Prince Sui’s grandson, Sui Ge, is here to welcome my younger sister to Dark Orchid. They will hold their wedding upon their return,” Ouyang Shengtian chuckled ruefully.","“Sui Ge?” Lu Yun blinked. “Isn’t Ouyang Shengxiang betrothed to the Dark Orchid crown prince? So why isn’t Crown Prince Wang Song here?”","“Um...?” Ouyang Shengtian hesitated. “It’s actually Sui Ge who will marry my sister, not Wang Song.”","“Huh?” Lu Yun started. “So... Prince Sui intends to mount a coup?”","“Um...” Ouyang Shengtian’s expression froze."]},{"number":2308,"title":"Chapter 2308: Chapter 2203.1: Hadal Fire","paragraphs":["Chapter 2203.1: Hadal Fire","With the cessation of the heavenly book’s power, Jade Ruins Realm was as if an unlocked vault. Anyone could come and go and take whatever they wished.","Worlds of cultivation were nothing worthy of note and the Jade Ruins Realm ranked very much at the bottom. They were also regarded as a lower world of cultivation.","Yet it was precisely this world that’d seen the appearance of Immortal Burial Valley. It shook the realm when it first appeared, but none of the other worlds—including Great Xia—thought much of it.","The only thing worth taking note of by some factions was that an immortal seemed to be buried there. However, nothing came of it.","But then the Human Emperor of Great Xia took up arms and led his eight titled kings and thirty-six marquises into the Celestial Realm Battlefront. He disturbed the heavenly book to negate its influence over this world.","That was when everyone realized Immortal Burial Valley was no ordinary place, so activity arose all over the world as people focused on the valley. None of it had anything to do with Lu Yun since he couldn’t run fast enough from what was buried within. Why would he draw closer to the hubbub?","There would be many immortals who would die in the coming disturbance—thus fulfilling the geographic location’s name. It was a nightmare for him, as well as despair. He even felt that he’d come to this world because of what was buried beneath the valley.","......","Sui Ge arriving at Dark City was both unexpected and entirely within reason. Dark Orchid needed a legitimate reason if it wished to move against Darklake. Their representatives to the Darklake capital would encounter certain friction, which would make a perfect pretext for war. In fact, it was highly likely that the entire delegation would be lost.","Sui Ge was Prince Sui’s most beloved grandson, and Prince Sui’s status in Dark Orchid was as if a god. Even the emperor needed to show him respect. Thus, this delegation of cannon fodder should not be led by someone so important to Prince Sui.","Given the prince’s background, he wouldn’t be oblivious about the Origin Sect’s matters.","Lu Yun’s eyes glinted as he watched Ouyang Shengtian depart.","“We can’t let them into the city,” he took a deep breath. “It looks like the true immortal from before was just cannon fodder to test grandfather’s trump cards...”","Lu Youya had been a threat to the Lu Clan whether alive or dead. If he died, the Origin Sect would understand Lu Tianling’s current level of strength. They would know that true immortals were insufficient to match the Lus and prepare accordingly. If he didn’t die, then a true immortal located in Dark City was a latent Detonation Talisman. He would destroy the entire nation when activated.","The only thing they didn’t know was that it wasn’t Lu Tianling, but Lu Yun who’d destroyed the true immortal.","There were certainly immortals mixed in with Sui Ge’s delegation. Letting them into the city would be giving the wolf access to the flock. But if they were denied entry, that gave them an ideal excuse to attack Darklake.","For something as massive as the Origin Sect, all they needed was a simple excuse to march on the Lu Clan.","......","Dark City’s walls were roughly one hundred meters tall. Lu Tianling, Situ Wenxian, Lu Xiaochi, and a host of officials stood on the ramparts.","For cultivators, city walls were decorations since they could fly right over obstacles. But for higher level cultivation empires or Great Xia, city walls were a boundary.","Once someone entered the city walls, they were subject to its control. Some cities possessed formations that could kill any cultivator or immortal within its walls at any time. Such defensive formations depended on the definition of city walls and helped the city fend off external attacks—such as Dark City.","It’d been roughly a year since Terra Demon joined. With his presence, it was much more convenient for Lu Yun to set up various preparations. After all, he was able to create any higher level material that he needed.","Whoosh whoosh whoosh!","Rays of brilliant sword light broke through the northern sky. They were obnoxiously resplendent and several dozen meters long each. It was plain to see that the ones riding the flying swords were all greater than nascent soul.","A massive golden war chariot led the rays—a flying treasure. A young man dressed in opulent robes stood on it. He was handsome, grace defined, and looked out over the world with a hint of unbridled pride.","“The Dark Orchid delegation has arrived! The emperor of Darklake Empire will come out in welcome!” A resounding voice boomed when the sword light was fifty kilometers away from Dark City. When it finished, the delegation was less than twenty-five meters away.","“Ignore them.” Lu Yun curled his lip and took a bite out of a spirit fruit.","Cheeks spasmed from the officials standing beneath Situ Wenxian. Only the Lu young master would dare be so impudent to the emperor!","After Situ Wenxian displayed power beyond the limits of a third rank empire, he thoroughly subdued his subjects. Combined with several days of bloody reckoning through the capital, Dark City was finally one one heart through and through.","Situ Wenxian then declared that he would lead Darklake beyond the shackles of a third rank empire. It was a bold announcement that met with widespread support. He now commanded utmost authority and respect in Darklake. Despite Lu Yun’s blatant lack of courtesy, no one dared say anything. The incredibly prejudiced Marshal Lu Tianling stood off to the side, merrily looking at his grandson with a benevolent expression.","Naturally, Situ Wenxian decided that he hadn’t seen anything.","“Smack them all to pieces, those Dark Orchid little shits! They bullied us for hundreds of years, so let’s not even allow them to go back this time!” Lu Yun complained as he crunched through the spirit fruit.","More than one eye roll occurred in the crowd, but people didn’t dare say anything all the same. There were more than three hundred in the Dark Orchid delegation, all of them stronger than nascent soul. The leading two dozen were soul projection powerhouses. If in any other third rank empire, this force would immediately sweep through the entire nation.","“Well, Situ Wenxian? Why haven’t you opened the city gates in welcome?” shouted an elder standing next to Sui Ge in the chariot.","“How dare you use the emperor’s name!” roared back a tyrannical voice. A fruit pit shot out from the city walls and landed in the elder’s mouth.","Clink!","The elder cried out with pain and fell off the chariot. His teeth were bloody nubs as he spat them out from his mouth.","“How dare you!” The development completely took the delegation off guard. “How dare you attack representatives from your superior nation!”","Sui Ge remained unmoved, but the other soul projection powerhouses brought out their treasures to rush forward.","“Wait.” Sui Ge waved his hand. “So it’s someone who tasted defeat at my hands!”","He easily recognized Lu Yun after the young man threw the fruit pit out. Although Lu Yun looked different from before, Sui Ge still recognized him.","“Tasted defeat at your hands?” Lu Yun raised a brow and jumped up to a part of the city walls that jutted out before anyone could react. He smirked at the other. “I wonder who it was that ran away with their tail between their legs in Ashflame City? And you have the nerve to say I lost to you?”","Denizens of Dark City took a sharp breath when they heard Lu Yun’s words. They all knew who it was that stood on the chariot—first among the Dark Orchid younger generation, Prince Sui’s grandson!","Darklake’s number one prodigal had sent Dark Orchid’s greatest genius running with his tail between his legs?","Based on what Sui Ge said, the two did seem to share a feud. When connected to how Lu Yun had forced down a Dark Orchid elder with a single fruit pit, the people understood that the famed Lu Tianling’s grandson was likely very different from what rumors made him out to be.","On the city walls, the group of youngsters standing with Situ Yun felt their faces burn with mortification. They’d all looked down on Lu Yun before and even felt that he was a disgrace to Lu Tianling’s name. Yet somehow, the young man had overtaken them at some point.","No one was surprised by Lu Yun’s attitude. He was arrogant, overbearing, pompous, and completely out of control save for Lu Tianling’s influence. This was Lu Yun, an absolute good-for-nothing.","Since Situ Wenxian didn’t say anything, none of the other officials dared utter a word.","“Hmph!” Sui Ge’s face darkened. “Dare you fight me, Lu Yun?”","Losing at Ashflame had become the greatest dishonor of his life. His greatest goal in coming to Dark City was Lu Yun. He wanted to triumph over Lu Yun and wash away his humiliation.","As for genius and prodigal... those were the appraisals of others. If Lu Yun didn’t care about the titles, neither did he.","“Not interested,” Lu Yun sneered from up high. “I’m not interested in stepping on someone I’ve already stepped on before.”","Sui Ge glowered at the response.","“Who would think that Lu Tianling’s grandson is a spineless coward!” he sniffed with a vicious smile.","“It’s not up to you to decide if I’m spineless or not.” Lu Yun yawned and stretched lazily. “What, is stepping on a loser the courageous thing to do?”","“Hahahaha!!” Sui Ge roared with laughter. “If I really had engaged you in combat in Ashflame, that would’ve leveled the city. I did not wish to damage Ashflame, which gave you an opening. Do you honestly think you can defeat me?”"]},{"number":2309,"title":"Chapter 2309: Chapter 2203.2: Hadal Fire","paragraphs":["Chapter 2203.2: Hadal Fire","“Don’t be provoked by him, Yun’er,” Lu Tianling frowned and transmitted a warning to his grandson.","“It is of no matter,” Lu Yun smiled. “Don’t worry, grandfather. I know what can and cannot be done.”","“Lu Yun, dare you fight in single combat in front of the citizens of the two empires?” Sui Ge’s voice carried clearly as he stared at the young man.","“Whyever not?” The Lu young master curled his lip. “But it’s boring to just fight. How about we add a forfeit?”","“What do you have in mind?” A smile curved Sui Ge’s lips. It was most ideal that Lu Yun was willing to fight.","“You are the leader of the Dark Orchid delegation, aren’t you?” Lu Yun scanned the group, identifying a couple hidden experts with the Eye of Nullification. However, they followed Sui Ge’s orders.","“I am,” the young man nodded.","“Then if I win, you shall announce on your emperor’s behalf that Darklake Empire is released from Dark Orchid’s control. How about it?”","A loud hubbub rose with Lu Yun’s response. Darklake Empire had been part of Dark Orchid ever since its founding. Over the past two thousand years, any soul projection cultivator that appeared in its lands was taken to Dark Orchid.","After all this time, Darklake was firmly tied to Dark Orchid. The superior nation fully commandeered all of the nation’s resources and mines. When a lower rank spirit vein appeared in Darklake one thousand years ago, a Dark Orchid powerhouse came to take it away.","Yet now, Lu Yun’s first demand was for Darklake to be freed from its vassal status. Although Situ Wenxian had announced several days ago that he would do the very same, it still induced panic when the possibility was close at hand.","“Darklake Empire wishes to be independent?” Sui Ge took in a sharp breath. This little empire had quite the ambition! Even those in the delegation exchanged glances with each other.","“Or can it be that the vaunted little prince cannot make the decision?” Lu Yun smiled.","“And if you lose?” Sui Ge asked instead.","“If I lose?” Lu Yun thought for a bit. “Whatever you want.”","“Whatever I want... I can represent Dark Orchid, but can you represent Darklake?” Sui Ge snorted.","“He can,” interjected the quiet Situ Wenxian. “If Lu Yun loses, we will strive to fulfill any requirement that Dark Orchid raises.”","“Alright!” Sui Ge immediately agreed.","It was the Darklake emperor on one side and the Dark Orchid delegation on the other. The latter also represented their emperor, so any agreement reached between the two was set in stone. There was nothing that could be changed. If one side went back on their word, they would be despised by other nations and even punished by the heavenly book when its power returned.","“But before that, shouldn’t the Darklake emperor open the city gates and let us inside?” Sui Ge continued.","“There’s no need for that, let’s fight first.” Lu Yun jumped down from the city walls. Immortals Forbidden flew to his hand in a streak of light. As he progressed in cultivation, so was the weapon reforged into a paramount rank spirit weapon. Glowing with crimson light, the flying sword burned like a miniature sun.","“So you’ve obtained a paramount rank spirit weapon, no wonder you’re so cocky.” Sui Ge gave a long peal of laughter and jumped down from the flying treasure. Snowy radiance flashed through his hand—another paramount rank flying sword!","Additionally, the energy ripples from his flare of power indicated that he was initial soul projection.","Soul projection and nascent soul were two entirely different realms. Entering soul projection meant that the nascent soul could separate and live outside of the body. It would survive even if the body died.","One only needed to find a treasure that could reform a physical body to fully recover. It was the equivalent of a second life.","Sui Ge hadn’t matched Lu Yun when he was latter nascent soul, but now that he’d broken through to soul projection, he was more than ten times stronger than before. In his eyes, Lu Yun was absolutely inferior to him now.","“Soul projection?” Lu Yun quirked his lips and didn’t waste time with speech. He leapt into the air and drew a fiery arc with Immortals Forbidden, bringing the sword down on Sui Ge’s head.","“Die!” The little prince roared and also flew into the air. He raised his paramount rank spirit weapon in front of him and met Lu Yun in the air.","Bam!","When the two paramount rank spirit weapons crashed together, Sui Ge’s body paused and shot back out. Lu Yun swiftly followed behind, not letting up.","“So strong! He’s latter nascent soul!” Sui Ge realized with dismay and stopped his momentum with a twist of his body.","“Should we help?” asked a brooding middle-aged man among the Dark Orchid delegation.","“Wait for Sui Ge to finish his fight.” A handsome twenty-some year old young man shook his head. “Although the heavenly book’s power has been dispersed, its surveillance remains. It will enact a reckoning after the fact for many things.”","The middle-aged man fell silent.","While the heavenly book no longer held sway over the world, its laws continued to keep an eye on Jade Ruins Realm. It was one thing if the offender was an immortal or cultivator from another world. They could just leave after the fact, placing themselves out of reach of the heavenly book’s power.","It was another matter entirely for those who lived in the realm.","The treasure didn’t interfere in trivial matters or private vows and promises. Everything related to nations, however, was under its purview. If one side broke their word, the heavenly book was sure to inflict heavy punishment when it returned.","The Dark Orchid delegation watched the fight with grim looks. Anyone could tell that Sui Ge had the losing hand.","“Lu Tianling’s grandson is Lu Tianling’s grandson alright...” A young man with silvery-white hair and the energy ripples of initial nascent soul regarded Lu Yun coldly.","Bam!","Sui Ge flew backward like a rag doll after an immense explosion.","“Do we continue, little prince?” Lu Yun smiled faintly at Sui Ge as he hovered over his sword. He’d yet to deploy most of his sword techniques—he was crushing Sui Ge through pure strength alone.","“Heh heh heh heh heh...” Sui Ge struggled up from the back and sneered coolly at Lu Yun. “Do you think you can beat me like this?”","Humm!","A loud reverberation sounded in the air as a flaming red gourd appeared in his hand. It irradiated the surroundings with a scorching heat wave, warming even Lu Yun’s face beyond his limits.","“A paramount rank dao weapon...” Whether it was those from Dark Orchid or Darklake, all those on the scene took in sharp breaths.","The flame-red gourd emanated a powerful aura that belonged to dao weapons. Its presence was a constant reminder that this was a paramount rank dao weapon.","Prince Sui certainly had gone to great efforts on behalf of his grandson! It was also apparent from this that neither Prince Sui nor Dark Orchid was as simple as they appeared on the surface.","Gravity appeared on Lu Yun’s face. He wasn’t afraid of the weapon’s rank, but what it contained; the fires of heaven and earth.","Indeed, the weapon was just a container for such a fire. There were one hundred and eight recorded fires of heaven and earth. Thirty-six heavenly fires, seventy-two earthly fires. Lu Yun’s disciple Kong Mengqian wielded only the lowest ranked earthly fire.","The fire in this paramount rank dao weapon was also an earthly fire, but it was far higher ranked than Kong Mengqian’s. It hadn’t been subdued by its wielder, merely confined to the gourd to be used at will.","Although Lu Yun’s connate li fire was much stronger than ordinary fires of heaven and earth, its power was connected to his cultivation. His fire was so much weaker than the one in the gourd.","Sui Ge’s hands flicked through hand seals and sent the gourd floating over his head. A gout of black flame jumped out from it and turned it pitch-black. The heat wave immediately billowed over everything on the scene.","“Hadal Fire, ranked number eleven on the ranking of earthly fires,” Lu Yun identified solemnly. He must make it his!","Whoosh!","The crimson gourd’s stopper popped off and a tongue of black flame shot out of the opening. It curled toward Lu Yun, who evaded it with a quick dodge. But the moment he moved, the flame exploded.","Scorching heat grazed Lu Yun when the fire simply grazed him. Sui Ge cackled to see Lu Yun run and waved the black gourd into his hand. Waves of Hadal Fire shot out from it, more than ten times stronger than before.","The black flames swiftly coalesced into a massive bird with a nine meter wingspan. It dove the moment it formed and brought down a blazing heat wave onto Lu Yun.","“A Hadal Fire Spirit...” His pupils contracted violently."]},{"number":2310,"title":"Chapter 2310: Chapter 2204.1: Capturing a Fire Spirit","paragraphs":["Chapter 2204.1: Capturing a Fire Spirit","The fires of heaven and earth gave birth to fire spirits when they evolved to advanced levels. Fire spirits were as if spirit beasts—they possessed domineering strength and could deploy the full might of their flame.","Most fire spirits could evolve into monster spirits and ascend to incredibly powerful monster immortals. Once they reached immortality, they were at least dao immortal and wholly unafraid of immortal overlords.","However, it was exceedingly difficult for a fire of heaven and earth to bloom. After it came into being, another one hundred million years of accumulation was needed for a fire spirit to be born from said flame. And for one to become an immortal... there had only ever been one in the world of immortals of old.","The Undying Immortal King under the High Lord of the Southern Sky had been the greatest beneath the immortal emperor. Lu Yun hadn’t anticipated meeting a spirit of Hadal Fire here!","Hadal Fire itself was a formidable spirit beast. This one was untamed and simply confined by a gourd that was a paramount rank dao weapon. The most likely story was that someone had captured its core essence soon after it metamorphosed into a spirit. Otherwise, even a paramount rank dao weapon wouldn’t be able to keep it confined.","No wonder Sui Ge was so confident, he had a spirit of Hadal Fire!","“Go!” Lu Yun cast his own hand seal when he saw the enormous bird of fire rushing toward him. A loud bird cry sounded behind him as a giant bird of golden-red flame soared out.","A piercing bird croon shook the skies.","“A Three-Footed Aureate Bird formed from Sol Truefire!” Many were the knowledgeable cultivators present who could immediately identify the bird.","“Should I go help?” Blue fire danced in Kong Mengqian’s hand as she watched nervously from the city walls. Sol Truefire was ranked a little lower than Hadal Fire, not to mention her master faced a fire spirit.","Fire from a true Aureate Bird wouldn't shy away from the fire spirit, but Lu Yun’s Sol Truefire was only derived from the core of a divine beast with the Three-Footed Aureate Bird’s bloodline.","“There’s no need.” Terra Demon calmed her nerves. “Sui Ge is nothing but a joke to the young master.”","Bam!","A black bird collided with a gold bird and surprised everyone when Lu Yun’s weaker Aureate Bird Truefire withstood the Hadal Fire Spirit!","Lu Yun took advantage of the opportunity to bring Immortals Forbidden down on Sui Ge.","“You seek death!” Sui Ge sneered to see the young man come for him. Another pillar of flame spewed from the gourd when he spun it, forming a second Hadal Fire Spirit in bird form.","With the fire spirit’s core essence trapped in the gourd, Sui Ge could summon any number of its replicas at will so long as he held the gourd.","Lu Yun paused when he saw the second bird and spun on his heel. He left an afterimage in the air and suddenly appeared behind Sui Ge, bringing his sword down with an overhang slash.","BAM!","When sword light bit into a curtain of light, Sui Ge bounced backward like a rubber ball. Lu Yun’s eyes also widened as he rapidly backed up, dispersing the enormous recoil.","“A paramount dao rank defensive treasure...” His eyes twitched as he looked at the little prince.","Not even the three ninth rank cultivation empires possessed that many paramount rank treasures. Even the law enforcers wielded only upper rank! Yet Sui Ge easily took out two paramount ranked ones with a flip of his hand? Damn, he’s richer than me!","“Chenguang, what do you think that thing on Sui Ge looks like?” came a taunting voice from the city walls—Yu Shuai.","“Ummm... a turtle shell?” responded a confused Zhao Chenguang.","“Yep, it’s a huge turtle shell!” Yu Shuai burst into uproarious laughter.","“Dang, that’s a huge turtle down there!” Zhao Chenguang joined his friend with hoots of mirth, drawing chuckles from others in the vicinity.","It was as if Sui Ge shouldered a massive turtle shell on his back as he solidly protected his body, leaving only his head and limbs outside. He truly did look like an enormous turtle.","“That should be a paramount rank defensive treasure refined from a ninth rank Black Tortoise...” Situ Wenxian sucked in a sharp breath. Lu Yun had no hope of winning this battle. A Hadal Fire Spirit raised the offensive while another paramount dao rank treasure brought up the rear. Although Sui Ge couldn’t deploy its full power, such treasures could instinctively defend their masters.","In either case, they were something that the current Lu Yun couldn’t overcome.","Aouuu!","The Hadal Fire Spirit devoured Lu Yun’s Sol Truefire. In the absence of an opponent, the fire spirit swallowed its copy and rushed the Lu young master again.","“Tsk...” Lu Yun snorted with laughter and waved another Aureate Golden Bird into existence.","Much weaker than the one before, it took only a few exchanges before the Hadal Fire Spirit swallowed the new bird.","Then there was a second, third, fourth, and fifth golden bird... Aureate Bird Truefire filled the skies and formed palm-sized birds of golden flame that flung themselves at the fire spirit.","The seemingly inexhaustible fire spirit devoured all comers; no one noticed a faint sheen of gold began to creep through its black eyes.","Humm!","An ancient pill cauldron with a simple design appeared over Lu Yun’s head. Rays of Aureate Bird Truefire rushed out with abandon and formed another flaming golden bird. The light in the Hadal Fire Spirit’s eyes intensified as it devoured more of the attacks, its aura growing more formidable as well.","“Hahaha, Lu Yun! Who could’ve thought that you’d bring out a lower dao rank weapon!” Sui Ge roared with laughter when he felt the fire spirit’s power grow stronger. “But so what? All the Aureate Bird Truefire is doing is just strengthening my Hadal Fire Spirit!”","“What an absolute idiot.” Lu Yun curled his lip and sent out more hand seals. The pill cauldron shook and spewed fire at a faster pace.","“Crafty kid.” The handsome young man within the Dark Orchid delegation smiled coolly. “He’s feeding Aureate Bird Truefire to the Hadal Fire Spirit to enhance its strength. He’s trying to help it break free of the Immortal Suppression Gourd. But heh, that’s so much easier said than done.”","The young man had accurately identified Lu Yun’s plan. Once the Hadal Fire Spirit broke free, it would immediately turn on its previous master. Although a paramount dao rank treasure protected Sui Ge, he would be burned to ashes regardless and left without a single bone fragment to his name.","The gourd was a second rank immortal treasure, but had been immensely damaged through the course of trapping the newly born fire spirit. Though it declined to a paramount dao rank treasure, it was still able to confine the fire spirit’s core essence.","As for Aureate Bird Truefire, the level that Lu Yun was producing it at wouldn’t help the fire spirit break free even in a hundred years. All it did was strengthen the bird’s power.","“Your dao treasure’s not bad to be able to release Aureate Bird Truefire. It can feed my fire spirit, so now it’s mine!” Sui Ge had run out of patience for the fight. He simply wanted Lu Yun to die right now.","He sent out another gout of Hadal Fire, keeping it in the form of fire instead of crafting a fire spirit. Black flames filled the sky as they churned toward Lu Yun.","“Heh, you won’t die if you don’t tempt death.” Lu Yun’s smile deepened. Instead of meeting it head-on, he deployed the Nine Forms of the Cloud Dragon and roamed the area as nine faint images.","While Hadal Fire was everywhere, Sui Ge couldn’t easily control it. If he could utilize a method like Kong Mengqian’s art of fire control, then Lu Yun would have no other choice but to run for his life.","Sadly for Sui Ge, all he mastered was rudimentary control over Hadal Fire.","“This is how you use fire.” Lu Yun suddenly paused and pushed out with one palm. A crimson fire dragon more than thirty meters long flew from his hand and snarled at the Hadal Fire.","Boom!","The two flames canceled each other out when they collided.","“Again!” Lu Yun pushed out another dragon of fire.","“Brahman Fire!” gasped the handsome young man in the delegation.","Brahman Fire was the lowest on the ranking of earthly fires, making it the weakest. But even so, it was not to be underestimated. A stunning genius of Great Xia once created a ninth rank formation thousands of years ago, calling it the Nineheavens Brahman Formation. It could summon any of the forbidden fires in the world. If Lu Yun was able to coalesce a dragon of Brahman Fire, that meant he’d subdued a bloom of said fire and brought it completely under his control.","“But I don’t sense the aura of any fires of heaven and earth...” The handsome young man frowned.","“Master, your grandson is impressive beyond belief...” Situ Wenxian clucked his tongue with amazement as he saw Lu Yun withstand Sui Ge equipped with a Hadal Fire Spirit.","The nearby officials, residents of Dark City, and cultivators gaped at the noble young man renowned for being trash in both deed and thought. They couldn’t connect the person flitting through the fight with the good-for-nothing called Lu Yun.","Aouuu!","Before anyone could react, the black bird in the sky suddenly shrieked a piercing cry.","PFFT!","Fully focused on controlling the Immortal Suppression Gourd, Sui Ge trembled and spat out a mouthful of blood."]},{"number":2311,"title":"Chapter 2311: Chapter 2204.2: Capturing a Fire Spirit","paragraphs":["Chapter 2204.2: Capturing a Fire Spirit","Amid a sea of shocked gazes, the paramount rank Immortal Suppression Gourd split open!","A gigantic black bird appeared out of nowhere. Its body ran thirty meters long and its wingspan stretched forty-five meters from tip to tip. Its long neck was soft and graceful; foreboding Hadal Fire trailed from three long tail feathers.","This was the true Hadal Fire Spirit! It was a spirit beast formed by Hadal flames—the Hadal Bird!","Legend had it that a drop of blood essence from the divine beast of the south—the Vermilion Bird—once landed in the hadal lands. Affected by hadal qi, it gradually became a blossom of black flames. This was known as Hadal Fire and indeed, the Hadal Bird possessed the bloodline of the Vermilion Bird.","“What?! Retreat!” shouted the handsome young man in the Dark Orchid delegation when the bird manifested. He himself fled for dear life, unable to look after Sui Ge’s survival.","Aouu!","The Hadal Bird erupted with a long bird call as black flames enveloped its body. Its ponderous wingspan snapped open as it dove at Sui Ge below. The bird’s eyes were entirely faint gold and sentience filled its previously empty look. At the moment, it glared with pure hate.","“Damn it!” Sui Ge gasped. While he couldn’t utilize the full force of a paramount rank dao treasure, it’d still saved him when the gourd split open. Now that the Hadal Bird rushed down, he was so terrified that his wits nearly deserted him.","The paramount rank spirit sword immediately appeared beneath his feet and shot into the sky with a trace of sword light thirty meters long. Yet, how would the Hadal Bird let him go? It shook its fiery wings and streaked into a massive shadow to pursue the little prince.","It was fully freed from the confines of the Immortal Suppression Gourd and could bring its entire strength to bear. Having devoured endless rays of connate li fire before this, it was now on par with an august immortal. Could a mere soul projection cultivator like Sui Ge evade its attack?","Probably not, not even with a paramount dao treasure protecting him.","Sui Ge didn’t even have time to cry out in fear when the massive body swept by him. He immediately vaporized into nothing; his paramount rank dao treasure turned into a pitted turtle shell that clanked to the ground.","Even almighty dao treasures couldn’t stand up to the strength of the Hadal Bird!","The bird threw back its head, flourished its wings, and headed for the north. That was where the Dark Orchid delegation had fled to and where the true master of the Immortal Suppression Gourd was.","......","Situ Wenxian and the others on the city walls looked at each other with shock.","“Yun’er, how did you do it?” Lu Tianling asked as soon as Lu Yun vaulted up to the crowd.","“I fed some stuff to the Hadal Fire Spirit,” he chuckled. “So does this count as my victory?”","“Heh heh heh,” Lu Tianling cackled. “The heavenly book just sent word that Darklake Empire is no longer a Dark Orchid vassal. It is an independent nation! From now on, we no longer need to be ruled by others.”","Although the heavenly book was no longer in effect over Jade Ruins Realm, it still observed the world nonetheless. The moment Sui Ge died to Hadal Fire, a tremor exuded from the book at the center of the Celestial Realm Battlefront and erased Darklake from Dark Orchid’s list of vassals.","Since Lu Tianling could conceal himself from the book’s senses, he naturally had his ways of communicating with it.","“Good!” Lu Yun smiled. “Grandpa, I leave the capital in your hands. I have some things to take care of and will be back shortly.”","He raised a pillar of sword light before anyone could respond and left in the northern direction.","“Is that kid thinking of something to do with the Hadal Fire Spirit?” Situ Wenxian chuckled ruefully, not minding Lu Yun’s attitude.","A trace of resignation also appeared on Lu Tianling’s face.","......","Immortals Forbidden traveled swiftly while Lu Yun followed the Hadal Bird’s traces, tracking it through the northern sky.","“Here!” He finally saw the bird in a mountain valley after a full day of travel. It’d retracted all of its Hadal Fire and shrank down significantly to a three meter wingspan. Resting quietly in a dip in the land, it appeared as a regular spirit beast.","“Hey little guy, remember me?” As Lu Yun slowly drifted down from the sky, the Hadal Bird lazily lifted its eyes. A trace of joy percolated through them when it recognized the human.","It’d truly coalesced its body with Lu Yun’s help and smashed the gourd’s restraints. It was a true spirit beast and sentient long ago, but had been trapped by the Immortal Suppression Gourd soon after its birth. Thus, its mind was on par with that of a four year old child.","Lu Yun grasped from the southern sky and gathered a ball of pure connate fire origin in his hand. The Hadal Bird brightened, staring fixedly at the bright red ball. It’d eaten Aureate Bird Truefire mixed with connate fire origin to finish its evolution. What Lu Yun held now was more than ten times stronger than before.","Lu Yun grinned at the bird and flipped the fire origin to it.","Stirring with interest, the bird arched its neck and swallowed the ball, then raised its developing claws and shuffled over to Lu Yun so it could nuzzle the human. In its current state, the Hadal Bird was as if a child. It grew close to whoever treated it well.","For a wily old fox like Lu Yun, it was a simple task to tame a fire spirit like this one. He didn’t care about the Dark Orchid delegation, the Hadal Bird was the only matter of importance. It would be extremely useful in battle as it was a weapon of war as soon as he taught it any fire combat art.","Ah... weapon of war?","His suppressed memories were bounding out of their seal again. But could something like that be brought into the world?","The bird imprinted onto Lu Yun after a few more balls of connate origin. It turned into a sparrow the size of a palm and perched on his shoulder. Smiling, the young man returned to Dark City.","......","“Qin Yu, isn’t that human’s aura very similar to the one that the lord told us to look out for?” Two figures stared intently at a crimson sword light streaking through the sky.","“That’s right, it’s him, the young man with the dragon egg!” Excitement dawned on Qin Yu’s face.","“Get him and make him hand over the egg! The lord will reward us if we bring it to him!” The other speaker, a young man with green hair, stood up eagerly from their watchpost in a mountain.","“Don’t be brash!” Qin Yu shook his head. “We can’t let word of the dragon egg get out. So many immortals have come to Jade Ruins Realm that not even the lord can hold all of them off. Let’s follow him for now and see where he’s going. Once we have the full picture, we’ll go back and tell the lord!”","Green Hair recognized the good sense he made. “Let’s go!”","......","The two trailed more than one hundred kilometers behind Lu Yun and their cultivation was far stronger than his. Thus, he didn’t notice that he had gained a tail. But he wouldn’t mind it even if he did—it was just two soul separation cultivators. With the Hadal Bird in hand, even their master would only be coming to his death.","“That’s the capital of Darklake Empire!” Eagerness flashed through Qin Yu and Chang Si’s eyes as they looked at a metropolis in the distance. “So he’s a junior of a third rank cultivation empire!”","“Haha, once the matter is concluded, we monster spirits of the Barren Mountains will come and trample this nation flat!” Chang Si chortled.","“The monster spirits of the Barren Mountains wish to march on Darklake?” A voice suddenly sounded in their ears. Qin Yu and Chang Si jumped with surprise and sprang aside.","“Who goes there?!” They whirled around to see an elder in long black robes and white hair. He’d soundlessly appeared behind them at some point in time.","“So it’s you.” Qin Yu frowned. “Greetings to Empyrean Immortal Jadecliff.”","Qin Yu and Chang Si bowed to the newcomer, but there was no hint of respect in their expression. Empyrean Immortal Jadecliff was Yuwen Zhuifeng’s master that Lu Yun had scared off in Dark City. He was known throughout the realm as being highly afraid of death. He never took up arms and had bowed and scraped in front of Ancestor Bichen of the Barren Mountains out of that concern.","“There is no need to stand on ceremony, gentlemen,” Jadecliff smiled charmingly.","“There are many immortals in the realm these days and they have all converged on Immortal Burial Valley for a share of the spoils. What might Empyrean Immortal Jadecliff be doing here?” Qin Yu asked probingly. They were most concerned about the dragon egg. Although it was with a gray jiao, they would be able to force the young man to retrieve it if they captured him and his family.","“Did this immortal hear correctly that the monster spirits of the Barren Mountains wish to march on Darklake?” Jadecliff didn’t mind Qin Yu’s attitude.","The two looked at each other, frowning in unison.","“Hahaha, don’t worry. This old man and a few others have some things to say about Darklake Empire as well. We happen to be looking for allies to exterminate it.”"]},{"number":2312,"title":"Chapter 2312: Chapter 2205.1: The Beginning of Despair","paragraphs":["Chapter 2205.1: The Beginning of Despair","“What?!” Qin Yu and Chang Si greeted Jadecliff’s words with incredulity.","Regardless of all else, Jadecliff was an empyrean immortal. No matter how cowardly he might be, he shouldn’t be wary of a third rank cultivation empire. The man’s caution, however, was no act.","“While Darklake appears to be an ordinary third rank empire, crouching tigers and hidden dragons abound within it. A true immortal died here a month ago.” Jadecliff felt quite lucky as he voiced these words. Thankfully, he hadn’t stubbornly set himself against Lu Yun that day. He would be the one dead in that case.","“A true immortal died?” Qin Yu and Chang Si’s eyes widened. “Was it the gray scaled-dragon?”","“What scaled-dragon?” Jadecliff furrowed his brow.","“We cannot make the decision in this. Please return to the mountains with us, Empyrean Immortal Jadecliff, and meet our lord.” Qin Yu abruptly turned respectful.","......","“That was close! If it wasn’t for the Teleportation Talisman I carry around, we would’ve died to the fire spirit.”","Although Ashflame’s spirit vein had been taken, Dark Orchid was still able to restore the city to full operations, albeit lacking its former prosperity. Within the city lord’s residence, the handsome young man from the empire’s delegation breathed out shakily.","“Your Highness, the fire spirit was plainly imprisoned. Why did it break free of the Immortal Suppression Gourd?” asked a puzzled middle-aged man.","“The fire spirit... likely swallowed the gourd’s core essence at some point and evolved without any of us knowing. The Aureate Bird Truefire was the last straw it needed. But Lu Yun was craftier than we thought and looks to have mixed in some Brahman Fire to help the fire spirit.” The young man sighed, “This is my oversight, one that fell on poor Sui Ge...”","The handsome young man was the greatest personage of Dark Orchid Empire—Prince Sui, Sui Wuye. He appeared to be a latter soul projection cultivator, a fact that no one believed. It was due to his presence that Dark Orchid was the only fourth rank empire in the world without a superior nation.","Many were the fifth rank nations that’d tried to bring Dark Orchid to heel, but they’d all failed. Stories circulated among the lower ranked nations of Jade Ruins Realm that Sui Wuye was the disciple of an immortal. Thus, fifth rank nations didn’t dare easily march on Dark Orchid.","Any who entered the Celestial Realm Battlefront also knew that Sui Wuye was ranked number three on the battlefront’s ranking. He was the third strongest in the entire realm.","“What do we do next? Is it over, just like this?” the middle-aged man asked unwillingly. He was Sui Wuye’s general and had watched Sui Ge grow up. The little prince’s death also caused him extreme heartbreak.","“Lu Tianling of Darklake Empire is not one to provoke,” Sui Wuye shook his head. “I’ve wanted to give it up a long time ago, but went along with everyone because I didn’t want to expose the empire and the sect’s people operating in it.”","The middle-aged man fell silent.","“Don’t worry, Sui Ge isn’t dead,” Sui Wuye sighed. “He just needs to start over. Sui Ge’s growth has been smooth and unobstructed his whole life. This will be a good trial for him.”","“Understood,” the middle-aged man heaved a long sigh. His lord wouldn’t be so composed if Sui Ge really was dead.","“We can’t let a mere Lu Tianling ruin our plans,” Sui Wuye mused. “If the Origin Sect wishes to move against Lu Tianling, let them do it themselves. Dark Orchid will no longer take part in this matter.”","“But the emperor...” the middle-aged man hesitated.","“That dog emperor has long become the Origin Sect’s puppet. We can use Lu Tianling’s hand to get rid of him.” Sui Wuye waved him off. “Jade Ruins Realm is the weakest of Great Xia’s three thousand worlds of cultivation because it lacks a ruler. Go make your preparations, Lan Shi. It is about time that this world had a master.”","......","After returning to Dark City, the black sparrow on Lu Yun’s shoulder drew a few surprised looks. Only Terra Demon and the gray jiao identified its origins. No one else, not even Lu Tianling, connected the palm-sized bird to the ferocious Hadal Fire Spirit.","“Young master, the Hadal Bird’s cultivation touches on the barrier of the gods. Its battle strength can more than rival peerless immortals. Some weaker aether dao immortals are no match for it either,” Terra Demon gave his assessment after studying the bird on Lu Yun’s shoulder.","“It is a pity that its spirit is too weak for prolonged battle,” Lu Yun sighed softly.","As strong as the Hadal Bird was, its unusually fragile spirit would be scattered to the four winds if it suffered an immense blow. It would return to being a bloom of Hadal Fire without sentience.","Hadal Fire with a fire spirit was an entirely different existence to one without. Additionally, the Hadal Bird’s spirit was so weak that it was nearly full after devouring one ball of fire origin. It needed some time to refine and absorb the elemental energy.","Regardless, the troubles to come were a walk in the park. As weak as the Hadal Bird was, that was only a concern if they faced powerful immortals.","“But with this little guy, the pressure on my shoulders is slightly relieved.” A rare smile appeared on Terra Demon’s stiff face.","Hadal Fire was far stronger than Aureate Bird Truefire and even superior to the level of connate li fire that Lu Yun could summon at his current strength. Terra Demon’s speed of cultivation would increase with the aid of Hadal Fire.","“Heh heh heh heh heh...” Lu Yun smirked at Terra Demon. “The Hadal Bird can’t help you with refining pills.”","“Um...” Terra Demon’s expression froze.","“Don’t bother with refining pills for a while.” Lu Yun ignored the man’s change in expression and took out a thumbnail-sized tea leaf from his storage ring. “Refine this tea leaf and thoroughly cleanse your body. Wipe away all traces having to do with Yong Heyu.”","“This is...” Terra Demon’s eyes widened as he took the tea leaf that showed signs of having been steeped before.","“Dao Comprehension Tea.” Lu Yun nodded.","Dao Comprehension Tea exceeded the limits of heavenly and earthly treasures. It was one of the legendary treasures of the world of immortals, one of the connate spirit roots. Harboring dense qi, its uses were incredibly varied. One of them was to cleanse the body and bring it closer to dao.","When Lu Yun broke the Severed Meridians Hold over Lu Xiaochi, he’d done so through Dao Comprehension Tea water, then refined his uncle as a pill. Not only did it cleanse the restriction from Lu Xiaochi, but also modified his ordinary spirit root into one of the connate five elements.","Lu Yun was able to manage the feat solely due to the spirit root’s effects.","Terra Demon’s body was that of an ordinary cultivator. It couldn’t sustain his ponderous immortal king nascent soul. Thus, the Dao Comprehension Tea was needed to thoroughly change it. This had been part of Lu Yun’s plans from the beginning, but he hadn’t been entirely confident at that time. Now with the Hadal Fire, his confidence grew that much stronger.","The Shennong Grass of the ten heavenly materials possessed enormous vitality. It was the key ingredient in the Shennong Life Restoring Pill—a panacea that could cure any sort of physical hurt or damage to the nascent soul.","Terra Demon’s nascent soul was injured and his physical body weak. Thus, the Shennong Life Restoring Pill was the perfect medicine for his needs.","During his three thousand lifetimes, Lu Yun successfully created the medicinal properties of the Shennong Grass with the strength of a cultivator. He then used the attributes to create the Shennong Life Restoring Pill.","However, he’d failed and only created an ordinary immortal pill. He almost died in the ensuing pill tribulation and all sorts of unsavory characters came for him after he refined the pill. He was chased throughout the world by a host of cultivators and wandering immortals. After experiencing his three thousand lifetimes, he didn’t dare make the same attempt despite possessing the relevant methods to.","......","Refining a piece of Dao Comprehension Tea the size of a thumbnail was the most that the current Terra Demon could manage. After absorbing the power within the tea leaf, it would thoroughly cleanse his body and fill it with sufficient strength to contain the nascent soul of an immortal king.","Lu Yun sat quietly on the ground within the seed storage formation in the Lu secret vault. Thirty-two lower rank spirit crystals floated in front of him—found in Sui Ge’s storage ring after his death. The ring remained in perfect condition thanks to protection from a paramount dao rank treasure.","The palm-sized Hadal Bird retracted all of its flames and sprawled quietly on the young man’s shoulder. Its pale golden eyes looked curiously at the thousands of low level spirit herbs in front of it."]},{"number":2313,"title":"Chapter 2313: Chapter 2205.2: The Beginning of Despair","paragraphs":["Chapter 2205.2: The Beginning of Despair","“Begin!” Lu Yun slowly inhaled and exhaled, one by one raising thousands of spirit herbs into the air.","Whoosh!","A bright red flame soared out of his hand—connate li fire. It was all that was needed for the process of recreating medicinal attributes. Hadal Fire came into play only during pill refinement.","The little sparrow’s eyes bulged. It flapped into the air, circling around the flame and chirping madly at it.","“Don’t worry, I’ll give you connate li fire to eat when your cultivation realm reaches golden immortal. You can’t eat this flame at your current strength,” Lu Yun smiled faintly.","The tiny Hadal Bird seemed to understand and circled around his head for a while before landing on the gray jiao’s head and plopping down. Napping while incubating the egg, the jiao lifted one eyelid, sneezed, and closed it.","Ranked number nine out of the ten heavenly ingredients, Shennong Grass was much more complicated than the Dragon Transformation Grass. Thousands of spirit herbs were needed to form its fundamental basis before a hint of Shennong Grass could come into existence.","Whoosh whoosh whoosh!","Connate li fire jumped in Lu Yun’s hand, thoroughly consuming and distilling the pile of ingredients into pure liquid. Attributes that weren’t of use and various impurities were expunged. Golden light flashed through his eyes as his mind raced through calculations, analyzing the structure of these ingredients.","A powerful presence began building in front of him.","“No, this isn’t right.” Lu Yun suddenly threw away the combination in front of him that was sixty percent complete. They’d deviated only slightly from the proper outcome, but it was sufficient to render them fully unusable. All the same, he didn’t find it a pity.","Lu Yun had started his preparations a year ago in order to create the attributes of the Shennong Grass. He’d returned with rich findings after his trip to Fallen Leaf Mountain three months ago—the dozen storage rings of spirit herbs were fully sufficient to achieve what he sought.","Damn it. He suddenly quite wished for the formula dao of his subconscious. If formula dao existed, he would succeed with one go!","But there was no formula dao here and he didn’t dare bring it into the world. He had to slowly experiment by himself.","Humm!","After ten failures, a dark green droplet completely lacking an aura appeared in front of Lu Yun.","“The first step is finally complete.” He waved the droplet into a jade flask, then erupted with connate li fire again and tossed more spirit herbs into the flame.","......","Ten days passed.","During these ten days, Jade Ruins Realm was completely lifeless. Even the energy of heaven and earth turned dull and inert.","RUMBLE!!","A pillar of black and red light soared to the heavens in the southern sky, dying the firmament dark red.","“It is indeed that kind of ripple...” Terra Demon had fully refined the tea leaf, his body was wholly his. Everything having to do with Yong Heyu was no longer. His nascent soul swiftly modified it into something approaching an immortal body.","However, he knew that this condition couldn’t be sustained for long. His nascent soul was damaged and less than one ten thousandth of his prime. There was also a fatal flaw to a body modified by a nascent soul. If it wasn’t addressed in time, his body would collapse.","“What is that?” Standing next to Terra Demon, Kong Mengqian stared agog at the southern sky. Even though they were five hundred thousand kilometers away from the pillar of light that’d suddenly shot out of the land, she could still sense how terrifying it was.","“His Grace says...” murmured Terra Demon in a voice that only he could hear. “It is despair.”","The power of the heavenly book that’d enveloped Jade Ruins Realm was concentrated over that part of the sky.","“Relay my orders that everything that answers to Darklake Empire is to avoid Profound Wing Empire.” Lu Tianling stared at the horizon with shock.","Within the seed storage formation.","Lu Yun sighed with relief when he refined the last drop of medicinal liquid and stored it in a jade flask. Only then did he look to the south.","“So they want to suppress that thing with the power of the heavenly book... I wonder what rank that treasure is? Are you fearless or ignorant to antagonize that thing at this time?” Lu Yun frowned tightly, detonating all one hundred and eight flasks in front of him with a wave of his hand. The droplets inside them swiftly gathered together into a jade green pill.","“The medicinal properties of the Shennong Grass have been taken care of, now it’s time to focus on the supplementary ingredients.” Lu Yun summoned connate li fire without hesitation and commenced forming the properties of other ingredients, some of which were even immortal ingredients.","Subconsciously, he felt that that thing was not yet mature. After all, the root of destruction for this world was never that. It was when life marched on the heavens.","Even now, there was something that Lu Yun did not yet realize, that the world would forever lose three people at a certain moment in the future.","......","Jade Ruins Realm, Immortal Burial Valley.","A magnificent man in yellow robes stood in the void. He seemed to be in his forties and his brows were sharply angled upward, framing brightly glittering eyes. He bore himself with a majestic bearing simply by standing in the sky.","A white scroll rested in his hand, emanating a milky-white haze and firmly suppressing the blackish-red pillar shooting out from the ground.","Everyone had thought that the Human Emperor of Great Xia would send immortals to investigate the valley, but the emperor himself and the dynasty’s eight titled kings and thirty-six marquises had come!","The immortals gathered to watch the show scattered in abject terror. Thankfully, they hadn’t committed anything untoward during this time.","The group’s eyes were fixed on the pillar of light, full of wariness and caution.","“Aouuu!” An earth-shaking howl reverberated the pillar as a crimson beast claw probed out of it, slamming toward the white scroll.","“Heh, We might fear you if you were mature and able to break out of the light, but you are suppressed by the heavenly book and unable to roam freely,” chuckled the Human Emperor. When he waved the scroll that was a replica of the heavenly book, it exploded with brilliant splendor that enveloped the claw.","“Aouuu!” shrieked the beast as it quickly jerked its claw back.","“Commence!” shouted the Human Emperor. The eight titled kings and thirty-six marquises were ready. An image of the heavenly book appeared in each of their hands. Though it was made of light, the pictures emanated a powerful presence.","The eight titled kings stood in the eight directions while the thirty-six marquises were split into groups of six, a nod to the notion of the six directions. The emperor stood in the middle, flaring with an undeniable aura.","The eight barrens and six directions, I alone am supreme!","BOOM!","The heavenly book flew out of the emperor’s hand and expanded in the air until it overshadowed the entire valley. With that, it instantly suppressed the pillar of light running to the heavens.","Immortals near and far gaped with shock.","“Close!” roared the Human Emperor. Answering radiance rose from the eight titled kings and thirty-six marquises—in this moment, they seemed part of the heavenly book. The images in their hand left their control and flew to the massive projection of the treasure in the sky.","The auras of the titled kings and marquises fully became one with the Human Emperor.","“The heavens as the hilt and the earth as the scabbard. Come forth, Sword of Chaos!” the emperor’s voice reverberated through the land.","If Lu Yun was present to hear the name of Sword of Chaos, his suppressed memories would likely stir again. This part of immortal civilization contained the marks of legacy from the immortal dao. A new immortal dao of latter generations would also appear, even if it was the divine dao.","BOOM!","A massive sword hilt manifested in front of the emperor as soon as he finished.","The image of a copper sword hilt with a simple, ancient design towered at three thousand meters. It stabbed into the ground like it’d grown out of the void. The sword seemed to be one with this world.","The Human Emperor stood three meters tall, but he was as insignificant as an ant compared to the sword. He wrapped his hands around the hilt and firmly pulled it out, raising an echoing hum from the land.","HUMMMM.","The void shook as a copper blade more than fifteen thousand meters long rose from the ground. Although it was just an image, the aura it flared with shook Terra Demon’s heart five hundred thousand kilometers out.","“What is this Sword of Chaos?” He stared fixedly at the sword in the emperor’s hand, having never seen or heard of it in the world of immortals. “It looks like I’ve underestimated this world... Its mysteries are more than the world of immortals of yore...”","The image’s aura rivaled that of an immortal overlord, and this was just a projection!","The Human Emperor held the sword aloft and waved it through the air. “Slash!”","“Slash!” roared the eight titled kings.","“Slash!” shouted the thirty-six marquises.","Unparalleled aura exploded out of them as the entire group became one through the heavenly book.","BOOM!!"]},{"number":2314,"title":"Chapter 2314: Chapter 2206.1: Shennong Life Restoring Pill","paragraphs":["Chapter 2206.1: Shennong Life Restoring Pill","The Sword of Chaos struck right at the center of the blackish-red pillar of light. An agonized scream rang out from it as countless scarlet beast or humanoid forms drifted apart as dust.","A dragon of black and red and five thousand kilometers long reared back with a proud croon, charging out the moment the light vanished. It came with a stomach-turning presence that induced waves of nausea in all living beings within five thousand kilometers. Even empyrean, true, august, and divine immortals staggered backward and retched.","The Human Emperor waved the Sword of Chaos again without a shift in expression and slammed it down on the dragon.","BAM!","A heaven-shaking collision rang out, vaporizing any immortals caught in the sound wave. The Human Emperor paled as a trickle of blood the width of his thumb dribbled out of his mouth. One of the eight titled kings behind him exploded. The king’s immortal soul was about to flee to safety when the sound wave crushed it to dust.","One of Great Xia’s titled kings had fallen!","Of the thirty-six marquises, six were shaken to dust and left nothing behind.","However, the emperor’s stroke managed to bisect the dragon. After writhing in the air for a while, it fell silent and gradually faded away.","......","The battle took a catastrophic toll. Everyone within five thousand kilometers, be they immortal, cultivator, or other living being, was shaken to dust. Someone as mighty as a Great Xia titled king had fallen, and six of the marquises had perished as well! The rest of the Great Xia delegation was covered with wounds.","The enormous Sword of Chaos in the Human Emperor’s hands began to disperse. In the sky, the tremendous projection of the heavenly book rained down beams of milky-white splendor. They defused the crimson strength lingering in the void, slowly returning the land to normal.","When the Human Emperor waved to it, the projection receded as well. The treasure’s replica and images returned to their places in their master’s hands. As for the ones that belonged to those who’d died, those images returned to the heavenly book in the center of the Celestial Realm Battlefront.","All was not over.","The milky-white power remained in the sky and coalesced into a massive cloud. Pillars of white radiance came into being and blasted the enormous pit, giving a cacophony of inhuman shrieks. There were plainly numerous scarlet creatures still inside the pit.","The cloud conducted its work for three straight days before fading away.","“The rules over Jade Ruins Realm will recover after half a year. Any foreign immortal is not to remain in this world,” the Human Emperor declared expressionlessly, his announcement instantly reaching every corner of the world. He and his delegation disappeared with a wave of his hand, leaving the realm in chaos.","......","“Is it over?” Lu Yun lifted his eyes to the horizon as he sat next to the Cauldron of Heaven and Earth and shook his head. “I didn’t expect that the heavenly book is able to contain those terrible things. No wonder the Human Emperor was willing to provoke them.","“But the power of heaven and earth is needed to counter them, no? So... is the heavenly book formed from the power of the world?” He grew lost in thought as black flames roiled in the dark green cauldron in front of him. Hadal Fire!","The Hadal Bird had long devoured the dragons made of Brahman Fire in the Cauldron of Heaven and Earth. Quite unexpectedly, the cauldron became its nest.","As it wasn’t a true living being, it wasn’t restricted from entering the cauldron. To a fire spirit, it could come and go at will from the treasure.","When Lu Yun first took the cauldron out, the Hadal Bird chirped happily and shot inside like a little black arrow. After that, the dragons of fire become its food.","Fires of heaven and earth could advance through swallowing each other. The Brahman Fire inside the cauldron was rootless fire from the formation’s summons. Seeing as there was no core essence of Brahman Fire within them, they just barely reached the edge of the fires of heaven and earth.","But with the Hadal Bird being a bonafide fire spirit, these rootless flames were a perfect meal. The runes from the Nineheavens Brahman Formation in the cauldron created the perfect conditions to nurture Hadal Fire.","When the Nineheavens Brahman Formation operated, it summoned boundless Brahman Fire from the void. Hadal Fire could continuously devour them to strengthen itself, albeit with limited effect since flames without foundation were too weak. Other than that, the rootless Brahman Fire had no effect on a Hadal Fire Spirit.","The Hadal Bird settled down in the Cauldron of Heaven and Earth and turned the scarlet premises of Brahman Fire into a world of black. Even the power of thunder and lightning that lived within the cauldron was suppressed by the black flames.","At the same time, the treasure’s power increased to a new height with the bird’s residence. Due to the fire spirit, the Hadal Fire within the cauldron didn’t reject Lu Yun. The young man could easily direct it as he wished.","He used the Cauldron of Heaven and Earth as a pill cauldron and sent in hand seals for pill refinement, coalescing the liquid within the treasure. The process swiftly consumed his Hongmeng qi.","“Refining immortal pills is certainly no easy task.” Sensing that his Hongmeng qi was moments away from depletion, one of the spirit crystals hovering in front of him shifted and turned into pure energy that streamed into his body.","One step away from emptying, his body quickly filled with energy again. If anyone learned that a lower rank spirit crystal just barely managed to replenish eight percent of Lu Yun’s Hongmeng qi, they’d likely faint from shock.","A lower rank spirit crystal was sufficient to support a soul separation cultivator for half a month—Lu Yun was just nascent soul! But it was also due to the unique properties of Lu Yun’s Hongmeng qi and its far superior quality that he was able to refine an immortal pill at his level. Otherwise, he would be unable to manage a regular immortal pill no matter his skill and knowledge in pill refinement, to say nothing of the ninth rank Shennong Life Restoring Pill.","It’d been one month since Lu Yun first sat down. Three jade-green pills were taking form in the Cauldron of Heaven and Earth, wafting a dense medicinal scent through the area.","Napping over the dragon egg, the gray jiao shook itself awake with a shudder and stared fixedly at the cauldron. Sprawled within the treasure, the Hadal Bird flicked a bored glance at the three immortal pills and looked back down.","......","A thick layer of multicolored clouds formed over the skies of Dark City. Thunder roared through the air and echoed in the vicinity.","“What is that?!” Even beings thousands of kilometers out from the capital noticed the enormous cloud formation and sensed the incredible power of rampaging lightning within.","“It’s... a pill tribulation! A tribulation that occurs only when an immortal pill appears in the world!” Nearby foreign immortals and powerful cultivators immediately recognized the origin of the cloud.","“Can it be that a senior is refining an immortal pill here?” some murmured to themselves as they looked to the horizon. No one dared make a move as the realm was in complete disorder these days. Countless seniors and heavyweights had emerged in the world, so whoever dared refine an immortal pill at this time was no mundane personage.","“An immortal pill! Senior, do you mean that someone is refining an immortal pill in Darklake Empire?” Within the royal capital of Dark Orchid Empire, someone dressed in dragon robes looked ardently at a man in white robes. Naked greed filtered through his eyes—Wang Tianba, the emperor of Dark Orchid.","A domineering and imperious ruler, Wang Tianba’s bearing paled in comparison to the white-robed man in front of him. White Robes was an immortal.","More than ninety percent of the immortals that’d entered Jade Ruins Realm was gathered at Immortal Burial Valley. Very few moved around elsewhere. The valley was fully opened after the Human Emperor of Great Xia left, leaving space for countless ancient treasures, pills, ingredients, and more to manifest in the enormous pit.","It took the world by storm, but also began to live up to its name as most of the immortals and cultivators who ventured in did not return alive.","However, when an awakened cultivator returned with an immortal weapon from the ancient times, immortals on the brink of giving up surged in like a pack of hungry wolves.","The Origin Sect sent in only a few members because they knew that a treasure on par with a high level immortal weapon could be found in Dark City.","......","“Judging from the strength of the tribulation, there is more than one immortal pill that is about to appear.” White Robes licked his lips as he looked to the southern sky. “Capture Lu Tianling. If you manage this task well, then rest assured that you will have your fair share of the immortal pills and weapons.”","“Milord! This emperor will accomplish the task!” Excitement appeared in Wang Tianba’s eyes."]},{"number":2315,"title":"Chapter 2315: Chapter 2206.2: Shennong Life Restoring Pill","paragraphs":["Chapter 2206.2: Shennong Life Restoring Pill","White Robes—an immortal from the Origin Sect—imperceptibly curled his lip. Contempt lingered in the corner of his eyes.","“But milord, someone who can refine an immortal pill should be an immortal themselves. Immortals are in Darklake Empire...” Wang Tianba fretted after his initial rush of excitement.","“Don’t worry, my Origin Sect will take care of the immortal. They’re at most an august immortal,” White Robes smiled.","Lu Youya had been sent to Darklake merely to probe Lu Tianling’s capabilities. It’d turned out to be a difficult undertaking to fend off a true immortal, so Lu Tianling’s trump cards couldn’t be anywhere near impressive. As for refining an immortal pill... sometimes low level immortals could also create high level pills.","“That is most wonderful!” Wang Tianba gushed. “Although Darklake Empire gained its independence thanks to that trash Sui Ge, we still have a secret pawn in place there!\"","......","Countless residents of Dark City raised their heads and gawked at the tribulation clouds covering the city.","“Is, is a senior undergoing their tribulation in the city?” Some nascent soul cultivators from well-known families swallowed hard. Experiencing a tribulation was the stuff of legends to cultivators of third rank empires! They weren’t superstitious as to believe that this was heavenly punishment for a wrong that Darklake had committed. The arrival of heavenly thunder was most likely attributed to a heavenly tribulation.","“Master, this is your precious grandson again, isn’t it?” Situ Wenxian smiled ruefully at the equally shocked Lu Tianling.","A cultivator undergoing a tribulation? Lu Tianling himself hadn't met with such terrifying tribulation clouds when it was his turn to be tested!","BOOM!","Tribulation clouds roiled in the sky and lightning as thick as a person’s wrist descended from above. It crashed into the city with overwhelming momentum. No one doubted that if it were to fully connect with its target, more than thirty percent of the capital would be destroyed!","Cultivators clutched their heads and scattered in all directions, immensely fearful of incoming disaster.","Humm!","A multicolored curtain of light appeared over the skies of Dark City, stopping the lightning in its tracks. Energy rippled through the curtain after halting the first bolt.","“A defensive formation?” Outside Dark City, immortals and cultivators alerted by the pill tribulation stared open-mouthed at the shifting radiance over the capital. No one anticipated that a mere third rank cultivation empire would have a formation safeguarding its capital! The curtain of light seemed to be a solid whole, indicating that it was one singular formation as opposed to a joint array.","“It’s not a formation, but a boundary!” Immortals whose knowledge ran a greater breadth swallowed hard. Boundaries differed from formations in that boundaries needed reinforcement from heaven and earth. A harmonious relationship between all things enabled it to bring more strength than formations to bear.","Formations needed to be overseen in order to manifest its greatest power, but boundaries didn’t. Once they were successfully set up, they could automatically defend against attacks!","But a complex procedure was required to lay down a boundary and a vast sum of qi was needed to support it. Neither ordinary energy of the world nor immortal qi was sufficient—multiple formidable immortal treasures were needed to be its foundation.","On the other hand, a variety of permutations were available to formations. Boundaries, however, were limited to simply offense and defense.","In this era, not even the cities of Great Xia would waste resources to set up boundaries. They would instead utilize several formations to set up a joint array for their cities. When it came to boundaries... there weren’t many in the dynasty who could craft one.","Yet in Jade Ruins Realm, a mere third rank cultivation empire possessed a boundary? Could it be that this realm that ranked last among the three thousand worlds of cultivation deserved far more of a reputation than what it had?","The heavenly tribulation cared not about what other immortals or cultivators thought. Bolts of heavenly tribulation rained down from the skies, ceasing only after thirty-six harrowing pillars of lightning struck the curtain of light.","......","“Three Shennong Life Restoring Pills, each with twelve instances of a pill tribulation...” Lu Yun waved three jade-green pills into his hand. A strong fragrance filled the seed storage formation.","He wiped off sweat on his forehead with a slightly shaking hand—he was very weak at the moment. Not only was his Hongmeng qi near depletion, but so was his heart and mind severely exhausted. Waves of dizziness assaulted his brain.","The young man glanced at the ardent gray jiao off to the side and smiled. A jade-green Shennong Life Restoring Pill landed in its mouth with a flick of his fingers.","Crooning with elegance, it sank into the pond.","“Thank goodness I made sufficient preparations before this. The pills would’ve been destroyed by the tribulation otherwise,” Lu Yun heaved an inward sigh of relief. As for whether or not the disturbance would catch the eyes of others... that was struck from his list of considerations long ago.","Refining an immortal pill would draw attention no matter where he was, so he might as well do it openly. He’d prepared enough surprises for them, anyhow. The boundary protecting Dark City was made from the countless treasures that he’d collected from Immortal Burial Valley.","While those treasures hadn’t been of high level, their core essence was genuine immortal treasure from ancient times. It was just that their core essences were incomplete and had become unusually weak. Ten thousand tattered treasures had formed one complete ninth rank immortal treasure. With Terra Demon’s help, that treasure became the foundation for the boundary around Dark City.","The treasures that were stripped of their core essence rested quietly in the Lu family vaults.","When Dark City underwent a thorough cleansing, Lu Yun utilized an enormous array of formations as the medium to bring the boundary into existence.","When the young man got to his feet, he wavered before managing to stop the waves of disorientation. He slowly padded out of the seed storage formation.","“Swallow this pill and refine it as quickly as possible to recover your strength.” Lu Yun handed one of the pills to Terra Demon after summoning the man and returned to his house. He was asleep before his head hit the bed.","Refining an immortal pill took too much of a toll. The resource depletion was so great that even he couldn’t endure it in his current state.","Terra Demon sucked in a sharp breath after receiving the Shennong Life Restoring Pill. A greater bloom of faith rose from his body and surged into the Seal of the Multitude. He had utmost faith in Lu Yun to begin with, and that faith deepened when he saw his lord refine an immortal pill with the body of a cultivator and mortal rank ingredients.","He practically worshiped the ground that the young man walked on.","The High Lord of the Northern Sky was capable of everything! Even if he’d lost his cultivation and was just a nascent soul cultivator, he could still accomplish what other immortal emperors could not do!","......","Lu Yun slept for ten days straight, waking slowly on the eleventh day. Dizziness still swept through his mind.","“Damn it, I should refrain from refining such high level immortal pills before I ascend to immortality.” He shook his head to clear it.","Time was exceedingly precious to a cultivator. Each minute spent in cultivation meant that one was that much stronger. The path of cultivation was one against the current. A lack of progress meant being set back, so no cultivator would dare let up on oneself.","Even the two great prodigals of Dark City put aside their lackadaisical attitudes after Lu Yun gave them certain items and bent their mind to training. That was why they were able to form golden cores within a year.","Lu Yun didn’t have this area of concern since the Nine Chapters of Dao operated even when he was asleep, constantly raising his cultivation level. Sensing the rich stores of Hongmeng qi within his body, the young man heaved a long sigh of relief. He calmed his mind and sat down cross-legged, directing the energy’s circulation with his entire being.","Hummm!","The barrier in front of peak nascent soul was pierced through like a finger through paper.","Whoosh!","Hongmeng qi circulated at a much faster rate and thundered into his dantian like coursing rivers. The nascent soul sitting over the dao character suddenly opened its eyes and shot forth two rays of hazy gray light.","Soul projection! The nascent soul could leave the body and journey the lands!","Humm!","Lu Yun shook as a powerful will descended from the skies and entered his mind. A heavenly dao combat art—Teleportation!","He could shift to any place within three hundred meters, but it consumed Hongmeng qi to do so. It wasn’t as ludicrous as the Petrification art.","“Teleportation? This is interesting. Compared to the Boundless Step... Eh? What’s the Boundless Step?” Lu Yun blinked and forcefully chased the thought out of his mind. So he’d known a similar combat art before!","Teleportation was absolutely a heaven-defying combat art, an unparalleled method to get away from danger!","......","Lu Yun nodded with satisfaction after carefully sensing his body’s condition.","“Soul projection huh... I can commence some of my cultivation plans. As strong as Terra Demon and some of the others are, my own strength is the most important.” He stood up into a hearty stretch. The breakthrough swept the cobwebs out of his mind and he was in prime condition.","BOOM!","A gigantic explosion ripped through the air and the massive boundary enveloping Dark City shook violently.","“Has it come?” Lu Yun bounded into the air and rose on the back of his sword.","“You’ve awakened, Yun’er!” Dressed in a set of scarlet armor, Lu Tianling presented a dashing sight on the northern city walls. He was delighted to see his grandson appear."]},{"number":2316,"title":"Chapter 2316: Chapter 2207.1: Evidence of Possession","paragraphs":["Chapter 2207.1: Evidence of Possession","A massive army bore down on Dark City outside the city walls. One million cultivators of golden core and above assembled into a massive battle formation that completely cut off the capital. A man emanating a terrifying aura stood in the air over the army.","“A soul separation cultivator?” Lu Yun looked solemnly at several others hovering in the sky.","“Not only that, but there are also several immortals hidden within the army,” Lu Tianling breathed out heavily. “It’s thanks to your boundary that Dark City hasn’t fallen already.”","The gray jiao and Terra Demon were in seclusion to refine the Shennong Life Restoring Pill; they were yet to emerge. It was a pill greater than ninth rank immortal pills. As such, it wasn’t something that the two could easily digest at their current stage.","But once they succeeded, their strength would improve on a quantitative level and they would no longer fear high level immortals from the Origin Sect.","“Situ Wenxian and Lu Tianling, the Ouyang family’s Ouyang Shengxiang is betrothed to this crown prince. Do you think nothing of Dark Orchid Empire to stand in our way at every possible turn?” Dressed in white robes, Crown Prince Wang Song stood on a flying treasure and hovered over the army. His bearing was extraordinary and his aura indicated initial soul projection.","“If the crown prince is here to welcome his bride, why the army?” Lu Tianling barked with laughter before the emperor could respond.","“Hahahaha!!” Wang Song sneered back. “Lu Tianling, you covet Ouyang Shengxiang’s connate fragrance constitution and want to snatch her for your trash grandson. Do you think this matter has gone undetected?”","“Oh?” Lu Tianling smirked at the crown prince.","“This old man can bear witness!” An elder darted out of the Dark Orchid army. It was the one that Lu Yun had met at the Ouyang Clan—Ouyang Biegui. He’d left the capital after Lu Youya’s death and escaped the purge of Dark City. To think that he’d reappear at this time!","“Lu Tianling, you savage! How would the family not know about your attempt to claim the Ouyang’s connate fragrance constitution?” Ouyang Biegui bit off his words as he glared heatedly at Lu Tianling on the city walls. Hate filled his tone and he seemed ready to rip the other to pieces through the sheer force of his stare.","“Grandpa... you saved this guy’s life before, didn’t you?” Lu Yun turned merrily to his grandfather. He didn’t bother to hush his voice and nearly everyone heard him since those present were of a high cultivation.","“Junior, I am speaking to your family elder! What right do you have to interrupt!” A cruel glint shone in Ouyang Biegui’s eyes when he heard Lu Yun.","“By the right that this young master can beat you so badly that you won’t be able to tell which direction the sun is shining from!” Lu Yun answered promptly.","“You!” Ouyang Biegui’s chest heaved as he forced down his anger.","“What about me?” Lu Yun curled his lip. “A dog will wag its tail at its savior, but an old dog like you bites your benefactor!”","“Do you not dare admit to what you’ve done, Lu Tianling, and send a brat to stir up the waters?!” Ouyang Biegui ignored Lu Yun and bawled at the Lu patriarch.","“Heh heh heh...” Lu Tianling chuckled, contempt in his eyes. Ouyang Biegui suddenly felt that he’d punched a ball of cotton.","“Hand over Ouyang Shengxiang, Lu Tianling, and we’ll stand down,” Wang Song said expressionlessly.","“Ouyang Shengxian? She’s an Ouyang, so do whatever you’d like, Your Highness.” Lu Tianling shrugged carelessly.","“Lu Tianling!” A tragic voice rang out from Dark City. “Hand over my sister!!”","Whoosh!","A figure appeared on the ramparts. “You old dog, you took my sister and imprisoned my family! You’re completely crazy!”","It was Ouyang Shengtian. Golden light sparkled around him as he pointed a massive golden spear at Lu Tianling. The young man’s aura raged to the sky and his energy ripples showed that he was a soul separation cultivator.","“You seek death!” Lu Yun exploded at hearing someone insult his grandfather. He was never lucky enough to have familial ties in his reincarnations, so he quite valued the ones he had in this life. It also meant that he very much held double standards.","He could call someone an old dog, but that could never be used on his grandfather!","A red flame rose around him as he pounced on the Ouyang genius.","“Do you really think I can’t beat you, Lu Yun?!” Ruthlessness blossomed in Ouyang Shengtian’s eyes. He’d stayed put all this time due to fear of Terra Demon. But with the million strong army outside the city walls and numerous immortals mixed in among them, Dark City wouldn’t be able to withstand the enemy even with a powerful boundary.","Not to mention, Terra Demon had vanished for the past couple of days. According to the Lu servants, he was in closed door cultivation to recover from old wounds.","Hence, there was nothing holding Ouyang Shengtian back anymore and he stepped forward into the light. All he needed to do was to capture this impudent brat and force Lu Tianling to act with caution. The fight would be half won then.","Humm!","Ouyang Shengtian brandished the golden spear and thrust it at Lu Yun’s chest with a burst of astounding aura.","“Master!” Situ Wenxian looked on nervously. The Ouyang genius had surreptitiously reached soul separation with neither him nor Lu Tianling realizing it! That made Ouyang Shengtian a latent Detonation Talisman within the capital. He was extremely dangerous once he went off!","“Don’t worry, he’s not worthy of being Yun’er’s opponent.” Lu Tianling waved off the Darklake emperor.","Heavyweights from the nation’s clans stood on the city walls. Of the seven great families originally in the capital, there were only the Yu, Zhao, and Lu Clans left. The Ouyangs were surrounded by the Hidden Dragons and there was nothing that their remaining nascent soul elders could do against imperial guards that were at least soul projection. At the same time, there was no sign of Ouyang Shenghe, Ouyang Shengmu, and Ouyang Shengxiang to be seen.","BAM!","Lu Yun and Ouyang Shengtian crashed into each other over the skies of Dark City. Their respective rays of gold and red brilliance threw off scintillating radiance so bright that cultivators below averted their eyes, unable to look directly at the light.","“This kid secretly broke through to soul projection after sleeping for ten days...” Lu Tianling smiled as he watched his grandson grapple with Ouyang Shengtian.","“He is indeed master’s grandson! This speed of cultivation would be unmatched even in Great Xia, wouldn’t it?” Situ Wenxian’s jaw dropped. Even an immortal pill was insufficient to help one advance from seventh level qi refinement to initial soul projection in less than a year and a half.","“Pace of cultivation is not important in Great Xia,” Lu Tianling shook his head. “There, they seek the ultimate peak and full comprehension of a cultivation realm. Some stunning geniuses can easily defeat ordinary soul projection cultivators when they themselves are golden core.”","He was suddenly reminded of Fengxian Wu, the granddaughter of the Fengxian King in Great Xia. She swept away a dozen nascent soul cultivators when she herself was at golden core. To the immortal dynasty, however, she merely possessed a noble background. She wasn’t a stunning genius.","“A golden core genius defeating soul projection cultivators?” Situ Wenxian tilted his head back at the sky. “This Ouyang Shengtian seems to be more than a soul separation cultivator... but the little guy can go toe-to-toe with him...”","Lu Tianling’s smile deepened. Toe-to-toe?","Lu Yun and Ouyang Shengtiang exchanged more than a dozen rounds of blows without a clear victor emerging. The crowd’s eyes went wide while they gaped at the fight. When could soul projection cultivators stand up to soul separation powerhouses??","It would be acceptable if it was a nascent soul paired with a soul projection cultivator, but soul separation was considered an earthly immortal. They could split out their nascent soul to coalesce images of heaven and earth.","Soul projection and soul separation was the first major moat dividing cultivators from each other.","“Not bad, Lu Yun. You’ve improved quite a great deal.” Ouyang Shengtian jerked to a pause and placed his golden spear behind him.","“Whereas you... could do with some improvement. Is this all you can manage after inheriting a wandering immortal’s power?” Lu Yun replied expressionlessly.","“So you never trusted me?” Ouyang Shengtian arched a brow and mentally drew up his guard.","“Someone else’s power is someone else’s power in the end. As strong as you appear, you are without foundations.” Lu Yun couldn’t be bothered to converse more. Immortal Forbidden flashed with crimson sword light that crashed down on the Ouyang genius.","“Hahahaha! My power? Someone else’s power? Whatever can defeat you is absolute power!” Ouyang Shengtian threw his head back with a long peal of laughter, wholly unafraid of Lu Yun’s attack. He brandished his spear into a ray of golden light and directed it at Lu Yun’s sword light. At the same time, he crossed his hands in front of his chest and condensed a spot of golden light in front of him that slowly expanded outward.","“An image of heaven and earth... one that makes use of a dao weapon!” Situ Wenxian identified solemnly. “The little guy is in trouble now.”"]},{"number":2317,"title":"Chapter 2317: Chapter 2207.2: Evidence of Possession","paragraphs":["Chapter 2207.2: Evidence of Possession","“Don’t worry,” Lu Tianling smiled faintly. “Yun’er seems to have gained a great personage for a master. The venerable one deployed the Dream Sutra to teach Yun’er in his dreams. Even I don’t know what he’s learned.”","“The Dream Sutra, disseminating dao through dreams?!” gasped Situ Wenxian, unconcealed shock in his eyes.","These things were no secret, Lu Tianling just hadn’t bothered to bring them up before. He did so now to prevent Situ Wenxian from reacting with surprise at every other development. The emperor talked too much.","BOOM!","A massive image of a forty-five meter long golden spear appeared in Ouyang Shengtian’s hands, shaking the ambient qi in the surroundings.","“Die, Lu Yun!” he roared and swung the spear around, stabbing down with unparalleled momentum. The actual spear entangling Lu Yun transformed into a streak of light at the same time and sank into the enormous image. Thus fortified, the gigantic spear’s might grew by thirty percent.","“You've only assimilated a lower rank dao weapon,” Lu Yun snorted and brandished Immortals Forbidden. A dense collection of sword light collected on his body, resulting in a crimson dragon sixty meters long forming over Dark City.","Hummm!","A powerful dragon croon echoed through the metropolis. Nine draconic shadows appeared in the air when it twisted its body, which then swiftly coalesced into real, tangible dragon forms.","The Eighteen Cerulean Sword Dragons and Nine Forms of the Cloud Dragon as deployed in conjunction!","Seven of the nine rushed toward the golden spear, whereas the remaining barrelled toward Ouyang Shengtian with sword qi beyond imagine.","“I knew you would use this move!” roared the Ouyang genius. He grasped in the void with both hands to manifest the image of a spear more than thirty meters long. It was much more tangible than the one earlier and thirty percent stronger.","It stabbed at Lu Yun’s two dragons as soon as it appeared, shooting with such domineering momentum that it was as if a pillar that stretched to the heavens.","Boom!!","Nine draconic shadows and two images of spears crashed into each other. The ensuing spirit ripples were so tremendous that they leveled countless structures within the city.","“No!” Ouyang Shengtian sensed a searing ripple of killing intent aim for the back of his head the moment his two spears went down with Lu Yun’s nine draconic shadows. He swung an arm behind him without second thought, manifesting another massive golden spear to block the cutting sword light.","“I’d thought all along that you practice an art of twin spears. To think that it’s one of three spears, and you’ve refined three lower dao rank weapons!” Lu Yun slowly shimmered into view behind the Ouyang genius.","Ouyang Shengtian’s back was drenched with sweat. Never did he imagine that his final trump card would save his life at a critical moment. He regarded Lu Yun with a frosty look; the three spears flashed through the air as his aura built.","The Lu young master snapped his fingers and collected drifting sword qi into one ray of crimson sword light. It landed in his hand as he faced off against his opponent.","“Lu Yun, this young master is not in the mood to fight you within the Dark City boundary today,” Ouyang Shengtian suddenly laughed and swept a look beneath him. Too many Hidden Dragons were gathering for his liking. A jade talisman appeared in his hand; he was gone after a flash.","“Situ Wenxian, Lu Tianling, my Ouyang Clan will reside in your Darklake Empire for temporary safekeeping. If anything happens to my family, I swear I will make rivers of blood run in Dark City!” Ouyang Shengtian’s voice rang through the capital.","“A Movement Talisman? Interesting.” Lu Yun didn’t prevent his opponent from leaving.","When Ouyang Shengtian reappeared, he was next to Ouyang Biegui.","“You’re back, good, good!” The elder was much relieved to see Ouyang Shengtian return. After Ouyang Batian and Ouyang Baiyi’s defeat, only Ouyang Shengtian, Ouyang Shenghe, Ouyang Shengmu, and Ouyang Shengxian were left of the clan’s direct bloodline. He didn’t care about the others.","“Lu Tianling, what do you have to say for yourself?” Envy flashed through Wang Song’s eyes as he looked at Lu Yun standing in the air. He gnashed his teeth and sneered up at Lu Tianling, “Darklake is a third rank empire, yet conceals soul projection cultivators. You do indeed harbor unsightly ambitions!”","“That’s certainly an overexaggerated accusation, Your Highness the Crown Prince,” Lu Yun interjected. “Darklake Empire was made independent from Dark Orchid a month ago. What does it have to do with you whether or not Darklake possesses soul projection cultivators?”","“Hmph!” Wang Song’s face darkened when he heard these words.","Rumble!!","Dark lightning split the sky as three figures in black appeared. Dressed in black battle armor, they wore upper dao rank blades on their backs and looked down impassively.","“Darklake Empire has seceded from Dark Orchid and Dark Orchid has no right to move against it for the next one hundred years. With what reason does it declare war this time?” majestically intoned the man in the middle. It was Terra Demon’s disciple—Helian Shan. He presented the image that he should, one of an impartial and just law enforcer.","Fourth rank empires did have the right to march on third rank empires and claim the subjugated as a vassal. But once a third rank empire won independence, its former superior nation could not take revenge within one hundred years.","Such was the ironclad law as established by the heavenly book.","“Milord enforcer!” Wang Song didn’t think much of the newcomers since he had a backer himself. As such, his tone wasn’t the most respectful. “Darklake disregards the dignity of Dark Orchid! They know that Ouyang Shengxiang is betrothed to me, but they still confine her and keep her hidden away. They show us not the slightest hint of respect!","“Does milord enforcer intend to stop me from seeking vengeance for my betrothed?”","“Well...” Helian Shan frowned tightly and sighed softly in Dark City’s direction.","“Hahahaha!!” Lu Yun roared with laughter. “Milord enforcer, please listen to both sides of the story!”","He waved three figures onto the city walls. Their cultivation levels weren’t high, but their identities made one quail. It was the missing Ouyang Shengmu, Ouyang Shenghe, and Ouyang Shengxiang!","“How is this possible?!” Waves of shock reared in Ouyang Shengtian’s heart. He’d quietly moved them out of the city three days ago, what were his siblings doing back here??","Ouyang Shengmu and Ouyang Shengxiang were standing dumbly on the city walls. Only Ouyang Shenghe pointed at Ouyang Shengtian and broke into loud curses.","“I don’t know where an old monster like you came from to take possession of my big brother’s body! You turned my family inside and out, and used Xiang’er as a pawn to start a war between two nations! You’re a fiend that’s completely mad!” Spittle flew from Ouyang Shenghe’s mouth as he swore at Ouyang Shengtian beneath the city walls.","“Shenghe, what’s wrong?” Ouyang Shengtian’s concern wasn’t a facade. The four siblings had grown up as a tight knit quartet and he cared very much about his brothers and sister. To hear his younger brother talk like this was unbearable, even though he’d consumed the qi of an wandering immortal and possessed the cultivation level of soul separation. “I am your big brother, I haven’t been possessed by anyone. I’m still Ouyang Shengtian!”","“Shengtian, someone’s controlling Shenghe. So Lu Tianling is still the strongest of us in the end...” Ouyang Biegui heaved a sigh. The other three siblings marked the total failure of the plan as soon as they appeared.","“You are Ouyang Shengtian?” Ouyang Shenghe sneered. He waved a jade talisman into his hand and crushed it, projecting a massive image into the sky. Two bedraggled young men sat facing each other. Their conversation also filtered out of the image.","......","“How much have you adjusted to your body?”","“About eighty percent, I’m almost there. Ouyang Shengtian’s foundations aren’t bad. I have a chance of becoming a real immortal after taking possession of him. I’ve also found some interesting things in his memories. The past Ouyang Shengtian didn’t know what they were, but the current one does.”","Everyone within the city heard the conversation."]},{"number":2318,"title":"Chapter 2318: Chapter 2208.1: Halberd","paragraphs":["Chapter 2208.1: Halberd","Jaws dropped all over the battlefield. No one imagined that Ouyang Shengtian really had been possessed, and by a wandering immortal! If word of this got out, then wandering immortals all over the worlds would go mad—not just the ones in Great Xia.","......","“So all of this was within his calculations from day one... Even Shenghe was a pawn that he purposefully left in the family...” Weakness overcame Ouyang Shengtian. “Lu Yun laid his plans from the moment he destroyed our trading headquarters. His scheme was in play then...”","Dark Orchid no longer had any excuses to declare war on Darklake. If they stubbornly persisted in their course of action, the three ninth rank empires would punish them accordingly. This was not a price that a fourth rank empire could pay.","“Lu Tianling is... deviously shrewd...” Everyone attributed the day’s outcome to Lu Tianling. No one believed that a young man of eighteen years old could set all this up from such a long time ago. They even thought that Lu Tianling had secretly approved the moniker of Dark City’s greatest pestilence for Lu Yun.","Their subject of admiration kept shaking his head with a rueful grin. All of his plans had to do with absolute strength. He really had overlooked a tiny pawn like the Ouyang Clan, yet it was this unimportant character that affected the entire situation and defused an incredible crisis.","“Hmph, whether or not Ouyang Shengtian is possessed by another, my fiancé is indeed in Darklake’s hands. What do you have to say for yourself, Situ Wenxian?!” Wang Song took a deep breath, he couldn’t back down now.","“Hahahaha!!” It was finally the right moment for Situ Wenxian to step forward. He flared the undeniable majesty of a sovereign ruler. “Wang Song, do you take Darklake for an easy target?! Dark Orchid’s armies have cut straight through Our nation since ten days ago, taking hundreds of cities in your progress. Did you mention Ouyang Shengxiang even once during this time? Did you present yourself as a wedding procession should?!”","He fixed his gaze on Wang Song like a hawk would on prey.","“The Ouyang Clan said...”","“Silence! The one in charge of that clan has been possessed by a vicious character whose ambitions know no bounds. His words cannot be regarded with any degree of veracity!”","Wang Song glowered. What they’d used as an excuse to threaten the Lu Clan had become a killing stroke against them. The image in the sky could not be faked as no one, not even the Human Emperor of Great Xia, possessed the ability to manufacture projections.","“Hahahaha!” Clear laughter rang out of the sky as sword radiance flashed by. A man in white robes and white hair appeared over the Dark Orchid army.","“Has Ouyang Shengtian been possessed by another just because you idiots say so?” He lifted his head proudly. “Dark Orchid’s might must be respected! If Darklake does not open the city gates to welcome our crown prince, then we will wipe a third rank cultivation empire from Jade Ruins Realm!”","“Sui Wuzhou!” A keen light glinted in Wang Song’s eyes when he saw the man.","“Is this the will of Dark Orchid Empire?” Killing intent surfaced on the faces of the three law enforcers in the sky.","“The law enforcers for the realm, is it?” Sui Wuzhou dismissed Helian Shan and his colleagues. “You three are hard pressed to save yourself at the moment. With a place like Immortal Burial Valley appearing in this world, do you think control over the realm still lies with you so-called law enforcers?","“I recommend you stay out of this or you’ll meet with bad ends.” The wind teased Sui Wuzhou’s white hair and his tone was in even higher spirits. He thought nothing of the three.","“As for your chief enforcer of the realm, he will likely step down after the next six months.”","Sui Wuzhou was Prince Sui’s older brother. He rarely ventured out and didn’t often interact with others. Thus, it was an enormous surprise that he was here today.","Prince Sui did not have good relations with the royal family. High-handed and so familiar with court it was as if he was a fish among water, even the Dark Orchid emperor cowered when he saw the prince.","It wasn’t until the Origin Sect came to Dark Orchid a dozen years ago and secretly bolstered the royal family that they had the ability to hold their own against Prince Sui. Sui Wuzhou was no longer someone they had to be fearful of by association.","Despite that, no one imagined that he would appear at this time to intimidate the law enforcers.","......","“He is indeed that person’s heir alright, just look at his bearing.” A man with ordinary features in an unremarkable corner of Dark Orchid’s million strong army looked at Sui Wuzhou with a slight smile.","“Sui Wuzhou, Sui Wuye, and Sui Wuchen are rare geniuses. Sadly, our Origin Sect is not willing to antagonize the person behind them,” sighed another person next to the ordinary looking man.","“The Sui brothers want Jade Ruins Realm, whereas we want only Lu Tianling. There is no conflict of interest between us and it is of no matter what happens to the Dark Orchid royal family.”","Dark Orchid royalty was just a pawn to the Origin Sect. Their survival or prosperity had nothing to do with the latter.","......","Morale soared in the Dark Orchid army with the appearance of Sui Wuzhou.","“Sui Wuzhou, do you and Dark Orchid wish to revolt?!” Helian Shan glowered and pressed down with the aura of an awakened cultivator.","“Heh, Helian Shan, do you honestly think that the law enforcers can do as you wish in the Jade Ruins Realm?” An aura that rivaled Helian Shan’s exploded from Sui Wuzhou’s body.","Latter awakened cultivation!","The personage who normally kept to himself was also an awakened cultivator! His aura was even stronger than Helian Shan’s!","Eyes wide, Helian Shan and the other two law enforcers took a half step back.","“I, Sui Wuzhou, will see for myself today what the mettle of Great Xia Dao Academy disciples looks like!”","Great Xia Dao Academy?","Lu Yun’s heart spasmed when he heard the name “Dao Academy”. But this time, his memories didn’t shift. Only an inexplicable sense of closeness and longing emanated from them. He didn’t want to go to the Dao Academy—he just missed someone too much.","Qing Yu.","The name silently disappeared the moment it formed, leaving sadness in the bottom of his eyes. He didn’t know what he needed to accomplish, only that he could not afford to fail. If he did, he would lose her forever.","......","Sui Wuzhou waved a black metal rod into his hand, swinging it around with the growing aura of a dao weapon.","“Hahaha, since Sui Wuzhou has made his move, then Nalan Tu naturally cannot fall behind!” Hearty laughter boomed the Dark Orchid army. Sword light flashed out as a man appeared in the sky wielding a longsword.","“Helian Shan, Zhan Taixuan, and Luo Yi—you have brought humiliation down on the Great Xia Dao Academy for being my senior brothers! How do Dao Academy disciples look to that empyrean immortal chief enforcer for support?”","Loose robes fluttering in the air, the man called Nalan Tu looked dismissively at the three enforcers.","“Heh, so another Dao Academy disciple is here on the scene. Nalan Tu? That is a very unfamiliar name.” Sui Wuzhou swept a careless glance over the newcomer.","“Nalan Tu is but a nameless nobody. It’s only to be expected that Brother Sui has never heard of me.” Nalan Tu grinned broadly, not minding Sui Wuzhou’s words in the slightest.","“Nalan Tu, you are the first among the younger generation in the Origin Sect. To think that you’ve joined the Dao Academy as well...” Helian Shan digested the unwelcome news.","A large batch of Dao Academy disciples were sent out every one hundred years to test themselves in worlds of cultivation and be their law enforcers. The ones that became this world’s enforcers were undoubtedly the lowest on the rankings in the academy. Worlds of cultivation were a small mud puddle compared to the vast Great Xia. No one was willing to come to this one in particular.","Helian Shan, Zhan Taixuan, and Luo Yi were those eliminated from the academy’s roster from the most recent batch. This was hardly an honorable accomplishment, so they never brought up that they were from the Great Xia Dao Academy.","“Senior brother Helian, this is a bit of a mess now,” Luo Yi chuckled ruefully. “They plainly don’t think much of us if they dare share everything about their background...”","“It’s alright.” Helian Shan comforted his junior brother and looked toward Dark City. Lu Yun’s expressionless face and aloof regard found him. “Our presence today marks the end of our involvement with this matter. None of these people will get away once the heavenly book recovers.”","“The heavenly book?” Sui Wuzhou snorted with laughter. “Since you three trash won’t be sticking your nose where it doesn’t belong, get out of the way.”","Whoosh!","An upper dao rank blade appeared in Helian Shan’s hand. He leveled the long black blade at the prince.","“Sui Wuzhou, although we have been eliminated from the Dao Academy, the law enforcers of the heavenly book are not people you can insult,” he snapped. “I, Helian Shan, challenge Sui Wuzhou in the name of the heavenly book!”","This turn caused Sui Wuzhou to jerk with startled solemnity.","“So you do have some courage about you.” He broke into loud laughter and brandished his spear. “I do not fight, I only kill.”","“Then kill.” Light exploded out of Helian Shan’s blade and a gigantic black lotus flower appeared in the sky, whirling toward his opponent.","“You seek death!” Sui Wuzhou roared and flourished his spear, throwing it at the lotus flower."]},{"number":2319,"title":"Chapter 2319: Chapter 2208.2: Halberd","paragraphs":["Chapter 2208.2: Halberd","“Senior brothers, since senior brother Helian is already sparring with Brother Sui, why don’t the three of us stretch our legs as well?” Nalan Tu smiled warmly. He sent his sword light to Luo Yi and Zhan Taixuan before they had a chance to respond.","......","“Kill!” Crown Prince Wang Song gave the order to charge as soon as he saw the combatants locked in combat in the air. Several million rays of sword light stitched into one massive pillar that rammed the boundary around Dark City.","BAM!","The ponderous boundary shook as frightening ripples undulated over it.","“We fight.” Lu Tianling and Situ Wenxian smiled at each other. “KILL!”","The capital’s city doors swung open to make way for an army that streamed out like an azure flood.","The Azure Dragons, one of Lu Tianling’s three trump cards!","One hundred and eight thousand Azure Dragons who were all at least latter nascent soul! Their core of two thousand elites were all soul separation powerhouses. Lu Tianling had quietly raised thousands of soul separation heavyweights in just two hundred years, and this was just one of his trump cards!","The azure flood transformed into an azure dragon as soon as it exited the city and soared into the sky. Dark Orchid’s one million strong army was nothing in its eyes.","“Lu Tianling!” Some Origin Sect powerhouses hidden within the Dark Orchid army jumped with shock when they saw the Azure Dragons.","“It looks like he’s gone to a great deal of effort over the years. He’ll be heartbroken if they’re wiped out, won’t he?” One of them licked his lips and shot into the sky. He flung a large mountain-like seal at the azure tide.","Bam!","A crimson halberd appeared in the air and stood between heaven and earth. It solidly rebuffed the seal.","“A true immortal from the Origin Sect? I, Lu Tianling, will bear witness to the strength of such a being!”","BOOM!","Lu Tianling took a step forward and arrived in front of his weapon, gripping it with one hand. He currently stood at nearly three meters tall and presented a hulking sight. Bathed in crimson flame with the weapon in hand, he resembled a war god of fire.","Initial awakened cultivation level, Lu Tianling faced a true immortal of the Origin Sect with just his halberd!","Whoosh!","He rushed the true immortal without further word and swept his halberd across the sky. The true immortal resisted for only the briefest of seconds before he was thrown backward.","Lu Yun swallowed hard on the city walls. “It looks like my own trump cards are nothing compared to grandpa’s...”","He’d known that Lu Tianling was strong, but not this strong. A true immortal couldn’t take even one hit from his grandfather! The man was only initial awakened realm, but he was deploying the might of an august immortal.","“It’s the treasure in grandpa’s hand... its aura...” Golden light sparkled in Lu Yun’s eyes, but the omnipotent Eye of Nullification couldn’t see through the crimson halberd! In fact, the Lus’ lower spirit rank weapon Brightfire Slayer seemed to be a copy of the halberd.","“The Origin Sect hunts grandpa likely because of this treasure... Its core origin is more frightening than the Seal of the Multitude!”","The seal was a gift from the heavenly dao and it was very high level among connate treasures. However, the halberd was still superior to it! What level did that make the weapon?","Connate spirit treasure? Connate peerless treasure?","At the same time, Lu Yun’s keen senses also perceived that as domineering as the halberd was, it was missing something that it should have possessed—vitality.","It was once alive, but was just a corpse now. Just like... the sword pagoda.","However, it also seemed different from the sword pagoda. The latter was something that the past him had created, and he kept wanting to call it the Sugato Sword Pagoda.","But that couldn’t exist in this time and age, only the sword pagoda could.","BAM!","An enormous collision echoed outside the city as the flaming halberd nailed the true immortal to the ground. His immortal soul didn’t even have the time to flee!","......","The fight’s swift ending stunned everyone into frozen shock. Sui Wuzhou, Nalan Tu, Helian Shan, Luo Yi, and Zhan Taixuan stilled their movements and stared dumbly at Lu Tianling.","That was a true immortal, and an elite that the Origin Sect had raised with painstaking care. Lu Tianling nailed him to the ground in plain view after just a few moves!","Pinpricks of horror traveled down everyone’s backs. Wang Song paled at the sight of the magnificent figure in the air.","“The real fight is upon us.” As Lu Yun took in the brief respite, he waved a ray of green light into his hands from the Lu residence.","“You do not disappoint us, Lu Tianling.” Another five figures appeared in the sky and surrounded the man. Their auras were far stronger than true immortal—they were august immortals!","Hate flashed through Lu Tianling’s eyes as he recalled the halberd. It had been these five who destroyed the Great Xia Lu Clan. The family only had three awakened cultivators then—the poor souls immediately turned to dust when faced with five august immortals.","He had been a young boy at the time and escaped only because of the halberd that he grasped. After fleeing by the skin of his teeth, he then spent a good deal of time scurrying from hiding place to hiding place.","“Gentlemen, I will seek from you some of what the Origin Sect rendered to the Lu Clan!” Lu Tianling declared coldly and swept his halberd around, filling the air with unbounded flames that churned toward the immortals.","“Lu Tianling, everything that you are is a function of that immortal weapon. Without it, you’re just a regular awakened cultivator!” One of the five barked with laughter and summoned his own immortal weapon, ready for a bitter fight.","Bam!","The two collided and bounced back at the same time, completely evenly matched.","“Kill Lu Tianling as soon as possible and take the halberd!” Another person with a remote expression brandished his sword, joining his brethren in attacking the Lu patriarch.","Lu Tianling took a deep breath and transformed his weapon into a dragon of flame. It wreathed protectively around him and firmly blocked the five.","“Aouuu!” A long croon sounded from Dark City, followed shortly by a long black shadow from somewhere in the metropolis.","“Finally!” A relieved smile appeared on Lu Yun’s face. There was no place for him in this kind of battle. It’d be one thing if it was only one august immortal—he could use his methods to set up some obstacles and traps.","However, it was five august immortals and there were certainly more hidden within the Dark orchid army. Knowing how formidable Lu Tianling’s halberd was, it wasn’t impossible that Marquis Origin himself would take the field.","“My deepest thanks to you, little fellow.” An exceedingly melodious, yet very dispassionate voice sounded in Lu Yun’s ears.","Startled, he jerked back to see a young woman of sixteen years old in a long black dress and hair down to her waist. Her form was lithe and shapely, her face worth cities and nearly rivaling that of Fengxian Wu. Her only flaw was that her expression was too unemotional. Even Lu Yun didn’t wish to draw closer to her.","“Are you... senior gray jiao?” he quickly realized.","“Gray jiao?” The girl tilted her face. “My name is Mu Ge. You are permitted to call me that.”","“Very well, Mu Ge.” Lu Yun tugged up the corner of his lips. Never in his wildest dreams had he thought that the fearsome gray jiao would be such an eye-catching young woman.","If only the look in her eyes wasn’t so frosty.","“My injuries were healed due to your Shennong Life Restoring Pill. Therefore, I will take care of this trouble for you.” A tiny smile crossed Mu Ge’s face. It was like an ice flower within a world of snow. Beautiful, but cuttingly cold.","Whoosh!","She appeared in front of an august immortal and gently reached forward. Her tender little hand easily passed through his body.","Puff!","The august immortal exploded into bloody mist before he had a chance to react.","“What?!” Those assembled were flabbergasted by the sudden appearance of a young woman who could kill an august immortal with one move.","“I finally understand why the law enforcers protect Darklake Empire so,” Sui Wuzhou said with resignation as he looked at the young woman. The five awakened cultivators had long stopped their fight.","Helian Shan and the others were likewise dumbfounded by Mu Ge’s way of introducing herself.","“Who are you?! Are you going to interfere in Origin Sect business?!” Another august immortal immediately stopped his attacks when he saw one of his companions go down.","“You talk too much.” Mu Ge furrowed her brow. Black light rose from a hand that she pushed at the speaker.","Shocked, the august immortal found that the delicately wrought hand bore down inexorably like a looming world in his eyes. He couldn’t move at all!","Bam!","Golden light flashed by just before Mu Ge’s hand pressed down on the immortal’s head, taking the four with it.","“Aether immortal?” Mu Ge looked at a man slowly rising from the ground.","“Your strength is the equivalent of one and I am an aether immortal. If the two of us fight, the city behind you will be completely leveled. Why don’t both of us stay out of this?” he said slowly as he fixed his eyes on Mu Ge."]},{"number":2320,"title":"Chapter 2320: Chapter 2209.1: Golden Immortal","paragraphs":["Chapter 2209.1: Golden Immortal","Mu Ge remained as frosty as before. She shot a look of ice at the aether immortal before slowly inclining her head. The four surviving august immortals relaxed slightly when they saw her nod. Aether immortals were the strongest beneath golden immortal. Their power could destroy worlds and as such, they were highly respected in Great Xia.","The four august immortals looked ruefully at each other. Who would’ve thought that such an esteemed personage would be present in this forsaken backwater? Thankfully they had an aether immortal among their number as well, or all would truly be lost this time.","“But a victor must be determined since you have come to Jade Ruins Realm. Shall we adjourn for another battleground?” Mu Ge proposed at an even pace.","The aether immortal’s expression froze slightly before he nodded. “Since the lady wishes it so, then Xu Chi will answer in kind. Let us head to the west.” He vanished into the western horizon before he finished speaking.","Mu Ge nodded at Lu Yun before streaking away in a ray of black light.","Everyone heaved sighs of relief to see the two aether immortals leave. Their auras were so overwhelming that the slightest twitch would obliterate all cultivators on the spot. Thankfully, they’d been conscientious of that possibility and hadn’t released their full force. Otherwise, the million strong army would be nothing but dust by now.","“It looks like we’ve underestimated the Origin Sect’s determination. They’ve even sent out their aether immortals.” Sui Wuzhou smacked his lips at Nalan Tu.","“Lu Tianling is the descendent of the Lus and once stirred up great trouble at the sect. We will naturally pursue him to the end for that.” Nalan Tu’s face darkened to see Lu Tianling hold his own against an august immortal.","“Is that so?” Sui Wuzhou replied with interest. “How about this, let’s work together. You can have Lu Tianling while we get his halberd.”","“Sure.” Nalan Tu arched his brow at Sui Wuzhou, giving the latter a bad feeling.","“Sui Wuzhou, this matter is not for the likes of you. I recommend you stay nicely put in Dark Orchid Empire.” Helian Shan’s black blade released pitch-black splendor as he pointed it at the man.","Sui Wuzhou’s mouth twisted. This law enforcer was different from the one of his memories. They’d fought each other to a draw before!","Helian Shan had been eliminated from the academy and was one of the weakest out of the eliminated batch. He wouldn’t have been assigned to Jade Ruins Realm otherwise. On the other hand, Sui Wuzhou had the help of experts and was among the upper echelon of disciples at the Dao Academy. Why wasn’t he easily triumphing today?","The other two enforcers were in much worse shape. They could barely hold off Nalan Tu and was absolutely no match for him.","BOOM!","Another explosion rang from the sky as Lu Tianling now faced four august immortals as a dragon of flame. Although he was on the losing side, his situation was much better than before thanks to Mu Ge killing one of them. At least he wasn’t scrambling to defend himself anymore.","“It looks like there is no need for us to fight any longer.” Sui Wuzhou put away his rod. “Our battle will not determine the greater outcome.”","He could not dictate the results, and neither could the law enforcers or even chief enforcer of the realm. The chief enforcer was only an empyrean immortal.","......","Lu Tianling’s halberd roared like a dragon. Countless fire origin gathered on him from the land, intensifying the flames around him.","Boom!","His full strength exploded when he fully turned into a man of fire. Caught off guard, an august immortal was blasted directly into the ground.","“Collecting the fire origin of heaven and earth...” Lu Yun took out a jade-green bow with a simple design. “Ah, I missed it earlier. Grandpa’s halberd isn’t similar to the sword pagoda, it’s the same idea as this bow, just in different form.”","Golden light flashed through his eyes—he’d suddenly discovered that the greatbow he’d overlooked this entire time also possessed a powerful core essence. Just like the halberd, it was something that he couldn’t fully see through.","“Master, I’m back!” Inky-green splendor flashed past Lu Yun as Kong Mengqian appeared in an outfit of black. “Wow, martial great-grandfather is amazing to fight four august immortals by himself! ...hmm?”","Her expression froze as she stared fixedly at the jade-green bow. The true origin in her body from the Azure Emperor Chapter of Inception suddenly circulated many times faster than normal.","“Master, can I... take a look... at that bow?” Her voice shook from the strong desire rising from her heart. She must have the jade-green greatbow!","Lu Yun smiled faintly at his disciple’s dusty figure and passed the weapon of incredible might to the girl.","“Thank you, master!” Kong Mengqian quickly closed her hand around it.","Hummm!","Inky-green splendor flared from her body and shot for the horizon the moment her hand touched the bow. A ponderous vitality slowly grew in her being. True origin from the Azure Emperor Chapter of Inception surged. Kong Mengqian nearly instantaneously refined the ownerless bow as soon as she touched it.","It was like it was always meant to be hers.","Jade-green brilliance flashed through her hands as the weapon entered her dantian.","“How do you feel?” Lu Yun stood with his hands behind his back and quietly watched the changing girl.","“My cultivation... has reached combination stage.” Kong Mengqian opened her eyes. “Sadly, it’s insufficient to mobilize the bow. I have to be at least awakened stage to utilize part of its power,” she concluded sadly.","“The bow is yours.” Lu Yun smiled faintly. “Even if you can’t use it for now, you still have the stick of bamboo.”","“The bamboo!” Kong Mengqian started. She’d thought of it as an ordinary item all this time, but could something that contained an unparalleled method like the Azure Emperor Chapter of Inception really be a mundane item?","“How did your mission go?” Lu Yun asked his disciple.","“Master, I got it.” Kong Mengqian waved a jade seal into her hand—a spirit vein swam through it.","Before Lu Yun entered seclusion to refine the Shennong Life Restoring Pill, he sent Kong Mengqian, Bloodbath, and Gun Xie to the eastern, western, and northern capitals of Dark Orchid Empire. Equipped with jade seals, they were to retrieve the spirit veins beneath the cities. As the jade seals were refined by Terra Demon, they had no trouble claiming a few lower rank spirit veins.","Kong Mengqian returned first from the eastern capital. Given the winds of change blowing through Jade Ruins Realm, everyone’s attention was focused on Immortal Burial Valley. No one paid much heed to even Dark Orchid losing a few spirit veins.","It raised a small disturbance through the nation since unknown assailants had stolen their spirit veins, but the empire could only mutely bear the loss given current circumstances. Even the ninth rank cultivation empires would have to do the same, to say nothing of Dark Orchid.","“Not bad.” Lu Yun smiled at the addition of another spirit vein.","“The old lord...” Kong Mengqian raised worriedly to see Lu Tianling fall to the losing side against four august immortals.","“Don’t worry, grandfather’s fine.”","Lu Tianling chose to occupy a higher vantage point in the sky so he could threaten the army below at the same time. Although he was forced back at every turn, his defense and offense remained in perfect harmony. For every blow he suffered, he and the halberd grew more familiar with each other.","While Lu Tianling could utilize the weapon’s might, he hadn’t fully refined it. The issue laid with the level of his cultivation methods, not himself.","“It looks like I need to get a proper cultivation method for grandfather after this matter is over.” Lu Yun’s thoughts traveled to his senior brother.","Boom boom boom boom boom...","The immense boundary over Dark City shuddered.","“Your Majesty, our east and west gates are being attacked by an unknown army!” A heavily armored Lu Xiaochi flew to Situ Wenxian on the back of a lower dao rank flying sword.","“An unknown army?” Situ Wenxian’s face darkened. “The west... is probably Profound Wing Empire. How dare they!”","Profound Wing had once been a Darklake vassal, relinquished after Immortal Burial Valley appeared. To think that they would take advantage of the chaos and launch an attack themselves!","The current Profound Wing Empire was certainly no longer what it’d once been. Perhaps even the royal family had changed. How would outsiders give up on a nation that had something like the valley within its borders?","As for who came from the east... that was an interesting question. Lu Yun’s boundary was formed from the core essence of a tattered ninth rank immortal weapon. Anyone who could shake it and create such massive ripples was no ordinary character.","“Terra Demon, smack those from Profound Wing to death. Make it quick,” Lu Yun said before the emperor could give his orders."]},{"number":2321,"title":"Chapter 2321: Chapter 2209.2: Golden Immortal","paragraphs":["Chapter 2209.2: Golden Immortal","A silver shadow flashed through the air as soon as the young man gave the word.","“Was that... Senior Terra Demon?” Delight colored Situ Wenxian’s eyes when he saw the ray of argent brilliance.","Terra Demon had recovered long ago, but Lu Yun held him in reserve and bade him stand guard on the side. The young man vaguely sensed the existence of a terrifying personage within the Dark Orchid army. He remained unmoving so long as the other did so.","But since those of Profound Wing Empire were attacking them, Lu Yun had no choice but to send out Terra Demon.","“Mmhm.” The young man nodded. While he respected the Darklake emperor, it was the respect he would naturally hold for someone older. He didn’t think much of the man’s identity of emperor. “I’m probably the reason for the attackers at the eastern gate, so I’ll take care of that.","“Mengqian, you don’t need to participate in this battle. Return to the residence and focus on your cultivation.” His disciple’s cultivation was not yet stable since she’d just broken through to initial combination.","“Understood.” Kong Mengqian wasn’t the sort to indulge in her temper. She immediately returned to the Lu residence when she heard her master’s words as she indeed wasn’t suited to fight others at the moment.","“Be careful, Yun’er!” Lu Xiaochi solemnly cautioned. This war would decide the fate of the Lu Clan and the entire Darklake Empire. At his current cultivation level, he did not have the qualifications to be involved either.","Any Lu family member would immediately become everyone’s target as soon as they showed themselves. Lu Xiaochi was merely peak latter nascent soul—not even a grain of sand to the million strong army.","Thus, he held down the fort and kept the army’s movements in sight. That was his area of strength.","“Don’t worry, second uncle.” Lu Yun smiled at the man before vanishing on the spot.","......","The eastern gate of Dark City.","An enormous army of five hundred thousand cultivators was gathered in front of it. They were very different from the one at the western gate as they were all stocky, heavyset, and oddly shaped. All of them rode a powerful spirit beast as their steed.","The weakest among them was soul separation, making them several times stronger than Lu Tianling’s Azure Dragons.","Monster spirits.","The army assembled at Dark City’s eastern gate was the most terrifying army of monster spirits in Jade Ruins Realm. Monster spirit auras soared to the heavens and tinged the ambient qi within five hundred kilometers with an eerie air.","“You’ve got some nerve, monster spirits of the Barren Mountains. You actually dare come to my front door.” A limber young man in white suddenly appeared on the eastern city gates. A cold light glinted in his handsome features as he looked down over the attackers.","“It’s you!” Bi Chen brightened at the sight of Lu Yun. “We will withdraw as soon as you hand over the item.”","Lu Yun curled his lip contemptuously.","“Hoi hoi, so it’s the venerated empyrean immortal. Long time no see, sir.” He chortled when he saw Empyrean Immortal Jadecliff among the monster spirit army.","“Lu Yun, disaster is at hand for Darklake Empire. You would be better served opening the city gates to let us in. That will avoid plunging the land into misery. I can also say a few words for you in front of my lord—that may spare some of the Lus. Now wouldn’t that be the best outcome?” Jadecliff’s eyes twitched before he broke into an awkward smile.","“Who the hell do you think you are?” Lu Yun sniffed. “It looks like after today, there will be only two left of the three great forbidden zones in Jade Ruins Realm.”","Bi Chen’s face darkened.","“Attack the city!” Although he was only an awakened cultivator, he possessed the battle strength of an empyrean immortal. There were numerous empyrean immortals within the monster spirit army as well—gathered by Jadecliff.","Apart from them, there were nearly one hundred monster spirit wandering immortals among their ranks. Their auras were expansive and imposing, not the least bit inferior to empyrean immortals. They were the true trump cards of the Barren Mountains.","There were no representatives from the Origin Sect among them. The monster spirit army surged as soon as Bi Chen gave the order and flung multicolored attacks at the city gates.","BOOM!","Dark City’s boundary shuddered intensely once again.","“So the mountains do actually amount to something after several hundred thousand years in the realm.” Lu Yun waved the Cauldron of Heaven and Earth into his hand. “I’ll have to trouble you this time, little guy.”","He flicked the cauldron and awakened the resting Hadal Bird. It was peak august immortal when it broke free of the gourd’s confinement and was starting to feel around the barrier of divine immortal. After ten days of nurturing from the Nineheavens Brahman Formation, it could be regarded as a half step divine immortal.","Being a Hadal Fire Spirit and half step divine, it could fully hold its own against aether immortals. Once it fully came into its power, it would dominate aether immortals.","Aouu!","Excitement flashed through its eyes when it received Lu Yun’s message. It threw its head back with a long croon and manifested in the sky with the full three hundred meters of its flaming glory.","“What, what is that?” A tongue-tied Jadecliff stared at the fiery bird in the sky.","“It seems... to be spirit of a fire of heaven and earth...” murmured an empyrean immortal next to him.","Whoosh!","Jadecliff was already gone.","For someone as famously cowardly as him, he wouldn’t stay a single second after seeing that his opponent was a Hadal Fire Spirit that was almost divine. He fled without another word. Unease ruffled the monster spirit army in his wake.","“Split up and run!” Bi Chen ordered without any hesitation. He himself shifted as well, ready to retreat.","Whoosh!","An immense sea of black flames was already upon them, turning everything within five hundred kilometers of the eastern gate into a sea of fire. Countless flame sparrows danced in the sea and swallowed everything they encountered.","The five hundred thousand strong army of the Barren Mountains monster spirits was swiftly reduced to cinders. Many of the wandering immortals and empyrean immortals that Jadecliff had recruited also perished.","“Don’t give chase!” Lu Yun quickly called out to the sea of fiery sparrows after it swallowed most of the enemy after a dozen breaths. The Hadal Bird was one of his aces at his current stage. Dark City remained under siege, so the bird needed to stay.","Casting an dissatisfied glance at the escaping monster spirits, the Hadal Bird reduced another few hundred of them to ashes before reluctantly flying back to the Cauldron of Heaven and Earth.","Lu Yun took a deep look at the direction that Bi Chen had run in before returning to the city’s northern gate. Terra Demon was already back at his post. His cultivation was combination stage after baptism in Dao Comprehension Tea and taking the Shennong Life Restoring Pill. He was even a bit stronger than Mu Ge. It’d taken just a few moments for him to smack the Profound Wing army—helmed by a true immortal and a few empyrean immortals—out of existence.","Terra Demon differed from Mu Ge in that he truly possessed his body. His immortal king nascent spirit was damaged and limited by his physical body. Lu Yun’s pill healed most of his nascent soul’s injuries, but he was still curtailed by a fragile body.","The pill that Lu Yun refined wasn’t the true Shennong Life Restoring Pill, the young man’s cultivation was too weak for that.","As for Mu Ge, she must have suffered indelible injuries to her nascent spirit and body a very long time ago. She was essentially reborn after all of his efforts.","......","The two armies had mostly retreated from the northern gate. There were roughly two hundred thousand left of Dark Orchid’s and less than one hundred thousand Azure Dragons. Although Dark Orchid consisted primarily of golden core and nascent soul cultivators, there were still a few powerhouses hidden within.","Lu Tianling was covered with wounds as he stood in the air over the northern gate. He’d nailed one of the four august immortals to death. Bathed in divine fire, flames burned in his eyes. The halberd’s connection to him had grown increasingly stronger and he was utilizing it to his maximum capabilities.","However, Lu Yun could tell that troubles would result from how forcefully his grandfather deployed the weapon. It might recoil on the wielder at anytime.","A new army of less than ten thousand stood in the air beyond the northern gate. Their auras were inexplicably wondrous, as if they were one with the world. Red immortal light washed the city with red brilliance.","Empyrean immortal.","This was an army made of empyrean immortals.","“Enough of this nonsense, Lu Tianling, you’ve brought out all of your trump cards. Come quietly with us—you are our only target.” A figure in gold led the army of empyrean immortals. No one could make out his features through a haze of golden splendor.","Golden immortal.","Their leader was a golden immortal!","“Lu Tianling is taken from the battlefield only as a corpse, not a captive!” The Lu patriarch leveled his halberd at the golden immortal.","“Do you think nothing of the hundred million citizens of Darklake Empire and care only about your own interests?” the golden immortal replied calmly."]},{"number":2322,"title":"Chapter 2322: Chapter 2210.1: Final Trump Card","paragraphs":["Chapter 2210.1: Final Trump Card","The golden immortal stood in the void as a faint smear of gold. There was nothing intimidating about him, but his image ignored the limitations of space and appeared in front of every cultivator. His voice reverberated in everyone’s ears.","Contempt curved Lu Tianling’s lips.","“When did the Origin Sect become so self righteous? If you really cared about the hundreds of millions in Darklake, why would you start this war?”","“I said,” the golden immortal’s tone remained calm. “If you present yourself for captivity, this war will end immediately.”","“In your dreams.” Situ Wenxian bounded to Lu Tianling’s side and stood shoulder to shoulder with the patriarch. “Darklake Empire prospers and declines with Our teacher. If you wish to take him away, you must destroy Darklake first.” Aura flooded out of his body as he stared down the golden immortal, not giving way in the slightest.","“Tribulation stage?” The golden immortal blinked, then smiled. “As expected from Lu Tianling’s disciple. The true cultivation of a third rank emperor is tribulation stage!”","“Tribulation stage!” gasped the bedraggled Wang Song on the ground. How was the emperor of a third rank cultivation empire a tribulation cultivator? It was an easy task for Darklake to vault to a seventh rank empire even without Lu Tianling!","“Damn it, how did they hoodwink the heavenly book? None of this was alluded to in our copy!” An extremely regretful Wang Song finally realized that Dark Orchid had been dragged into a fight between two unfathomable powers. The slightest misstep would irredeemably doom the Dark Orchid royal family.","“Sui Wuye seems to be in full favor of this struggle... He must want to use Darklake to cleanse Dark Orchid for him. What a vicious plan!” Wang Song inwardly cursed out Prince Sui’s ancestors.","Mounting a coup would be too much of a blow to Prince Sui’s reputation. But if an external force eliminated the royal family, then Sui Wuye would become the next emperor through widespread acclaim.","There was no sign of Sui Wuzhou to be seen when Wang Song scanned the battlefield. The man had disappeared long ago.","......","“You sound quite brave. It looks like Lu Tianling has brainwashed you rather successfully,” the golden immortal chuckled.","“Look at a golden immortal playing mind games in front of a tribulation ant,” Situ Wenxian roared with laughter. “If it wasn’t for teacher saving us twenty years back, Darklake Empire would have ceased to exist long ago.”","His words dispersed certain thoughts forming in the Dark City citizens. The battle of Tiger Suppression Pass twenty years ago had been incredibly gruesome. Lu Tianling’s strongest troop of the Vermilion Birds ended up entirely eliminated.","Judging from how mighty the Azure Dragons were on the battlefield, what did that make the Vermilion Birds of old?","What had happened at Tiger Suppression Pass? Had Tianlong Empire matched the current Darklake in strength?","“And how do you know that the affairs of two decades ago weren’t the result of Lu Tianling’s faults?” The golden immortal remained unmoved. He looked solely at a silver-haired man standing behind Lu Tianling and Situ Wenxian. He wouldn’t bother with saying all this to Lu Tianling if it wasn’t for that man.","The man’s spirit ripples were similar to the golden immortal’s, but there seemed to be a formidable strength biding its time in the man. If it erupted, even the golden immortal would have a difficult time of things.","“You know complete fuck-all!” To everyone’s stunned incomprehension, the majestic emperor burst out with profanity.","Tianlong Empire didn’t know the truth behind Tiger Suppression Pass, neither did the Darklake citizens. Only Lu Tianling, Situ Wenxian, the dead Vermilion Birds, and the million strong Tianlong army knew what had happened.","“Second uncle... what’s going on?” Lu Yun transmitted to Lu Xiaochi. He was also curious about that battle—it looked to be an ancient battlefield with countless carcasses buried five thousand kilometers beneath it.","“Are you curious why your second uncle was initial nascent soul at thirty years ago, but is still the same now?” Lu Xiaochi transmitted back.","Lu Yun rubbed his nose. His second uncle was nearly one hundred years old and had spent seventy years still as a nascent soul cultivator. He’d thought this was perfectly natural before he understood his grandfather’s background. It wasn’t uncommon for a nascent soul cultivator in a third rank empire to spend more than a hundred years on a minor cultivator breakthrough.","But Lu Tianling was a person who could train the Azure Dragons, White Tigers, Vermilion Birds, and Black Tortoises. He also had a secret army of the Hidden Dragons. Was it really possible that Lu Yun’s genius second uncle would be bottlenecked at nascent soul for nearly seventy years?","“I was soul separation before that battle,” Lu Xiaochi sighed. “I lost my cultivation after and nearly died. Your grandfather expended enormous effort to bring me back.”","“Ah...” Lu Yun paused.","“Tiger Suppression Pass is a terrifying place. It’s best you go there as little as possible.” Even at his strength, fear appeared in Lu Xiaochi’s eyes when he spoke of the landmark.","Lu Yun refrained from asking further. It would seem that there were certain reasons why Jade Ruins Realm was the weakest of the three thousand Great Xia worlds of cultivation.","......","The golden immortal glowered in the sky.","“In that case, let us go down together.” He waved at the army behind him—energy from ten thousand empyrean immortals burst out in unison.","“Teacher, it looks like we won’t be making it through this one,” Situ Wenxian chuckled ruefully at Lu Tianling.","“Ai...” the man sighed. “who would’ve thought that the Origin Sect’s vice leader, Yan Lengqiao, would be here in person. Surrender after I die. Darklake Empire is recorded in the heavenly book, so they won’t do anything to you.”","Lu Tianling summoned a terrifying ripple out of the halberd in his hand, but found the scene darkening in front of him. A figure in white and silver hair stood in front of him.","“Your opponent is me.” Terra Demon’s silver locks flowed wildly while his robes cracked loudly in the wind.","“You’ve finally stepped forward.” Wariness flared through Yan Lengqiao’s eyes, but he still approached Terra Demon. “Even if you block me, can you block the ten thousand empyrean immortals behind me?”","The battle formation they were assembled in exceeded high level battle formations by at least one hundred times. Not even an august immortal might have the courage to face this army.","“Leave them to me,” a cold voice sounded in their ears.","“Aren’t, aren’t you...” The golden immortal’s expression froze.","“The aether immortals are dead.” Mu Ge sent three rays of green immortal light, a storage ring, and three immortal souls without consciousness to Lu Yun’s hand.","“Thank you, that was an enormous undertaking.” The young man smiled with great relief and placed the items into the sword pagoda.","“Well? Do we fight?” Terra Demon smiled cruelly.","“We’ve gone to all this effort and stand right in front of the situation of our own making. How can we back down now?” Yan Lengqiao breathed out. “Stop hiding, all of you come out.”","Another sixty forms appeared in the air. They comprised of an aether immortal, three origin immortals, a dozen divine immortals, and several dozen lower rank immortals. These were most of the immortals that the Origin Sect had sent into the Jade Ruins Realm and would be a formidable force even in Great Xia. This would make anyone a premier faction beneath the titled kings and marquises.","The newcomers, the three august immortals who’d fought Lu Tianling, and all those hidden in the void gathered together and looked covetously at Lu Tianling. There would be others who preoccupied Terra Demon and Mu Ge for them. What they needed to do was destroy Dark City’s boundary and capture the remnants of the Lu bloodline.","“In that case, let us fight. Show me the capabilities of the Origin Sect of Great Xia.” Silver light danced over Terra Demon as he released his aura.","Yan Lengqiao quickly backed away. “You’re a mid golden immortal...”","Mu Ge likewise flared her arctic power and gave room for her aura to expand.","“Initial golden immortal... no wonder you killed Xu Chi and the others so easily,” Yan Lengqiao’s voice shook slightly. He hadn’t thought that the frosty young woman in a black dress was playing a pig to eat the tiger. She had the strength of a golden immortal, but pretended to be much weaker.","Yan Lengqiao had sent another two aether immortals to help Xu Chi after the two took their fight elsewhere. Who would’ve imagined that she’d kill all three of them!","Aether immortals were very precious to the origin sect!"]},{"number":2323,"title":"Chapter 2323: Chapter 2210.2: Final Trump Card","paragraphs":["Chapter 2210.2: Final Trump Card","Terra Demon made his move, sending argent radiance at Yan Lengqiao like it was sword light. The golden immortal crossed his arms and raised green immortal light in response, firmly blocking the attack.","BAM!","He was flung backward like a cannonball.","The ripples resulting from a fight between two golden immortals could only be described as earth-shattering. Dark Orchid soldiers who didn’t have time to escape were immediately vaporized. It was to Crown Prince Wang Song’s benefit that he’d fled with his confidantes as soon as he saw that Sui Wuzhou was gone. Otherwise, the entire Dark Orchid army would be lost at this stage of the game.","Darklake’s armies and the law enforcers had long retreated into the city. They were sheltered by the boundary. Lu Tianling and Situ Wenxian swiftly did the same when they saw golden immortals commence combat.","Hum hum hum...","The boundary shook and trembled, emitting groans as it was overtaxed.","Mu Ge followed in kind when she saw Terra Demon go on the offensive. Just like her compatriot, she lacked weapons and treasures. She rushed into the Origin Sect army with her bare hands.","Her movements were ruthlessly decisive as Mu Ge’s battle experience was just as varied as Terra Demon’s. Each time her slender hands swung through the air, a ray of black light reaped an immortal’s life.","The capital’s residents gaped at the sky. Immortals of legend were falling from the sky like dumplings being dropped into a pot!","“Immortal Burial Valley? Why do I think Dark City should be renamed to that instead...” Lu Xiaochi murmured as he watched the scene.","“Pfft, only a few have died so far.” Lu Yun rolled his eyes.","“Young master, we’re back!” Gus Xie and Bloodbath returned at this time with a jade seal. They didn’t dare approach the northern gate given the harrowing ripples of battle, so they circled around to the southern gate.","“Well done, there’s nothing more for you here. You may go home and rest.” Lu Yun nodded when he saw two lower rank spirit veins.","“Ah... master... are those... immortals outside the city?” Bloodbath licked his lips as he looked at the rain of immortal corpses. He’d fully recovered his cultivation and was initial combination stage.","“Yep,” Lu Yun nodded again.","Bloodbath and Gui Xie looked at each other, then raised cupped fist salutes after a heavy exhale. They shot toward the Lu residence.","“Yun’er, what did you send them out for?” Lu Tianling was reminded of Kong Mengqian when he saw the two men return.","“Grandpa, you’re not in good condition right now. Eat this pill.” Lu Yun brought out a pill with a dense medicinal fragrance. “I’m sure you can if you borrow the might of that treasure.”","“This is...” Lu Tianling’s expression shifted when he received the pill.","“The Shennong Life Restoring Pill,” the young man answered calmly. His grandfather’s internal injuries were so severe that his internal circulation was a complete mess. If it wasn’t for the crimson halberd supporting the man, he would’ve already keeled over.","“The Shennong Life Restoring Pill?” Situ Wenxian’s eyes went wide. This was a legendary pill recorded in books! Not even the Human Emperor ever owned one, but the young man easily took one out?","Lu Tianling brightened and swiftly swallowed the pill, sitting down cross-legged on the walls to recover. The crimson halberd returned to his body, giving rise to rays of crimson splendor circulating around the man.","......","The battle outside the city was reaching its conclusion. Rays of silver light danced around Terra Demon, overpowering Yan Lengqiao. The latter had to work in tandem with several other immortals to barely keep his opponent in check.","Mu Ge was ensconced in a massive scaled-dragon shadow. It swallowed countless immortals every time it moved.","There was no doubt whatsoever what the final outcome would be. Terra Demon and Mu Ge were respectively mid golden immortal and peak initial golden immortal. As numerous as the Origin Sect was, they were no match for two powerhouses of the ancient world of immortals.","Pfft!","The image of a silver sword appeared in Terra Demon’s crossed hands. It easily ran Yan Lengqiao through when it moved. Eyes wide open, the golden immortal stared incredulously.","“How can you... I already...” Vitality drained from his body.","“That lamp may be able to protect the brand of your nascent soul, but it cannot deter my immortal king nascent soul.” Terra Demon shook his head and grabbed Yan Lengqiao’s corpse, throwing it at Dark City. “What’s to come will always come.”","He stood down after killing Yan Lengqiao, looking deeply at the northern sky. Mu Ge paused her movements and drew close to Terra Demon. The Origin Sect immortals lost their direction with the death of Yan Lengqiao. They cheered at Mu Ge’s reprieve and swiftly gathered in the northern direction.","Out of the more than ten thousand immortals, two thousand would forever remain in this world.","“Terra Demon, leave only three alive,” Lu Yun commanded coldly as he flew up from the city walls.","The man immediately formed hand seals and brought down a curtain of silver light from the sky. It fully enveloped the less than ten thousand survivors.","Kaboom!","Overwhelming energy of heaven and earth trembled, causing vacant looks in those trapped by the curtain of light. There were no vital signs coming from them anymore. Three august immortals with their cultivation sealed were thrown onto the city walls.","Lu Yun waved the sword pagoda out of his dantian and swiftly collected all of the immortal corpses on the battlefield.","......","A collection of incomparably enormous black clouds rushed toward this part of the world from the northern horizon. A domineering man dressed in golden armor stood in front of them, at least one hundred thousand immortals of varying cultivation arranged behind him!","“Arcane immortal,” Terra Demo said slowly when he saw the man. Lu Yun took a deep breath, gravity flashing through his eyes.","“Was my assumption incorrect and it’s not Marquis Origin who’s come?” The young man frowned.","“Mu Ge and I should be able to force him back, but the one hundred thousand immortals behind him are another trouble.” Terra Demon was uncharacteristically grave. He and Mu Ge were not true golden immortals —they just possessed the battle strength of mid and initial golden immortal. They were still weaker than arcane immortals.","“How dare you kill this king’s men!” As the black clouds drew closer, the man in golden armor stared down Terra Demon and Mu Ge. He was more than three meters tall and exuded a presence of being loftier and superior to all. His expression was remote to the core—there wasn’t a hint of emotion to be found within it.","“This king? You are one of the titled kings of Great Xia?” Lu Yun furrowed his brows at the speaker.","“Yun’er... he is Marquis Origin.” Lu Tianling’s voice rang out as he exited the boundary. “To think that you would become a titled king and come in person! This is truly the honors of honor for our minor Darklake Empire.”","Three parts despair, three parts sarcasm, and three parts relief filled Lu Tianling’s tone. The remaining part was a heavy weight of bitterness.","“Lu Tianling, this king has arrived. You and your grandson will come with me.” Marquis Origin—the Origin King intoned emotionlessly. “The others and this Dark City will be burial goods for my Origin Sect.”","Origin King Yan Guichi ever-so-slightly lifted his hand to collect a ray of purple light within his palm.","“Burial goods for your sect?” Lu Yun burst out laughing. “Marquis Origin, the Origin King, Yan Guichi, once a slave of the Lu Clan!” He rapidly switched through four terms of address as he jeered, “Darklake Empire has been beset by calamity due to the slave that you are. Since you’ve brought so many immortals with you, all of you can be the burial goods for the people of my nation!”","“What?!” Yan Guichi stuttered to hear Lu Yun speak so brazenly. A great disturbance rippled through the immortals behind him. The noble Origin King, Great Xia’s greatest titled king... was once a Lu slave? What was going on here?","“Showing disrespect to this king...” Yan Guichi was interrupted by a massive boom before he could finish.","KABOOM!","A massive warship running three thousand meters from bow to stern broke through the air. It was colored black throughout and was crafted with a simple and ancient design. It appeared out of nowhere beneath Lu Yun’s feet and hovered in the air. A cannon mouth that spanned three hundred meters across took aim squarely at the knot of black clouds.","A tremendous suction force appeared the moment the warship did, drawing Lu Yun and the others into the vessel. The Cauldron of Heaven and Earth flew out with a wave of the young man’s hand and settled down in the center of the vessel.","“A cross ark...” Changes finally flickered through Yan Guichi’s face.","“Slave Yan Guichi, this young master will show you today just who is going to be burial goods for whom!”","BOOOOOM!","A pillar of black light that was three hundred meters wide erupted from the cannon and crashed into Yan Guichi’s cloud with a searing aura.","All was quiet between heaven and earth."]},{"number":2324,"title":"Chapter 2324: Chapter 2211.1: Crimson Emperor Chapter","paragraphs":["Chapter 2211.1: Crimson Emperor Chapter","The pillar of black light lasted for less than ten thousandth of a breath, but it molded eternity in that singular moment.","All was quiet between heaven and earth. When the pillar of light passed through, it ripped the enormous black cloud to pieces. Yan Guichi was a tattered remnant of his former self—his golden armor barely clung to his body in bits and pieces. At least twenty thousand of his immortal troops had been reduced to dust while the remaining eighty thousand were injured to varying degrees.","“Lu. Tian. Ling!!” Yan Guichi’s noncommittal expression finally vanished, replaced by deep-rooted fury.","A dragon desired to step on an ant, but in turn suffered some damage from the ant’s final stand! THough he was an arcane immortal, his dao heart wavered from the indignation and he went berserk.","Hummm!","The black cannon at the tip of the cross ark lit up again before Yan Guichi could respond. Another pillar of light one hundred meters across cut through the sky and blasted the army of immortals.","“Split—”","Boom!","Yan Guichi and the eighty thousand behind him were swallowed by the pillar of black before he could finish speaking.","As Great Xia’s premier battle weapon, the cross cannon was so fast and powerful that not even the initial arcane immortal Yan Guichi could adequately react to it.","The Origin Sect lost another twenty thousand immortals to this blast, leaving less than sixty behind. They were all very much worse for the wear with their clothes and armors in shredded pieces. Many of them were stark naked.","The closer to the front they were—such as the golden immortals—the worse their injuries. Standing at the very front, Yan Guichi’s remarkably opulent armor was thoroughly crushed. However, he wore a dark-green immortal rank robe that protected the newly promoted Origin King from running naked through the streets.","It took only two blasts to kill more than forty percent of the Origin Sect’s representatives. Not only that, but it also erased their morale.","“I’m going to kill you, Lu Tianling!” roared Yan Guichi. Purple light sparkled over his body as a deep purple blade formed in his hand. He vanished from the spot and reappeared over the cross ark.","BAM!","Purple light flared balefully and swallowed the enormous vessel.","Humm!","The shadow of a large seal appeared over the cross ark and stood in front of the purple light.","Kaboom!","The purple blade of light crashed into the seal and shoved the cross ark belowground with its force of impact. How great was Yan Guichi’s strength being an arcane immortal!","But as the cross ark fell, its cannon lit up again and fired another pillar of black light. It was the ark’s third firing! Yan Guichi wanted to lose his mind!","Without his protection and reeling from the first two impacts, thirty thousand immortals were swallowed by the blast this time. Some of the more quick-witted ones, however, dispersed when Yan Guichi brought down the cross ark. Those who died in this salvo were those who couldn’t think on their feet.","“Attack the city and raze it to the ground!” screamed an enraged Yan Guichi.","Up on the city walls, cultivators goggled with disbelief. Lu Tianling and the others faced real immortals, and not just one or two of them, but a full hundred thousand! Only three cannon blasts were needed to reduce them to less than thirty thousand. What kind of a terrifying battle record was this?!","Lu Yun’s lips quirked upward.","Cannon? Strictly speaking, these were weapons of war. But ah, that couldn’t be their name at this time. They had to be cross cannons, or a corner might be lifted on his sealed memories and the entire seal blown.","The surviving twenty thousand immortals finally came to their senses and swiftly took out healing medicines and pills. Brilliant splendor burst from their bodies as they took a few moments to recover and then shot toward Dark City.","Panic reigned in the capital. The warship that’d killed thousands upon thousands of immortals had been blasted into the ground by the immortal emanating purple light. As powerful as the city’s boundary was, it would not hold off the incoming horde.","“A cross ark... why is there a cross ark??” Yan Guichi looked at the vessel in the ground with a trace of horror. Cross arks were important weapons in Great Xia, while cross cannons were forbidden objects. They were exceedingly difficult to make and only the royal family possessed the method. More importantly was that Great Xia royalty only owned ten cross cannons!","It was said that a stunning genius of legend had invented the cross arks and cannons. The one in front of him seemed even more terrifying than the ones of Yan Guichi’s memories. It seemed to have been... modified somewhat.","“Thankfully they don’t have Dao Rune Pills to power the cannon with...” Yan Guichi shuddered. If his opponent possessed sufficient numbers of Dao Rune Pills to bring the full power of the cross cannon to bear, then he would’ve been blasted to bits long ago. “I must get my hands on that ark and cannon...”","Boom!","The void shook just as Yan Guichi was about to make a move.","“That is enough, everyone stand down.” An ethereal voice traveled out of the air. The immortals about to attack Dark City were flung back to their starting positions.","“Who is it?!” Purple lightning flashed through Yan Guichi’s eyes as he took out a healing pill from his storage ring.","“Origin King, this matter ends here. Go back from whence you came,” sounded the ethereal voice again. It echoed in everyone’s ear, but no one—including Yan Guichi—could catch a glimpse of the figure.","“So it’s you,” Yan Guichi frowned. “Does the Fengxian King wish to interfere in Origin Sect matters?”","“Lu Tianling once saved Little Wu’s life, so the Fengxian King owes him a favor,” the voice responded calmly.","“I can accept that,” Yan Guichi nodded. “But the Origin King Estate has suffered heavy losses, so I require compensation.”","Having been made the Origin King, the Origin Sect’s name was thereby changed as well.","“What a shameless mangy cur!” A figure flew out of the cross ark. “Compensation?! I’ll give you compensation!!” Lu Yun paid no heed to his image and jabbed a finger at Yan Guichi’s nose. “You’re an old fart without a trace of self dignity, a traitorous slave who isn’t worth the air he breathes! How dare you want compensation?! How about I drag out eighteen generations of your ancestors as compensation!”","Dragging out eighteen generations of the Origin King’s ancestors... Lu Yun really had possessed that ability once upon a time. He particularly wanted to dig up Yan Guichi’s ancestral grave—tomb raiding?","For reasons unknown, his heart itched when he thought of tomb raiding. Had he been a tomb raider in his sealed memories? In any case, he was completely incensed.","If he hadn’t consumed all of the goodwill in the Seal of the Multitude and called upon its strength to protect the cross ark, it would’ve been destroyed in that blow. Apart from Terra Demon and Mu Ge, no one else inside the ark would’ve survived.","Lu Yun’s temper rose at the notion that he could’ve died.","“You court death!” Yan Guichi had lost the balance of his dao heart long ago and flew into a rage when he heard Lu Yun’s cursing. Brilliant purple splendor sped through the air at the young man.","Humm!","A curtain of white light drifted down from the sky and stopped the purple radiance in its tracks.","“Do you wish to defy the Fengxian King?” The voice remained otherworldly, but was tinged with anger.","“I wouldn’t dare!” Yan Guichi took a deep breath. The Fengxian King was Great Xia’s greatest king, a half step away from the Human Emperor and the second greatest in the dynasty. A newly promoted king such as he didn’t dare antagonize this personage.","“Since you dare not, you may leave,” the voice softened.","Yan Guichi took a deep look at Lu Yun and clenched his fists before walking away.","“We go!”","Everyone from the Origin King Estate vanished without a trace, leaving behind charred earth.","“Lu Tianling, the favor that the Fengxian King owes you has been repaid in kind. Look well after yourself.”","......","“Hoo...” Lu Yun heaved a long sigh of relief after Yan Guichi and the others disappeared. He raised cupped fists to the sky and slowly drifted to the ground.","The Hadal Fire Spirit withered within the Cauldron of Heaven and Earth, once more reduced to a flame state and flickering silently inside. In that split moment, Lu Yun had used it to ignite the four lower rank spirit veins and thousands of immortal corpses to draw upon the power of connate yi wood. That had powered the cross cannon.","Otherwise, the cannon wouldn’t have been able to erupt with such power—not even with the fire spirit. Everything had been under his control—apart from the fact that Yan Guichi was an arcane immortal.","There was only one step between arcane and golden immortal, but the difference was heaven and earth. Lu Yun was confident that he could blast a peak golden immortal to death with one shot, but he could only deliver slight damage to an arcane immortal.","Thankfully, the Fengxian King’s men had interfered at the last possible second or they would be in true danger this time. While he still had some trump cards up his sleeve, he would no longer know any peace once he used them. He would be able to eliminate Yan Guichi, but also open himself up to more unsavory characters."]},{"number":2325,"title":"Chapter 2325: Chapter 2211.2: Crimson Emperor Chapter","paragraphs":["Chapter 2211.2: Crimson Emperor Chapter","The worlds shook after this event. A vaunted arcane immortal met with ghastly battle in a lower ranked world of cultivation and lost nearly one hundred thousand troops?! The newly promoted Origin King would find it hard to lift his head in front of other immortals in the future.","“Are you alright, Yun’er?” Lu Tianling finally found the way to exit the cross ark and quickly grabbed his grandson to determine his condition. He sighed with relief to find the young man safe and unharmed.","“I’m fine, just exhausted,” Lu Yun smiled. “How are you, grandpa? There’s no lasting side effects, are there?”","“No, and it’s all thanks to your pill, otherwise...” Lu Tianling shook his head, gratification on his face.","......","Tranquil moonlight spilled over the earth.","Given the tremendous boundary encircling Dark City, there were no defenders camped against its walls. A young man in white brocade robes and a sleeveless downy-blue overcoat strolled over the northern city walls. He held an exquisite wine flask and admired the moon between sips of wine.","It was Lu Yun and he was a bit depressed. He’d fired three blasts from the cross cannon to send one hundred immortals into an uproar. How much was the admiration and goodwill that should’ve resulted from that!","But none of it went to him; it was a complete wash as no one believed that the Lu young master was responsible for the deed. All of it focused on Lu Tianling. His name was on everyone’s lips and the entire realm talked about the legendary figure that fought four august immortals by himself, killing one of them. This level of accomplishment would make him a premier genius even in Great Xia—he would rival those perverse geniuses.","Lu Yun rose to his feet and threw his wine flask over the walls. A long moment passed before a crisp shattering sound traveled back to his ears. He heaved a long sigh and murmured, “Senior brother, I’ll come to you if you don’t come to me.”","He sat down cross-legged again and sent his mind into his dantian, trying to communicate with the hazy dao character that his nascent soul used for a seat cushion.","Humm!","A definitive hum later, Lu Yun found the scene changed around him. He was in a void of silver and probed around with his mind.","“As I thought, my physical body isn’t here. It’s just my nascent soul.”","The void was as if before, the unbounded cosmos around them. The center was land formed of starlight; a stone table and stone stools were placed in the very middle.","“Master? Senior brother?” he called out as he walked toward the table. The starlight sensed his arrival and shook a ray of blue out of them, one that solidified into a humanoid form.","“What brings you here, little junior brother?” Sky looked quizzically at Lu Yun.","“I’m here to request a cultivation method for my grandfather,” the young man cut straight to the chase.","“Cultivation method?” Sky blinked and made a few calculations. “So you’ve already obtained the bow and guessed its connection with the halberd!”","“What exactly is the bow and the halberd?” Lu Yun frowned.","“You would know if you understand dao,” Sky smiled.","“If I understood dao... I would be an immortal overlord,” Lu Yun calculated. Sky’s response corresponded to the Understanding Dao chapter of the Nine Chapters of Dao, which was the equivalent of immortal overlord. “Since senior brother has the Azure Emperor Chapter of Inception, surely you have the Crimson Emperor Chapter?”","Sky smiled. “I do not, but your guess is correct. Your grandfather will be able to refine the halberd if he masters that method.”","“Where is it?” Lu Yun asked hurriedly.","“Immortal Burial Valley,” Sky responded. “You will obtain it if you visit that locale, but that place is extremely dangerous and possesses things that will agitate your sealed memories...”","The man’s face grew solemn. He didn’t mind danger since none of it would truly threaten his junior brother. Lu Yun’s memories, however, were extremely important and could not be unsealed due to happenstance.","“If your grandfather does not master the Crimson Emperor Chapter before he reaches immortality, his body and nascent soul will be assimilated by the weapon to become part of it.”","“I understand,” Lu Yun nodded.","“Very well, you should go back now.” Sky dismissed Lu Yun’s form with a wave of his hand.","......","“Immortal Burial Valley...” Lu Yun came back to his senses still seated in a cross-legged position on the city walls. He smiled ruefully—he really didn’t want to go to Immortal Burial Valley as the things inside were beyond the scope of his current abilities.","But his senior brother said that the Crimson Emperor Chapter was within the valley, so he had to go.","“The Human Emperor of Great Xia summoned the image of the Sword of Chaos with his strength alone...” His expression took a turn for the better when he thought of what had taken place a few days ago. The Sword of Chaos was a legendary existence even in the world of immortals. The Sword of Chaos...","Another thing that Lu Yun was intimately familiar with and missed terribly.","Morning the next day.","The sun slowly rose in the sky as the earth returned to its usual hustle and bustle. Ouyang Shengtian gradually materialized in a remote cave.","“Was that Lu Tianling’s true strength?” Wryness filled his mouth. Even though he’d refined a wandering immortal’s nascent soul and inherited everything that was the immortal, he was still an ant in Lu Tianling’s eyes.","After the Ouyang genius lost to Lu Yun, he’d escaped in the chaos of the Azure Dragons battling Dark Orchid’s army. But given the blows between a million strong army, he suffered deep injuries as he fled.","“Thank goodness the injuries don’t touch my core essence...” Ouyang Shengtian heaved a slight sigh of relief. “But Lu Yun won’t easily let me go. Immortal Burial Valley... if I want to grow strong fast, I must go to the valley!”","He looked to the western sky with a resolute gaze. Although the Ouyang Clan still existed, it was now a Lu pawn. Ouyang Shenghe, Ouyang Shengmu, and Ouyang Shengxiang had fallen under Lu Yun’s control.","“Shenghe, Shengmu, Shengxiang, I’ll save you!” The young man clenched his fists. Although his siblings misunderstood him, he wasn’t willing to forsake them.","Ouyang Shengtian suddenly felt the back of his neck tighten and cold air come for him. He subconsciously drew taut like a bow and darted out like a panther.","BAM!","A pit three meters across appeared where he’d been standing.","“Not bad, not bad, you evaded a blow from my Lil Black.” A voice akin to withered wood rubbing against each other sounded when Ouyang Shengtian stood up. It sent goosebumps all over his body.","Whoosh!","He summoned a golden spear into his hand and lifted his head in the direction of the speaker. He swore that he’d never seen someone so ugly in his life. The young man in front of him was incomparably ugly with thick lips, a flattened nose, one eye twice the size of regular eyes and the other smaller than a peanut.","His skin was pitted and coarse. Other than a human form, there wasn’t anything human about his appearance.","“How can someone so ugly exist...” Ouyang Shengtian murmured to himself.","“Hmph.” The ugly young man flicked a sideways glance at him. “You have the right to become my servant since you’ve evaded Lil Black’s blow.”","A snake fifteen meters long and as thick as a bucket reared next to the young man. One pale-golden horn the length of a meter grew from its head and it glared coldly at Ouyang Shengtian.","“A blackwater snake king... you have a soul separation blackwater snake king?” Ouyang Shengtian didn’t lose his temper as he’d matured after experiencing the rises and falls of life in the wandering immortal’s memories and experience. While he maintained his composure, he would never become another’s servant!","Hummm hummm.","Two pale-golden spear images appeared next to him. A contemptuous smile spread across the ugly young man’s face and he shifted, turning indistinct.","Ouyang Shengtian’s pupils constricted violently. Massive force came from behind him just as he was about to take action and threw him out before his true origin had a chance to operate.","Thump!","Soul separation Ouyang Shengtian didn’t last even one move against the ugly young man!","“Kid,” his opponent stooped next to the Ouyang genius. “Either be my servant or Lil Black’s food. Choose wisely.”","He smiled merrily, drying up the tears in Ouyang Shengtian’s eyes.","......","A few days later, Lu Yun left Darklake Empire with only Terra Demon. The nation had become a forbidden zone in Jade Ruins Realm. Foreign immortals did not dare easily draw near. Forbidden items such as cross cannons had appeared! No one wanted to be caught in the crossfire.","Not to mention, there were two golden immortals in residence. Yan Guichi was in no shape to return for Lu Tianling given the losses he’d suffered.","Immortal Burial Valley now fully lived up to its name. Great Xia had lost six marquises and one titled king in battle of that day, taking the worlds by storm. It also looked different after suffering a blow from the Sword of Chaos. It was now a valley ten thousand kilometers across, the entrance to the valley at its center.","Immortals were forbidden from entering Immortal Burial Valley!"]},{"number":2326,"title":"Chapter 2326: Chapter 2212.1: Ghost Zombies","paragraphs":["Chapter 2212.1: Ghost Zombies","Immortals were forbidden from entering Immortal Burial Valley.","With the valley as the center, everywhere within five hundred thousand kilometers was off limits. It had truly become a place that buried immortals as those who entered this range suffered mysterious attacks that scattered their souls.","No one dared test the prohibition after a golden immortal turned to dust in front of everyone’s eyes. Cultivators were unharmed if they attempted to enter.","A gigantic formation array enclosed the valley. Guarded by countless empyrean immortals, there was a tiny opening at its easternmost side that was freely open to cultivators. Of course, no one would stop an immortal brave enough to try.","......","The entrance to the array was a hotbed of activity. Countless cultivators gathered there, breathing life into this barren part of the world. There was even a small marketplace that sprang up.","“Ninety-nine mid rank formations huh? What a great deal of effort,” Lu Yun clucked his tongue at the curtain of light.","“Those immortals are too much!” Nearby complaints rang loud and clear. “They seal off the area because they can’t enter. We cultivators need to hand our treasures over if we get our hands on any!”","A combination cultivator glowered at the formations and couldn’t resist voicing his thoughts.","“The heavenly book’s rules will return in less than five months, making all visiting immortals leave. You can just wait until then,” someone jeered in response.","The rest of the cultivators discussed enthusiastically among themselves after the two started. This formation array had appeared ten days ago. Many cultivators entered it during this time, but none made it out. There were more waiting on the sidelines in observation.","“Great Xia’s Human Emperor isn’t an idiot.” Relief appeared in Lu Yun’s eyes when he saw the array. Others might not know the truth behind Immortal Burial Valley, but he did.","“Young master, is it really... that buried here?” Shock appeared in Terra Demon’s eyes when he assessed the formations. “If it is, then these small formations won’t hold them.”","“Don’t worry, it should just be remnants here. Otherwise, this realm would’ve long become theirs.” Lu Yun was unconcerned. There were taller people than him who would hold the sky up if it caved in—he was a shorty at the moment. There was still an undercurrent of pressure running through his mind, however. He seemed to have overlooked something.","He was indeed a shorty, but if the three who could support this realm were already...","“Alright, wait outside while I take a look.” Waving off Terra Demon, Lu Yun approached the entrance by himself.","“Hey there, little guy!” Someone stopped him before he drew close—a latter soul projection middle-aged man.","“Yes?” Lu Yun tilted his head with a sideways glance.","“Immortal Burial Valley is filled with danger and you might run into some if you go in yourself. Why not join our team and go together?” The middle-aged man smiled and pointed behind him.","Eight cultivators looked back at them, all of them soul projection. The middle-aged man was the strongest out of them.","Lu Yun had noticed earlier that the cultivators stood in groups of five to eight. It would seem that temporary teams had sprung up, ones comprised of mostly the same cultivation level. Thus, it made sense that the stronger ones had banded together.","Most of the participants were wandering cultivators since those from strong families or clans wouldn’t accept outsiders.","Lu Yun shook his head, then flashed to the entrance.","“Another kid who wants to die!” A young girl dressed in red spirit armor walked out, rolling her eyes in Lu Yun’s direction. “He’s probably one of those snobby trash young masters.”","“Forget it, we don’t need him. Let’s go in after we find another person.” The middle-aged man didn’t mind.","Although several empyrean immortals stood guard at the entrance, they were just sitting cross-legged in the void. They didn’t prevent anyone from entering and seemed more like decorations.","“Young man,” a female empyrean immortal opened her eyes just as Lu Yun was about to enter the array. “There is incredible danger within this array and more than ninety percent of the cultivators who have entered have died. Being a soul projection cultivator, there is no chance that you will survive. It would be better for you to enter in the company of others.”","Lu Yun paused and turned toward the lady, flashing her a brilliant smile. “My thanks to fairy big sis, but I’m used to being alone. Rather than teaming up with others, I’d like to retain freedom of movement.”","The empyrean immortal smiled to hear the young man call her “fairy big sis” and said nothing more.","Lu Yun smiled again and was about to turn around when a familiar figure entered his line of sight. He raised a brow and plastered a pleasant smile on his face before walking over.","“Aiyaya, and here I wondered who it was. Isn’t this young master Ouyang!” He grabbed the other for a bear hug.","Ouyang Shengtian jumped with surprise and froze when he saw Lu Yun. These days, he feared most any member of the Lu Clan. Lu Tianling was an old monster and Lu Yun was a young monster. As for Lu Xiaochi... who knew how deep he concealed his monstrosity?","“Eh? It’s only been a few days—what’s happened to young master Ouyang?” Lu Yun assessed Ouyang Shengtian with genuine surprise. Formerly pristine white robes were now gray and his handsome face was covered in dust. Was that a... spirit beast collar around his neck?","Had someone captured him to be a spirit pet—no, human pet?","“I say, Ouyang Shengtian, how are you getting along so poorly in life?” Lu Yun blinked with astonishment.","“It’s all thanks to you,” huffed Ouyang Shengtian as he looked at Lu Yun out of the corner of his eyes. He had a sudden thought—would the ugly young man want to take Lu Yun for a pet if he saw the Lu young master?","Thus, he surreptitiously glanced behind him as they talked.","The ugly young man was leisurely making his way over on the back of the blackwater snake king. He held a large bag in his hand that was filled with various spirit fruits and snacks.","Lu Yun looked at him with puzzlement. Who is this guy? The Eye of Nullification can’t see through him. He’s spirit separation, but he must be someone if he can treat Ouyang Shengtian as a pet.","“Master!” The Ouyang young master shuddered when the ugly young man arrived and respectfully lowered his head.","“Mmhmm, there’s a good boy,” cackled Ugly. He caressed Ouyang Shengtian’s head, failing to catch a deep flicker of viciousness in the latter’s eyes.","“Who is this?” Ugly threw a spirit fruit into his mouth and chewed on it, pointing at Lu Yun with his chin.","“Greetings to this fellow daoist, I am Lu Yun!” Since Lu Yun couldn’t see through the other, he maintained a congenial smile and raised cupped fists. The ugly young man looked one or two years younger than him, but his cultivation was much higher than Lu Yun’s.","“Lu Yun?” Ugly scratched his head. “Grandson of Lu Tianling, the strongest in Jade Ruins Realm?”","“Precisely.” Lu Yun nodded, not the least bit put out by the other’s attitude.","Some cultivators looked over when they heard the name Lu Tianling. There was no helping it, Lu Tianling was so renowned at the moment that even cultivators near Immortal Burial Valley knew of him.","The strongest of Jade Ruins Realm wasn’t a title that he’d given himself; he’d eclipsed the reputations of the other three strongest in the world long ago—the chief enforcer, Bi Chen, and Lang Ye. As his grandson, Lu Yun’s name was also out there.","However, most of the stories having to do with him revolved around his ludicrous acts.","After receiving an affirmative response, Ugly jumped down from the blackwater snake king’s head and inspected Lu Yun closely.","“They say that young master Lu is one meter tall and has a smashed-in face. You’re supposed to be uglier than me, but you...” he said, perplexed.","Lu Yun blinked. “What kind of nonsense is that? I am so dashing and noble that ladies fall at my feet. How am I one meter tall and have a smashed-in face? Heresy and blasphemy!” He stroked his chin lovingly. “At the very least, I’m better looking than you.”","Ugly blinked his misshapen eyes. “Are you not afraid that I’ll kill you?”","Lu Yun curled his lip. Kill me? Terra Demon’s right there, you’ll be the first to die if you do anything.","Ugly seemed to read the contempt in his eyes and cocked his head, sizing up Lu Yun again. “My principles are that I steal valuables and do not take my pleasure, or I take my pleasure and do not steal valuables. If you can provide neither, you will become my human pet.","“So, do you have valuables, can offer me pleasure, or nothing at all?” An evil smile spread across his face."]},{"number":2327,"title":"Chapter 2327: Chapter 2212.2: Ghost Zombies","paragraphs":["Chapter 2212.2: Ghost Zombies","Ugly looked Lu Yun up and down and smacked his lips.","“You steal valuables and do not take your pleasure, or you take my pleasure and do not steal valuables?” Lu Yun didn’t mind the gaze—what kind of person hadn’t he seen in his three thousand lifetimes? Regardless, Ugly’s words briefly took him aback—why did they sound so familiar?","“Do you have valuables or can you offer me pleasure?” Ugly repeated.","Some of the cultivators watching the show abruptly recalled something shocking as they looked at Ugly. They swiftly turned tail and ran, unwilling to be in his vicinity.","“This young master has neither.” Lu Yun spread out his hands; he recalled who this person was. Fengxian Wu had cursed him out plenty of times when she resided at the Lu residence. Plainly, he was the one who’d robbed her of all her valuables and inflicted heavy injuries on her.","“Heh heh, then be my pet.” A golden collar appeared in Ugly’s hand and he waved it around. Standing next to him, Ouyang Shengtian smirked coldly. Given what he knew of Lu Yun, a vicious fight was about to ensue. But as strong as the Lu young master was, he was no match for Ugly.","The latter’s cultivation was soul separation, but his battle strength... He’d robbed more than one combination cultivator on their way here.","“Um...” Lu Yun scratched his head and asked in innocent tones, “Bro, you do know I’m the grandson of the most powerful in Jade Ruins Realms, right?”","Ugly paused.","“And um... you do know that two golden immortals answer to my grandfather’s banner?” Lu Yun continued.","Ugly blinked.","“So... do you think my grandfather would’ve let me come here by myself?” Lu Yun concluded merrily. If he hadn’t transmitted orders to Terra Demon seconds ago, the man would’ve already smacked Ugly and Ouyang Shengtian to death. The ugly young man held his fair share of secrets and Lu Yun wanted to know what they were.","“Eh... ahem, isn’t the weather good today!” Ugly changed the topic. A thundercloud quickly scuttled across the sky and covered the sun after his words. “Since you have no valuables, young master Lu, you will bring me pleasure!”","He ignored everyone’s gazes and bawled in his broken voice, “From now on, Lu Yun is Mo Ran’s consort! I will show no mercy to any man or woman who dares approach him!”","Lu Yun: ......","His mind spun and bile bubbled up at the back of his throat. So this guy likes men...","“You’re right, the weather is indeed good today. I’m outta here!” Lu Yun’s hands formed a seal, taking him away from the scene.","Ouyang Shengtian stared dumbly at Ugly and subconsciously clamped his legs together. Should he just end things and detonate his nascent soul right now?","“Don’t worry, you’re not my type.” Ugly rolled his eyes at the Ouyang young master.","......","“That ugly young man is a crafty fellow, it’s just that his methods are a bit awkward.” Having entered the formation array, Lu Yun chuckled ruefully as he thought of what’d just happened.","Ugly had been concerned about the Terra Demon hidden beside Lu Yun. He’d made that surprising announcement to scare off the Lu young master and prevent further confrontation. More friction would develop if the two of them remained on the scene.","Just as Ugly was on the alert against Terra Demon, so was Lu Yun cautious of the mysterious young man. The former’s methods certainly left a... deep impression.","All was foggy within the formation. The assembly of ninety-nine mid rank formations gave rise to a strength that ordinary formations could not measure up to. Even the current Lu Yun could do nothing in the face of this assembly.","He adopted a prudent manner and opened the Eye of Nullification to scan everything within fifty kilometers.","“Aouu!” A bright red being flung itself at him, crossing several kilometers within the blink of an eye.","Lu Yun could clearly see that it was a cultivator, but it no longer looked human. A bloody light enveloped it and the Eye of Nullification could make out a decrepit, rotting body beneath.","“It’s this thing alright,” Lu Yun sighed. Immensely tense, Immortals Forbidden appeared in his hand. The term “ghost zombie” was suppressed as soon as it arose in the depths of his memories.","Hummm!","Crimson light exploded from Immortals Forbidden, as scintillating as a miniature sun. A dozen rays of sword light flared from its point and slashed down on the bloody being.","Bam!","It ruptured the bloody head, dispersing the light around it. The being toppled over as a rotten corpse of a cultivator.","“All of the cultivators that entered before have likely turned into these things.” Lu Yun sped toward the eye of the formation array with Immortals Forbidden upraised. Five thousand kilometers wasn’t too far for him.","“I wonder how Bloodbath and Gui Xie are.” He could see everything within fifty kilometers, so he easily dodged all of the bloody beings.","Given his methods, entering the array with a team of soul projection cultivators would be attaching deadweight to himself. As for those stronger, they wouldn’t think much of Lu Yun. Thus, it was better for him to venture forth by himself. That offered a certain degree of flexibility and he didn’t need to be beholden to anyone else.","Bloodbath and Gui Xie had arrived at the valley before him as a vanguard. They’d likely entered the formation array since Lu Yun didn’t see them outside. They were respectively combination and tribulation stage. With Terra Demon’s tutelage, their strength advanced by leaps and bounds everyday. He wasn’t worried about them.","The Eye of Nullification wasn’t constantly active since the combat arts of heavenly dao exhausted mental capacity, even though they didn’t drain Hongmeng qi. Lu Yun opened it once every one hundred kilometers to scan his immediate vicinity.","“Damn it, what are those things? Why won’t they die?!” Sounds of fierce fighting came from up ahead, most likely some of the cultivators that’d entered before him.","Three young men and one young woman that were all soul separation faced down a bloody being. It was wholly unafraid and emitted ghastly shrieks, pouncing on the four with a haze of bloody light. There was no rhyme or reason to its attacks. It barged about like a berserk wild beast, somehow suppressing the four cultivators.","The sword light from their weapons were all from lower dao rank blades. They were stronger than Ouyang Shengtian. Plainly, they were elites from Great Xia.","Their sword light bit into the bloody being and pulverized it to pieces. The chunks of flesh regathered the next second and reformed into the creature. It continued unabated, like nothing had happened, and charged the young woman who happened to be the weakest among them.","The young girl of eighteen years old wore a jade-green dress and randomly waved her weapon around. Her previously orderly attacks were dissolving into confusion, and it was obvious to see that she didn’t have much battle experience. While her cultivation was high, she was a flower in a greenhouse. All thought had flown out of her head as she faced the bloody creature with the rotting presence.","“Dodge it, little sis!” desperately roared a man with a luxurious hat.","The creature was so fast that the other three didn’t have time to react. The younger girl could already see a maw dripping with decrepit liquid coming for her.","Whoosh!","Crimson light flashed across her field of vision before the creature’s head exploded. Rotting flesh sprayed in all directions. Her green dress was a dao treasure as well; it raised a curtain of green light to protect its owner from the fallout.","Thump!","The ferocious creature fell to the ground, lacking its haze of bloody light and its head. The girl couldn’t help but bend over and throw up.","“Little sis!”","“Junior sister Ling!” The other three quickly flew over to support the girl.","“Many thanks to fellow daoist for your help! Ling Chu is extremely grateful!” The man in the luxurious hat quickly raised a cupped fist salute when he saw Lu Yun gracefully fly in on the back of his sword. The other two helping the girl also gave thanks when they walked over.","Four streams of strong goodwill flowed into the Seal of the Multitude.","“It was just a passing favor, think nothing of it.” Lu Yun waved them off with a smile.","“I am Ling Chu, this is my younger sister Ling Ling.” Ling Chu looked to be twenty-four, but was already latter soul separation. Naturally, Lu Yun could tell his true age was over fifty.","Ling Ling was truly only eighteen years old, the same as Lu Yun. She was already initial soul separation, hampered only by her lack of battle experience. She must spend her days sparring with others and had never experienced true combat.","Of the other two, the one in green dao robes was named Shi Jian and was the same cultivation as Ling Chu. The other young man looked the same age as Ling Ling. Handsome and dressed in long white robes, he was mid soul separation and named Song Yi.","What surprised Lu Yun was that all four were disciples of the Great Xia Dao Academy."]},{"number":2328,"title":"Chapter 2328: Chapter 2213.1: The Forefather of Ghost Zombies","paragraphs":["Chapter 2213.1: The Forefather of Ghost Zombies","The Dao Academy of Great Xia was where all of the dynasty’s geniuses gathered. They were nurtured with the full resources of the nation. Anyone who could enroll in its august halls was an unparalleled genius.","The four in front of him, however, were far from being hailed as geniuses. They were certainly accomplished and elites, but only Ling Ling could be considered a genius. Even so, she completely lacked the proper experience for her peerless potential.","Lu Yun showed none of those thoughts on his face and smiled, “Ah, so it’s fellow daoists from the Great Xia Dao Academy. I am Lu Yun, a cultivator of the Jade Ruins Realms.” He didn’t bother concealing his identity.","Startled, Ling Chu and the other four looked at each other. Wasn’t Jade Ruins Realms the weakest out of Great Xia’s three thousand worlds of cultivation? Where did a guy like him come from? The four of them had hacked at that bloody being for four hours! Although they pulverized it each time, it seemed to be undying and reassembled even when they cut it into a thousand pieces.","They’d also tried destroying its head, but it simply grew a new one each time.","“Ah...” Ling Chu looked at Lu Yun, the words on the tip of his tongue.","“There is a blood rune the width of a hair at the center of its forehead. Those things die when that rune is destroyed.” Lu Yun was very forthcoming with his knowledge.","The vicious spirits emanating bloody light were exceptionally brutal. They’d run rampant through the world of immortals and if it wasn’t for the five immortal emperors working in tandem to summon the Sword of Chaos, the world of immortals would’ve become their land.","Vicious spirits were what these bloody creatures were called, but Lu Yun somehow felt that they should be called ghost zombies. Well... they were a little different from the ghost zombies of his subconscious. The blood rune was their only weakness, but the ghost zombies to come had no weaknesses. The power of heaven and earth was their only bane.","These vicious spirits looked to be the forefather of the ghost zombies in the future, but the latter was more terrifying. Even so, these vicious spirits represented despair to Lu Yun. Each of them had once been a living being!","“Our thanks for fellow daoist’s enlightenment!” Ling Chu and the others immediately felt closer to Lu Yun when the latter spoke of this secret so easily.","Lu Yun could tell that not only were these four Dao Academy disciples, but they were also royal offspring. They were flowers nurtured in greenhouses—as strong as they were, their experience was far too lacking. They’d come to Jade Ruins Realm for tempering.","“Not at all!” Lu Yun chuckled.","“Fellow daoist, danger lurks around every corner in Immortal Burial Valley. You might run into danger if you travel alone. Why don’t you join us? It’s easier to look out for each other in a group,” Song Yi offered a friendly gesture. In their eyes, while Lu Yun knew how to kill the vicious spirits, he was still in a precarious situation since he was only initial soul projection.","Lu Yun wanted to decline, but hesitated when he looked at the four. Ultimately, he agreed to their offer.","Ling Chu, Ling Ling, and Shi Jian were very happy that he agreed. Their new companion could tell that the quartet wasn’t the sort to hide their thoughts and feelings beneath multiple layers.","......","Travel became a more boisterous affair when multiple people traveled together. Lu Yun hadn’t wanted to form a team at first because soul projection cultivators were too weak. Letting them follow him was just creating additional work for himself.","These four were different in that they were extremely powerful and only lacked experience. He was happy to make their acquaintance and gain powerful backers for the Lu Clan.","Ling Ling was a lively girl and flitted around Lu Yun like a little bird, asking him all manner of questions. When the others heard that the Lu Clan had a death feud with the Origin King, they frowned.","However, the frown wasn’t a precursor to estrangement. Song Yi gnashed his teeth, like he held a grudge against the Origin King as well.","Lu Yun didn’t ask further.","“Yan Guichi is utterly shameless!” Ling Ling waved her fists around after hearing Lu Yun’s story. He didn’t keep it from them since it was no secret. The four would easily find out once they returned.","Ling Chu didn’t say anything. He simply clapped their new companion’s shoulder.","......","Bloody vicious spirits thronged the hazy world, so the group proceeded with caution and didn’t travel too quickly. Lu Yun’s Eye of Nullification could only scan fifty kilometers around them. The vicious spirits were so swift that his art’s range was but a joke to them.","The third day.","“A massive amount of vicious spirits are coming this way from one hundred kilometers ahead!” An excited Song Yin flew back amid sword light. Being the fastest among them, he was the group’s scout as his spirit root was a mutated wind spirit root; it didn’t fall within the five elements. Mutated spirit roots were extremely rare and each one possessed unbounded potential.","Lu Yun looked in that direction with the Eye of Nullification.","“Damn it!” he cursed. There were twenty spirits and three combination cultivators flying in front of them, heading their way. The incoming trouble was less than fifty kilometers from the quintet.","Lu Yun would fear facing the vicious spirits by himself, but something was amiss if there were cultivators leading them.","“Prepare to fight!” Ling Chu summoned a scarlet lower dao rank flying sword. The other three brought out their weapons as well, ready to fight.","The three of them had killed a dozen spirits over the past three days in accordance with Lu Yun’s instructions. Morale was high and even the timid Ling Ling was eager to test her mettle.","Three resplendent rays of sword light flew over their head after one hundred breaths.","“Big brother, look, there’s some little fellows below!” A bald combination cultivator brightened when he caught sight of Lu Yun and the others. They’d sought cover and were ready to deal fatal blows to the vicious spirits when they passed.","“They can be our meat shields!” Their leader was a middle-aged man with a sinister expression. Dressed in dark-red robes, he slashed downward without second thought.","Bam!","Tremendous sword light split the earth open, shocking Ling Chu and his fellow disciples. They hadn’t thought that the fleeing cultivators would attack them!","As they hastily scrambled out from cover, Lu Yun seemed to be ready and grabbed the surprised Ling Ling.","“Haha, little guys, it’s up to you now!” The bald guy roared with laughter to see that they’d forced the cultivators into the open.","Vicious spirits possessed extremely weak consciousnesses and relied on their eyes. Preoccupied with chasing the three combination cultivators, they would’ve been hard pressed to see the five hidden in the ground.","Yet once the living appeared in front of them, they tirelessly gave chase. It was clear to see that the three combination cultivators had realized this, which was why they forced Lu Yun and the others out.","The Lu young master knew what they wished to do, but didn’t say anything because growth only came after personally experiencing certain things. Being descendents of Great Xia royalty, Ling Chu and the others had only ever enjoyed lives of smooth sailing.","“Damn it!” Shi Jian had a fiery temper and grit his teeth as he looked at the departing sword light.","“Ignore them, prepare for battle!” Ling Chu frowned tightly. With the five of them in the air, the twenty spirits immediately changed targets and pounced on them in a howling mess.","“Kill!” screamed Ling Chu, his scarlet sword of flame unleashing a long arc of sword light. It stabbed at the vicious spirit at the forefront.","Pfft!","The sword light cut the spirit’s head into perfect halves, destroying the blood rune at the center of its forehead.","Lu Yun, Shi Jian, Song Yi, and Ling Ling quickly joined the fray.","Pfft pfft pfft.","Five rays of varying sword splendor flashed through the sky, resulting in five headless bodies. However, that gave time for the remaining vicious spirits to surround them.","The spirits moved extremely quickly. While they didn’t know how to dodge, it was very hard to kill them in close quarters. The ones remaining were each initial combination, but their speed was beyond that level.","“Be careful!” Song Yi’s sword was a cerulean blade the width of a finger. Cerulean light blossomed from it and flung radiance in all directions like a scintillating firework.","Pfft pfft pfft!","The glorious sword light stabbed at the spirits’ foreheads. However, the shifting creatures were so close and flying in changing trajectories that when the light hit them, it didn’t destroy the blood rune.","“Don’t let them bite you, you’ll turn into a vicious spirit too!” Lu Yun frowned and bade light to erupt from Immortals Forbidden. It slashed at the closest spirit with a howl.","Pfft!","He pierced the spirit through with one stroke while the others hastily activated their defensive treasures.","Bam!","A vicious spirit appeared behind Shi Jian and clawed the sturdy barrier of light around him. Although the treasure remained intact, the young man was sent flying like a rubber ball.","Eight spirits immediately pounced on him.","“Damn it!” Blood trickled out of the corner of his mouth as he burned with hatred toward the three combination cultivators from earlier. If they hadn’t forced the quintet out from hiding, they wouldn’t be mired in such a difficult fight.","“Kill!” Shi Jian exploded with strength as his broadsword answered in kind, sectioning the spirits in the blink of an eye."]},{"number":2329,"title":"Chapter 2329: Chapter 2213.2: The Forefather of Ghost Zombies","paragraphs":["Chapter 2213.2: The Forefather of Ghost Zombies","Although the vicious spirits possessed the strength of combination cultivators, they lacked corresponding attack methods. They couldn’t bring the full strength of real combination cultivators to bear—some soul separation experts were able to beat them back at the first encounter.","What was terrifying about them was their undying body, inexhaustible strength, incomparable speed, and reckless fighting style. They could exhaust a cultivator to death through sheer attrition.","Once a vicious spirit broke through a cultivator’s defenses and injected their bloody light into the cultivator, that changed the human into another vicious spirit. That was the most horrifying of all.","Lu Yun’s group had run into just the lowest level of their kind.","Pfft pfft pfft!","Shi Jian promptly obliterated the eight vicious spirits, but they recombined with a flash of bloody light. However, that gave him enough breathing space to bisect the head of a spirit that was yet to regain movement after coming back together.","When the nearby Song Yi registered his friend’s actions, he brightened and flicked his thin sword around, forming a net of sword light and churning the three spirits in front of him to pieces. As they recombined, he took careful aim and slashed through three heads at nearly the same time.","“Finally got them all.” Ling Ling breathed out in relief after killing the last spirit.","“Thank goodness these things aren’t intelligent or we’d be in real trouble.” A smile appeared on Ling Chu’s face. Lacking intelligence made them the same as walking corpses, which meant they wouldn’t hide or dodge. The group could easily take out a spirit once they connected with a vital point.","“These are just the lowest specimens of their kind,” Lu Yun shook his head. “For some of the higher level ones, they live even when you connect with their blood rune.”","“Ah...” Ling Chu and Ling Ling looked at each other, not sure of what to say.","“What we’re facing are just newly infected cultivators, they’re not true vicious spirits.” Lu Yun simply wanted to remind them that if these spirits were so easy to manage, he wouldn’t need to be so wary of Immortal Burial Valley. The attitude they bore now would very likely lead to their demise.","“Old brother Lu, have you met these things before?” Shi Jian finally gave in to his inner curiosity.","“Yes,” Lu Yun nodded without further word. He’d met them in the world of immortals and there were even greater horrors in his sealed memories.","As inexperienced as Ling Chu and the others were, they were no fools. Everyone had their own secrets, they wouldn’t press for more.","“I finally understand why His Majesty sealed off this area with formations... It’s because of these guys,” Song Yi swallowed hard.","“There might be even stronger vicious spirits the deeper in we go, dare you go?” A smile appeared on Lu Yun’s face. After spending three days together and viewing these four through the lens of his three thousand lifetimes, he knew that they were worth befriending.","“What don’t we dare?” Ling Ling was the first to jump out and puff up her sizable chest. She’d grown much stronger over the trials of the past three days and was no longer a frantic mess when vicious spirits drew close.","“Didn’t we come here to temper ourselves?” Ling Chu smiled faintly. All three of them had benefited enormously from the three days of battle. While their cultivation hadn’t advanced, their battle experience was so much more than what they possessed before.","“Of course we must go,” answered the fiery Shi Jian. “Those three bastards may have already entered the valley. If I see them, I’m going to twist their heads off!”","Song Yi said nothing, merely continued to polish the thin sword in his hand.","“Alright then,” Lu Yun stood up and stretched.","They traveled much faster than before, encountering a denser concentration of vicious spirits the closer they drew to Immortal Burial Valley. Lu Yun discovered a massive group of more than five hundred at one point and quickly led the group around it.","Five hundred would drown them in a second and leave not even bone fragments behind.","......","The five finally reached the heart of the valley seven days after entering the formation array. It was as if a volcano—the ground protruded to form a small mountain three hundred meters tall. Dense clusters of innumerable vicious spirits gathered on the landmass, all glowing with a bloody hue.","They differed from the ones that the quintet met before in that the flesh beneath the bloody light was blood-red and exuded the pungent scent of decay. Blood-red eyes occupied two thirds of their faces. Hunched over, hands that’d turned into sharp claws dug into the cliff face while unblinking scarlet eyes scanned the premises.","“Ah...” Hidden in a corner, Ling Chu swallowed hard.","“That’s a real vicious spirit,” Lu Yun whispered with a quirk of his lips. Thank goodness they’re just vicious spirits and not ghost zombies... or it would be the start of real despair then.","Whoosh!","A vicious spirit on the cliff face suddenly streaked into a ray of body light and elicited a pained scream from the sky. A figure in gray fell to the ground—a cultivator in long gray robes. Bloody light quickly shimmered over him and covered his entire body. The dead cultivator then swayed to his feet and shuffled aimlessly around.","Ling Ling was pale with fright—though she’d heard Lu Yun say that vicious spirits were transformed from cultivators, it was another thing entirely to see it with her own eyes.","“Vicious spirits don’t have consciousnesses, but their senses are exceptionally keen and won’t be fooled by ordinary Invisibility Talismans.” Lu Yun narrowed his eyes. There were more than one thousand vicious spirits sprawled on the mountain less than three hundred meters tall. They wouldn’t be able to pass with their individual strength.","“That spirit had the strength of latter combination, but it killed a tribulation cultivator in a split second,” Song Yi swallowed hard.","“It was the tribulation cultivator who was careless. He was confident he couldn’t be detected—he wouldn’t have died in one pass otherwise.” Ling Chu pursed his lips and smiled ruefully. “But it’s not like we can handle these vicious spirits either.”","“Let’s go back!” Lu Yun waved them into a quiet retreat.","“Countless treasures litter Immortal Burial Valley. Many of the cultivators who entered first obtained heaven-defying treasures,” Song Yi raised. “I’m not willing to give up just like this.”","Those who entered first did obtain some treasures, but the subsequent appearance of vicious spirits in quick succession and unbridled slaughter turned some of the cultivators into them.","The Human Emperor had reacted quickly and directed the formation array over the spirits almost as soon as they appeared. It sealed off an area five thousand kilometers around the valley so that most cultivators didn’t know what’d happened inside.","The only news that made it out was that there was treasure to be had, which caused cultivators around the world to flock to the valley. All of the vicious spirits that the quintet had met along the way were formerly of those cultivators.","Lu Yun looked at Song Yi, reading urgency in the young man’s eyes.","“Don’t worry, we’ll help you!” Shi Jian patted his friend’s shoulder.","“Lu Yun, you always have a ton of ideas. Think of something.” Ling Ling ran over to Lu Yun and pulled on his arm.","Lu Yun smiled ruefully. The female cultivators of Darklake couldn’t run fast enough when they saw him. A young woman tugging on his arm was a first.","“Ling Ling!” Ling Chu hastily pulled the girl back when he saw. Although the four accepted Lu Yun as one of them, her actions overstepped the bounds of propriety.","Ling Ling shrank in on herself and quietly stuck out her tongue.","“We should disseminate the method to kill vicious spirits and collect everyone to destroy these ones together,” Lu Yun declared.","“Huh?” Shi Jian couldn’t wrap his mind around it. “But the method to kill vicious spirits...”","“Ole brother Lu is right!” Ling Chu nodded. “These spirits are too dangerous and will be a cataclysm upon Jade Ruins Realm and even Great Xia if they were to break out of here. It will be much safer once cultivators know how to kill them.”","Lu Yun nodded. He was no saint, but he had a clear sense of priorities. Knowledge like this could not be kept to oneself. The world of immortals had been devastated by these spirits back in the day—such scenes of horror were still fresh in Lu Yun’s mind.","If a single one of them ran out and wasn’t killed in time, the entire world would become their paradise.","I wonder if the others will call me a saint if they learn of this.","“We can share the method, but it can’t come from us,” he said after consideration.","“Why not?” Ling Ling didn’t understand.","“Because of the human heart,” he responded. Unbidden, the four thought of the three combination cultivators they’d encountered earlier.","Lu Yun hadn’t forgotten either what ultimately happened to the dao immortal who deduced how to kill the vicious spirits in the world of immortals. Far from becoming a hero, his nascent soul was refined alive, his memories stripped, and his soul scattered to the wind.","No one believed that he’d discovered the secret by accident and even if they did, they pretended not to. Human desire was endless and everyone wanted to know if there were any other secrets on the immortal.","Not even the immortal emperor had discovered it, so how had a dao immortal achieved it? To do so was not his good fortune, but his greatest disaster.","Lu Yun’s original goal in accompanying the four was to observe them. If any of them displayed anything out of the ordinary, he would kill them without hesitation. He was not a good guy, and with his experience and instincts, he knew that these four were worthy of being roped in."]},{"number":2330,"title":"Chapter 2330: Chapter 2214.1: Ingrate","paragraphs":["Chapter 2214.1: Ingrate","Ling Chu and Song Yi looked at each other.","“I, Ling Chu, do solemnly swear that if I reveal anything regarding ole brother Lu, I will die in a myriad of disasters and never find redemption!” Ling Chu stuck out his right hand and raised it to the sky.","“I, Song Yi, also do solemnly swear that I will not reveal anything about ole brother Lu to others, I will die to a myriad of disasters and my soul will scatter upon the wind!” Song Yi made his vow soon after.","Startled, Shi Jian and Ling Ling looked at the two, completely failing to understand what was taking place. Shi Jian was a bit quicker on the uptake and grasped the situation after momentary hesitation. He also raised his hand to swear upon the heavens.","Ling Ling was more simpleminded and thought less about the twists and turns of human nature. She still didn’t understand after seeing the three make their vows, but she was no fool. Seeing that her companions had promised so solemnly, she quickly joined them as well.","“Brother? Lu Yun? What’s going on here?” she asked with confusion when she finished.","The consequences of cultivators violating their oath would always take place due to the existence of the heavenly dao. Therefore, they would not make such vows if they had any other options available.","“Ole brother Lu Yun is most generous to tell us the secrets of the vicious spirits, how can we ever run the risk of dragging him into danger?” Ling Chu breathed out more easily after he made his promise. After all, they’d only known Lu Yun for a few days and their mutual trust was yet to reach the level of placing their lives in each other’s hands. Openly swearing in front of him was the best method.","Otherwise, not even Ling Chu could be certain that he wouldn’t betray Lu Yun after they returned to Great Xia.","“His Majesty the Human Emperor descended upon the Jade Ruins Realm with the Sword of Chaos to personally eliminate most of the vicious spirits in Immortal Burial Valley. Plainly, this isn’t the first time that these beings have appeared,” Ling Chu sighed. “If HIs Majesty knows about them, then these vicious spirits must certainly be a plague elsewhere.”","“But not a single cultivator within the valley’s range knows how to destroy them. We can only seal them in place with the formation array. Even His Majesty kills them strictly through absolute domination,” Song Yi added. “Ole brother Lu teaches us a way to kill them that not even His Majesty knows. What do you think will happen when other people find out that the cultivator who knows the weakness of the vicious spirits is only at soul projection?”","Shi Jian and Ling Ling looked at each other, shaking their heads at the same time.","“Our brother certainly bears some secrets!” Ling Chu chuckled ruefully. “The blood rune at the center of their forehead is smaller than a wisp of hair. Who would pay attention to it if they didn’t know if it beforehand? The vicious spirits can only be eliminated when it is fully destroyed.”","Shi Jian and Ling Ling blinked.","“This is all too complicated. Matters of the mind are not to my liking,” Shi Jian shook his head.","“Brother, are you saying...” As simpleminded as Ling Ling was, she was very smart and understood the ramifications of the supposition.","Destroying the blood rune was the only way to kill the vicious spirit. It would be reborn if a single strand was left. However, it fully vanished once the spirit was gone, so who would know that there’d once been a rune the width of a hair at the center of the dead spirit’s forehead?","Whoever knew of this secret would certainly be no ordinary person. It was one thing if they were a powerful immortal, but if they were a weak soul projection cultivator? Anyone would think that there was much more than met the eye.","Lu Yun would be a hero on the surface after the secret was made public, but who knew how many heavyweights would lay their eyes on him from the shadows?","Ling Ling nodded.","Shi Jian scratched his head and smiled honestly, “Although I don’t understand what’s going on, I promise I’ll never speak of it.”","“Ole brother Lu, you must have a plan since you’ve spoken of this, right?” Song Yi smiled at Lu Yun.","“I just need to change my appearance and aura.” Lu Yun was fully at ease after the four made their oaths and was completely candid with them. “And then I’ll die.”","“Um... what? That simple?” Shi Jian blinked.","“How complicated do you want it to be?” Lu Yun snorted. “Three days. Don’t wait for me if I’m not back in three days.” He raised sword light and vanished from their view.","“Be careful!” Ling Chu couldn’t help but call out as he watched Lu Yun’s departing figure.","......","Immortal Burial Valley ran ten thousand kilometers across with the place of burial at its center. Deep grooves crisscrossed throughout after the Human Emperor battled the vicious spirits. Instead of the vast plains it once was, there were many ridges and canyons undulating over the terrain.","Lu Yun brought Immortals Forbidden down in a random canyon and slapped a jade talisman onto himself. His aura immediately changed into something wholly different and he grew much taller. Previously two meters tall, he was now more than three and his skinny body began filling out.","A hulking man with a curly mustache and muscles that rivaled Zhao Chenguang appeared a few breaths later. The ripples of initial soul projection that originally ran through his aura were now that of peak awakened realm.","His fire spirit root was also a wood spirit root. While the ripples of cultivation could be modified, one’s innate spirit root could not be altered. After Lu Yun obtained the sapling of the Builder Tree, his spirit root morphed from a singular fire attribute to dual fire and wood.","The jade talisman he used was a Metamorphosis Talisman, one more useful than a Transformation Talisman. It would take the arrival of an immortal to see through Lu Yun’s true form.","Thank goodness that all of the heavenly book’s rules were gathered here in a zone that was off limits to immortals. Any that tried to enter was executed by the treasure. This was a world of cultivation. If an immortal turned into a vicious spirit and escaped, it would bring the end of the world.","After completing his preparations, Lu Yun took out a wood attribute lower dao rank flying sword and flew in another direction. The current Lu Clan did not lack for dao weapons.","......","The Eye of Nullification swept an area fifty kilometers around him. He located a group of cultivations twenty-five kilometers to the southwest that was fighting a large collection of vicious spirits.","There were roughly thirty cultivators, yet they faced a hundred vicious spirits. The spirits were newly assimilated, but they possessed the same undying bodies.","Surrounded by the spirits, there was nowhere for the cultivators to run. If it wasn’t for four awakened powerhouses protecting them, they would’ve been torn to pieces long ago. Even so, deep-seated anguish tinged their fear. Many of the spirits attacking them were once their companions.","“Master, what do we do?” A teary twenty-five year old woman flung out a red ribbon and snarled it around a vicious spirit. However, she was so weak at latter soul projection that she couldn’t hold it in place.","Her treasure was swiftly torn to pieces and the vicious spirit moved in for the kill. Despair flashed through her eyes as a haze of bloody light with a pungent scent of decay loomed over her.","Whoosh!","Jade-green light flashed by as ninety meters of sword light stabbed down from the sky, slicing the vicious spirit’s head open.","And then, the terrifying entity sagged to the ground without getting up again.","“What...”","A vicious spirit was dead from the sudden attack. Everyone froze—weren’t these horrific things undying? How had they died so easily?","“What are you standing around for? Kill them!” came a rough shout. A bulky, coarse man wearing long black robes came flying in with a massive jade-green flying sword.","Whoosh whoosh whoosh!","He waved his sword around three times and exterminated another three vicious spirits with three scintillating rays of sword light.","“What’s happening?!” The four awakened cultivators looked askance at Lu Yun, but more so at his sword.","“Does his dao rank weapon have the ability to kill these bloody creatures?” Greed sparkled in the eyes of a man with black hair.","Dangers abounded in Immortal Burial Valley and these creatures were everywhere. A cultivator was assimilated in a single moment of carelessness. Having a treasure that could kill them would be the basis by which one could ensure safety in this place.","“There’s a blood rune in the center of their foreheads that’s as thick as a hair. You can kill them if you destroy it!” Lu Yun cursed inwardly—he’d saved a group of ingrates. He hadn’t received a wisp of goodwill after killing ten vicious spirits. Even Red Ribbon wasn’t the least bit thankful, despite looking at him with teary gratitude.","The thirty cultivators started when they heard his words, but the vicious spirits didn’t give them time to react. One of them broke through an initial soul separation’s defenses and grabbed him.","“Martial uncle, save me!” Fear rose on the young man’s face as a bloody light brewed from the depths of his eyes. Bloody radiance slowly enveloped him.","The faces of the four awakened cultivators sank."]},{"number":2331,"title":"Chapter 2331: Chapter 2214.2: Ingrate","paragraphs":["Chapter 2214.2: Ingrate","“What a bunch of fools.” Lu Yun could be certain that this group didn’t come from Great Xia or a highly ranked Jade Ruins empire. They came from another world. The cultivators of Great Xia, even the lowest ones, had much stronger mentalities than these fellows.","One of the four awakened cultivators was the first to react and hoisted his flying sword, stabbing it at the center of a spirit’s forehead.","Pfft!","The mid dao rank flying sword pierced it through, but the vicious spirit remained unbothered and continued shrieking. It brandished its claws and pounced on the awakened cultivator.","“Why didn’t it work?!” the powerhouse screamed with fury. He propelled his sword and sliced the vicious spirit to bits, but it swiftly reassembled again. “Give me your flying sword!”","Being peak latter awakened, the powerhouse flung himself at Lu Yun after he slashed the spirit apart. His silver sword light formed a straight line that made for Lu Yun’s head, wanting to slice the young man into two.","“Damn it, I really did save a bunch of ingrates!” Lu Yun swore. He’d planned on using the vicious spirits’ secret to collect some goodwill. At his stage of soul projection, he found that he could use goodwill to enhance his cultivation, manipulate the Seal of the Multitude, and also improve the heavenly dao combat arts.","Too much goodwill was needed for the latter, however. The tiny bit he’d collected before was far from enough.","But he’d met a bunch of blithering idiots! They didn’t focus on how to kill the enemy, but turned their swords on their own kind instead! Lu Yun highly regretted saving them.","The awakened cultivator’s strike had hit the blood rune, but hadn’t fully destroyed it. Leaving even a squiggle behind permitted it to be reborn.","All of the hairs on Lu Yun’s body stood on end to see such a powerhouse locked onto him. He wasn’t Terra Demon, he had no ability to face a peak awakened heavyweight!","Hongmeng qi churned inside of him as the sword light reached him and he disappeared.","“Die!” Lu Yun reappeared behind the powerhouse, silver light flashing past his fingertip and piercing through the latter’s defensive treasure.","There was no match for the sharpness of connate gang metal. As long as he didn’t attack an immortal rank defensive treasure, there was nothing that he couldn’t penetrate in his current state.","The awakened heavyweight hadn’t imagined that someone just in front of him would suddenly shift behind him.","Pfft!","He felt his dantian ache and silver radiance shoot out from it. The powerhouse in a towering fury sagged weakly to the ground. Lu Yun’s jade-green sword brilliance exploded once more and chopped him to pieces before a mouthful of fire burned the man to ashes. A cultivator’s body had to be destroyed or they would still turn into a vicious spirit if polluted with blood light.","“Master!”","“Senior brother!”","“Martial uncle!” screamed the cultivators when they saw Lu Yun kill one of their own.","“The Yu Mountain Sect will pursue you to the ends of the world for killing our senior brother!” The other three awakened cultivators simultaneously abandoned the fight and about-faced for Lu Yun.","How could the remaining cultivators possibly defend themselves? Wails and shrieks rose and fell and Red Ribbon’s defenses were shattered. She was so weak that more vicious spirits pounced on her before she could finish turning. They ate her alive, leaving not a single bone fragment behind.","The others cried out with disbelief and some female cultivators dropped weakly to the ground. The vicious spirits also ate people?!","These cultivators were the young disciples of a major sect from another world. They were here to test and temper themselves and had never seen anything like this! In the absence of protection, they panicked and fled in all directions.","They might’ve stood a chance had they remained together and worked in tandem.","Pfft pfft pfft!","The clean skies immediately turned into a slaughterfield. Six vicious spirits attacked one cultivator at a time; no one was able to fight back, not even combination cultivators.","The spirits were too fast!","Blood spewed through the sky as the stronger ones were assimilated and the weaker became food.","“Bastard!!” The awakened powerhouses vented their spleen on Lu Yun to see their sect’s disciples fall and their attacks grew more furious.","Lu Yun smirked and didn’t bother exchanging further words with these people. He shifted several kilometers out with a few teleportation moves.","“The Yu Mountain Sect?” Lu Yun left after glancing at the three awkward cultivators surrounded by vicious spirits. He didn’t think much of what’d just occurred—his three thousand lifetimes had brought so many experiences to him that he was long since numb to it all. If the three died, they well deserved it.","They had a chance of living if they could think through what he’d said and grasp the method to kill the vicious spirits. Unfortunately, they were predisposed to thinking that Lu Yun was able to kill the spirits only because of the treasure in his hand.","......","As more cultivators entered the formation array, so did the number of vicious spirits grow. Those newly entered were ill-prepared and swiftly turned into more vicious spirits when attacked. After Lu Yun left, he searched for a new target.","“Oh?” He raised a brow at two scintillating rays of stark white and blood red rising in the distance. Shooting for the horizon, they were as if two constantly moving pillars of light. There were more than five hundred vicious spirits gathered around them.","Gui Xie roared with laughter. His hair was stark white due to practicing the Immortal Canon of Life and Death; white light also enveloped his body. The Cosmic Flag fluttered and waved in his hand. While it was unable to communicate with the stars due to the formation array, the stark white light scythed through spirits.","Next to him, Bloodbath remained the same as he always was—long blood-red hair with long blood-red robes... He looked no different from the vicious spirits. No, Bloodbath was several times more formidable than the spirits.","What surprised Lu Yun was that Bloodbath had reached tribulation stage. He would be an awakened cultivator as soon as he weathered his tribulation!","Gui Xie and Bloodbath were like two killing machines, endlessly reaping the lives of the vicious spirits. The five hundred spirits were completely cleared out after two dozen breaths.","“I’m sure I’ll beat his brains out if I meet that empyrean immortal again!” A keen light shone in Bloodbath’s eyes.","Jadecliff’s ambush and subsequent hanging of him and Lu Xiaochi on a flagpole had become an internal demon. If he didn’t personally kill the immortal, he stood almost no chance of making it through his tribulation.","With the incredible increase in his cultivation and full comprehension of the profound meaning within the Canon of the Blood God, his battle strength was on par with a real immortal.","“Don’t worry, I’ve heard of that Empyrean Immortal Jadecliff. He’s as timid as a mouse and will never set foot outside Jade Ruins Realm. You’ll find him one day!” Gui Xie comforted.","“You two...” Disguised as a hulking man, Lu Yun approached the duo.","“Who are you?” Bloodbath dismissed the light around him and furrowed his blood-red brows. Gui Xie looked at Lu Yun as well. Although it’d been less than a month since the two ventured into the array, they’d long since grasped the true meaning behind all of their cultivation methods after repeated encounters with death. They’d also killed more than a few peak awakened powerhouses.","“I almost forgot that this is the perfect environment for the methods you guys cultivate.” Lu Yun smacked his forehead and returned the Metamorphosis Talisman into his hand with a flash of green light. His appearance and aura underwent drastic changes.","“Young... young master?” Gui Xie and Bloodbath gaped, their confidence crumbling before their eyes. How had they failed to see through a minor art of disguise?","The Immortal Canon of Life and Death absorbed the power of death from the vicious spirits to enhance Gui Xie’s strength. At the heart of things, the spirits were evolved from dead things. When that power disappeared, they were truly dead.","As for the Canon of the Blood God, the bloody light around the vicious spirits was the most optimal nutrient for Bloodbath.","Due to the presence of heavenly dao in the world of cultivation, all things had a chance of survival and one sliver of weakness. Thus, the vicious spirits here had their counters and weaknesses. Apart from the blood rune in the center of their forehead, the Canon of the Blood God could also temporarily restrain them.","“Well done.” Lu Yun was very satisfied with Bloodbath and Gui Xie.","“You praise us too highly, young master. It’s all thanks to young master’s cultivation method. The two of us wouldn’t have these accomplishments otherwise!” Gui Xie responded sincerely.","He was just a wandering cultivator and practiced the lowliest cultivation method. If it wasn’t for Lu Yun giving him the Immortal Canon of Life and Death, he would still be an ordinary combination cultivator even now. Meanwhile, Bloodbath would still be tormented by a fragment of the Canon of the Blood God.","“Alright, be careful. In here, cultivators are much more frightening than the vicious spirits,” Lu Yun reminded solemnly.","“We understand!” Bloodbath nodded. They were no fools—it would be very dangerous if word got out that they could enhance their cultivation through killing vicious spirits. If Lu Yun hadn’t dismissed his disguise earlier, they would’ve attacked the young man."]},{"number":2332,"title":"Chapter 2332: Chapter 2215.1: Where Immortals Are Buried","paragraphs":["Chapter 2215.1: Where Immortals Are Buried","Bloodbath and Gui Xie had kept a low profile for the past month. They couldn’t resist the urge to explode with power when they fully comprehended their methods earlier, which was what drew Lu Yun to them.","After the three discussed their next steps, Lu Yun returned to the form of the hulking man and left by himself. Bloodbath and Gui Xie headed for the center of the array, toward the entrance of the place of burial.","Lu Yun traveled through the valley of ten thousand kilometers over the next three days, sharing the way to kill vicious spirits and collecting plenty of goodwill in return. Not all of the cultivators were similar to the ingrates that he met first. There were still many with kindness in their hearts.","The entire valley knew of the method after three days. Sadly, the hero who shared it with everyone ran into a thousand vicious spirits in a massive battle. Unwilling to become one himself, he self-detonated when it was obvious that he would lose.","......","“I’m finally free.” Lu Yun was back to his original appearance and raised a ray of crimson sword light to reconvene with Ling Chu and the others.","“Huh?” When he reached the designated place, he found that the quartet was gone. Traces of fighting were evident on the scene—something had happened during these three days. Instead of lingering, Lu Yun changed course for the entrance to the heart of Immortal Burial Valley.","There were now more than one hundred thousand cultivators within the formation array, a number that only continued to grow. Since everyone knew how to kill vicious spirits, they cut through the valley and headed for the entrance.","They didn’t all arrive at the same time; there were more than ten thousand cultivators gathered on site. The weakest among them was soul separation, while the strongest was peak awakened.","Several dozen awakened powerhouses stood in the air, facing off against the terrifying spirits on the cliff face. Beneath them, ten thousand cultivators huddled into various groups and tensed for action.","Vanguards had gone out to plumb the capabilities of the vicious spirits at the entrance. Domineering in strength, they far eclipsed the spirits roving through other parts of the valley. Each of the ones here were the equivalent of initial awakened stage and their speed reached the limits of cultivator limits. Ordinary awakened powerhouse couldn’t keep pace at all.","“Who would’ve thought that there’d be someone here to easily dispatch the vicious spirits. That was a pleasant surprise.” A young man of roughly nineteen years old stood at the head of nearly fifty awakened powerhouses in the sky. A faint smile hung on his face. He was only initial awakened stage, but he was their leader.","“It’s a pity he died,” sighed a middle-aged man behind him.","“Died?” The young man’s smile deepened with meaning. “I certainly hope he did.”","A contemplative expression appeared on the rest of the group’s face as they grasped the young man’s meaning.","“Sir, when do we begin?” asked the middle-aged man.","“Let’s wait a bit longer, there’s not enough cannon fodder yet.” The young man waved to the group behind him, signaling for them to stand down. “How sad that Lu Tianling didn’t come. If he was here, these spirits wouldn’t make him break a sweat.”","“Lu Tianling offended the Origin King and would already be dead if it wasn’t for the Fengxian King’s protection. How would he dare come here?” snorted the middle-aged man.","“The Origin King? If it wasn’t for affairs back in the day, the seat vacated by the Argent King would belong to the Lus,” the young man sneered. “Yan Guichi’s scheme against the Argent King caused the king’s death. Although the heavenly book made him a titled king, the other seven do not accept him. Regardless, history is written by the victors. It is testament to Yan Guichi’s strength that he can become a titled king.”","“Sir, do you mean to...” The middle-aged man blinked.","“What does the death feud between the Lus and Yan Guichi have to do with me? It is the Fengxian King on one side and the Origin King on the other. They are both titled kings as hailed by the heavenly book. I do not need to insert myself between them.” The young man curled his lip.","“The Fengxian King?” blinked the middle-aged man. “Didn’t the Fengxian King already return the favor that he owed Lu Tianling?”","“Return the favor?” the young man snorted with laughter. “The Fengxian King owes far more than that. He laid down a clever plan and sent his granddaughter to this world. Sadly for him, the Lu good-for-nothing didn’t take a liking to her.”","Pausing, the middle-aged man said nothing else. The young man’s identity was very special. If it wasn’t for immortals being forbidden in the formation array, a mere latter awakened cultivator such as he wouldn’t have the right to stand next to the young man.","“Lu Tianling is so shrewd and deliberate that he raised such a faction after a mere two hundred years in a low ranked world of cultivation that lacked ambient qi and resources. He might be able to come for the Origin King Estate if he had another thousand years or two,” the young man waxed eloquent.","While Lu Tianling’s Azure Dragons, Vermilion Birds, White Tigers, and Black Tortoises weren’t much to Great Xia, one had to know that this was a world of cultivation. Even ninth rank empires would require more than a thousand years to raise such a batch of elites. Not to mention, Lu Tianling had built everything from scratch in a third rank empire.","What impressed the young man the most was Lu Tianling’s fortitude. He bided his time when people bullied him to his face and obscured the Origin Sect’s vision by scrapping with the ants of Darklake Empire that were its great families.","Of course, much of this had to do with the Fengxian King’s care and support from the shadows.","......","Lu Yun saw Bloodbath and Gui Xie again when he opened the Eye of Nullification. The two had their arms slung around each other and were thick as thieves with some other tribulation powerhouses. They’d become the leaders of a clique.","“Have Ling Chu and the others run into some trouble?” Lu Yun furrowed his brow. He still didn’t see signs of Ling Chu and the others even here. His eye for people wouldn’t be wrong; he’d spoken candidly with them because he understood their character. If there was no trace of them to be found here, that meant they’d encountered an accident.","Just as worry rose in his heart, Ling Chu and the others flew in from another direction. As bedraggled as they were, they were inordinately excited, like they’d just achieved something of great satisfaction.","“Haha, Brother Lu!” Shi Jian roared with laughter when he saw Lu Yun. “We finally slaughtered those three sons of bitches! Damn that feels good!”","Deeply tanned muscles peeked through his ripped robes while excitement danced in his eyes.","Lu Yun understood what’d happened with a quick turn of his thoughts. The four had likely encountered the three combination cultivators that’d previously moved against them and killed them.","Those three were likely from another world of cultivation. Being elites of Great Xia, Ling Chu and the others could kill them even though their cultivation levels were a step lower.","“What a pity that one of their nascent souls escaped.” Concern shone out of Ling Chu’s eyes.","“Don’t worry, it’s just a nascent soul. It won’t amount to much.” A rare smile appeared on the aloof Song Yi’s face.","After a round of pleasantries, the five landed on the ground.","......","Cultivators streamed to the area until there were more than twenty thousand of them. The vicious spirits at the entrance finally started agitating, sweeping their scarlet eyes across the assembly, but not going on the attack.","They seemed to be protecting something and prevented cultivators from entering the burial place proper.","“There’s enough people, we can do it now.” The young man in the air flung a sword at the entrance.","Kaboom!","Even Lu Yun jumped with surprise at the attack without forewarning. It was like a hornet’s nest had been kicked over as the vicious spirits shrieked and boiled over the mountain peak. The entrance was leveled and one thousand vicious spirits blurred into blood-red shadows that pounced on the cultivators.","“Let’s go!” The aloof young man retrieved his flying sword and darted for the entrance. The fifty awakened cultivators behind him were close on his heels. The situation on the ground was an absolute mess. He only wanted to use those beneath him as cannon fodder and distraction, so that he and his entourage could enter the burial place proper.","“Ignore the vicious spirits, we head in as well!” Five jade talismans appeared in Lu Yun’s hands and he slapped them onto his group. Everyone’s presence and ripples of power were immediately concealed.","“My jade talismans won’t fool the spirits, but we can get by for now because there’s so many people around us. It’s each to their own luck after we go inside!” Lu Yun was already gone.","Ling Chu and the others naturally didn’t hesitate. They might’ve wanted to discuss things if the situation had been the same as it was four days ago, but after multiple encounters with life and death, they’d reached an unspoken accord in situations like these.","......","One thousand vicious spirits barreled toward the cultivators in streaks of blood-red light. Those who didn’t react in time became their victims. Bloody light rose from the horde of cultivators as more and more were turned into spirits, but even more were those who didn’t care and rushed for the entrance as well."]},{"number":2333,"title":"Chapter 2333: Chapter 2215.2: Where Immortals Are Buried","paragraphs":["Chapter 2215.2: Where Immortals Are Buried","Immortal Burial Valley was confirmed by the Human Emperor to contain more treasures than the Celestial Realm Battlefront. There were barely any left in the latter after countless eons of excavation.","As maddened as the cultivators were, the vicious spirits were ten times more berserk. Bloody light streaked by, ripping through cultivators in their way. Not even awakened cultivators could withstand the spirits.","Thankfully, there were only one thousand spirits. While they wished to stop all of the cultivators, many out of the twenty thousand still made it inside. Of course, even more were those who were assimilated by the vicious spirits.","The new converts weren’t as savage as the spirits with blood-red skin. In the blink of an eye, more than five thousand cultivators were transformed into attacking their own kind.","......","Lu Yun’s body slowly manifested inside the place of burial.","“So this is what’s inside?” He assessed the surroundings with the Eye of Nullification.","The heart of Immortal Burial Valley was a massive space one hundred kilometers wide. Broken slabs and cliff faces could be seen everywhere, as if a great battle had once taken place here.","Countless vicious spirits dwelled here before, but the Human Emperor had cleansed the place with the Sword of Chaos. The few that remained must have been left behind on purpose.","Lu Yun wasn’t the first one inside—a dozen cultivators beat him to the punch. Everyone split up as soon as they made it in and went off in search of their own fortune.","Ling Chu, Ling Ling, Song Yi, and Shi Jian successfully found their way inside. They remained in a group and set off in a certain direction.","Lu Yun was in no hurry. This place seemed much more complicated than he’d imagined.","“Where did the pills and treasures erupting from the valley come from?” He frowned and swept the Eye of Nullification over the place again and again, wanting to find some clues.","This place formed its own void, but it wasn’t a seed storage formation. It was a seed storage locale, a true minor world much more sophisticated than any seed storage.","He’d once owned such a place in his three thousand lifetimes—his residence, the Northern Sky Palace.","As more cultivators entered and some followed by some vicious spirits, Lu Yun chose a certain direction and flew away.","“If I’m seeing things correctly, this used to be a cluster of palaces. Everything’s been destroyed though. ...eh?” He halted in front of a massive palace. It, too, had been destroyed by massive external force and the protective restriction outside it laid in tattered pieces.","A dozen cultivators attacked the faltering restriction.","“A soul projection cultivator? How lucky you are!” Contempt curved the lips of a combination cultivator. “You, come here!” He pointed imperiously at Lu Yun. “There’s a gap there, go inside and see what’s there!”","The young man followed his finger and saw a gap one meter wide and two meters tall. There was a pool of blood outside of it and some fragments of a body. It would seem that someone had already tried entering, but had been churned to pieces by the restriction.","Golden light flashed through Lu Yun’s eyes, clearly identifying that apart from some ruins, there was nothing else inside the palace. It was empty.","“Hmph,” he snorted and circled around, wanting to fly elsewhere.","“Didn’t you hear him, kid?!” An initial soul separation cultivator stood in front of him and spat at the young man.","Lu Yun couldn’t be bothered. He answered with a flash from Immortals Forbidden.","The soul separation cultivator didn’t have time to react before the stroke cut his body into two. A pale-golden nascent soul was smashed to pieces as soon as it revealed itself.","“You’re weaker than Ouyang Shengtian, so how dare you strut around in front of this young master?” Lu Yun curled his lip.","While Ouyang Shengtian was also initial soul separation, he possessed the full experience of a Great Xia wandering cultivator. His true battle strength was no less than peak latter soul separation.","If Lu Yun could defeat even Ouyang Shengtian, he naturally thought nothing of an initial soul separation opponent.","The cultivators gathered around the palace shuddered. Not even a combination cultivator could slay an initial soul separation cultivation in one second! Everyone watched Lu Yun leave; no one dared step in his way.","“Wauuuuugh!” A piercing shriek entered Lu Yun’s ears not long after he left the group. A scarlet vicious spirit was surrounded by a group of cultivators.","“So there are indeed vicious spirits here!” Lu Yun remained hidden in the dark. Those attacking the vicious spirit were quite strong—a sign they came from Great Xia. It was no trouble for them to take down the spirit.","Just as he was about to back away, brilliant purple splendor brewed beneath his feet and a fragrant pill fragrance burrowed into his nose.","“Seventh rank immortal pill, the Unselfish Hateless Pill!” Lu Yun brightened and grabbed the purple ray of brilliance. An immortal pill of purple and gold appeared in his hand.","The Unselfish Hateless Pill was a paramount treasure amongst seventh rank pills. Whether immortal or cultivator, anyone who took it would advance one major stage in cultivation.","True immortals who fully refined it would immediately break through to august immortal. The pill’s effects were gentle and mild. Despite being a seventh rank immortal pill, it was one that even cultivators could endure.","However, it was very complicated to refine this precious pill. Ordinary cultivators who were fortunate enough to obtain one usually chose to take it after reaching immortality.","“An immortal pill!”","“An upper rank immortal pill!” The cultivators mobbing the vicious spirit instantly dropped their quarry and rushed for Lu Yun. When the spirit lost its target, it also came in howling pursuit.","“Tsk tsk tsk.” Lu Yun chuckled and turned away.","The seven cultivators were all combination stage. Since they came from Great Xia, they were heads and shoulders above the country bumpkins of the worlds of cultivation.","Lu Yun was just initial soul projection and had a chance of triumphing over others from worlds of cultivation. Against Great Xia cultivators, however, he didn’t wish to give rise to any other problems. He raised a ray of sword light without any hesitation and fled for the inner depths of the place of burial.","The seven gave furious chase since the young man had taken the immortal pill.","“So fast!” Their leader was a woman in a red silk dress. Other thoughts began to cross her mind when she saw an initial soul projection match them in speed.","“Big sis, this person’s probably from the Great Xia Dao Academy. We can’t afford to provoke him!” said a much younger girl behind her who was dressed in the same fashion.","The others began to slow down, but reluctance shone in their eyes.","“This is Immortal Burial Valley—even Dao Academy disciples might possibly die here. Who’ll know that we’re the ones who killed him?” complained an initial combination man.","The others wavered upon hearing him and looked at the woman in the red silk dress.","“We chase!” She set her jaw. “That immortal pill is obviously a high level immortal pill. If we get it, we’ll soar to the heavens and not have to worry about our tribulations if we have sufficient cultivation materials!”","The seven were siblings and three were peak combination stage. They weren’t confident enough in their abilities to set foot into tribulation stage—that was a unique cultivation realm. There, cultivators needed to be constantly on guard against a heavenly tribulation. Anyone in this stage needed to endure three total tribulations before being deemed as successfully passing the test. Those who failed were scattered upon the wind.","Awakened stage was the beginning of a transformation. The consciousness transformed into an immortal consciousness, the nascent soul into an immortal soul, and true origin into immortal origin.","After those three steps came the immortal tribulation. When one transformed one’s body into an immortal body through the tribulation, that completed the process and left the cultivator as an empyrean immortal.","Tribulation stage was the most dangerous for cultivators as the immortal tribulation was more like a heavenly favor bestowed upon cultivators. Tribulation stage was entirely a trial of death.","For peak geniuses such as Gui Xie and Bloodbath, tribulation stage was further trial and tempering. They were not afraid of it and naturally entered tribulation stage once they reached a sufficient cultivation level.","In worlds of cultivation, cultivators who survived a heavenly tribulation were one in a million. Even the more humble of cultivators in Great Xia ran a high risk of dying if they faced a tribulation.","“After him!” Sword light expanded a hundred meters long once the seven received approval from their elder sister; they were more than twice as fast compared to before.","“Obtaining an immortal pill and exchanging it for resources will ensure that big sis makes it past tribulation stage. When she’s an immortal, that’s hope for us all!” murmured an honest-looking man among the seven as he thought rapidly about the future.","“Those seven are surprisingly annoying.” Lu Yun flicked a glance behind him and frowned, he didn’t want to be entangled with these people. Others would sense something amiss if the situation dragged on and he’d be in great trouble if more joined the chase.","Thus, he deployed the Nine Forms of the Cloud Dragon and transformed into various images, vanishing in the blink of an eye.","The siblings’ jaws dropped when Lu Yun disappeared in front of their eyes."]},{"number":2334,"title":"Chapter 2334: Chapter 2216.1: Refining the Sword Pagoda, An Image of Heaven and Earth","paragraphs":["Chapter 2216.1: Refining the Sword Pagoda, An Image of Heaven and Earth","Lu Yun deployed the Nine Forms of the Cloud Dragon and not Teleportation. The latter was his ultimate ace and would create enormous threats for himself if others saw it. He wouldn’t use it unless his back was against a wall.","After shaking off the seven, Lu Yun heaved a long sigh of relief.","“Only damaged pills and treasures resulted from the previous eruptions. Who would’ve thought that there’d be a complete immortal pill to be found!” Lu Yun’s eyebrows raised as he studied the Unselfish Hateless Pill in his hand.","Seventh rank pills such as these had been extraordinarily precious back in the world of immortals of old. If this one in particular wasn’t limited to those beneath august immortal, it would definitively surpass ninth rank immortal pills.","At the same time, Lu Yun never encountered this pill in any other world apart from the world of immortals. Plainly, it was a local speciality.","He didn’t give that too much thought since Empress Myrtlestar’s Cosmic Flag had already appeared. It wasn’t that shocking that an Unselfish Hateless Pill would come from Immortal Burial Valley.","He placed the pill—glowing with a purple haze—in front of his nose and opened the Eye of Nullification, sighing after his observations.","“It won’t be that easy to discern the recipe for this pill,” Lu Yun shook his head. It was more pressing to raise his cultivation level. Without absolute strength in this place, death was a very possible conclusion.","Since he’d already made a careful study of the pill, all he needed was some time to experiment after his return. He’d find the right recipe and process one day.","In the same vein, it wasn’t an easy task to create an immortal pill. When he refined three Shennong Life Returning Pills, he’d relied heavily on the Shennong Grass’ innate attributes. Without it, he would never craft an immortal pill.","He took a look around and located a secluded spot, taking out some spirit stones to set up a maze formation.","“I wonder if this Unselfish Hateless Pill can help my cultivation take a leap forward.” Lu Yun took a deep breath and swallowed it.","It transformed into a current of purple and gold as soon as it entered his mouth and rushed into his stomach. Vast medicinal power exploded in his body and traveled to his limbs. His form took on the hue of the pill as the nascent soul in his dantian opened its eyes. Two rays of lightning shot out from it while it formed hand seals, devouring the ponderous medicine effects.","As vast as the Unselfish Hateless Pill’s energy was, it was unusually gentle and didn’t cause any damage to his body. The nascent soul directed medicinal power to continuously meld with Hongmeng qi and enhance the qi’s strength.","The Nine Chapters of Dao operated furiously, breaking through Lu Yun’s current level of limitation.","“Reincarnation Grass...","“Root of Heaven and Earth...","“Myriad Tribulation Flower...","“Unselfish Springwater...","“The inner core of the scarlet ape divine beast...”","Five ingredients appeared in Lu Yun’s mind—immortal ingredients that were the components of the Unselfish Hateless Pill. While they weren’t part of the ten heavenly or thirty-six earthly treasures, they rivaled any of the earthly treasures.","Reincarnation Grass, Root of Heaven and Earth, and Myriad Tribulation Flower were easy enough. Lu Yun would be able to replicate their properties if given enough ingredients. But Unselfish Springwater and the inner core of the scarlet ape divine beast? There was nothing he could do about those.","Unselfish Springwater was a spring of spirit water in the world of immortals. It held the properties of cleansing the mind and purifying the heart. Erupting once every ten thousand years, it produced three hundred and sixty-five droplets at a time. Each droplet was extremely precious.","Lu Yun could not replicate the properties of the inner core of the scarlet ape divine beast either because inner cores were not spirit herbs or likewise ingredients. They formed when a divine beast absorbed the essence of heaven and earth and contained the beast’s essence and soul.","“No wonder there are so few Unselfish Hateless Pills around. Just the Unselfish Springwater and inner core of the scarlet ape alone are far more valuable than this pill,” Lu Yun chuckled ruefully.","Seeing that only three hundred and sixty-five droplets of the spring water emerged every ten thousand years, even the immortal emperor could only think wistfully about it. The inner core of the scarlet ape was no less valuable than that of a dragon’s. It was too priceless to be assessed for a marketplace.","Using these two items to refine a seventh rank immortal pill that could be taken only by those below august immortal? The immortal emperor wasn’t that wasteful.","Lu Yun gave up the notion of refining the Unselfish Hateless Pill when his thoughts traveled here and focused on the enormous medicinal power circulating within him.","......","Various secret zones opened throughout the burial place, the treasures within so startling and precious that it threw cultivators into a frenzy. However, they went hand-in-hand with danger and this burial place could easily become theirs as well. Vicious spirits, formidable restrictions, and unfathomable mysterious power continuously reaped their lives.","After seven days, every cultivator within the formation array had received word that the entrance was open. Increasing numbers of cultivators poured into the array as well. The one thousand vicious spirits standing guard had long been exterminated. There was nothing blocking the entrance anymore.","But new dangers were swift to arrive.","After one secret zone was completely plumbed, contingents of skeletal troops darted out of the air. Each of them was the equivalent of a combination cultivator and even more terrifying than the vicious spirits.","As strong as the vicious spirits were, they didn’t employ treasures. They had only their claws and teeth to rip at cultivators. The skeletal soldiers, however, wielded immortal weapons that left no room for escape for ordinary cultivators.","There were only five hundred of them, but that was sufficient to dominate most of the cultivators within the place of burial. Each time they killed someone, they swallowed their victim’s nascent soul to strengthen themselves.","......","Lu Yun finally refined most of the medicinal power within himself on the seventh day. HIs cultivation broke through to soul separation—the sixth turn of the Seeing Dao chapter!","“Combat art of heavenly dao—Split Shadow?” The young man blinked. The heavenly dao combat art he obtained this time was one that enabled the cultivator to split out a shadow with the same aura as the primary body. Bereft of any battle capabilities, it could only be used to bewilder the enemy.","“So it’s another combat art to run away...” he chuckled ruefully. This one didn’t seem to ring any bells, so he hadn’t seemed to know it before. Plainly, the heavenly dao was worried he’d die here and therefore sent him this combat art.","Split Shadow and Teleportation together were unparalleled arts for escape. He could first leave a shadow on the spot to confuse the enemy while he shifted to safety through Teleportation. The combination of both could be hailed as the Ultimate Arts of Escape.","At the same time, Lu Yun understood that if he utilized them properly, he would be able to kill those stronger than him like he was chopping through vegetables.","“My cultivation is now soul separation, it’s time to raise my strength.” Lu Yun took a deep breath and stayed in seclusion.","Soul separation meant the separation of the nascent soul and refinement of an image of heaven and earth. Far from being an abstract concept or simple manifestation of the nascent soul, this was a true refinement.","Cultivators at this stage chose a treasure to refine and make one with their nascent soul, so that their image became tangible and real. Ouyang Shengtian, for example, chose the lower dao rank spear that he wielded. Another option was to use a combat art. The true immortal that’d appeared in Dark City had used the Greedy Wolf Star combat art of the Greedy Wolf King.","The higher the level of weapon or combat art, the greater the cultivator’s potential would increase.","In the world of immortals, Lu Yun happened to refine the connate treasure Reincarnation Disk, an act which bequeathed upon him the potential to become an immortal emperor and ultimately, the High Lord of the Northern Sky.","“I could use the Cauldron of Heaven and Earth if the Hadal Bird didn’t take up residence in it. What a pity,” Lu Yun sighed. The cauldron possessed boundless potential and the Nineheavens Brahman Formation within was extremely powerful.","“I now have six combat arts of heavenly dao—Petrification, the Connate Great Dao of the Five Elements, Eye of Nullification, Size Manipulation, Teleportation, and Split Shadow. I can use the Connate Great Dao of the Five Elements as the basis for my image...”","He took a deep breath as he considered his choices. That was the greatest combat art he possessed and it was quite suited to become an image of heaven and earth. In comparison, the other five were rather useless for the task.","“Oh?” He paused when he was about to refine the Connate Great Dao of the Five Elements. “I seemed to have forgotten another heaven-defying item...”","A black sword pagoda silently hovered in his dantian, occupying the same level of importance as his nascent soul. His nascent soul was the core essence of dao as bestowed by the heavenly dao. That the sword pagoda was on the same level as it was testament to its might.","“Should I try to refine the sword pagoda? If I can’t, I can try the Builder Tree next...” Lu Yun licked his lips and formed hand seals. He somehow felt that the sword pagoda had something to do with him, that it wasn’t impossible to refine it into his nascent soul.","The gray nascent soul in his dantian abruptly disassembled into pure origin qi and surged toward the sword pagoda. The treasure seemed to be dead and didn’t resist; even the incomparably keen ray of sword qi remained motionless.","As Lu Yun’s origin qi thundered into it, the sword pagoda grew indistinct and became one with the nascent soul’s qi.","A nascent soul from the Nine Chapters of Dao was incredibly domineering. As mighty as the sword pagoda was, it was just a dead thing at the end of the day, a treasure. Lu Yun was well versed in refining treasures since he’d once claimed a connate treasure.","Whoosh!","Lu Yun’s mind trembled and he discovered a tenuous connection between his mind and the sword pagoda. His nascent soul solidified once more, this time with a shadow of a black pagoda around it.","His refinement was a success!"]},{"number":2335,"title":"Chapter 2335: Chapter 2216.2: Refining the Sword Pagoda, An Image of Heaven and Earth","paragraphs":["Chapter 2216.2: Refining the Sword Pagoda, An Image of Heaven and Earth","The sword pagoda’s core essence was much stronger than a connate treasure’s. At his current level of strength, Lu Yun was unable to fully refine it. After all, he’d claimed the Reincarnation Disk in the world of immortals only when he reached immortal overlord.","Right now, he merely communicated with the pagoda through his nascent soul and borrowed its strength. Although it was an insignificant portion of power for the sword pagoda, it was of tremendous help to Lu Yun.","“So the sealed version of myself did indeed prepare this sword pagoda for me!” Joy crossed his face. “Oof!”","The unexpected took place next. A domineering sword intent appeared in his mind and occupied his thoughts.","“The Nine Oscillations of the Heavenly Sword!” he murmured subconsciously. Ponderous sword intent gathered in his dantian and summoned all of Lu Yun’s Hongmeng qi to itself, forming a ray of gray sword qi.","The Nine Oscillations of the Heavenly Sword was the other sword method originally in the sword pagoda, and stronger than the Eighteen Cerulean Sword Dragons. However, it was still less than the Vast Dragon Seaturner.","Lu Yun had a hunch that if he were to obtain the Vast Dragon Seaturner, his sealed memories would break forth. That would be an utter disaster.","“To think that this kind of surprise would be in store after I refined the sword pagoda as my image of heaven and earth...”","He remained in seclusion and took out Immortals Forbidden. With his cultivation at initial soul separation, he could fully deploy the strength of a lower dao rank weapon. Thus, he wanted to reforge his weapon into that level.","Immortals Forbidden was crafted from paramount rank materials. He’d forced it into a spirit weapon through his methods and could raise it to dao rank anytime he wished to. Reaching to the southern void, Lu Yun grasped a ball of connate li fire.","The Cauldron of Heaven and Earth and the Hadal Bird remained in storage within the sword pagoda. Only connate li fire was needed for a lower dao rank weapon.","The task was complete after four hours and Lu Yun rose to his feet, removing the formation that he’d laid beforehand. It’d been seven days since he entered the place of burial. Danger walked side by side with opportunity during this time and many immortals had sought out fortune unique to them. In comparison, Lu Yun’s Unselfish Hateless Pill wasn’t much at all.","However, more cultivators had died here than anywhere else. He was besieged by a group of skeletal soldiers as soon as he walked out.","“Their white bones have a gold sheen and soulfire burns within their head...” Lu Yun jumped with shock when he saw the soldiers. This description indicated that the soldiers had been golden immortals when alive. Although they were the spirits of the dead now, they retained their golden immortal strength.","“That’s strange, what are dead spirits doing here? Shouldn’t they be in the underworld? But wait... although they’re manifestations of golden immortals, they’re ridiculously weak. Are they only the equivalent of awakened cultivators?” The young man’s pupils constricted sharply. The underworld... there was no Yellow Springs or kingdom of the underworld in this world...","“Immortal weapons!” He took a sharp breath when he noted the level of weapon that the soldiers wielded. Their core essence seemed to have been destroyed, leaving them as lower rank immortal weapons.","“My cross cannon needs some fuel. Although something’s sucked the core essence out of your bones, you’re the skeletons of bonafide golden immortals!” Lu Yun shifted forward and rushed the soldiers.","As he utilized the Nine Forms of the Cloud Dragons, he flickered in and out of sight among the soldiers. A skeleton’s soulfire was shattered everytime he appeared, its body and weapon taken in its demise.","“Someone’s challenging the skeletal soldiers!” The fight drew in some spectators.","“That young man is so strong! Those soldiers have swallowed countless nascent souls already and are awakened stage dead spirits. He’s... hacking through them like he’s chopping vegetables?” Stares of disbelief shot in the relevant direction.","“What a marvelous body method!” A young man in long amethyst robes and a gold crown in his hair watched raptly. “Although the dead are ferocious, they are without intelligence. The young man must know their weakness if he is able to kill them with one blow and it’s his incredible body method that enables him to do so!”","“It... seems to be the Nine Forms of the Cloud Dragons from eight thousand years ago, the legendary Slaughterless from the Celestial Realm Battlefront!” Some people next to him recognized Lu Yun’s method.","“Coming and going with utmost mystery in those nine movements... even immortals cannot make out his form. I must have the Nine Forms of the Cloud Dragons!” A keen light sparkled in the young man’s eyes.","......","Having spent one of his lives in the underworld, Lu Yun knew how to kill spirits of the dead. But given that he sensed a crowd gathering, he didn’t utilize the combat arts of heavenly dao, even though they would instantly eviscerate all of the skeletal soldiers.","He eliminated all five hundred after an hour and collected their skeletons and weapons.","“Please stay, fellow daoist!” Nearly one hundred cultivators flew out of the dark when he was about to leave and surrounded him.","“Fellow daoist, we have pursued those soldiers for many days and have decided ownership for these immortal weapons. Please return them to us,” said a merry peak awakened cultivator. He wore a green upper dao rank robe and stroked his white beard, the image of an otherworldly figure.","“And you guys? Are you here for the immortal weapons as well?” Lu Yun looked around him instead of answering.","“I want your body method.” The young man with a gold crown walked out. “This seat thinks nothing of those treasures.”","Anyone still alive after seven days and openly sauntering through the place of burial was the cream of the crop. Two dozen awakened cultivators stood in a battle formation behind the young man and were ready to pounce on Lu Yun any time.","Humm!","Immortals Forbidden flared with scintillating light so bright that the others had to avert their eyes.","“You want the treasures and my body method? Why don’t you try?” Lu Yun rose into the air with a cold smirk. Though he’d just entered soul separation and hadn’t had time to practice many combat arts, his strength and cultivation had taken a qualitative leap forward after refining the sword pagoda and learning the Nine Oscillations of the Heavenly Sword.","It was the perfect time to test himself on some opponents.","Thus, he’d showed off his prowess not to avoid trouble, but hoping that it would come for him and provide targets for practice.","He stood in the air with his long hair and white robes flowing elegantly, Immortals Forbidden so bright that no one could look upon it. Some cultivators couldn’t help but take a few steps back.","“How arrogant!” the young man barked with laughter. He summoned a cerulean blue longsword into his hand and commanded sword qi to soar out of it. It was an immortal weapon!","“Where did this bumpkin come from? You think you’re invincible after some fortuitous encounters! My young lord is the thirty-sixth son of Marquis Skycloud, one of the thirty-six marquises of Great Xia. Kneel and beg for mercy in front of His Grace!” roared an awakened cultivator behind the young man.","Seeing that the young man was the son of Marquis Skycloud, the elder who’d demanded the treasures quickly turned around with a cupped fist salute. He smiled fawningly, “Mosi Yuxiu was unaware of the young lord’s arrival. Please forgive me if I gave offense earlier!”","It was as if the young lord didn’t hear him.","Yun Shuige, the thirty-sixth son of Marquis Skycloud, was a preeminent genius in Great Xia. He was already peak awakened stage in his early thirties and his true origin fully transmuted to immortal origin. All he needed was for his immortal tribulation to arrive to complete his ascension to immortality.","He ranked among the top ten of the Great Xia younger generation and was known in the Dao Academy.","“The thirty-sixth son of Marquis Skycloud?” Lu Yun frowned. Marquis Skycloud was ranked among the upper half of the thirty-six marquises, his strength and faction unusually formidable. Most importantly was that he was steadfast friends with the Origin King.","He might’ve reconsidered his course of action if it was any other noble son.","“The son of a mere Marquis Skycloud wants this young master to get on my knees? Do you want to die, or do you want to die?” Lu Yun sneered with contempt.","“You court death!” erupted the sanctimonious Mosi Yuxiu before Yun Shuige said anything. “What backwater did a bumbling fool like you spring out of? How dare you disrespect the young lord? Pay with your life!”","He waved his hand and sent forth curtains of silver splendor from his fly-whisk. It was a paramount dao weapon!","Mosi Yuxiu was definitely one who knew how to adapt to the situation. Although he had his own sect in Great Xia, it was not a premier faction. The benefits went without saying if he were able to latch onto a big thigh like the young lord!","Mosi Yuxiu’s actions goaded those around him into a quick response. They’d just witnessed Lu Yun kill the skeletal soldiers, so they swiftly assembled into a formation that trapped him inside."]},{"number":2336,"title":"Chapter 2336: Chapter 2217.1: The Nine Oscillations of the Heavenly Sword","paragraphs":["Chapter 2217.1: The Nine Oscillations of the Heavenly Sword","“It’s the Roving Dragon battle formation of the Roving Dragon Sect!” Yun Shuige brightened when he saw Mosi Yuxiu’s men assemble together. “Fellow daoists of the Roving Dragon Sect, I will remember this favor!” A keen light danced in his eyes.","While the Roving Dragon Sect was only a mid tier sect in Great Xia, its potential was enormous. It would be quite ideal if he could recruit the sect to his father’s banner on this trip. Yan Guichi had just been made a titled king and Marquis Skycloud was of the same mind as him. They were one faction and in the midst of expanding their power.","Being one of the marquis’ sons, Yun Shuige naturally inherited his father’s ambitions. Making new allies and drawing in others came as easily to him as eating and drinking.","The cultivators from Marquis Skycloud’s side swiftly shuffled into a formation after Yun Shuige spoke and trapped Lu Yun inside. Mosi Yuxiu’s paramount dao weapon emanated waves of silver illumination. They hid razor-sharp silver threads that came down around Lu Yun.","Immortals Forbidden flared with light and cut through the threads with searing energy, but the threads were as if parasites and clung to Lu Yun. In just a few moments, he was trussed up in a silver cocoon.","“I want him alive!” Yun Shuige lit up. To him, the only thing of note about Lu Yun was his body method. Mosi Yuxiu’s weapon happened to be the perfect counter to it.","“Hahaha, just give it up, junior! My fly-whisk is the accumulation of... eh...” Just as Mosi Yuxiu was about to launch into proud speech, an even more scintillating ray of silver erupted within the cocoon and sliced through all of the silver threads.","It even reduced Mosi Yuxiu’s weapon to an empty stick.","“How is this possible?! My fly-whisk is made from the silk of the Silverleaf Silkworm! Ordinary immortal weapons cannot destroy it, how did you do it?!” gasped the elder. He’d once employed it to take an empyrean immortal alive, but a mere soul separation cultivator had ruined it!","“Pfft, Silverleaf Silkworms are second rank immortal beasts, the equivalent of true immortals. Their silk is a rare treasure, but you turned it into a dao weapon? If I were you, I’d be too embarrassed to speak of it.” Lu Yun curled his lip and employed his body method, flashing through the air as numerous indistinct shadows.","The void was sealed off by two battle formations working in tandem. Immense and forceful attacks continuously cut through the sky.","“This won’t do!” The young man frowned. These two formations exceeded high rank battle formations. He would be injured if he was hit by them.","Bam!","The void trembled as the haphazard attacks coalesced into nine cerulean dragons. When the dragons roved through the air, the ambient energy of the place of burial was agitated and surged in their direction.","Replete with scales and claws, the nine seemed like true dragons and each emanated a terrifying aura. They would be able to tear even empyrean immortals to pieces!","They pounced on Lu Yun as soon as they formed; the Ly young master discovered to his shock that they’d sealed off this area!","“The Roving Dragon Sect’s battle formation is definitely something. No wonder they’re a mid-tier faction when they lack an origin immortal!” Yun Shuige licked his lips, greed flashing through his eyes. He must recruit the sect and have their battle formation at his command!","“If I can’t dodge it, then I’ll meet it straight on! Kill!” Lu Yun roared as Immortals Forbidden erupted with light. He seemed like a war god wielding the sun.","Humm!","Immortals Forbidden erupted with crimson splendor and a twenty-seven meter long ray of sword light arced toward the horizon.","The Nine Oscillations of the Heavenly Sword!","Lu Yun wrapped both hands around his sword and brought it down in front of him. Piercing radiance filled the void; even Yun Shuige couldn’t help but shade his eyes with his hand.","BAM!!","Twenty-seven meters of brilliance smashed into a dragon, obliterating it after a massive collision.","It was not yet over.","A second stroke!","Sword light churned through the air and chopped up another three dragons with a series of violent tremors.","A third stroke!","Sword light exploded into thousands of rays and churned the remaining five dragons into dust.","Break!","A flushed Lu Yun stood in the air, his chest heaving and panting for breath. All was silent between heaven and earth.","Apart from Mosi Yuxiu, the seventy remaining members of the Roving Dragon Sect were reduced to clouds of bloody mist by the enormous vibrations. Even their nascent souls didn’t have the chance of escape.","Those of Marquis Skycloud’s manor were thrown every which way, vomiting copious amounts of blood when they landed. The battle formation in the air broke without further pressure. Yun Shuige remained unmoving, but his face was dark. Most Yuxiu trembled like a leaf and didn’t know what to do in the throes of his horror.","There were nine strokes to the Nine Oscillations of the Heavenly Sword, but a lack of definitive techniques. Their sword qi melded into the void and made it impossible to guard against. Each stroke accumulated on the ones before and was stronger than each preceding one. If all nine were deployed, heaven and earth would shift and immortals terror-stricken.","All Lu Yun could manage at his current level of strength was three strokes, but they were still sufficient to kill immortals.","“What a tremendously strong attack!” Yun Shuige’s longsword flared with cerulean luster. “You’re just soul separation... If you had enough time and space to grow, you’d be another White. Unfortunately for you, you do not have such luxury.”","Bathed in gentle blue light, Yun Shuige slowly floated up from the ground. Rays of splendor circulated around him. He was a premier genius, but compared to the truly monstrous geniuses, he was too far removed from them. The perverse geniuses of Great Xia were able to kill immortals when they were cultivators.","Yun Shuige defined Lu Yun as one such genius.","However, the young man was only soul separation at the moment and had yet to fully come into his strength. Yun Shuige was confident that the current Lu Yun was no match for him. He needed to eliminate the young man before he could grow further.","“Die!” Yun Shuige shouted as his sword erupted with scintillating blue radiance. He became one with his immortal sword and streaked toward Lu Yun as a ray of light.","“Man and sword as one...” Lu Yun narrowed his eyes.","Pfft!","The combination of man and sword pierced through Lu Yun’s body.","“No!” Yun Shuige shouted in horror. A crimson dragon of dense sword qi rampaged through where he’d come from. Wails and shrieks rose and fell as his men and Mosi Yuxiu were ripped apart.","The cultivators were already reeling from the backlash of the formation and dealing with heavy injuries. They’d relaxed when they saw their young lord deploy an ultimate move and run through Lu Yun’s body. Who would’ve thought that their quarry would run through them and erupt in slaughter instead?","“So it’s you, no wonder you dared set yourself against me... You’re Lu Yun, grandson of Lu Tianling!” Yun Shuige recognized the Eighteen Cerulean Sword Dragons as soon as the other deployed it.","Marquis Cloudsky and the Origin King were on the same ship. The former naturally investigated anyone who was enemies with the Origin King. The Eighteen Cerulean Sword Dragons was Lu Yun’s trademark move.","“If my guess is correct, the pagoda from the legendary Mindful Immortal Potentate of the world of immortals is in your hands,” Yun Shuige said coolly as he calmed down.","Lu Yun frowned faintly to hear Yun Shuige call out the potentate’s name. He would’ve been baffled before, since the world of immortals was but myth and legend to present day immortals. The Mindful Immortal Potentate’s name could not possibly have been passed on.","But after true immortal Lu Youya deployed the Greedy Wolf Star, Lu Yun understood that this was likely all due to the Greedy Wolf Immortal King.","If Terra Demon could survive, then being on nearly the same level as him, of course the Greedy Wolf Immortal King could as well.","“The Mindful Immortal Potentate’s legacy is indeed with you. It looks like the Marquis Skycloud Manor has a chance of becoming the Skycloud King Estate!” Yun Shuige didn’t care about his dead followers—they were just a few minions and no one important.","He threw his head back with a howl as the cerulean radiance around him deepened and locked onto Lu Yun. “I know how to create images of myself too!”","Whoosh whoosh whoosh!","He split into nine as soon as he finished and rushed toward Lu Yun from nine different directions.","“Image replicas?” Lu Yun curled his lip. That was a far cry from his Split Shadow combat art. He could determine which was real and which was fake without even employing the Eye of Nullification.","But he’d gravely exhausted his Hongmeng qi earlier after utilizing the Nine Oscillations of the Heavenly Sword. It wasn’t the time to go head-to-head with Yun Shuige. The Nine Oscillations of the Heavenly Sword was more domineering than the Eighteen Cerulean Sword Dragons and thus consumed more qi.","It was because Lu Yun possessed Hongmeng qi from the Nine Chapters of Dao that he was able to do all this. Any other cultivator wouldn’t be able to do the same.","Pfft!","Yun Shuige’s nine images simultaneously arrived in front of Lu Yun and sliced him to bits.","“A fake?!” Yun Shuige’s heart skipped a beat.","“I’m over here!” Lu Yun appeared thirty meters behind his opponent."]},{"number":2337,"title":"Chapter 2337: Chapter 2217.2: The Nine Oscillations of the Heavenly Sword","paragraphs":["Chapter 2217.2: The Nine Oscillations of the Heavenly Sword","Yun Shuige’s heart raced and he enveloped himself with cerulean sword light without a beat of hesitation. As man and sword were one, his speed was the peak of his limits. He flashed to Lu Yun within a thousandth of a second.","Man and sword being one was the highest realm of sword cultivation. Man resonated with sword and truly comprehended the meaning of sword dao. In the world of immortals, it took reaching golden immortal before Lu Yun touched this level.","However, Yun Shuige accomplished it as an awakened cultivator. He would be a peerless genius even in the world of immortals of yesteryear!","Pfft!","Cerulean radiance cut through the void and unending sword splendor nearly drowned Lu Yun.","“I’m over here,” Lu Yun’s voice sounded in Yun Shuige’s ear, still thirty meters behind the man!","Cerulean sword light faded away as Yun Shuige reappeared in the void, staring coldly at his opponent.","“It would seem that you have a tremendous immortal treasure on you,” he breathed out. Blue luster began gathering around him again. “But as strong as it is, it is an external object. You are but soul separation—how much of its power can you bring to bear?”","He’d struck Lu Yun’s images more than once; they were identical to the young man’s primary body. Yun Shuige was beginning to suspect that Lu Yun owned a heaven-defying immortal weapon.","Countless immortal treasures had appeared in the place of burial over the past seven days. Therefore, Yun Shuige naturally surmised that the young man had laid hands on one such treasure in some part of the area.","“Luminosity of Sky and Cloud!” Yun Shuige called out as he transformed into wisps of cloud, then faded away from the void.","Pfft!","Cerulean radiance exploded over Lu Yun’s head and cut him into two.","“I’m over here,” Lu Yun’s voice sounded.","“I know!”","Pfft!","Another ray of cerulean sword light descended as soon as Lu Yun appeared and destroyed his body.","“Here!” The young man once more reappeared elsewhere.","Whoosh!","Yun Shuige’s attack arrived at nearly the same time.","The Luminosity of Sky and Cloud was Marquis Skycloud’s signature move. For use in assassination and ambush, the wielder came and went like a ghost and was everywhere at the same time. It was a combat art nearly superior to Lu Yun’s Nine Forms of the Cloud Dragon.","“Over here!”","Whoosh!","“Here!”","Whoosh!","“I’m over here!”","......","Lu Yun and Yun Shuige’s body flitted in and out of sight in the void, a dense collection to be seen everywhere. One of them appeared before the other disappeared. If there were any other cultivators present, they would be utterly bewildered and confused.","Gradually, the coolly composed Yun Shuige’s eyes turned bloodshot. This combat art consumed too many resources and despite his internal force having transmuted to immortal origin, he could not sustain this kind of drain.","He was one step behind Lu Yun each time and failed to capture the young man’s true body. It was aggravating him to an endless degree.","This had never happened before.","Yun Shuige admitted that he was less than the truly preeminent geniuses of Great Xia, but this Lu Yun hailed only from a world of cultivation. As stunning as his abilities were, his environment constrained the limits of his potential.","The other perverse genius from the Jade Ruins Realm—Mo Qiyue—possessed the qualifications of a perverse genius due to his potential. But due to where he’d grown up, all he was now was just a slightly stronger genius.","“Die!!” Yun Shuige could finally bear it no longer and sent his sword out with a shout. It exploded in the air and rained keen sword light in all directions.","The nearby ruins and rubble were obliterated by the terrifying brilliance.","“I might fear you a bit if you’d brought your strength together, but since you attack in such an idiotic manner... heh.” Dispersing one’s attacks brought widespread damage to bear, but it also diminished the strength of the attack. Lu Yun pressed his advantage when Yun Shuige showed weakness and shifted in front of his opponent with a twist of the Nine Forms of the Cloud Dragon.","“You fell for it!” Yun Shuige leered when he saw Lu Yun less than a meter away from him. A blue sword appeared in his hand and enveloped him with blue sword light. He was transformed into a keen sword blazing with sword qi.","Man and sword as one! The void trembled!","Hummm!","Bam!","A sliver of hesitation appeared in the air as Lu Yun’s body faded away in a bloody shower after being struck by the massive sword light.","“No, wait!” Yun Shuige’s eyes widened with dismay. This Lu Yun was fake too!","“You fell for it too!” Lu Yun’s voice ran over his head.","Searing heat appeared over Yun Shuige as crimson sword light once more split through the void, careening straight toward him. Lu Yun didn’t give his opponent a chance to react. He gathered his strongest strength and lashed out with the Nine Oscillations of the Heavenly Sword, infusing the air with terrifying sword qi and swallowing Yun Shuige.","Clang!!","A teeth-numbing sound rang out as Lu Yun’s hands shook. He almost lost his grip on Immortals Forbidden.","Yun Shuige’s body drilled into the ground from the force of the Lu young master’s technique. The sound came from a golden bell that’d appeared over him. It trembled as bright peals echoed through the air.","A fifth rank immortal treasure.","Lu Yun’s arms ached slightly. He wielded only a lower dao rank weapon, one that would’ve been destroyed had it not been refined from such heaven-defying materials. A sweet taste welled up in the back of his throat and blood trickled out of his mouth.","......","“This is the Profound Bell... The young lord is in trouble!”","Enormous bell peals filled Immortal Burial Valley. Cultivators scattered throughout were amazed by what they heard, while some were downright dismayed. The Profound Bell was a defensive treasure that Marquis Skycloud had given to Yun Shuige. A situation that’d forced him to bring it out meant that his life was in danger.","Regardless of their cultivation level, all cultivators affiliated with Marquis Skycloud put down their task at hand and sped toward the source of the bell’s tolls.","......","“Your old man’s pretty decent to you, you have a fifth rank immortal treasure to defend yourself with!” Lu Yun stood in the air and looked imperiously down at the crawling Yun Shuige.","“You’re quite strong.” Yun Shuige’s clothes were tattered and his golden crown had long disappeared somewhere. His hair dangled in a tangled mess over his shoulders. “But you can’t kill me since I have an immortal treasure defending me and my men will be here shortly. You’ll be the one to die then.”","He’d lost to Lu Yun whether in terms of strength or strategy, but Yun Shuige wasn’t depressed. True geniuses didn’t sink into mental slump after one loss—they grew stronger with each failure.","Such was the kind of person he was.","The golden bell over his head tolled with increasing grandeur, gathering the cultivators in the valley that answered to his father.","“You think I can’t kill you?” Lu Yun cackled, sweeping the fifty kilometers around them with the Eye of Nullification. There were no other cultivators on the scene as of yet. Marquis Skycloud’s cultivators were spread out in a bid to cover more ground in the valley. Thus, it would take them a while to arrive. Yun Shuige had said that just to persuade Lu Yun to stand down.","Goodwill surged out of the Seal of the Multitude and flowed into Lu Yun’s body, replenishing his consumption of Hongmeng qi.","At soul separation stage, he no longer wished to use goodwill to enhance his cultivation. He’d rather save it to enhance the might of his heavenly dao combat arts. There were other methods to enhance his cultivation, but the strength of heavenly dao combat arts could only be increased by goodwill.","But now... he could tell that Yun Shuige was a fat cat for skinning. That fifth rank immortal treasure was no ordinary specimen of its kind since it could withstand the Nine Oscillations of the Heavenly Sword.","The Nine Oscillations of the Heavenly Sword melded sword qi into the void and attacked through the limits of space. Ordinary defensive immortals weapons couldn’t even touch a wisp of sword qi, to say nothing of defending against it","As goodwill replenished Hongmeng qi, Lu Yun rapidly formed hand seals and collected sword qi over his head. They interwove with each other until they formed the image of a silver pagoda. Growing until it reached twenty-seven meters tall, each floor was one meter tall and the entire structure made of sword qi. Simple, yet ancient patterns snaked over it.","Sword qi cascaded down from the peak of the mountain and enveloped Lu Yun, bathing the young man with silver sword qi.","The image of the sword page was dignified and stately. While it was black, it was overlaid with a faint hue of silver due to being refined as Lu Yun’s image of heaven and earth. There was also something a little more special about this image compared to when it was just the pitch-black pagoda.","“Ready or not, little marquis, here I come!” Lu Yun threw his head back with laughter when his image finalized and crossed his hands in front of his chest. The sword pagoda overhead shot and came down on Yun Shuige beneath him.","The Yun young lord paled and the Profound Bell over his head tolled with the strain of overextension. His marvelous treasure began to darken and dim.","“Die!!” Lu Yun pressed down with both hands and bid the gigantic sword pagoda to swallow Yun Shuige’s body."]},{"number":2338,"title":"Chapter 2338: Chapter 2218.1: The Profound Bell","paragraphs":["Chapter 2218.1: The Profound Bell","Sword qi rampaged so furiously that Yun Shuige didn’t have a chance to defend himself, despite the protection of a fifth rank immortal treasure. His body was swiftly churned to pieces and a fully transmuted immortal soul sliced and diced the moment it showed itself.","......","An inexplicable void.","Numerous oil lamps flickered weakly with dim yellow glows.","Whoosh!","One of them abruptly flared with intensity, the flame gathering into a human face full of terror. It was a perfect resemblance of Yan Shuige’s features.","“Save me, dao master!” it shrieked with terror.","Puff!","The oil lamp exploded, consigning itself and the face to dust.","A desiccated elder with white hair and long eyebrows slowly opened his eyes in the middle of the void. He looked toward the terminated oil lamp.","“Cultivators protected by soul lamps have died one after another...” The elder fell silently as he stared at where the last soul lamp had been. “It’s a good thing that such a person has appeared. I hope he keeps the bigger picture in mind...”","......","Only a storage ring and a dimmed fifth rank Profound Bell was left after Yun Shuige fell to the sword pagoda’s furious barrage.","“Thank goodness Yun Shuige wasn’t an immortal and couldn’t bring even twenty percent of the treasure’s power to bear. It wouldn’t be that easy to kill him within a few days otherwise. But if he was an immortal, he wouldn’t be able to enter this land.” Lu Yun collected the immortal rank treasure and storage ring, vanishing from the premises with a few flashes of his body.","Cultivators under the Marquis Skycloud banner streamed to the location after another fifteen minutes. Everything had been leveled to flat ground through the course of Lu Yun and Yun Shuige’s battle.","......","“Who would’ve thought that the image of the sword pagoda would possess so much strength! It’s one that can both attack and defend!” Lu Yun sat down on the ground when he was two hundred and fifty kilometers away from the site of battle and sorted through his spoils.","“Paramount rank spirit crystals!” First to greet his eyes when he accessed Yun Shuige’s storage ring was ten thousand paramount spirit crystals!","What he lacked most at the moment were cultivation resources. The Nine Chapters of Dao consumed entirely way too many resources during cultivation. Since he wasn’t willing to use goodwill to enhance his strength, he had to rely on lower rank spirit crystals.","While qi within spirit crystals was pure, it was far from sufficient compared to the Hongmeng qi resulting from the Nine Chapters of Dao. Obtaining paramount spirit crystals at this time was as vital to him as a parched man in the desert receiving a drink of water.","Paramount spirit crystals also counted among the rarer resources in Great Xia.","“Oh? This is...” Lu Yun’s eyelids twitched as three purple pills entered his line of sight. The sparkled with faint hues and didn’t emanate any fragrance. Most noteworthy about them was the golden rune etched on each of them.","“Dao Rune Pills...” Lu Yun took a deep breath when he saw the pills. Such pills didn’t exist in the world of immortals—only a world on the level of Great Xia possessed them.","As Great Xia lacked immortal crystals, immortals depended on Dao Rune Pills for cultivation. The rune on them contained the harmony of dao. It aided immortals in comprehending heavenly dao, understanding nature, and was more precious than immortal crystals in some aspects.","After all, only immortal qi was present in immortal crystals, there was no harmony of dao. In the world of immortals, however, the circulation of the laws of heaven and earth were many times more forthright than in a plane like Great Xia. Immortals could comprehend the myriad facets of nature directly from heaven and earth without needing the help of the Dao Rune Pills.","The Dao Rune Pills themselves were categorized from one rune to nine. The more runes one pill contained, the more harmonies it boasted of. A nine rune Dao Rune Pill would be extremely precious even in the world of immortals.","“He’s prepared even Dao Rune Pills—looks like Yun Shuige was ready to ascend to immortality after leaving Immortal Burial Valley. Pity he had a death wish and decided to provoke me instead.” Lu Yun transferred the Dao Rune Pills into his own storage ring. Apart from the pills and spirit crystals, there was nothing particularly special about the other contents. They were the run-of-the-mill pills, medicines, ores, and ingredients.","Yun Shuige had reaped quite a harvest in the valley. He’d found a dozen immortal weapons, of which one was a seventh rank flying sword.","“I have no use for the treasures apart from the flying sword.” Lu Yun shook his head and turned to studying the Profound Bell.","“This bell seems to be a broken treasure. It shouldn’t be like this.” He could see everything about the bell with the Eye of Nullification. Its core essence was fragmented, but it was somehow still able to form a complete fifth rank immortal treasure despite its inadequacies.","“Wait!” He realized what was amiss. “This treasure is coalesced from that tattered core essence... What did this bell look like originally?”","The young man’s eyes widened. The Profound Bell came from the partial core essence of a treasure, formed after continuously devouring the essence of heaven and earth. He found this incredulous even with his experience of three thousand lifetimes.","Instead of attempting to refine it, Lu Yun decided to see how he might repair the shattered core essence or find its other parts.","Any ordinary immortal treasure was unsalvageable if its core essence was damaged. It would never leave behind a tiny bit that could absorb the essence of heaven and earth and come back together.","A smile crossed Lu Yun’s face—he didn’t care about killing Yun Shuige. The latter was just the son of a golden immortal, so what if he died? It was entirely expected that even awakened cultivators die in Immortal Burial Valley; Marquis Skycloud would never find anything no matter how strong he was.","Having sorted through his loot, Lu Yun stood up to leave. He hadn’t forgotten what his goal here was—locating the Crimson Emperor Chapter of Inception for his grandfather.","Lu Tianling was initial awakened stage and would be consumed by the halberd when he ascended to immortality. With the Lu patriarch’s potential, becoming an immortal was all too easy for him.","There wasn’t much time left for Lu Yun.","It was unfeasible for Lu Tianling to enter the valley himself. With his current reputation, numerous immortals near Dark City kept an eye on him. If he dared set out, Great Xia immortals would be the first to stand in his way.","Lu Tianling was too strong—he would face concerted pushback from other factions if he came to Immortal Burial Valley. He would be hobbled at every turn, so Lu Yun didn’t bother telling his grandfather what his plans were. Instead, he set out under the guise of training and came here with Terra Demon.","With Terra Demon playing bodyguard, Lu Tianling was perfectly at ease letting his grandson roam around.","......","“If the Azure Emperor Chapter of Inception is held within a stick of connate spirit bamboo, then the Crimson Emperor Chapter of Inception should have something to do with fire.” Lu Yun operated the Connate Great Dao of the Five Elements as he carefully sensed the distribution of the five elements within the land.","Other than summoning the elements for his own usage, the Connate Great Dao of the Five Elements could also be deployed to search for elemental treasures. At Lu Yun’s current level of cultivation, he could sense the makeup of the elements within five hundred kilometers.","But he could only discern their composition—he didn’t know anything about their actual condition.","“There’s a powerful blast of fire energy to the east!” Lu Yun brightened and flew to the east in a surge of sword light.","The energy of fire was so intense that it indicated a fire attribute treasure. It was very likely the item that held the Crimson Emperor Chapter of Inception. Since it was his goal for this trip, the young man would follow every clue he gleaned.","An obnoxiously opulent ray of crimson sword light split through the air, completely out in the open. Lu Yun brought his speed up to his greatest capability and slowly mapped out the terrain as he flew.","“This place of burial was once a massive palace... What a pity that it’s been completely destroyed and its former structure impossible to make out.” Although the structure was severely damaged, he could still sense that it must have been bigger than his Northern Sky palace in its heyday.","It must have belonged to someone at least a chaos immortal. Sadly, something had devoured its core essence and treasures. It was similar to what’d happened to Empress Myrtlestar’s king rank Cosmic Flag—that, too, was just an upper dao rank treasure now.","The remaining treasures were but ninth rank. They may be precious to Great Xia immortals, but Lu Yun didn’t think much of them.","The ripples of battle raised his attention as he flew toward the east.","\"Spare the woman and the jade talisman they just obtained. Kill the rest!” Seven men in black outfits and vicious expressions were assembled in an eerie battle formation that trapped four cultivators.","The men were initial soul separation, but their battle formation was so incredibly strong that it firmly suppressed the four combination cultivators they faced. Those four were Ling Chu, Ling Ling, Song Yi, and Shi Jian."]},{"number":2339,"title":"Chapter 2339: Chapter 2218.2: The Profound Bell","paragraphs":["Chapter 2218.2: The Profound Bell","The four encountered a fair number of fortuitous opportunities after entering the place of burial and broke through to combination stage. Previously the weakest, Ling Ling was now the strongest at mid combination.","Through the Eye of Nullification, Lu Yun could see a faint purple haze inside each of their bodies. They’d plainly each refined a paramount pill, but its effects were so strong that they needed more time to fully digest it.","“It’s the Purple Magnificence Assimilation Pill—an immortal pill that can change a cultivator’s foundations!” Lu Yun sighed with appreciation at their luck.","The Purple Magnificence Assimilation Pill was a king rank immortal pill that could only be taken by cultivators. Once swallowed, the cultivator’s potential underwent a complete change and they had the potential to become a dao immortal.","One had to know that even in the world of immortals, only one or two out of ten million immortals had a chance of comprehending that stage and breaking through. It was thus easy to imagine how valuable such a pill was.","Not only had each of them taken a Purple Magnificence Assimilation Pill, but they’d utilized the tremendous effects within to break straight through to combination stage. In contrast to the gentle effects of the Unselfish Hateless Pill, the Purple Magnificence Assimilation Pill was a domineering and savage pill. More than ninety-nine percent of those who took it exploded instead of finding any benefit. When cultivators took it in the world of immortals, they needed to be watched over by a dao immortal. Otherwise, their death was a foregone conclusion.","Hence, Lu Yun found the four very lucky indeed.","......","“Brother, are we going to die here?” Although Ling Ling held the highest cultivation, she was the weakest out of the four. She was the first to falter when facing their seven enemies.","Despair flashed through Song Yi’s eyes. He’d thought that he would be able to revitalize the family after encountering good fortune in Immortal Burial Valley and raising his potential. No, he would die here instead.","The seven’s attacks were vicious and merciless. If it wasn’t for the fact that the quartet had taken the immortal pill earlier, all four would be dead long ago.","“We are descendants of Great Xia nobility! Many saw you chase after us. Are you not afraid of creating trouble for yourself?!” Being a straightforward man, Shi Jian yelled at them as he beat back an attack with his broadsword.","“Descendants of Great Xia nobility?” sneered the leader of the seven. “We wouldn’t dare kill you if you’re that Human Emperor’s descendent, but other than that, we’ll kill you even if you’re the son of the Fengxian King!”","“Shi Jian, Song Yi!” Doggedly defending the quartet, the mute Ling Chu suddenly broke his silence. “Take care of my sister in the future and don’t take revenge!”","His aura blasted in all directions as he hauled out a ghastly white flag with several strange and twisting patterns on it. Rays of ghastly radiance erupted when he unfurled it. The seven’s eyes widened and they dropped the offensive, raising the defensive treasure to defend themselves instead.","Ling Chu put away the flag when a gleaming white jade lion formed over his head. He pushed Ling Ling toward Song Yi. “Take her out of here!”","With a lion roar that shook the heavens, he flung himself at the seven.","“NO!!” Ling Ling keened to see her brother thus and struggled to get back to him.","“Big brother Ling!” Song Yi’s eyes reddened; he maintained a firm clamp on Ling Ling’s arm and doggedly reminded himself that he could not do the same as her.","“I’m going to kill you!!” Shi Jian went berserk as bloody tears flowed out of his eyes. His personal image appeared over his head as well—one of a blade with the hilt of a ghostly face. He threw himself at the seven without any hesitation.","“You guys want to detonate your images?” the group’s leader snorted. He blurred into two afterimages and flashed to the two young men.","Bam bam!","Ling Chu and Shi Jian bounced back at almost the same time. They vomited blood as their images faded away.","“Idiots, we brothers would have to expend some effort taking care of you if the four of you acted together. But rushing forward like this? You just want to die!” cackled the leader as he stepped on Ling Chu. “Hand over the jade slip you just got and I’ll consider letting you die faster.” Though he smiled, the look in his eyes was inordinately cold.","“Let them go, I’ll give you everything I have!” A palm-sized jade slip appeared in Ling Chu’s hand.","The man toyed with it. “You guys still have to die.”","“But I don’t want them to,” came another voice. A young man in white robes walked through the air, approaching the two parties.","“Yo, another fat cat to be skinned eh?” The leader smiled at Lu Yun’s arrival.","“Lu Yun!” A strange look flashed through Ling Chu’s eyes when he saw the young man. “Go away, these people are too strong, you’re no match for them!”","“Get out of here, ole brother Lu!” Song Yi and the others yelled as well.","Lu Yun smiled without a word. He’d seen everything through the Eye of Nullification and revised his assessment of the four. He also truly wanted to befriend them now. Their first thought upon seeing Lu Yun was not for themselves, but for his safety.","He couldn’t help but smile.","“Friend...”","Bam!","An enormous surge of strength struck the man in the chest just as he was about to speak and sent him flying.","“Are you alright?” Lu Yun helped up Ling Chu and took out four healing pills from his storage ring. “I think you took a jade slip from my friend just now, didn’t you? Hand it over.” He turned to the seven.","Their leader had flown several hundred meters out from Lu Yun’s kick and took a while to recollect his thoughts.","“Who... who are you?” He looked askance at Lu Yun. He hadn’t even seen where that kick came from! If it’d been a treasure, he’d already been dead.","“Didn’t you hear Brother Ling? I’m Lu Yun, the grandson of Lu Tianling—the strongest in the realm.” Lu Yun lifted his head with an arrogant prodigal expression.","“Um...” The seven looked at each other. Lu Tianling? While the man was just awakened stage, he could kill even august immortals! They were nothing but ants to him.","......","Lu Tianling was the current head honcho of the realm. Lower level immortals were no match for him and higher level ones didn’t wish to run afoul of him. The Origin King of Great Xia had come himself at one point, but also ran off with his tail between his legs.","The name of Lu Tianling was known throughout the worlds. Who would be his match once he became an immortal?","Everyone who entered Jade Ruins Realm was highly wary of the Lu patriarch. Some immortals had already gathered at Immortal Burial Valley, ready to block him from entering if he appeared.","“Form up!” roared the leader in black just when everyone thought the seven would give up the fight.","Well practiced in acting together, the seven melted into the void as soon as their leader gave the word. A cloud of black fog wafted over Lu Yun. Strange cries echoed through it; all the young man knew was that an eerie killing intent lingered nearby.","“The Southern Dipper, Ox, Girl, Emptiness, Rooftop, Encampment, and Wall... It’s the Seven Mansions of the Northern Sky! Are these seven their reincarnations or heirs?” Lu Yun frowned slightly, having recognized their method. It was the Seven Mansions of the Northern Sky from the world of immortals that was part of the Twenty-Eight Mansions of the constellation system!","The twenty-eight generals were the true overseers of the world of immortals. Answering to the banners of the four divine beasts, each of them was a chaos immortal. While they weren’t as strong as the five immortal emperors, they were the cream of the crop.","But since the twenty-eight stars safeguarded the four cardinal directions, ordinary immortals were unaware of their existence. Only the five immortal emperors could communicate with them.","Back in those days of the world of immortals, talent abounded. There were more than the five immortal emperors when it came to chaos immortals, but only those five could become emperors of the world because they were the only ones with the cardinal directions’ approval.","During that time, the Black Tortoise of the Northern Sky had bestowed a law of water upon Lu Yun, giving him the strength by which he ruled."]},{"number":2340,"title":"Chapter 2340: Chapter 2219.1: Void Sacred Flame","paragraphs":["Chapter 2219.1: Void Sacred Flame","Lu Yun had once thought that the four divine beasts were mysterious beyond compare. Now he understood that the beasts were as if his senior brother—manifestations of the rules.","I wonder who is stronger, the four divine beasts or Sky?","He’d wanted to kill the seven, but changed his mind after discovering the aura of the seven mansions on them and seeing how they were able to utilize the moves of the northern sky. If he could subdue the group instead, that would be an incredible boon to his cause.","He could tell that there was nothing special about them apart from the methods of the Seven Mansions of the Northern Sky. Thus, he immediately called upon the Eighteen Cerulean Sword Dragons.","A crimson dragon nearly one hundred meters long raged through the black fog. It ripped the gloom to bits and forced the seven to tumble out of the void.","Lu Yun slowly appeared in front of them with Immortals Forbidden in hand.","“They say that the four directions bow their heads when a tiger shows its dominance with a shake of its body. Do all of you concede defeat?” Immortals Forbidden spat out sword light and aimed it at the leader’s forehead.","“Are you not killing us?” the man started.","“This young master treasures talent, of which the seven of you are since you could defeat Ling Chu and the others. I will show you mercy if you return the jade slip to Ling Chu and become my followers.” Lu Yun’s lips curved upwards and there was no hint of hostility in his words.","The leader turned back to look at his brothers.","“Big brother, we follow your call!” they chorused.","They were no fools. While they had few enemies in Great Xia and were feared by some of the nobility, they’d just been defeated in one move. So what if the Dao Academy had issued multiple invites that they’d turned down? They were aware of stories circulating in recent days and didn’t think that Lu Yun would show them the same grace and courtesy that they enjoyed in Great Xia.","“Nan Ting greets the young master.” Their leader bowed his head as he took another look at his brothers. With that, the remaining six also introduced themselves.","Their leader was Nan Ting, second eldest Sun Xiao, then came Yu Xuan, Chang Yingxuan, Wen Yan, Mo Yunxiao, and lastly Qin Luo. They were sworn brothers, but so close knit that they were as if blood brothers. They didn’t even need to verbally communicate to know what each other wanted.","“Hand over the jade slip.” Lu Yun reached out his hand.","Nan Ting hesitated, then retrieved the jade slip from his storage ring. Lu Yun gave it to Ling Chu when he took it.","“Old brother Lu...” Ling Chu didn’t immediately close his hands around it.","“Brother Ling, don’t be like this since you call me your brother.” Lu Yun smiled and tossed the jade slip over.","Ling Chu caught it and looked at him with gratitude, goodwill rising from all four of them. Lu Yun sighed to himself. If it was Yu Shuai and Zhao Chenguang here, they’d already be joking and playing around. They wouldn’t be so solemn and serious.","But it was alright, his relationship with these four didn’t run that deeply yet. They were just friends for now.","“Young master...” Nan Ting breathed out with relief when Ling Chu accepted the jade slip. The rest of his words stuck in the back of his throat.","“I don’t fully trust the seven of you yet.” Lu Yun looked at him superciliously. “I’m keeping that ray of sword qi in your bodies until you fully adhere to me. You can try breaking it before then—let’s see if you die.”","While these seven possessed the abilities of the seven mansions, he didn’t really trust them. Their auras were dark and sinister. Plainly, they were the type to hide a dagger in their smiles.","Now that Lu Yun had reached soul separation, he could call upon certain methods that he couldn’t utilize before. The art of sword implantation was a very cruel restriction. It planted sword qi directly into the nascent or immortal soul, dictating the life or death of the victim with a single thought of the caster.","However, one needed to reach a certain level of comprehension of sword dao in order to use such a restriction. One’s command over sword qi also needed to reach a certain height of innateness. The nascent soul was the core essence of a cultivator. It was extraordinarily fragile, and easily destroyed if the sword qi wasn’t properly controlled.","There’d been only two immortals who mastered the art in the world of immortals—Lu Yun and the Mindful Immortal Potentate. As for those who could break it... there was no one who could, not even chaos immortals.","When he broke their attack, Lu Yun simultaneously planted seven rays of sword qi in their hearts and minds. The brothers didn’t know what it was, but they could sense the frosty killing intent lurking in their nascent souls. Otherwise, they would’ve at least managed to escape if they couldn’t beat their opponent.","The seven had just said that they didn’t think much of anyone other than the royal princes of Great Xia, that they would kill even the Fengxian King’s son.","It wasn’t that their backgrounds were that impressive, but that their methods of escape were that heaven-defying. They were able to easily retreat from even a formation set up by an immortal. Who would’ve thought that they’d run into a wall with Lu Yun this time?","The young man wouldn’t have been able to implant sword qi into all seven at the same time if it wasn’t for them deploying the methods of the Seven Mansions of the Northern Sky. Lu Yun was all too familiar with that one.","He spontaneously seized their mobility and made his move. Even if it was anyone else, even arcane immortals—they’d be hard pressed to subdue the seven. The methods of the seven mansions were too extraordinary.","The seven looked at each other ruefully. They’d dominated Great Xia ever since swearing brotherhood to each other. They weren’t afraid of immortals, but had fallen into the hands of a renowned good-for-nothing in the tiny Jade Ruins Realm.","“We will not be able to remove the sword qi unless we detonate our nascent souls,” Nan Ting sighed as he looked at his brothers.","“Alright, I have plenty of talents under my banner. I don’t need you guys to do anything other than focus on cultivation. When you get to Great Xia, support Ling Chu and the others well,” Lu Yun gave his conclusion after thinking things over.","“Huh?” LIng Chu and the others looked at each other, startled and not sure of what to say.","“Brother Ling, I’ll be frank with you since things have reached this point,” Lu Yun began when he saw the expressions on the other four.","“Old brother Lu Yun, you’re our savior. Just give the world if you need help!” Being the straightforward man he was, Shi Jian cut straight to the chase.","“Mmhmm,” Lu Yun nodded. “Based on what I see, the four of you aren’t particularly valued in your families, yes?”","Ling Chu frowned, but nodded. “Ling Ling, Shi Jian, and I come from cadet branches of our families. They don’t care about us—they wouldn’t have forgotten about us after shoving us into the Dao Academy otherwise.","“In contrast, Song Yi... is the son of the Argent King.”","Song Yi grit his teeth when he heard the king’s title and a vein throbbed on his forehead. When the Human Emperor brought his subordinates to Immortal Burial Valley, Yan Guichi and several other marquises took advantage of the battle to scheme against the Argent King. With the death of the Argent King and Yan Guichi being the strongest of the Great Xia marquises, he naturally became the new king after he broke through at a critical moment.","It went without saying that the new Origin King took over everything that’d belonged to the Argent King as well.","The Argent King’s eldest son was golden immortal and had been made a marquis by the Human Emperor. But he was just an ordinary marquis, so the vast Argent King faction declined overnight.","To the victor went the spoils and legitimacy in Great Xia, so the death of the Argent King and conferment of the Origin King’s title meant that some of those who’d sworn fealty to the Argent King immediately switched their allegiances. The Argent King’s faction quickly fragmented and although some portions remained staunchly loyal, they were a far cry from what the Origin King commanded.","Song Yi’s elder brother’s ambitions did not correlate to his talents at all. He was happy with the status quo after he was made a marquis and gave no thought to revenge.","Lu Yun looked at Song Yi with surprise.","“Brother Song, it seems that we share similar fates.” He smiled wryly, drawing a bewildered glance from Ling Ling.","“Everyone knows that the Lus have a feud with Yan Guichi, but that seems to stem from the Origin King lusting after one of your treasures, doesn’t it?” Shi Jian scratched his head.","“The Origin King? Yan Guichi? He’s just one of our slaves,” Lu Yun sneered. The upper echelon of Great Xia society knew of what’d befallen the Lu Clan. While Ling Chu and the others were descendants of nobility, no one told them these stories as they weren’t important to their families.","Not to mention, Yan Guichi had been the leader of the thirty-six marquises before. Who would dare talk behind his back? It was normal that Shi Jian was unaware."]},{"number":2341,"title":"Chapter 2341: Chapter 2219.2: Void Sacred Flame","paragraphs":["Chapter 2219.2: Void Sacred Flame","“Ah... I know about this.” Qin Luo, the youngest of the seven, smiled. Since Lu Yun wanted the seven brothers to support these four noble sons and daughters down on their luck, it was an appropriate time to demonstrate their worth.","The Lu young master held their lives in the palm of his hand, after all.","Qin Luo was a feminine name and his features were uncommonly delicate. If it wasn’t for the ruthless air around him, he would seem to be a dashing gentleman. He cleared his throat when he found that Ling Chu and the others were looking at him. “Sir Lu’s family should be the once Marquis Skyflame.”","Lu Yun looked at Qin Luo and inclined his head.","“Marquis Skyflame?” Ling Chu and the three looked at each other.","They were familiar with the name, but that had been a marquis from nearly three thousand years ago. Great Xia’s records of this marquis were inordinately vague. The only information was that he’d died in a massive battle.","“Marquis Skyflame was unparalleled in battle and wielded three kinds of fires of heaven and earth. He was definitively top three in the rankings of the thirty-six!” Qin Luo slotted in some casual flattery. He and his brothers were sharp and quick on the uptake. Dignity and face were less important than a piece of lower rank spirit stone to them.","“He was deeply injured in a campaign against alien races three thousand years ago, but nothing was life-threatening. He only needed to rest for a few decades before making a full recovery.","“Yet when his steward heard the news, he took advantage of the opening to kill the resting marquis and seized the entire complex. He butchered nearly every single member of the clan, leaving few survivors behind.","“Two hundred years ago, that steward discovered remnants of the clan that’d escaped and hunted them down again. Senior Lu Tianling of Darklake Empire should be the last of Marquis Skyflame’s bloodline...” Qin Luo sighed. “And that steward is the now Origin King Yan Guichi.”","“Ah...” Ling Chu and the others looked at Lu Yun with astonishment.","“I see... Ole brother Lu, who would’ve thought that we’d both have blood feuds with Yan Guichi.” Song Yi walked up and clapped Lu Yun’s shoulder. While Lu Yun had mentioned the feud before, he himself didn’t know all these particulars.","“I need you guys to help me.” Lu Yun had observed the four multiple times and noted that their expressions grew stiff each time Yan Guichi was mentioned. It was no act, which was why he reached out to them now.","Song Yi was more than happy to render a helping hand. The Argent King had had only two sons and loved them dearly. Father and sons enjoyed a very close relationship, but his elder brother was timid by nature. He didn’t dare think about revenge, yet that was all that was on Song Yi’s mind. He wanted to kill Yan Guichi and regain his family’s seat!","Great Xia’s positions of titled king were not hereditary. The primary requirement to become one was to be an arcane immortal. The other was for a titled king to perish and for the heavenly book to acknowledge a new one.","If a king perished and there was another arcane immortal within their family, then the position would go to the second arcane immortal. However, that was much easier said than done. There was only one arcane immoral in most titled king households, and it wasn’t that easy for a titled king to die since they were protected by the heavenly book.","Lu Yun had known all of this when he reincarnated through Great Xia. It was a time so far removed from present day that who knew how many Human Emperors had sat on the throne since then?","“Us siblings owe our lives to ole brother Lu and Song Yi regularly looks after us. Since our brother has asked us for help, the only thing for us to do is to say yes,” Ling Chu responded with a glance at Ling Ling. His tone was calm as opposed to being charged with heroism, but the more he was thus, the more at ease Lu Yun was.","“Heh, Song Yi is generous and ole brother Lu is a good guy. Who am I helping if not you guys?” Shi Jian laughed.","“In that case, I thank all of you!” A smile crossed Lu Yun’s face. “I only hope that you’ll help me create a foundation in Great Xia, that I might have a place to stand on when I return.”","“Don’t worry!” Song Yi heartily clapped Lu Yun’s shoulder. He knew he had to ally with others if he wished to take revenge on Yan Guichi. It wasn’t feasible for him to do it by himself. Since the Lus also had a blood feud with Yan Guichi, the two parties stood a chance if they worked together.","As for the gap between the two—the founder of Great Xia had come from nothing and made his way to the top from the humble beginnings of qi refinement. Song Yi and the others had located their fortuitous opportunity in Immortal Burial Valley. They would be able to eliminate Yan Guichi one day when they accumulated sufficient strength.","“I leave these seven in your hands.” Lu Yun glanced at Nan Ting and the other six. “Their methods are bizarre and their potential is limitless. They’re perfect sparring partners.”","Ling Ling narrowed her eyes and looked around rapidly, already debating how to turn the seven inside and out. The brothers could only hang their heads in dread.","They thought very highly of themselves and didn’t think much of even Great Xia nobility. But they were now someone’s henchmen and they didn’t dare think of resisting given Lu Yun’s ray of sword qi in their nascent spirits.","“In that case, this matter cannot be delayed. The four of us will head back first—it’s the perfect time for us to stretch our legs since most of Great Xia’s factions are gathered here!” Ling Chu stood up and took a deep breath, the keen light of wisdom shining in his eyes.","“Alright then, let’s go back right now!” Song Yi concurred. “My elder brother may not have great ambitions, but he’s very good to me. I can borrow our family’s strength for certain things.”","Lu Yun nodded. He’d chosen these four for the factions that stood behind them. Being descendants of nobility, it wouldn’t raise untoward attention that they’d formed a group of their own.","“Very good, go back first and I’ll send more people to help you after a while.” Lu Yun was planning on sending Terra Demon to Great Xia. Building a faction in the immortal dynasty was his predetermined plan—he’d just lacked a spokesperson. Knowing their character, these four were the perfect candidates. They were loyal people who highly valued relationships.","They were grateful to Lu Yun for saving their lives twice. Ling Chu and Shi Jian deciding to sacrifice themselves for the others was the final reason why he chose them.","Ling Chu, Song Yi, Shi Jian, and Ling Ling had located their fortunes in Immortal Burial Valley. Their strength had taken one large step forward and they could not be placed among the ranks of the greatest geniuses of Great Xia.","Nan Ting and his brothers were also premier geniuses. These eleven weren’t the strongest now, but they would truly come into their own if given enough time.","Lu Yun had thought that he was in this world only to experience the vicissitudes of life and experience heavenly dao, but another desire brewed in his heart at this moment.","He wanted to save the world.","It wasn’t just an urge from his sealed memories, but his most direct thoughts in this current moment of time. He wanted to defy the heavens and change destiny.","......","Lu Yun continued toward the east after sending off Ling Chu and the others. The power of fire grew stronger until the void was dyed red.","“This is it! There’s no doubt about it!” Cracks emitting blazing air fissured the ground. This was a zone of a sea of magma. Other cultivators had also discovered the abnormalities of this area—there were no less than one thousand gathered on the premises.","“There’s the aura of a fire of heaven and earth! One of those flames is here!” someone called out, prompting waves of enthusiasm through the crowd. More crowded the depths of this area.","A massive sea of leaping fire could be found at the end; a pinprick of scarlet was particularly eye-catching at its center. Many people regarded it with ardent gazes.","“Good, good, very good!” a handsome young man roared with laughter. Surrounded by three dozen peak awakened cultivators and wearing purple brocade robes, a purple ribbon in his topknot gave him a magnanimous bearing. “It’s the flame ranked third highest on the ranking—the Void Sacred Flame!”","“The Void Sacred Flame!” Lu Yun jumped with shock when he saw the smear of scarlet in the depths of the fiery sea.","The original form of the greatest immortal king in the world of immortals, the Undying Immortal King who answered to the southern immortal emperor, was the Void Sacred Flame! What was it doing here?!","The Eye of Nullification showed clearly that a small flame jumped quietly over a lotus of fire. While it was full of spirituality, it’d yet to form a fire spirit. It was just a pure flame of heaven and earth."]},{"number":2342,"title":"Chapter 2342: Chapter 2220.1: Origination Mountain","paragraphs":["Chapter 2220.1: Origination Mountain","“It’s the Undying Immortal King’s personal weapon, the Luminous Lotus Throne...” Lu Yun took a deep breath. So someone had shattered the Undying Immortal King’s true spirit and it’d returned to its origins to appear here! “What kind of place is this?” The question rose in the young man’s heart.","The sword pagoda belonged to the Mindful Immortal Potentate and Terra Demon once slumbered inside it. The auras of the five immortal kings under the central immortal emperor had appeared here, and the entrance to this place of burial was sealed by the sword pagoda before he claimed it.","“Forget it, I need to get the Void Sacred Flame first.” Lu Yun put everything out of his mind.","Numerous cultivators were already charging for the flame. However, being ranked third on the list of heavenly fires, the Void Sacred Flame’s might could be only described as world-ending. The sea of flames twenty-five kilometers around it was the fire that it was projecting into its surroundings.","Whoosh!","Many flung themselves into the sea. Despite operating incantations to part the flames, they didn’t even have a chance to scream before being reduced to ashes.","“What a bunch of idiots.” The young man in purple didn’t move; he simply sneered at the cultivators fighting each other to fling themselves to their deaths. “It looks like no one can fight me for the Void Sacred Flame.”","A happy smile spread over the young man’s face. “The ninety-ninth prince has gone to the north. He’s the only one in this place of burial who can possibly pose a challenge to me.”","“What should we do, Your Grace?” asked a fawning peak awakened cultivator next to the young man called Yan Beifei.","“Wait for everyone to die. We can collect the flame then.” Yan Beifei crossed his arms over his chest and looked on with amusement.","After the Origin King’s army lost at Dark City, most of them returned to Great Xia. There were only a few who stayed, including Yan Guichi’s youngest son, Yan Beifei.","Yan Beifei and Nalan Tu were the two most accomplished youngsters of the Origin Sect’s younger generation. Both were awakened stage and their potential beyond compare. Yan Beifei was a hair weaker than Nalan Tu, but he was much younger than Nalan Tu.","As much as Yan Guichi doted on his youngest son, he didn’t overly spoil the child. Yan Beifei’s accomplishments were solely due to his own efforts. None of it came from his father.","“Your Grace, look over there!” Another awakened cultivator suddenly pointed at Lu Yun. “That... seems to be Lu Tianling’s grandson!”","“What?!” Yan Beifei shook and snapped his gaze in the relevant direction. “You’re right, it’s Lu Yun! You spurn the avenue to heaven and force your way into hell instead... Since I’ve caught sight of you, Lu Yun, come and meet your fate!”","He ignored the cultivators fighting over the Void Sacred Flame and flew toward the Lu young master.","“Lu Yun! To think that I’d see you here!” Yan Beifei landed right in front of the other and brandished an immortal sword that belched lilac sword light. “Come quietly with me or I’ll break your limbs and cripple your cultivation.”","Three dozen awakened cultivators jointly sealed off the void to reinforce his threat.","“And you are...” Lu Yun frowned, not recognizing the speaker.","“You’ll know who I am when you come with me,” Yan Beifei cackled and didn’t wait for a response. Sword light flashed from his weapon and made for Lu Yun’s head. He knew that this was a rare chance in a thousand years, that it would be beyond difficult to capture Lu Yun after leaving Immortal Burial Valley.","While the Fengxian King said that he’d repaid the Lu family for their favor, he still secretly opposed the Origin King. Thus, the latter didn’t dare openly move against the Lus.","Killing intent flashed through Lu Yun’s eyes. Though he didn’t know who the newcomer was, someone who bore him so much enmity could only come from the Origin King’s side.","“You court death!” Lu Yun twisted into a massive crimson dragon when he saw the sword light and pounced on Yan Beifei.","“I knew you’d do that!” the young man roared with laughter. He stepped through the air and exploded into thousands of images. Each of them erupted with cutting sword light that slashed at Lu Yun.","Pfft pfft pfft!","Lu Yun’s dragon image was eviscerated in less than half a breath. If it wasn’t for him roaming through the air through the Nine Forms of the Cloud Dragon, this move would’ve gravely injured him.","“Void Fissure, Slash!” Yan Beifei’s second technique arrived before Lu Yun could catch his breath.","Purple sword radiance ballooned thirty thousand meters tall and the void trembled with the movement of Yan Beifei’s sword. Hints of what seemed like spatial fissures bubbled up in the air.","Yan Beifei’s just a cultivator, but he’s feeling around the trajectory of the rules and beginning to comprehend his own dao! Lu Yun’s eyes widened. Yan Beifei was an incredible genius!","Someone like him possessed boundless potential and would be one of the most preeminent immortals once he ascended. It was possible that he'd bypass the lower ranks and jump ahead to a mid rank immortal!","The trajectory of the rules was typically accessible after one reached golden immortal. One used a hint of that understanding to slowly set foot on one’s own dao. Yan Beifei’s Void Fissure showed signs of the rules and not the five elements. His was the rule of the void.","He can’t be permitted to live! A cold light flashed through Lu Yun’s eyes as his aura flared and he deployed Fire Slaughter of the Five Elements of Absolute Slaughter. Rays of fiery sword light revolved around him and blocked Yan Beifei’s Void Fissure. At the same time, he was flung back for nearly two hundred meters.","“So strong!” Lu Yun’s arms were slightly numb.","“You blocked a move at sixty percent of my full strength?” Yan Beifei blinked. He wanted to take Lu Yun alive and force Lu Tianling to acquiesce to their demands, so he hadn’t brought his full strength to bear. “You’re Lu Tianling’s grandson alright! Since sixty percent won’t kill you, I’m using my full strength next!”","As his subordinates had sealed off the area with a massive formation, he wasn’t afraid of his quarry getting away. Yan Beifei raised his sword with both hands and slashed at the air. A black fissure grew beneath it, instantaneously cutting through the void and shooting for Lu Yun.","It was only one meter long, but it was a true void fissure. Spatial turbulence could be glimpsed through it and it arrived at its target in one thousandth of a breath.","Pfft!","The fissure ripped the young man apart.","“Oh? That was a fake? Looks like you obtained quite an immortal treasure here.” Yan Beifei wasn’t surprised to see Lu Yun be cut apart. Lu Tianling’s grandson wouldn’t be who he was if he died so easily.","“You comprehended a hint of the trajectory of the rules as an awakened cultivator. You’re stronger than Yan Guichi.” Lu Yun reappeared three hundred meters away from his opponent. “But I’ve seen too many people like you and few are those who can make it to the end.”","“My thoughts precisely,” Yan Beifei answered leisurely instead of flying into a rage. “There have been plenty of perverse geniuses since time immemorial, but even more fall on their way to becoming one of the truly powerful. You will join their numbers today.”","His sword erupted with radiance once more; sword light filled the void like it was a river.","“Void Shift!”","Whoosh!","Under the purple sword light, Lu Yun found the void growing turbulent. There would likely be numerous unexpected outcomes if he tried his Teleportation combat art now. This turbulence was layered onto the void fissure from earlier. “If I can’t dodge it, then I’ll just kill you!”","Humm!","Immortals Forbidden flared with scintillating crimson light. It was as if a blazing sun rose from the air.","The first stroke of the Nine Oscillations of the Heavenly Sword!","Lu Yun utilized another sword dao technique alongside the Nine Oscillations this time—Fire Slaughter! Raging sword qi permeated the air!","A brilliant sun rose, so blindingly bright that it threatened to blind onlookers. Each ray of light was a terrifying beam of sword light that could destroy the world.","Crimson and purple sword light clashed against each other, drawing groaning sounds of overtaxation from the void. Void Shift was a sword technique that threw space into disorder. The Nine Oscillations of the Heavenly Sword melded sword qi into the void. When the two crashed together, the void itself was ripped apart. How else would mere cultivators affect space?","Boom!","The two rays of light negated each other and created a brief vacuum in the air. The energy of heaven and earth was churned to pieces and destroyed.","Cultivators off the battlefield regarded the disturbance with incredulity.","“Who are these two? Can immortals actually come inside, after all?” Some hearts pounded ferociously.","“Who would’ve thought that this level of character would be here... I wonder who they are to fight like this?” Those from Great Xia understood that only perverse geniuses from Great Xia could issue a challenge that would create this kind of commotion. It was a chance to broaden their horizons since fights between this level of genius were far and few in between."]},{"number":2343,"title":"Chapter 2343: Chapter 2220.2: Origination Mountain","paragraphs":["Chapter 2220.2: Origination Mountain","“I’d always thought that our young prince was just slightly less than Nalan Tu. Judging from the situation, Nalan Tu can’t even begin to compare!” An awakened cultivator who’d come with Yan Beifei swallowed hard.","Yan Beifei and Nalan Tu were the twin pride and joys of the Origin Sect. They were both premier geniuses, but Yan Beifei was a hair weaker than Nalan Tu due to his younger age. With Yan Beifei’s full strength on display, however, he was plainly a perverse genius many times stronger than Nalan Tu.","“Lu Yun can stand toe-to-toe with the young prince, no wonder His Majesty is so wary of Lu Tianling!” Another awakened cultivator looked deeply at Lu Yun. “No matter what the result of this battle is, we must leave and notify our lord!”","......","Lu Yun and Yan Beifei both took a step back in the air.","“You can block my Void Shift...” Yan Beifei's expression changed. “I’ve underestimated you.”","“But I haven’t underestimated you. A cultivator who’s comprehended part of the laws of the void does indeed have some skill to his name.” A small smile flashed across Lu Yun’s face—he’d begun to comprehend some of the methods contained in the Nine Oscillations of the Heavenly Sword.","The sword method was greater than the Eighteen Cerulean Sword Dragons and lacked definitive moves. It was one that could be combined and deployed at the same time with other sword techniques. He’d just used it in conjunction with Fire Slaughter, creating a joint move that was more than double the strength of the first stroke of the Nine Oscillations of the Heavenly Sword.","“Then now, the game is over.” Killing intent rose from Lu Yun’s body as Immortals Forbidden disappeared, replaced by a jade-green immortal sword.","“You’re finally willing to use immortal weapons, huh?” Yan Beifei took a deep breath and locked his gaze on Lu Yun.","“First stroke of the Nine Oscillations of the Heavenly Sword, Wood Slaughter!” Lu Yun roared and sent a burst of light from the jade-green sword. A crescent of jade-green light that rivaled the earlier Fire Slaughter hurtled toward Yan Beifei with domineering killing intent.","Having taken root in Lu Yun’s body, the Builder Tree had produced a sapling that bestowed a wood spirit root to the young man—an empyrean wood spirit root!","Thus, his moves of Fire and Wood Slaughter were the strongest that the Five Elements of Absolute Slaughter could bring to bear.","Yan Beifei gravely considered the looming attack and waved his immortal sword in return, sending out rays of purple light.","“Void Fissure!”","Humm!","A crack in the void a meter long grew beneath the sword, a direct answer to Wood Slaughter. Yan Beifei no longer nursed the idea of capturing Lu Yun alive—he wanted to kill the young man where they stood!","Hummm!","Two terrifying sword techniques clashed into each other, creating a tremendous shockwave. The formation that sealed off the void splintered and the awakened cultivators in charge of maintaining it paled with dismay. They scattered in all directions.","Some that didn’t run in time were churned to pieces by the horrific ripples and left with only their immortal souls.","Bam!","The first rank immortal sword in Lu Yun’s hands shattered to pieces.","“Second stroke of the Nine Oscillations of the Heavenly Sword, Fire Slaughter!”","A blazing sun burst forth and rose high over the assembly, throwing off boundless radiance. Immortals Forbidden had reappeared in Lu Yun’s hand at some point. This instance of Fire Slaughter was more than five times stronger than the one earlier due to being overlaid with the first stroke. Wood stoked fire, so the combination of both increased the attack to incredible heights!","The ponderous sun in the air paused for less than a thousandth of a breath before it landed on Yan Beifei.","The latter’s breathing hitched and he stared fixedly at the sun growing larger in his line of vision. Time seemed to stop; ruthless killing intent locked onto him. He would be doomed if he wavered or sought to evade the attack.","Yan Beifei’s purple immortal sword groaned, thin cracks snaking over its blade.","“Void Fissure!” he finally gave voice to an inhuman howl and spat out blood intermixed with spittle. Beads of blood and sweat dotted his skin.","Bam!","His mid immortal rank flying sword exploded into pieces and melted into the void as motes of lilac light. The void burst open into a black hole yawning in front of Yan Beifei. The blazing sun smashed into the hole.","KABOOM!","A tremendous aura washed over everyone as the power of Fire Slaughter, even when removed, still made hearts quail. Yan Beifei spewed out a mouthful of brilliant essence blood and flew backward, breaking uncountable numbers of bones in his body.","“The third stroke of the Nine Oscillations of the Heavenly Sword, Eighteen Cerulean Sword Dragons!” came Lu Yun’s voice again. He gripped his sword with both hands and transformed into a crimson dragon of sword light almost three hundred meters long.","He melded into the void and hovered in and out of sight. The gargantuan body twisted with palpitating killing intent and pounced on the yet reeling Yan Beifei.","The young man was nearly scared out of his wits to see such a massive being bearing down on him, but he didn’t try to stop his momentum. Instead, Yan Beifei grit his teeth and formed hand seals.","“I summon my personal image, Origination Mountain!” The image of a mountain three thousand meters tall appeared over his head, as weighty as an entire world. Instead of protecting its bearer, it flung itself toward the dragon of sword light.","BAM!!","Yan Beifei’s image of heaven and earth crashed into Lu Yun’s Eighteen Cerulean Sword Dragons. It was Lu Yun’s turn to feel blood well up in the back of his throat and vomit scarlet liquid. He was thrown out of his connection with the Eighteen Cerulean Sword Dragons and flew backward.","“Origination Mountain!” Lu Yun nearly lost his mind on the spot. His jaw dropped at the massive mountain’s image.","Origination Mountain was the foremost divine mountain in the world of immortals. Its profound mysteries went beyond comprehension and it rivaled a connate treasure. It’d existed for as long as the world did, and there were people who said that it would yet remain if the world of immortals was no longer.","Origination Mountain symbolized the world of immortals, but here it was, and as someone’s image of heaven and earth!","“Young lord!” A host of awakened cultivators answering to the Origin King rushed to Yan Beifei. They poured a varied assortment of healing pills and medicines into his mouth—Yan Beifei’s injuries healed at a rate visible to the naked eye.","“Lu Yun, I thought I was the ancestor of playing a pig to eat the tiger, but I almost became a real pig in front of you!” Yan Beifei wiped away blood from the corner of his mouth and raised up the mountain with his hand.","He normally kept his full abilities strictly under wraps and presented himself as an ordinary genius of Great Xia. He was a hair weaker than Nalan Tu, a position that brought him neither respect nor contempt. It was the best way to protect himself and prevent others from coming for his head.","The fame and esteem of the Origin Sect’s younger generation was concentrated on Nalan Tu. It was an arrangement perfectly fine for Yan Beifei as few of the perverse geniuses in Great Xia and the endless worlds could truly come into their power.","“You’re the first cultivator to force me into these straits...” Yan Beifei’s injuries were half healed after taking the concoction of pills and medicines. His true origin operated in a nearly berserk fashion, surging into the image over his head.","He stalked toward Lu Yun, one hand still holding up the mountain image. The aura of Origination Mountain spread in a domineering fashion in all directions.","Lu Yun stood up from the ground, Immortals Forbidden glowing dimly. If it wasn’t for its materials being so supreme, this lower dao rank weapon would’ve been destroyed long ago.","Lu Yun wiped off the corner of his mouth and stared coldly at Yan Beifei. “How do you get your hands on the Origination Mountain?”","He could tell that Yan Beifei had more than refined one portion of the mountain—he owned the entire mountain. Rooted in the world of immortals, Origination Mountain would never leave it. If it was here, then the world of immortals...","Sorrow appeared in Lu Yun’s eyes. Of his three thousand lifetimes, he spent the longest time in the world of immortals. To him, it was his second home.","“Hahaha! I’ll tell you when you’re dead!” Yan Beifei roared with laughter when he saw Lu Yun’s expression, but he remained highly alert. “Die!!”","He crossed his arms and brought the massive mountain down on Lu Yun.","“Do you think you’re the only one with an image of heaven and earth?” Lu Yun barked, manifesting an image of a pagoda over his head. Twenty-seven meters tall, it was an iridescent silver throughout and filled the void with sword qi as soon as it appeared.","Though Origination Mountain loomed over the young man, the sword pagoda prevented it from descending one millimeter downward.","The sword pagoda is on the same level as the dao character. As impressive as Origination Mountain is, it’s just a connate treasure. Lu Yun sneered inwardly while goodwill flowed into his body from the Seal of the Multitude, replenishing his steadily decreasing Hongmeng qi.","Light flared from the pagoda and silver sword radiance burst forth.","“Break!” Lu Yun roared and spun in the air. The sword pagoda spun with him like it was a drill and split the Origination Mountain image apart!","“What?!” A cocky sneer still on his face, Yan Beifei’s expression froze.","Bam!!","His heart shook as his image of heaven and earth exploded.","“Pfft!” Yan Beifei spat out a mouthful of blood and drooped. An image’s destruction also recoiled onto the cultivator. As Yan Beifei reeled with shock, the world in front of him was replaced by rays of silver sword qi before he could do anything else."]},{"number":2344,"title":"Chapter 2344: Chapter 2221.1: Execution","paragraphs":["Chapter 2221.1: Execution","The sword pagoda overshadowed Yan Beifei, churning his defensive treasures to shards like they were made of paper.","“Go! Bring word!” he screamed at the last possible second. The followers who were about to rush over to save him jerked to a halt.","Lu Yun’s sword pagoda image was so domineering that awakened cultivators couldn’t even mount a resistance to it. The only course of action available now was to report this to the Origin King Estate and have the king come to a decision.","Yan Beifei’s followers looked at each other and promptly scattered in various directions. Their young lord was as good as dead. They would only needlessly sacrifice themselves if they stayed.","Lu Yun ignored them. Instead of killing his opponent, the entrapped Yan Beifei was retracted into the sword pagoda proper and suppressed. Having secured his victory, Lu Yun breathed out with relief and stood imperiously in the air. White robes fluttered as he regarded the scene with cold eyes.","Nearby cultivators couldn’t help a shudder and uniformly take a step back.","“Who is that young man and what was that golden pagoda? Even immortals would die if they were here, wouldn’t they?” murmured a combination cultivator with a hard swallow","“Is he one of the legendary Great Xia powerhouses? But he’s just soul separation... Great Xia is truly a place that we all yearn for.” Some peak awakened cultivators looked ardently at Lu Yun. Once those from worlds of cultivation ascended to immortality, they had the right to enter another world—Great Xia.","It was a world no different from the world of immortals to these cultivators—a place both mysterious and sacred.","......","Lu Yun looked upon the fiery sea raging with waves. Numerous cultivators were battling in the flaming waters, fighting over the Void Sacred Flame.","Immensely capable heavyweights abounded in Great Xia. Although the Void Sacred Flame was ranked number three on the ranking of heavenly fires, this one was far below what it should be, so cultivators would be able to subdue it through special methods.","Ten cultivators dueled in the fiery sea, one of them wearing long scarlet robes and sporting red hair and beard. He laid about like a tiger, directing the flames within the sea to follow his command.","“A mere Jade Ruins Realm cultivator dares fight us for the heavenly flame? You court death!” A middle-aged man in a set of immortal rank armor flicked a glance at the red-haired elder. Black hair and a black beard framed a contemptuous curve of his lips.","“Ji Lin, I recommend you stand down. You won’t be able to hold onto the flame even if you obtain it. It might drag in your Primordial Empire!” sniffed another Great Xia cultivator.","“Bah, are Great Xia cultivators supposed to be impressive?” As wizened as Ji Lin looked, he stood upright with pride.","Ji Lin was one of the premier geniuses of the Primordial Empire. Though his potential was so mediocre that it’d taken him several hundred years to coalesce his nascent soul, his cultivation speed was unmatched after that. He endured his heavenly tribulation in less than twenty years and reached awakened realm.","His rate of ascension was incredibly fast and comprehension of dao methods so incredible that he was ranked number ten on the Jade Ruins Celestial Battlefront Rankings. The population sizes of worlds of cultivation were counted in units of hundred millions. Being ranked in the top ten was more than evident of his talent.","Ji Lin swung a flaming spear around, directing the fiery sea to surge wherever he pointed it and sweeping out other cultivators here to fight over the flame.","“Great Xia cultivators? Impressive?” snorted the Great Xia cultivator in armor. “I’ll destroy your Primordial Empire for sheer disrespect alone when I leave this place!”","While the speaker’s position in Great Xia wasn’t humble by any means, his cultivation was mediocre. He was only combination stage and far weaker than Ling Chu and the others. His treasures, however, were all paramount rank and his immortal rank armor a third rank immortal treasure. The fiery sea would be too much for him otherwise.","“Hahaha!!” Ji Lin regarded the combination cultivator with disdain. “Destroy Primordial Empire? Nothing will save you if it really falls, not even one of the Great Xia marquises!”","“Oh?” Some of the nearby cultivators blinked when they heard his response and subconsciously slowed their movements.","“It so happens that there is a Great Xia marquis behind me!” The combination cultivation laughed arrogantly. “I, Xia Houwan, am the only grandson of Marquis Skyrule! Let’s see who dares make trouble for me after I raze your Primordial Empire!”","Xia Houwan thought nothing of the threat and raised a long streak of sword light from his third rank immortal sword, bringing it down on Ji Lin.","Marquis Skyrule Xia Houyun was once ranked number two among all Great Xia marquises. After Marquis Origin became the Origin King, Skyrule was elevated to the position of foremost marquis. Profoundly strong, he was known for being extremely prejudiced toward his own. Having only one son and one daughter, his daughter married the son of the Truefall King.","His son died early, leaving only Xia Houwan behind. Xia Houyun naturally doted on his grandson like no other—he once eliminated a sect with a golden immortal in residence simply because his grandson wanted the sect leader’s daughter.","“Marquis Skyrule?” Ji Lin’s expression tightened with concentration. “Hah, some Jade Ruins cultivators will enroll in the Great Xia Dao Academy in the near future. If you cause trouble at this juncture, the Dao Academy will show no face to your grandfather when it’s time for a reckoning.”","“Future Dao Academy disciples?” Xia Houwan jerked and his face darkened. The other cultivators around him likewise stilled.","The Dao Academy held utmost authority in Great Xia. Even the Human Emperor respected it. It would be the flip of a hand if the academy wished to depose a marquis.","The Great Xia Dao Academy recruited disciples from the three thousand worlds of cultivation every one hundred years. No Great Xia cultivator dared cause trouble in these worlds during that time as death would be a luxury if things got out of hand.","“I see...” Although Xia Houwan was a good-for-nothing, he was no fool. There was no need to get on the Dao Academy’s bad side. He said nothing further, instead waving to his comrades and charging Ji Lin.","They could all tell that if they didn’t eliminate Ji Lin, none of them stood a chance to obtain the Void Sacred Flame. The elder must have encountered a bizarre opportunity in this place of burial that gave him the ability to control the elements.","While the elder was indeed a genius, he paled in comparison to Great Xia cultivators prior to his stroke of fortune. Xia Houwan himself would be sufficient to kill the man, to say nothing of Ji Lin fighting ten Great Xia cultivators by himself.","As subpar as Xia Houwan was, he was still from the immortal dynasty. Third rank immortal treasures glittered over his form; they were more than enough to overwhelm Ji Lin.","However, Ji Lin was latter awakened stage and he was more than ten times stronger than before. This wasn’t due to a particular treasure, but a metamorphosis from inside out. The elder’s blazing spear was as if a dragon of fire, rampaging through the fiery sea like it was water.","Pfft!","He ran through an awakened cultivator in front of him with a muffled sound. Flames spat from the spear and pulverized the body, consuming an immortal soul before it had time to escape.","“Die!!” True origin blazed and a pillar of crimson flames shot out from Ji Lin’s body. He seemed to be on fire as he charged at Xia Houwan.","Paling, the man quickly hastily formed hand seals. His immortal armor sparkled with light as he barely managed to block the harrowing stroke.","“Little marquis, you would be dead if I actually wanted to kill you.” Ji Lin floated away, landing within thirty meters of the Void Sacred Flame.","“Hmph!” Xia Houwan’s expression was unpleasant. He’d also detected that if it wasn’t for Ji Lin pulling his strength, his immortal armor would already be punctured through.","“Hahaha! We meet again, Ji Lin!” A sinister cackle echoed through the air as a young man dressed in long green robes floated out of the sea. He had inky-green hair that reached his waist and even his pupils were green.","“Bi Chen!” Ji Lin was not pleased to see the newcomer.","Bi Chen was one of the three strongest powerhouses of the Jade Ruins Realm, the master of the Barren Mountains. While Ji Lin was much stronger than before, he was still quite wary of one of the three greatest of the realm.","“What, you don’t seem happy to see this seat.” Chen Bi flicked out his long forked tongue and licked his nose. “It looks like the memories from my heritage are right, this is indeed the Void Sacred Flame, heh heh heh...”","A faint thread of red shone out of his inky-green hair and eyes. It wasn’t a reflection of the fiery sea, but a subtle change in his body.","“This must be the grandson of Marquis Skyrule of Great Xia. Xia Houwan, do you think your grandfather would lose his mind if this seat kills you?” A crimson rod appeared in Bi Chen’s hand. There were nine knots on it, like it was the spine of a certain animal.","“You can try!” Violence flashed through Xia Houwan’s eyes and the dozen cultivators they’d come with hovered in front of him, protecting the man. While they weren’t part of Marquis Skyrule’s faction, they didn’t mind doing the marquis a favor."]},{"number":2345,"title":"Chapter 2345: Chapter 2221.2: Execution","paragraphs":["Chapter 2221.2: Execution","“Hahahaha!!” Bi Chen threw his head back with laughter to see the cultivators so nervous, utter glee in his heart. He’d been depressed ever since an ignoble brat by the name of Lu Yun had beaten him in Dark City. Now that he was able to vent his spleen on formidable Great Xia cultivators, it soothed him from head to toe.","“Very well, let me try!” Bi Chen was a monster spirit and completely unbridled in his style. Others might fear Marquis Skyrule, he did not. He’d kill whoever he wanted and damn the consequences.","A crimson dragon shadow surged around his body and slowly sharpened into focus. It was three hundred meters long and replete with claws and scales, but there were no dragon horns on its head. It was the image of a chi-dragon.","Chi-dragons were a cadet branch of the dragon bloodline. They were less than their draconic cousins, but they were still divine beasts.","The fiery sea jerked in a bizarre direction when the scaled-dragon image formed and created a fiery vortex that wrapped around Bi Chen.","“It’s the bloodline of the divine beast chi-dragon! He’s fully activated it!” Xia Houwan gasped with dismay. The cultivators around him backed away as the power emitted by the chi-dragon shadow was too enormous to bear.","Of the draconic cadet branches, ying-dragons controlled water, qiu-dragons controlled lightning, chi-dragons controlled fire... Since Bi Chen had the chi-dragon bloodline in him, this fiery sea was his domain.","He was in full control of the tossing waves. The previously docile sea erupted like a volcano.","“Damn it, stop!” Ji Lin yelled. Xia Houwan would be dead without a doubt if the fiery sea raged out of control. If he died, then Marquis Skyrule might very well punish the Jade Ruins cultivators, given his personality.","Although he would ultimately be curtailed by the Dao Academy, many in the realm would have to suffer first before he was brought to heel.","Thus, Ji Lin didn’t hesitate to raise his spear and stir up a wave of fire, stabbing the weapon at Bi Chen’s chest. If things were as if before, Ji Lin would cower in front of Bi Chen and not even dare raise his voice. He was absolutely no match for the other.","But after his cultivation took a great leap forward thanks to the fortuitous encounter in the place of burial, he no longer feared Bi Chen.","“How dare you raise your hand against this seat, Ji Lin!” Bi Chen snorted at Ji Lin and raised a singular claw, probing the air. A massive flaming draconic claw came for Ji Lin.","However, the other was unafraid. He shook his spear and flung the claw away. The fiery sea surged at the same time and countless flames gathered in his direction.","“Oh?” Bi Chen frowned. Ji Lin’s command over fire rivaled his!","Whoosh whoosh whoosh!","Blazing waves reared in the fiery sea. Flaming vortexes surrounded both Bi Chen and Ji Lin. All of the flames within a half dozen kilometers were gathered on them. The terrifying ripples flung Xia Houwan and the others out. Their true origin was in disarray and they didn’t dare linger; they ran for their lives.","As precious as the Void Sacred Flame was, one needed to be alive to enjoy it.","Bi Chen ignored the scurrying Xia Houwan and others. Someone like the marquis’ grandson could be killed at any time. He didn’t think much of Marquis Skyrule either. Given enough time, even the marquis was but a reptile to a dragon.","His priority at the moment was the Void Sacred Flame.","Bi Chen and Ji Lin were like two walking pillars of flame as they continuously crashed into each other. Horrific waves of heat lashed out through the area, prompting the other cultivators to flee for their lives. They didn’t dare remain for a second longer.","......","“Who would’ve thought that Bi Chen wouldn’t be able to stay out of it.” Lu Yun stood in the air beyond the fiery sea. The sea seemed to have formed its own space as his battle with Yan Beifei hadn’t affected it. The cultivators inside hadn’t even noticed anything taking place outside.","Lu Yun had discovered the concealed Bi Chen early on, but he hadn’t expected that the monster spirit would fully activate his chi-dragon bloodline. With that step complete, Bi Chen was now evolving in the direction of the chi-dragon divine beast and had received its heritage memories.","Divine beasts with access to the memories of their heritage were a walking trove of knowledge. But Bi Chen wasn’t a true chi-dragon, so he didn’t receive many memories. Otherwise, he would’ve already executed Ji Lin.","......","“That bastard Yan Beifei’s going to laugh at me after this!” Xia Houwan cursed after he escaped from the sea of flames. “Eh? Where’s that little bastard?”","He scanned the premises, but saw no sign of Yan Beifei. The sea behind him flared at this moment and Xia Houwan shuddered, hastily operating his true origin to activate his immortal armor and block the wave. At the same time, he retrieved a handful of pills and medicines from his storage ring and stuffed all of them into his mouth.","“This Xia Houwan is quite a character—he’s a bit like the former me.” Lu Yun saw hints of his prodigal self in the Great Xia cultivator.","“Oi, you floating in the air. Have you seen an over-the-top guy strutting around in purple robes?”","There were no other cultivators around given the flames howling through the void. Lu Yun particularly stood out as he hovered in the air.","“An over-the-top guy strutting around in purple robes?” Lu Yun blinked, then thought of Yan Beifei’s previous appearance and chuckled. “I did! His mom missed him, so he went home for dinner.”","“What?” Xia Houwan blinked and subconsciously looked around. “Yan Beifei’s mom? Are you kidding me?”","Lu Yun spread his hands out and ignored the man. The fiery sea chose to explode at this time, making way for two beasts.","“Heavens above!” Xia Houwan yelped and ran off.","“It looks like your mom misses you too,” Lu Yun chortled as he watched the man leave. Immortals Forbidden flashed in his hand.","A jade-green dragon three hundred meters long with crimson motes sparkling between its scales snaked through the air. It gripped a stick one meter wide and thirty meters long in its hand, waving it with abandon. Blurry afterimages filled the air, forming a massive formation that confined the beast in front of him.","His opponent was one hundred and fifty meters tall with scarlet scales throughout. Its head was like a horse, eyes like a lion’s, body like a deer, and back like a tiger’s. Cow hooves held it up and a dragon tail flicked behind it. It burned with flames—the divine fire qilin.","However, its form wasn’t very precise—it seemed to be a shadow that’d yet to fully solidify. Standing on its head, Ji Lin wielded a spear that glittered with cold radiance and swept the stick shadows aside.","“Oh damn, Ji Lin’s obtained the inner core of a fire qilin and refined it into his own image of heaven and earth!” Lu Yun smacked his lips with amazement.","Fire qilin differed from dragons and phoenixes in that the latter could transform into monster spirits and cast off their beast form. The original form of qilins, however, was incredibly strong. They retained their original appearance even when they ascended to chaos immortal.","Of the divine beasts, the physical durability of the qilins was ranked the highest.","There were many avenues for cultivators to refine an image; most of them utilized treasures. Another way was to employ the inner core of a divine beast and activate its internal spirit. At the same time, it was a very dangerous process as backlash could hit the cultivator in a single moment of carelessness. Their mind would be erased and they’d become a spirit beast lacking sentience.","Ji Lin was extremely lucky to obtain the inner core and successfully refine it. Having a qilin as his personal image meant that his road ahead was bright with limitless possibilities.","Two divine beasts continuously clashed against each other in the air and raised waves of fire. While Ji Lin possessed a powerful image, Bi Chen had fully activated his divine beast bloodline, so that still made him stronger than his opponent.","Despite his superior strength, it wasn’t easy for him to take down Ji Lin.","“Two idiots having it out.” Lu Yun couldn’t be bothered with the two brawling in the air. He shifted into multiple afterimages, evading the heat waves to arrive in front of the Void Sacred Flame.","It was the size of a palm and red throughout, emanating a shocking temperature. A ninth rank lotus flower formed from flames rested beneath it. One meter across, it was the Undying Immortal King’s personal treasure—Luminous Lotus Throne.","“This Void Sacred Flame should be his primary body... What a pity that the strongest immortal king of the world of immortals would die here.” Lu Yun sighed and was about to collect the flame and treasure when he suddenly sensed two heat waves come for him. He subconsciously dodged twice and evaded two attacks by the skin of his teeth.","“I wondered who would be so bold as to try to steal treasure out from beneath our nose! So it’s you!!” Bi Chen nearly spat fire from his eyes to see Lu Yun. The crimson dots of light over his body intensified and he twisted in the young man’s direction.","He hated Lu Yun the most—the human bastard had swallowed one hundred thousand Barren Mountain monster spirits with a single formation! He’d even scared off Bi Chen!","Ji Lin was likewise livid as he had made up his mind to obtain the Void Sacred Flame. How dare a mere soul separation cultivator try to take advantage of the chaos!","Thus, the two divine beasts reached an unspoken accord to eliminate Lu Yun first."]},{"number":2346,"title":"Chapter 2346: Chapter 2222.1: The Primary Body of the Immortal King","paragraphs":["Chapter 2222.1: The Primary Body of the Immortal King","“These two damned shameless old farts!” Lu Yun cursed to see the two come for him instead. He altered his footwork to evade Ji Lin’s attack once more and flung out Immortals Forbidden. It exploded into rays of sword radiance and enveloped Bi Chen.","“A lower dao rank weapon won’t even break this seat’s defenses!” Contempt dawned in Bi Chen’s eyes and he came straight for the human, not bothering to dodge the response.","Pfft pfft pfft!","The crimson sword light instantly pierced through Bi Chen’s armor and sprayed blood through the air amidst his anguished howls.","“You dare take my sword light straight on?” Lu Yun sneered at the divine beast almost flayed alive in the air.","“A sword cultivator!” Ji Lin gasped and hastily dismissed his own momentum. He stood on top of the fire qilin image and looked warily at Lu Yun.","Flying swords were the easiest treasure to master; flying through the air on a sword was almost the hallmark of a cultivator. While many possessed a flying sword, they used it only as any other treasure. Few were those who truly walked the way of the sword.","Sword cultivators condensed sword qi and possessed devastating attacks. Even their true origin was uncommonly sharp.","In the world of immortals, Lu Yun practiced the Reincarnation Record of the Major Five Elements Demolition Godslayer Record. His immortal soul had been a sword soul and his immortal origin the strongly offensive sword origin.","The current Lu Yun practiced the Nine Chapters of Dao and coalesced Hongmeng true qi. He was not a sword cultivator. However, he received the sword pagoda’s strength after refining it as his image of heaven and earth, making his sword light uncommonly keen. It stood on the same footing as real sword cultivators.","Sword cultivators were incredibly rare—even Yun Shuige, one who’d comprehended the height of man and sword as one, was not one. It wouldn’t have been that easy for Lu Yun to kill him otherwise.","Sword cultivators were also unmatched in speed. They could easily ensure their escape if they found themselves on the losing side.","Ji Lin knew he was no match for the young man after seeing Bi Chen injured with one stroke. But he must have the Void Sacred Flame! Thus, he subconsciously turned toward Bi Chen.","The divine beast had recovered his human form and his green eyes were now fully bloodshot. As time went on, more and more of his chi-dragon bloodline was released in his body. He was drenched with blood, but battle intent glinted out of his eyes. Lu Yun had become his internal demon and it would not disappear unless the young man died. Bi Chen would never reach immortality so long as his internal demon existed.","Thus, the divine beast ignored Ji Lin and swung his stick around, smashing it down on Lu Yun with numerous afterimages.","Having evolved into a divine beast, Bi Chen’s physical body was unparalleled. His core essence remained unharmed despite being pierced through by multiple rays of sword light. This kind of injury was nothing to him.","The stick transformed into thousands of draconic shadows that devoured Lu Yun’s body.","“Open!” shouted the young man. Light shimmered over Immortals Forbidden in response and circulated around his body, rebuffing the draconic shadows.","Ji Lin brandished his spear without hesitation and streaked into a crimson blur of shadow and light, aiming for Lu Yun’s chest. His fire qilin image also moved, swallowing its master. Its maw yawned open as it also came for Lu Yun.","Ji Lin knew that he stood a chance of seizing the Void Sacred Flame from Bi Chen, but he stood no chance whatsoever if it came to the young man. If Lu Yun’s blow had connected with him instead, Ji Lin’s body would’ve collapsed and his nascent soul have to flee for its life.","Thus, he smartly chose to ally with Bi Chen for the immediate present.","Exuding a terrifying aura, the qilin image pounced on Lu Yun.","“He’s combined his spear method with the qilin image! Nice going, Yun Shuige won’t be worth shit if this guy has enough time to develop!” Lu Yun flashed in and out of sight, deploying the Nine Forms of the Cloud Dragon nine times. Eighty-one shadows winked in and out of the air, dodging Bi Chen’s attacks. Ji Lin’s fiery spear, however, locked onto Lu Yun’s primary body under the cover of the qilin image.","As the image broke through the air, its terrifying aura caused the void to coagulate.","“Break!” Lu Yun twisted into a crimson dragon twenty-seven meters long. Sword light circled around it as it crashed into the qilin.","Bam!!","Lu Yun’s crimson dragon was as if a massive drill, puncturing the qilin straight through. Ji Lin was dislodged from the image when it broke and fell out.","The core essence of Ji Lin’s image of heaven and earth was the inner core of the fire qilin. It was one that he could access only through compelling the inner core. He hadn’t had enough time to assimilate it into himself and bring the true power of the qilin image to bear.","At the same time, this meant that Ji Lin didn’t suffer any injuries when the image broke.","“What an incredible sword technique!” He sucked in a sharp breath and tightly gripped his spear, fixing his eyes on the crimson dragon rampaging through the air. His throat bobbed up and down as he watched.","Meanwhile, Bi Chen had gone completely berserk. His red stick transformed into a red dragon three hundred meters long that howled at Lu Yun.","The young man brought the Eighteen Cerulean Sword Dragons to bear again—once more deploying it alongside the Nine Forms of the Cloud Dragon. The two overlaid combat arts gave rise to nine draconic shadows flashing through the air. They smashed into the red dragon in front of them.","Bam!","The red dragon flew backward with an anguished howl, but Lu Yun also wavered on his feet. He looked at Bi Chen with astonishment.","“This is a treasure refined from the spine of a true dragon, no wonder Bi Chen can activate the chi-dragon bloodline in his body!” he gasped. These two were simply too lucky! One had obtained the inner core of a qilin and the other the spine of a true dragon! It would seem that the treasures within Immortal Burial Valley were much more than he thought.","“ROAR!” The qilin snarled behind Lu Yun as it moved forward again. It came atop a wave of flame as it charged the young man.","These two guys are only a hair weaker than Yun Shuige now. They’d be incredible geniuses in Great Xia! Lu Yun silently gave his assessment of the two divine beasts. He showed no mercy in his response—a ball of scarlet aura bloomed around his body, making it seem like he was on fire.","“The Reincarnation of the Five Elements—Flame Reincarnation!”","Immortals Forbidden flared with radiance, becoming the heart of this void and a true sun. A crimson wheel of light three hundred meters across condensed over Lu Yun’s head. Unbidden, the flames in the void drew close to the wheel of light. Even the quietly burning Void Sacred Flame tilted in Lu Yun’s direction.","But in the next moment, Hongmeng qi circulated and blasted the Connate Great Dao of the Five Elements in all directions. The young man reached a hand into the void, eliciting a burst of golden radiance from the Void Sacred Flame. It was instantly summoned to the crimson wheel over his head and absorbed within.","Humm!","The void turned into one of complete fire. All of the other five elements, even the ambient qi in the surroundings, were forced out by the terrifying flames.","The Flame Reincarnation of the Reincarnation of the Five Elements!","There was the Five Elements of Absolute Slaughter in the Major Five Elements Demolition Godslayer Record, and the Reincarnation of the Five Elements was the advanced version of the Major Five Elements Demolition Godslayer Record in the Reincarnation of the Major Five Elements Record.","When Flame Reincarnation was deployed, all heavenly and earthly flames were available for the wilderness's use!","“It looks like I’ve much underestimated the Reincarnation of the Major Five Elements Record... It’s a method from the Reincarnation Disk connate treasure after all.”","Reincarnation...","Lu Yun licked his lips. The Flame Reincarnation he deployed at present rivaled the second stroke of the Nine Oscillations of the Heavenly Sword and surpassed the Eighteen Cerulean Sword Dragons!","This wasn’t due to the Eighteen Cerulean Sword Dragons being inferior to Flame Reincarnation, but that the latter had been one of Lu Yun’s five great technique aces in the world of immortals. He’d also long comprehend the true meaning of Fire Reincarnation.","As mighty as the Eighteen Cerulean Sword Dragons was, Lu Yun hadn’t practiced it for long and the ray of sword qi within his dantian wasn’t strong enough, to say nothing of grasping the true meaning behind this move.","“Kill!” Lu Yun roared and struck with both hands around his sword. The enormous wheel of fire shifted with him, spraying rays of cutting qi in all directions and filling the air. Combined with the Void Sacred Flame, the earth beneath them was turned into magma.","“Damn it, he’s definitely Lu Tianling’s grandson! Lu Tianling is a perverse talent and this kid is even more so!” Bi Chen shook, blood pouring out of his body. Someone as sturdy as him was gravely injured before the sword qi even reached him!","He didn’t dare take the attack head-on. The dragon bone stick in his hand transformed into a red dragon that twined protectively around his body and broke through the void in a hasty retreat.","Ji Lin was in even worse shape. His body had nearly collapsed under Flame Reincarnation. Despair dawned in his eyes to see the wheel of light about to reach his head. However, he trembled a second before annihilation as a blazing inner core flew out of his body. It transformed into the image of a fire qilin and melded with the qilin image over his head!","Astonished delight shone from his eyes. He fully refined the qilin inner core in this moment of life and death and incorporated it into his image!","Ji Lin’s fingers flew through hand seals and summoned the image back into himself as a streak of light. Fiery radiance enveloped him and vanished into the air.","BOOM!","The fiery wheel descended upon the earth and drowned the void. Lu Yun’s figure appeared several kilometers out.","“Flame Reincarnation is strong enough, but it’s too slow,” the young man tutted. “So Ji Lin fully refined that inner core in the last possible second. He should actually be thanking me, shouldn’t he...”"]},{"number":2347,"title":"Chapter 2347: Chapter 2222.2: The Primary Body of the Immortal King","paragraphs":["Chapter 2222.2: The Primary Body of the Immortal King","Golden light flashed through Lu Yun’s eyes as he gazed upon everything within fifty kilometers. He saw Ji Lin and Bi Chen fleeing with their fiery tails between their legs. They were fifty kilometers away in less than five breaths.","Lu Yun didn’t go after them. Bi Chen was useful alive and since Ji Lin had gotten away... well, he could keep his life. It was too much of a hassle to go after him. Besides, he was a Jade Ruins cultivator. He might very well become Lu Yun’s subordinate in the future.","Lu Yun spread out his right hand to look at a scarlet flame interspersed with gold flecks dancing in his palm. This was the original form of the Void Sacred Flame.","“Does this flame contain the Crimson Emperor Chapter of Inception? Is it the item that senior brother spoke of?” Lu Yun scanned it with the Eye of Nullification. “Wait, it really is in here!”","The heavenly dao combat art detected runes exuding profound presence jumping within the flame. They seemed to speak of an unparalleled great dao, one that felt very similar to the bamboo stick that Sky had given his junior brother.","The Crimson Emperor Chapter of Inception!","Lu Yun smiled faintly, he’d finally attained his goal for this trip. He moved to the Luminous Lotus Throne with a waver of his body.","“The personal treasure of the Undying Immortal King is the connate treasure that manifested his primary body...” Lu Yun easily discerned the relationship between the Void Sacred Flame and the Luminous Lotus Throne that was a connate treasure.","“This kills two birds with one stone! Although the Luminous Lotus Throne is just a connate treasure and thus less than the Reincarnation Disk or Seal of the Multitude, it’s very strong for its rank.” Lu Yun smiled faintly. “Second uncle has reached the latter stage of his cultivation. He needs a treasure for his image of heaven and earth when he breaks through to soul separation. This is perfect!”","He casually tucked the Luminous Lotus Throne away. While Lu Xiaochi had previously reached soul separation, his nascent soul and image of heaven and earth had been destroyed by a domineering powerhouse during that great battle. He needed to refine his image anew.","Connate treasures were few and far in between. Apart from the five immortal emperors, only a few chaos immortals in the world of immortals possessed any. Most of those were refined into images of heaven and earth, becoming part of their body.","The Undying Immortal King was a monster spirit immortal, blessed with domineering potential but unable to coalesce an image of heaven and earth. Thus, he’d used this Luminous Lotus Throne as his personal treasure. That they came from the same roots perfectly concealed the connate treasure aura from the lotus. Otherwise, some of the wandering chaos immortals would’ve made a play for it.","“I wonder if second uncle can comprehend the Reincarnation of the Major Five Elements Record from the Major Five Elements Demolition Godslayer Record.” Lu Yun scratched his head with uncertainty.","The Major Five Elements Demolition Godslayer Record was a premier method of the world of immortals, but its killing intent was so intense that if one was turned into a killing puppet if the cultivator's concentration relaxed for a single moment.","Lu Yun had nearly been controlled by this method in the world of immortals. Thankfully, he comprehended the Reincarnation of the Five Elements at a critical moment and disengaged from the overwhelming emotions of slaughter.","“Second uncle’s cultivation is too weak for now, he won’t arouse the will of slaughter,” Lu Yun murmured to himself before he vanished from the locale.","......","Ji Lin rematerialized in the depths of the place of burial. Pale as a ghost, relief and gratification shown in his eyes.","“Thank goodness I fully refined the inner core and comprehended the combat arts of the qilin in the last possible second. I would really be dead this time otherwise.” Ji Lin stroked his cheek. His unusually wizened face was now that of a young man’s. Completely refining the qilin inner core meant that his physical body was tempered by the core’s essence. His haggard body was returned to its youth.","“I’ve actually benefited from disaster. My strength will take another step forward after I heal from my injuries. It’ll be a bit more likely then that I can join the Great Xia Dao Academy.” Ji Lin wiped away a trace of blood from the corner of his mouth and gave his surroundings a cursory look.","He was in the ruins of a massive palace; broken walls and shattered buildings could be seen everywhere. Some of the vicious spirits roaming through the area immediately pounced on Ji Lin when they saw him land.","His spear flashed through his hand and tapped each of their blood runes. The vicious spirits were thus executed before they could begin to terrorize their new quarry.","“These things are damned terrifying. Thank goodness the unknown powerhouse made their weakness public.” Ji Lin wiped away beads of sweat from his forehead. He’d been part of the first batch of cultivators to enter the formation array and was well acquainted with the horrors of the spirits after watching others be turned one by one.","If they weren’t executed in one stroke and dogged the cultivator’s footsteps, it was then a difficult task to escape from them. The ones who were blood-red throughout were particularly horrifying. They were more formidable than the spirits mutated from cultivators.","“Ji Lin, we meet again!” A voice echoed over Ji Lin’s head just as he relaxed.","“Bi Chen!” Ji Lin narrowed his eyes, tightening his grip on his spear. He’d been wary of Bi Chen moments before, but had nothing to fear after fully refining the qilin’s image. He would be able to triumph against even empyrean immortals so long as he didn’t run into someone as heaven-defying as Lu Yun.","“Hahaha, Ji Lin, you’re getting ever more bold after obtaining the qilin inner core. How dare you directly use my name!”","Ji Lin sneered and pointed his spear at Bi Chen.","“Hand over the inner core and I’ll spare your life!” Bi Chen looked down on Ji Lin, contempt in his eyes. The latter was gravely injured and his aura in disarray. Bi Chen himself had relied on the sheer durability of his body to avoid severe injuries from Lu Yun’s last blow. Ji Lin, however, was a fragile human and just the aura from the flame wheel alone had shattered his meridians.","“Hmph, come get it if you’re so able!” Ji Lin took a deep breath and forced his true origin to rise and suppress his internal injuries.","“Then die!” Bi Chen waved his stick around and summoned fiery dragons out of the void that pounced on Ji Lin.","The latter raised his spear and summoned his qilin image, throwing himself on the fiery dragons.","BAM!","The qilin image shattered and Ji Lin spat out blood intermixed with pieces of his organs. He flew backward, unable to do anything against a new dragon from Bi Chen’s stick. Sorrow flashed through his widened eyes.","I hope Mo Ran can take care of himself... The thought lingered in his mind.","Silence descended upon heaven and earth, as if time had paused. A black figure had appeared in front of Ji Lin at some point and grabbed the fiery dragon. The dragon that was several dozen meters long froze in his grasp and Bi Chen found his blood freezing in his veins. His true origin sank like lead in his meridians; he fell straight down from the sky.","“How dare you attack my master... Do you want to die, reptile?!” rasped a voice shot through with anger.","“Mo Ran?” Ji Lin struggled to his feet, looking incredulously at the figure in front of him.","“Master!” A smile blossomed over the ugly young man’s face and he quickly took out a pill flask, emptying it into Ji Lin’s mouth. Color instantly returned to the man’s wan complexion and his wounds fully healed!","“This...” Ji Lin gaped. Not even healing pills had such incredible effects! “Are you really Mo Ran?” He stared dumbly at the young man in front of him. Although it was the same familiar ugly sight, there was a refreshing presence about him.","“It’s me!” Mo Ran nodded.","Five hundred years ago, he’d lived on the streets as a child bereft of all cultivation. He met the already-renowned Ji Lin just when he was about to die from starvation. Pity rose in the man and he took in the young man that everyone disliked, teaching him how to cultivate.","What delighted Ji Lin was that Mo Ran’s potential was profound. He successively broke through in five years and reached soul separation, drawing ever greater affection from his master. The scene in front of him at the moment, however, stunned Ji Lin.","Bi Chen was already able to hold his ground against empyrean immortals before he obtained the dragon spine. After he found it and activated his chi-dragon bloodline, the law enforcers of the Jade Ruins Realm were no match for him.","But Ji Lin’s disciple had immobilized the other with one blow!","Had Mo Ran encountered some heaven-defying heritage in this place of burial? Ji Lin heaved a sigh of relief and smiled, truly happy for the child.","Killing intent brimmed in Mo Ran’s eyes as he stalked toward the crumbled Bi Chen.","“Reptile, this young master has a set of principles.” Mo Ran’s tone was frosty and its grating qualities turned even more vicious given his current mood. “First, I can kill you and refine you into a treasure. You will burn day and night with the fires of tribulation and never find release!”","Bi Chen narrowed his eyes and suddenly shrugged off the black light around him, throwing himself at Mo Ran.","Bam!","Mo Ran smacked Bi Chen to the ground like he was shooing a fly and stepped on the latter’s face.","“Two, become my master’s soul pet and answer his every command!”","Half of Bi Chen’s face was already ground into the dirt; his eyeballs threatened to pop from the massive pressure."]},{"number":2348,"title":"Chapter 2348: Chapter 2223.1: Tai Sui Immortal King","paragraphs":["Chapter 2223.1: Tai Sui Immortal King","Tai Sui is a Chinese term for the stars directly opposite the planet Jupiter during its roughly 12-year orbital cycle. Personified as deities, they are important features of Chinese astrology, feng shui, Taoism, and Buddhism to a lesser extent.","Ouyang Shengtian tumbled out of a hiding place with the blackwater snake king in tow.","“Master, this guy has draconic bloodline in him. If he doesn’t agree, let’s use his mind to refine a treasure and feed his body and nascent soul to Little Black!” Ouyang Shengtian smiled fawningly. He’d fully witnessed the depths of the ugly young man’s capabilities over the past several days and no longer entertained the slightest notion of resistance.","Bi Chen was renowned throughout Jade Ruins Realm for being one of the three major powerhouses, but he was as if a reptile in front of Mo Ran. He couldn’t even withstand one move!","With Ouyang Shengtian’s level of cultivation, he would’ve been devoured by a host of vicious spirits long ago if not for Mo Ran’s protection. What he focused his efforts on now was feeding suggestions in his master’s ears everyday, wanting him to look for Lu Yun.","He’d completely relinquished his dignity as the eldest young master of the Ouyang Clan and placed himself in the role of Mo Ran’s butler. Having refined the immortal soul of a Great Xia wandering immortal, he knew full well how terrifying Mo Ran’s background was.","Serving his master well would help him ascend to the skies with one leap and put revenge for his family within sight.","“Mmhmm, mmhmm, Ouyang’s right. If you’re not willing to be my master’s pet, I’ll use your mind to refine a treasure and feed the rest of you to Little Black.” Mo Ran brightened and smiled sinisterly.","“I... I am willing to be Ji Lin’s pet!” Bi Chen jumped with shock, he didn’t think the ugly young man was joking.","Divine beasts had their pride. Some would rather have their souls refined alive and suffer the daily torture of tribulation fires than be another’s pet. A lower level spirit beast devouring their body was something they tolerated even less.","While Bi Chen wasn’t a full divine beast yet, he still couldn’t stomach the notion of a lowly blackwater snake king eating him.","The blackwater snake king looked on with disappointment. Mo Ran cackled and took out a beast collar, snapping it around Bi Chen’s neck. Light flashed through it as it sank into the latter’s body and confined his nascent soul.","Immense sorrow assailed Bi Chen. He’d escaped from Lu Yun’s hand, why did he lust after the qilin inner core and follow Ji Lin here? He’d run into someone more perverse than Lu Yun and become Ji Lin’s pet!","......","Lu Yun had no idea what took place between Ji Lin and Bi Chen; he was exploring the place of burial.","“Is this area a destroyed treasury?” He kicked aside a rock and picked up a jade flask sealed by a restriction. There were three second rank immortal pills inside. “Second rank healing pills... not bad.”","They were useless to him since he bore the sapling of the Builder Tree. No matter how severe his injuries, they would heal swiftly so long as his soul wasn’t scattered. But while he didn’t have a use for the pills, his family certainly did.","Wielding the Eye of Nullification, Lu Yun could avoid danger and seek out fortune. Everything within fifty kilometers was laid out in front of him. All pills, medicines, treasures, and vicious spirits were within his full purview.","After a few days, his storage ring was piled high with numerous treasures that couldn’t be found in worlds of cultivation. It’d been roughly a month since he entered the place of burial.","“Oh? I’ve finally found it!” His eyes lit up to see an intact palace hall roughly forty-five kilometers ahead. All sorts of treasures and pills surrounded it—they were all once at least ninth rank, with some even king rank.","Something was absorbing their power and causing their ranks to decline to dao, spirit, and fine treasures. There seemed to be a massive entity sleeping inside the palace hall.","“That one should be the thing swallowing all of their core essences. The formation outside the palace... Damn it, the Eye of Nullification is too low level to see through the formation!” Lu Yun paused before throwing himself upward and rushing toward the palace in a streak of sword light.","Numerous cultivators were gathered outside of it. This was one of the few intact structures left in the place of burial, so it naturally drew a great deal of attention and curiosity.","“It’s an immortal rank formation!” The young man first to attack the vicious spirits in the valley and open the place of burial was among those assembled. He wore a clean white robe and a purple ribbon set with jade in his hair. Waving a folded fan, he frowned at the formation.","“I say, ninety-ninth prince, have you not gotten anything after a spin around this place?” Xia Houwan was irreverent as ever, but the treasures he bore had been swapped out for a full complement of sixth rank immortal treasures. Plainly, he’d reaped a tremendous harvest during the past couple of days.","“Do not call me a prince here!” The ninety-ninth prince glared impatiently at Xia Houwan.","“Then, alright, Brother Yu Hen, remember to share whatever you find with your brother! Look at me, all I have to show for these days is this pile of trash...” Xia Houwan swayed to and fro, showing off his glittering armor and baubles with a resigned look.","“Take this.” The ninety-ninth prince of Great Xia, Yu Hen, was at a loss when it came to Xia Houwan. He threw over a jade pendant.","“A ninth rank immortal defensive treasure? Nice!” Xia Houwan lit up and quickly caught the pendant. He bit through his finger to drip a drop of blood on it and gave it a cursory refinement before storing it within his body.","“I say, Brother Yu Hen, what kind of place is this place of burial to contain so many treasures?” Xia Houwan swallowed hard when he looked at the pills, medicines, and treasures circling over the hall. They looked to be in wondrous condition and the cultivators outside couldn’t determine their ranks through the curtain of light.","“If my guess is right, this was once the palace of a supreme heavyweight. It was ruined in a massive war.” Yu Hen and Xia Houwan seemed to be good friends as the prince was very tolerant of the irreverent young man.","“Hey, do you think it might be the palace of the immortal emperor from the world of immortals that the books in the Dao Academy talk about?” Xia Houwan licked his lips and cackled.","“Very possibly!” Yu Hen nodded emphatically.","Xia Houwan beamed brightly—the palace of the immortal emperor! The academy’s tomes painted it as a cornucopia of treasures and that legendary immortal crystals grew all over the ground.","“But it’s also possible that it’s not,” Yu Hen said when he saw Xia Houwan’s expression.","“Whatever it is, it doesn’t change the fact that there are a lot of treasures here!” Xia Houwan didn’t care, despite the long held suspicion from the academy’s cultivators that the place of burial was very similar to the palace of the immortal emperor in the records.","BAM!","A combination cultivator finally gave in to impulse and brought his sword down on the curtain of light.","Hummm!","The curtain began trembling.","“That idiot! Retreat!” Yu Hen swore and grabbed the dumbly staring Xia Houwan, backing away as fast as he could.","The void where they’d just stood was submerged by the curtain of light. Cultivators that’d drawn near didn’t have a chance to react before they were reduced to balls of bloody mist and absorbed into the radiance.","The combination cultivator who attacked the curtain suffered the worst fate. His physical body was destroyed and his nascent soul drawn into the palace.","A harrowing cry of anguish echoed from the palace, lasting a dozen breaths. Cultivators who’d managed to escape the curtain’s reaction looked at each other with horror.","“Kekeke, the heavens are kind to me and have sent me such wonderful nutrition less than ten years after I’ve awakened.” Hair-raising cackles sounded from the palace.","“Who is it!” A furious Yu Hen stood in the air and brandished his snowy immortal sword.","“You are an interesting child and your image of heaven and earth is even more interesting.” Savage bloodlust suffused the raspy voice. “This is an ideal body for me to take possession of. Looks like I’m luckier than that Terra Demon...”","All of the hairs on Yu Hen’s body stood on end—it was like an awful beast had him in its sights. An uncommonly frosty air rose from the bottom of his feet.","Whoosh!","Bloody light flashed out of the hall and beelined for the prince.","A grim look in his eyes, Yu Hen grit his teeth and summoned three hundred meters worth of sword light out of his sword, smashing it against the bloody light.","Pfft!","The bloody radiance vanished after being hewn apart, but Yu Hen remained coldly regarding a certain part of the air.","BAM!!","Another streak of bloody light appeared as a wave several hundred meters tall. It enveloped all of the cultivators around Yu Hen.","“Mommy, what is that?!” Xia Houwan nearly peed himself with fright. The jade pendant that the prince had gifted him sparkled furiously, raising a green barrier of light.","“Star of Celestial Rotating Jade, Kill!” Yu Hen remained unmoved as a massive star glittered over his head. It sent waves of sword qi toward the incoming radiance.","Snowy sword light formed a massive vortex that became the center of this part of the world for a moment. Sword light rampaged within, churning through the bloody illumination."]},{"number":2349,"title":"Chapter 2349: Chapter 2223.2: Tai Sui Immortal King","paragraphs":["Chapter 2223.2: Tai Sui Immortal King","“It’s a real star of the seven ancients...” The voice sounded again within the palace, this time with a flicker of excitement. “Hahaha, the seven stars of the ancients share the same roots as me. If I obtain one, I’ll have a chance of repairing my broken nascent soul!”","BOOM!","The treasures and weapons circulating around the palace spontaneously crumbled away. A fey man the color of blood strode out of the palace. He was tall, limber, and naked. Standing at three meters tall, blood-red hair trailed down to his ankles. A blood rune could be found between his brows!","A vicious spirit.","The man with skin the color of blood was a vicious spirit! The spirits weren’t typically sentient, but this one was no different from ordinary living beings.","“Expending all that effort to throw those items outside was worth it. I have indeed lured some nice talent to me...” The man’s bloody irises were focused on the ninety-ninth prince and the scintillating star above the young man.","“What? You threw out all the treasures and pills that erupted from here before?” Yu Hen’s face slackened with shock.","“Heh heh heh heh hehe... and it is all thanks to the Sword of Chaos for breaking the seal over this locale. If not, I’d still be trapped in the Sagittarii Palace! Greedy Wolf, Seven Kills, Army and Yinghuo—how dare the four of you scheme against me! When I get out of here, I will have all of you pay!” The man stuck out a long tongue and licked the corners of his lips, hate flashing through his eyes.","“Kill!” Yu Hen ignored the man’s words. He could tell that although the man appeared domineering, especially having transformed into a vicious spirit, he was a tattered nascent soul at the heart of things.","As powerful as his core essence was, it was just a facade.","The enormous star was magnificent and breathtaking. All cultivators had their eyes on it and had long removed themselves from the clash of powerhouses. The crowd regathered three thousand kilometers away to observe, Xia Houwan part of them. He looked ardently at Yu Hen.","“Heh! Do you see that? That’s my brother Yu Hen! He doesn’t back down when facing an ancient monster, and he’ll still be my brother if he’s defeated and taken possession of!” Xia Houwan brayed with brainless laughter.","The other cultivators rolled their eyes and didn’t say anything.","Ninety-ninth prince Yu Hen possessed some of the highest potential among the Human Emperor’s numerous princes, but for reasons unknown, counted good-for-nothing Xia Houwan among his closest friends. This was so shocking that it was hard to digest for many.","The prince stood in front of the palace hall, a massive star over his head and the immortal sword in his hand flaring with cutting sword light. Sword strokes filled the air like starlight, being everywhere and anywhere. He was a sword cultivator and would be a sword immortal after he ascended. Sword origin surged, resulting in sword qi so sharp that it cut through qi.","“Hahahaha!!” the man roared with laughter. Although he only had a nascent soul left to him, it rivaled Terra Demon’s. Astounding strength exploded in the air; void fissures ripped through the area.","He swung out with a simple punch that contained the boundless meaning of heaven and earth. The prince’s sword qi was as if paper in front of it, so fragile it didn’t bear mentioning. The simplistic punch swerved through layers of space to reach the prince three hundred meters away.","Yu Hen paled with dismay, finding the unadorned punch like a world. It was so overwhelming that he could barely breathe. He wanted to avoid it, but couldn’t seem to move his body. Even his true origin was trapped and unable to circulate.","This was pressure from momentum.","When the fist was less than a third of a meter from his face, a massive foot broke through the air and stepped on Yu Hen’s face a split second before the punch was delivered.","Yu He flew out like a cannonball and smashed into the wreckage of a nearby palace.","BAM!!","A terrifying explosion ripped through the air as two fists smashed into each other. Suffocating ripples spread in all directions as even the cultivators far removed from the battlefield were sent flying by the aftershocks.","“Hot damn, this guy’s fist is seriously hard.” Several hundred meters away, Lu Yun shook off his hand with an expression of pain. One of his arms was broken and dripping blood onto his robes. The Builder Tree sapling flared with illumination and instantaneously repaired his arm.","“Looks like I need a defensive treasure as well.” Although his injury was healed, it still hurt like none other.","The man in front of him looked at Lu Yun with a grim look. If it wasn’t for this young man’s interference in kicking Yu Hen away, his punch would’ve obliterated the prince’s nascent soul and paved the way for his possession.","A bedraggled Yu Hen crawled out of a pile of rubble fifteen hundred meters away and raised cupped fists at Lu Yun. “My deepest thanks for your aid, brother! Yu Hen offers my gratitude!”","Lu Yun tilted his face and inclined his head. At least Yu Hen isn’t the ungrateful sort.","Several rays of significant goodwill blossomed in the void and flowed into the Seal of the Multitude. Apart from Yu Hen, his subordinates and Xia Houwan also felt immensely grateful to Lu Yun.","Just a little more until I form an incense stick of goodwill. An incense stick worth is sufficient to raise the level of the heavenly dao combat arts! Delight rose in Lu Yun’s eyes.","Goodwill was measured in terms of incense sticks. One stick was boundless without end, a level that eluded him ever since he obtained the seal. After entering Immortal Burial Valley, however, he often saved cultivators surrounded by vicious spirits and shared the method to kill them with everyone. Almost every cultivator that’d faced the spirits was grateful to him.","He truly wasn’t a saint, but there were some things he had to do after receiving this treasure. The heavenly dao was forcing him to be a saint, he didn’t actually want to be one himself!","Goodwill brimmed in the Seal of the Multitude, swirling into a small vortex. When it fully took shape, that would be one incense stick of goodwill.","Lu Yun turned around and regarded the blood-red man with a frosty look.","“Who are you?” The man frowned and looked warily at the young man. “I sense a hint of a familiar presence on you.”","“Oh?” Lu Yun’s lips curved upward. “Is that so? You should think again.”","Immortals Forbidden shimmered in his hands as he leveled it at the man. When the latter saw the curve of Lu Yun’s lips, he couldn’t help a shudder.","He could sense that the aura of Lu Yun’s core essence wasn’t that strong—just a hair stronger than Yu Hen’s—but it somehow sparked immense fear from the bottom of his heart. It was a fear that stemmed from prior to being the Tai Sui Immortal King, one that was deeply etched in his heart.","Meanwhile, Lu Yun naturally recognized the person in front of him. This was one of the five inauspicious star kings beneath the central immortal emperor—the Tai Sui Immortal King. It didn’t surprise him that the man was here, given that the Undying Immortal King had perished here.","His condition was no better than when Lu Yun encountered Terra Demon. However, Terra Demon was more fortunate than the immortal king in that he’d nurtured a Yong Heyu to possess.","All that was left of the Tai Sui Immortal King was a naked nascent soul.","The nascent soul of an immortal king, even a fragmented one, was uncommonly strong and nothing that an ordinary cultivator could stand up to. Given Tai Sui’s extensive injuries and the lack of a physical body, on the other hand, fighting cultivators was the current limits of his abilities.","Lu Yun wasn’t afraid of a tattered nascent soul. He could take it back as nourishment for Terra Demon. The latter was also a heavily damaged immortal king nascent soul. Though he’d refined a Hongmeng Fruit, he still couldn’t bring more than a hundred millionth of his full strength to bear. Another immortal king’s nascent soul would be perfect fodder to shore up his deficiencies. Not to mention, Tai Sui’s immortal soul was already polluted by the vicious spirits.","Tai Sui narrowed his eyes, trying to place where he knew the young man from. The damaged state of his nascent soul, however, affected his memories. No matter how he tried, he couldn’t recall who the young man in pristine white robes was.","“Smoke and mirrors!” Tai Sui was nearly overcome with fear, but he forced it down and shouted with indignation. Streaking into a ray of bloody light, he flung himself at Lu Yun.","Pfft!","The young man’s body shattered, but he quickly reappeared over Tai Sui’s head. Immortals Forbidden erupted with a ring of sword light and stabbed at Tai Sui’s forehead.","Jerking with shock, the immortal king hastily dodged and raised rays of bloody light to protect him.","“You’re not the one who absorbed the core essence of these treasures... is there something else inside the palace?” Lu Yun tilted his head. HIs Eye of Nullification couldn’t see through the restriction around the building structure.","“Why... why am I this afraid of you?” Tai Sui trembled like a leaf and couldn’t exert even half of his usual strength.","“Hmph,” Lu Yun curled his lip. There was no way he was telling Tai Sui that he’d killed the man five times in the world of immortals. Although the central immortal emperor had resurrected him with heaven-defying power each time, his terror when it came to the High Lord of the Northern Sky was branded in his soul.","The Tai Sui Immortal King was the most unpropitious of the central immortal emperor’s five inauspicious stars. Disaster accompanied him every time he showed himself. He often did so in the world of immortals, creating disasters to further his cultivation.","At that time, Lu Yun was yet to reach chaos immortal, much less the High Lord of the Northern Sky. He’d merely used the strength of an immortal overlord to kill the man five times, planting the seeds of fear deep in his heart."]},{"number":2350,"title":"Chapter 2350: Chapter 2224.1: Sagittarii Hall","paragraphs":["Chapter 2224.1: Sagittarii Hall","The Tai Sui Immortal King was an immortal king at the end of the day. Contrary to immortal overlords, he was protected by the laws of immortal kings. Thus, while Lu Yun scattered his soul to the four winds every time he killed the man, the central immortal emperor was able to resurrect him so long as Tai Sui’s immortal king rules remained.","That was why there had been a feud between the High Lord of the Northern Sky and the central immortal emperor. Killing Tai Sui once or twice would’ve already formed a blood feud, but Tai Sui had died five times, and each time quite thoroughly at that.","A deep knot of fear had long taken root in Tai Sui’s heart.","The Black Tortoise of the Northern Sky promptly made Lu Yun the immortal emperor of the north when he ascended to chaos immortal. It only served to deepen Tai Sui’s horror. After ascending to his position, Lu Yun possessed the strength to permanently eliminate immortal kings.","Even now, though Tai Sui still didn’t recognize Lu Yun, his horror wasn’t the slightest bit abated.","......","“It’s him!” Three thousand meters away, Xia Houwan’s jaw dropped as he watched Lu Yun face off against the Tai Sui Immortal King. He also felt very lucky at the same time.","“Do you know him?” Yu Hen had reconvened with his friend and the others. They remained where they were, observing the battle.","The prince hadn’t suffered any physical damage since Tai Sui wanted to obliterate his nascent soul, not his body. While Lu Yun’s stomp had bruised his handsome face, a quick circulation of true origin returned everything to its rightful place. If not for that stomp, Tai Sui’s blow would’ve landed on Yu Hen no matter what the prince tried. He understood the chain of actions, so he didn’t resent Lu Yun for his move.","“That person was present for the battle over the Void Sacred Flame. With his ability, he must have claimed the heavenly fire.” Although Xia Houwan was a good-fo- nothing, he still had a certain broadness of vision. Not even Yu Hen was a match for the man the color of blood, but this Lu Yun could suppress him. It was easy enough to hazard a guess at the newcomer’s terrifying might.","“The Void Sacred Flame... is listed as third on the ranking of heavenly fires in the books of the Dao Academy,” Yu Hen sighed. “What a pity. I would definitely fight him for it if he didn’t just save my life.”","“Do you think you can beat him?” Xia Houwan rolled his eyes.","“Um...” Yu Hen looked around awkwardly and refocused on the skies above the palace. Lu Yun was already clashing with Tai Sui.","Being infected by the vicious spirits, the immortal king possessed strength like theirs. Bloody light shimmered around his body—he seemed more like Bloodbath than the Bloodbath practicing the Canon of the Blood God.","A crimson sword dragon circled around Lu Yun, twisting and turning to churn through the bloody light with imperious momentum.","“The Eighteen Cerulean Sword Dragons! Who are you?! Are you the Mindful Immortal Potentate or his heir?!” Tai Sui growled. The Mindful Immortal Potentate was dead, of that there was no question. He would not come to life even if he was protected by the laws of immortal potentates.","It looks like he really doesn’t know anything... While he can detect the existence of Terra Demon, senior brother must have obscured his perception that day. Lu Yun’s mind flew rapidly. Tai Sui could utilize various methods to sense that Terra Demon was trapped in the sword pagoda and learn that he was raising Yong Heyu for possession. It was also no coincidence that Sky had appeared when Lu Yun found the sword pagoda.","The young man eschewed more talk and twisted his body, becoming one with the sword dragon and deploying the first stroke of the Nine Oscillations of the Heavenly Sword.","BOOM!","The void shook as boundless pressure unfurled in all directions. Even though they were three thousand meters out, Yu Hen and the others paled before running for their lives.","Utilizing the Nine Oscillations of the Heavenly Sword in conjunction with the Eighteen Cerulean Sword Dragons affected the void for a dozen kilometers around. A dense array of sword light suffused the air, melting into the void and being impossible to defend against!","All cultivators within the palace’s range were scared off. Not even Yu Hen was able to withstand the aftershocks of this battle.","“What terrifying might... What kind of sword technique is that!!” Yu Hen swallowed. He held Xia Houwan by the collar with one hand and raised sword light with the other, fleeing without a look back.","Under Lu Yun’s full strength, the cerulean sword dragon was fifteen hundred meters long. It twisted seventeen times before rushing Tai Sui on the eighteenth gyration.","“Ahhhhh!!” Tai Sui emitted an inhuman shriek. He abruptly expanded into a blood-red giant three hundred meters tall. Bloody scales covered his form instead of skin.","“The image of disaster! The arrival of Tai Sui brings apocalyptic disaster!!” Tai Sui waved his fists around and punched the sword dragon. It came with the presence of catastrophe—all things would suffer in the presence of calamity!","BOOM!","Tai Sui’s fist connected solidly with the sword dragon; the tremendous recoil flung him two hundred meters back.","Humm!","A wheel of jade-green light rose in the void before he could recover his footing. It transformed into a ray of sword light and descended upon Tai Sui.","“The Reincarnation of the Five Elements... Wood Reincarnation...” moaned Tai Sui as horror flooded his eyes. He knew who he faced!","There was only one person in the three worlds, six paths, and the world of immortals who could utilize the Reincarnation of the Five Elements—the immortal emperor of the north, the High Lord of the Northern Sky!","Even though this Wood Reincarnation was more than a hundred million times weaker than what the high lord had brought to bear in his prime, it was still a true Wood Reincarnation!","It was said that the northern immortal emperor once employed the Reincarnation of the Five Elements and combined all five reincarnations to eradicate a world overrun by vicious spirits. Such was the might of the Reincarnation of the Five Elements!","Fear exploded in Tai Sui’s heart the moment Wood Reincarnation appeared. He didn’t even have the courage to block it before being swallowed by the wheel of jade-green light.","Lu Yun wouldn’t defeat him so easily if it wasn’t for already killing Tai Sui five times over in the world of immortals.","The wheel of light that was Wood Reincarnation fully suppressed the immortal king, giving Lu Yun space to wave the actual sword pagoda into his left hand. Tai Sui was thus transferred to the pagoda for safekeeping.","All Lu Yun did now was borrow the sword pagoda to manifest his image of heaven and earth—he’d yet to fully utilize it. Thus, the pagoda remained an independent treasure, but the young man’s control of it grew ever more complete.","Lu Yun looked around the premises—the sword dragon released by the Nine Oscillations of the Heavenly Sword was so frightful that all of the other cultivators that’d been gathered nearby had long since fled for safer vantage points. They slowly filtered back after a peaceful one hundred breaths.","“I say, brother, you’re damn good! Where’s that big guy?” Xia Houwan was the type to easily befriend others. He slapped Lu Yun’s shoulder with a hearty grin.","Lu Yun wasn’t the prim and proper sort either, Xia Houwan’s actions were right up his alley. “This young master did him in, of course!” he responded with a cocksure grin.","“Nice nice nice. I admired Yu Hen the most before this, but now I look up to you the most!” Xia Houwan roared with laughter, goodwill rising from his body. It was goodwill borne out of reverence!","The good-for-nothing Xia Houwan admired Lu Yun? What kind of situation would it be if his grandfather, Marquis Skyrule, learned of it?","“Many thanks for this brother’s helping hand earlier! I am Yu Hen, might I know...” Yu Hen approached Lu Yun with a cupped fist salute.","“Yu Hen? The national surname of Great Xia, Yu?” Lu Yun raised both brows without answer.","“Heh heh, my brother is the ninety-ninth prince of the Great Xia Human Emperor. Although he has yet to ascend to immortality, he will be a heaven-shaking powerhouse once he does. Of course, he’ll still be a bit weaker than you, ole bro!” Xia Houwan concluded fawningly.","Lu Yun suddenly found this young lord similar to Zhao Chenguang and Yu Shuai. They were all so... thick-skinned!","“So you are a prince of Great Xia. Lu Yun offers his greetings.” Lu Yun patted Yu Hen’s shoulder, aping Xia Houwan’s mannerisms and almost flinging his arm around the prince.","“Eh... Lu Yun? Which Lu Yun?” Yu Hen was still digesting the introduction.","“My grandfather is the strongest of Jade Ruins Realm, Lu Tianling! I’m his grandson!” Lu Yun thumped his chest with pride.","“You’re... Lu Tianling’s grandson?” Xia Houwan’s jaw dropped and Yu Hen stared dazedly. Seeing as how similarly Lu Yun was acting to his close friend, it was nearly impossible for the prince to connect the young man to the one who’d battled the man of blood earlier...","Lu Yun looked nothing more than a good-for-nothing who refused to learn and swaggered around causing trouble with his family’s name!","Eh, well, that was indeed what the Lu Yun of the stories did. But... they didn’t seem right either...","The quick-witted ninety-ninth prince of Great Xia suddenly found it hard to think through this conundrum.","“Hahaha, Lu Yun!! So you’re Lu Yun! You’re the glory of our generation!” Xia Houwan roared with laughter and threw his arm around Lu Yun’s shoulders. The two clapped each other on their backs and were quickly embroiled in a raucous conversation, like they were old friends of many years.","“Lu Tianling... he fought four august immortals with the strength of initial awakened realm and killed one of them. Not many Great Xia perverse geniuses can manage this feat. What does Yan Guichi want from the Lus?” A keen light sparkled in Yu Hen’s eyes.","To many, Lu Tianling was just an incredible talent of their age. Yan Guichi had destroyed the Lu Clan of Great Xia simply to prevent his former masters from enacting vengeance on him."]},{"number":2351,"title":"Chapter 2351: Chapter 2224.2: Sagittarii Hall","paragraphs":["Chapter 2224.2: Sagittarii Hall","“Lu Tianling is a perverse genius, but this Lu Yun seems even more heaven-defying. Yan Guichi’s kicked a hornet’s nest this time.” Yu Hen suddenly thought of something and asked probingly, “Brother Lu, did you come across Yan Beifei before this?”","The prince recalled Xia Houwan mentioning that Yan Beifei had been present where the Void Sacred Flame was discovered. With the death feud between the Lus and Yan Guichi, it was inevitable that all out war would erupt if Lu Yun and Yan Beifei ran into each other.","Xia Houwan had also mentioned that he’d seen no sign of Yan Beifei after he left the area with the heavenly fire.","“Yan Beifei?” Lu Yun smacked his lips. “I took off his head.”","“Huh?” A tongue-tied Xia Houwan gaped at Lu Yun while a knowing expression appeared on Yu Hen’s face.","“Hot daaaaaamn. Brother you’re something else alright! Yan Beifei is one of the Dao Academy’s premier geniuses, but you took off his head!” Xia Houwan blinked for a few moments after hearing the news, then broke out in a broad grin. He plainly didn’t get along with Yan Beifei.","Lu Yun didn’t plan on concealing his actions as some of Yan Beifei’s followers had escaped. News that their young lord had died at Lu Yun’s hands should’ve already made its way back to the Origin King Estate.","The reality was that Yan Beifei was still alive and imprisoned within the sword pagoda, but it would be quite convenient for Lu Yun once the world thought Yan Beifei was dead.","“Well done!” Yu Hen nodded as well.","Xia Houwan and Yu Hen were both in their twenties. As such, they held the mindset of the young. They weren’t particularly elevated above their peers as there were plenty of awakened and combination cultivators in their twenties when it came to Great Xia.","Xia Houwan’s potential wasn’t very high, but he was the apple of his grandfather’s eye and had been pushed to his cultivation level through endless pills and medicines.","As for Yu Hen... he was one of the most preeminent geniuses in Great Xia.","“Your Highness!” Yu Hen’s guards clustered around them, watching Lu Yun warily. They would attack the young man the second he did anything out of the ordinary. Although Lu Yun had just saved their master’s life, these Great Xia royalty deathsworn were eternally on their guard.","“We have fully investigated the palace, there seems to be a seed storage hidden inside.” A young man shrouded in black armor reported stiffly to Yu Hen. He was part of a tremendous force nurtured by the Great Xia royal family—the Iron Dragons.","“A seed storage?” Yu Hen frowned.","The curtain of light outside the palace disappeared after Lu Yun suppressed the Tai Sui Immortal King. However, Sagittarii Hall was so mysterious that the Eye of Nullification could see through it, so Lu Yun didn’t immediately head in.","Some of the other cultivators did, but obtained nothing for their efforts.","“Let’s go take a look!” Yu Hen paused and glanced at the Lu young master.","“Yes, let’s!” Lu Yun understood the prince’s intentions; he wanted to recruit his savior to his side.","Lu Yun couldn’t be bothered with playing dumb or other games. Yan Guichi’s faction was exceedingly strong and too much for the current Lu Clan to manage. Attaching themselves to the ninety-ninth prince’s big thigh would deter some unnecessary trouble.","Not one to fall behind, Xia Houwan blustered at some of the prince’s guards to protect him and followed the other two in.","“Sagittarii Hall...” Lu Yun murmured to himself as he took in the magnificent building. It seemed to be the primary residence of the southern immortal emperor. Was this his Southern Palace?","Confusion crept into the young man’s eyes. The Undying Immortal King had died here and then Formation Hall... But the appearance of the Tai Sui Immortal King was a very strange twist. If this hall was what he thought it was, then this should be the heart of the Southern Palace.","However, they were far from the heart of the place of burial. They were also in a place that was many times larger than the Southern Palace.","All was a foggy haze inside Sagittarii Hall, as if it was filled with red mist. Even Lu Yun’s Eye of Nullification was greatly curtailed here.","“This really is Sagittarii Hall, the primary hall of the Southern Palace!” Lu Yun narrowed his eyes. All was empty inside the building, not even the emperor’s throne to be found in the center.","“What a massive palace hall—royal father’s palace is only one ten thousandth of this place!” Yu Hen looked around with amazement. “There is indeed a seed storage here, but it’s too bad the associated key isn’t present.”","Lu Yun snorted silently. A seed storage? There was another seed world. It looked like Sagittarii Hall’s true treasures were held in that locale, but there was nothing he could do about it given his low cultivation level.","On the other hand, he wouldn’t make the attempt even if he had the ability to access that world. The ponderous entity that he’d sensed in the hall hadn’t been the Tai Sui Immortal King. There was something else absorbing the core essence of all those treasures.","Is it the southern emperor? The thought suddenly occurred to Lu Yun.","Space was vast inside the sword pagoda and it was a world unto itself. It was deathly quiet with no sign of life. All was lifeless even at the heart of the pagoda, where the meter-high sword qi stood.","Two bedraggled figures were sprawled on the ground next to the sword qi, unable to twitch even a finger. One of them gnashed his teeth hatefully, the other was full of terror.","A thin ray of sword qi suddenly flew out of the sword pagoda’s core essence and coalesced into a person.","“Lu Yun!” Yan Beifei nearly crushed his teeth when he saw the figure.","Since Lu Yun had conducted an initial refinement of the treasure, he could use the inner void within the pagoda. He ignored Yan Beifei and walked straight up to the Tai Sui Immortal King.","“Tai Sui Immortal King, to think that you’d ultimately die by my hands still. The central immortal emperor will no longer be able to resurrect you.” He smiled warmly at the crestfallen immortal king.","Tai Sui smiled ruefully. He would resist with every fiber of his being if it was anyone else imprisoning him. He would never submit even on pain of death! Resistance wasn’t even a possibility when he faced the High Lord of the Northern Sky. He’d long accepted his fate.","Lu Yun might’ve considered converting the man into one of his subordinates if he hadn’t become a vicious spirit. But given Tai Sui’s transformation... he was a plague in human form. He would spread vicious spirits wherever he went.","“His Majesty is dead,” Tai Sui chuckled wryly.","“Tell me, what happened to the world of immortals?” Lu Yun cut straight to the chase.","Yan Beifei snapped out of his fury when he heard their conversation. Immortal King? Immortal emperor? World of immortals? Who was Lu Yun, really?","Unbidden, he held his breath and listened to them converse.","“I do not know...” Tai Sui shook his head. “When the five of us battled the Mindful Immortal Potentate, we suffered grave injuries despite overcoming him. We were trapped by his black pagoda and awoke in Sagittarii Hall, our nascent souls shattered.”","“We? There were others apart from you?” Lu Yun narrowed his eyes.","“Seven Kills, Army, Greedy Wolf, and Yinghuo were there as well. They joined hands and plotted against me when we first awoke. Those four concentrated the entire seal on me to make their escape.” Hate overflowed in Tai Sui’s eyes.","Lu Yun snorted with laughter. Tai Sui was very unliked in the world of immortals. Even his fellow inauspicious star immortal kings didn’t wish to befriend him. Who wouldn’t they sacrifice in critical moments, if not him?","“The Greedy Wolf Immortal King should be somewhere in Great Xia.” Lu Yun rifled through the memories of three thousand lifetimes. Although the world of immortals disappeared from his later lifetimes, he was able to find mention of the world in various books and records.","The ten heavenly materials, thirty-six earthly treasures, and the one hundred and eight fires of heaven and earth all had to do with the world of immortals. It looked like this knowledge had been purposefully disseminated by the four immortal kings. With Lu Youya deploying the Greedy Wolf Star a while ago, Lu Yun could essentially be certain that the Greedy Wolf King was in Great Xia.","But since the four of them survived, why didn’t they share the way to kill the vicious spirits?","More questions swirled in Lu Yun’s heart.","“What’s in the Formation Hall?” Tai Sui started trembling. “I don’t know what it is, just that it’s an incredible existence. My nascent soul and that of Seven Kills, Army, Greedy Wolf, Yinghuo, and Terra Demon trapped on the black pagoda were most likely swallowed by that person...”","Lu Yun frowned and dismissed his projection.","......","“Who is Lu Yun?” Yan Beifei couldn’t help but ask.","“You dared set yourself against him without even knowing who he is?” Tai Sui flicked a glance at the man, pity and jeering tinging his tone.","“Is he a reincarnated powerhouse from the world of immortals?” Yan Beifei suddenly lost his confidence and thought of his captor with trepidation.","“A reincarnated powerhouse from the world of immortals? Hahahaha!!” Tai Sui crowed with maniacal laughter. “He is the immortal emperor of the north, the High Lord of the Northern Sky! He stands at the apex of the world of immortals and is one of the five greatest of the three realms and six paths. How is powerhouse sufficient to describe him?”","“An immortal emperor, is he? But he’s a failure in the end and dead. Even if he reincarnates, he will still be a failure in the end. The world belongs to us now!” Yan Beifei narrowed his eyes and began considering how to escape."]},{"number":2352,"title":"Chapter 2352: Chapter 2225.1: Where Has the World of Immortals Gone","paragraphs":["Chapter 2225.1: Where Has the World of Immortals Gone","“Failure?” Tai Sui looked at him as he would an idiot. “Any one of the five immortal emperors might die, but he will never die!”","In this moment, he was certain that the young man in front of him was the real northern immortal emperor, not a reincarnation or anything else! That unforgettable impression of terror was etched into his very soul.","......","“I’ll be able to see through the truths and falsehoods of the Formation Hall if I can elevate the Eye of Nullification into the Heavenly Eye. It’s a pity that I can’t do so right now.” Lu Yun sighed inwardly once his nascent soul returned—he didn’t plan on provoking the entity draining the treasures anymore. It could devour even the nascent soul of immortal kings. What could a tiny Lu Yun do to it?","He’d have to be a chaos immortal to accomplish anything.","“Apart from the seed storage that we cannot access, there is nothing else in this vast hall,” Xia Houwan concluded with resignation after exploring the building structure that was fifty kilometers from end to end. “The real treasures should be inside the seed storage, but we can’t get inside without the key.”","The hat was magnificent, opulent, and regal, but completely empty. There were only nine bare pillars made of stark-white stone. Three meters thick and bereft of qi, they held up the roof of the hall. Many cultivators had already studied them and found them worthless.","“Perhaps there’s an incredibly domineering vicious spirit inside the seed storage...” Yu Hen offered.","“Pfft!” Xia Houwan offered a rude gesture to the prince. “What do you think, ole brother Lu?”","“This doesn’t seem to be a nice place, we should go.” Lu Yun smacked his lips meaningfully.","“Cowards!” Xia Houwan shrugged. “Fine, let’s go!”","It was a very strange place; an eerie air suffused the sumptuous building. Cultivators didn’t wish to make a return visit after entering once.","“What a pity there’s nothing else here apart from these useless stone pillars,” Xia Houwan grumbled. He punched the nearest pillar to vent his frustration.","Hummmm!","The pillar cracked and golden radiance spilled forth from it. Gentle and mild, it enveloped Xia Houwan before anyone could react. He stood slack-jawed in the golden light, entering a profound state of mind.","“What is this?!” Yu Hen was about to drag Xia Houwan out of the radiance when Lu Yun stopped him.","“Don’t disturb him, this is his fortuitous opportunity!” The Lu young master kicked away the closest cultivator to the nine pillars.","“Throw all of the other cultivators out of here! Kill whoever dares touch the stone pillars!” the prince instantly shouted at his men. The mysteries of this Sagittarii Hall were likely contained in the stone pillars, but Yu Hen wasn’t certain if they were one entity. Thus, he didn’t touch the pillars and instead gave the command to clear the area.","But how would cultivators leave without protest when they saw an opportunity was at hand? They approached the stone pillar closest to them; some even threw out their flying swords from several kilometers away, wanting to smash the pillars.","The great hall was fifty meters wide. As impressive as the prince’s men might be, they were unable to immediately herd everyone out.","“Die!” Yu Hen wasn’t a kind and gentle soul; violence flared in his eyes to see cultivators defy his command.","Great Xia’s Iron Dragons were the most elite force of Great Xia royalty. They gathered all of the geniuses from the worlds to create a troop of cultivators that was loyal to the royal family alone. Being cultivators, the guards were able to enter zones off limits to immortals to carry out their missions. No matter where they were placed, each of the Iron Dragons was a premier powerhouse.","Three dozen expressionless guards sent sword light flying from their weapons and executed several cultivators blasting the stone pillars. Many of the pillars still broke, however, and golden brilliance filled the hall.","Hum hum hum hum hum...","Loud reverberations echoed through the hall as rays of golden light surged out of the broken pillars. They collected together and flew toward Xia Houwan! He was the first one to absorb the light, resulting in the remaining radiance recognizing only him.","All nine pillars were shattered in a few short breaths and nine rays of golden light circulated around the man. an image of a golden immortal residence slowly coalesced over his head.","“So it’s the residence of the Nine Radiance Immortal King! Xia Houwan’s a lucky one, alright.” An imperceptible smile spread over Lu Yun’s face. The Nine Radiance Immortal King answered to the southern immortal emperor’s banner. While he was weaker than the Undying Immortal King, he was still a premier immortal king like the five inauspicious stars.","But he’d died for unknown reasons when Lu Yun was still in the world of immortals and his residence gone missing as well. So the southern immortal emperor had refined the core essence of his residence in the stone pillars of Sagittarrii Hall!","Xia Houwan must share a joint destiny with it as he wouldn’t have broken the pillar with a casual touch otherwise. No one could stand in the way of the right timing.","“It’s an immortal residence! Kill him and take the residence!” Greed bloomed from the cultivators when they saw the image taking shape over Xia Houwan’s head. They flung themselves at the lucky recipient with abandon and threw a jumbled heap of offensive treasures at him.","Most of these cultivators came from Great Xia, but there were also quite a few from other locales. Even if they knew Xia Houwan’s identity, they could not resist the siren’s call that was an immortal residence. They’d all witnessed the level of treasure to be found in the place of burial—every single one could be hailed as heaven defying. It was easy to tell that this immortal residence was no ordinary item.","While Great Xia cultivators showed Xia Houwan a certain degree of respect, outsiders couldn’t care less that he was the grandson of Marquis Skyrule. Immense attacks swiftly filled the air.","“Show no mercy!” Yu Hen roared and unsheathed a gleaming sword. He charged the nearest cultivator in a piercing move.","“The ninety-ninth prince of Great Xia? Let me see how much you’re worth!” His target was an ordinary-looking cultivator dressed in yellow robes. Wholly unafraid of Yu Hen, his treasure was a pair of pale gold meteor hammers. They circled around his body like two massive stars.","The prince sneered and commanded a burst of sword light from his sword, creating a waterfall of radiance in front of him. The cultivator wielding the meteor hammers didn’t have time to react before Yu Hen’s sword split him into two.","......","“There’s so many people in front of you, why did you come for me? I’m at the very back of the pack.” Yu Mo looked glumly at Lu Yun standing firmly in front of him.","“I like the look of you, so here I am.” The young man winked at his opponent.","Yu Mo wore long pastel green robes. His hair glowed with a purple hue and was secured in a small topknot by a green hair ribbon. A gentle smile graced a delicate face set with exquisite features. Limber and lean, Yu Mo was taller than Lu Yun by half a head. Countless ladies would fall at his feet if he was found in a city.","What put Lu Yun ill at ease was the ponderous strength that brewed inside this seemingly gentle cultivator. He was stronger than Yu Hen!","“How about we make a deal?” A strange feeling rose in Yu Mo’s heart as he looked at the merry Lu Yun. Does this kid like men?","Being a latecomer to the palace hall, he hadn’t seen Lu Yun fight the Tai Sui Immortal King earlier. He wouldn’t be near this coolly composed if he had.","“Oh?” Lu Yun raised his brow.","“Pretend you didn’t see me and we’ll both go about our business?” Yu Mo beamed with a casual air, not the least bit in a rush.","The cultivators in front of them were locked in fierce battle with the Iron Dragons. Some of them were thorny characters that could hold their own against the Great Xia deathsworn! There were only three dozen of the guards, after all, and several hundred cultivators. Even Prince Yu Hen was scrambling around in his response.","“Go about our business...?” Lu Yun stroked his chin. “How about this, Rouge Pavilion in Dark City of the Darklake Empire is filled with marvelous delights. We can have a good time there!”","He threw a knowing glance at Yu Mo, prompting an awkward shift from the other. The latter abruptly brightened when he saw an Iron Dragon fall to the combined blow of a dozen cultivators. The guards behind their perished comrade didn’t have time to fill the gap in their ranks.","Thus, an opening developed on Xia Houwan’s side.","“I’m not interested in visiting that place, but I’ll treat you to a tea tasting next time.” Yu Mo took full advantage of the opportunity and jumped upward, wrapping himself in a ray of purple sword light and rushing for the opening.","Bam!","A muffled impact sounded from the void as purple sword light met with crimson sword light. Yu Mo’s body wavered and he stopped.","“Aiyaya, if this young master says I’m going to show you a good time, then we need to go have some fun together!” Lu Yun drawled.","The other cultivators had previously witnessed how strong the Lu young master was, so they were delighted to see him preoccupied with someone else.","“Well now, I admit I didn’t see things clearly. I hadn’t thought that you’d be a hidden powerhouse...” Yu Mo admitted dejectedly. He’d thought he was the strongest on the premises apart from the Great Xia prince. He had a chance of claiming the immortal residence so long as he avoided direct confrontation. Who would’ve thought that there’d be another person playing the pig to eat the tiger here!","But he wasn’t the sort to easily give up. A purple immortal sword appeared in his hand—a seventh rank immortal weapon.","“Now that’s more like it!” Lu Yun took a deep breath. A keen glint sparkled in his eyes as Immortals Forbidden likewise exploded with illumination."]},{"number":2353,"title":"Chapter 2353: Chapter 2225.2: Where Has the World of Immortals Gone","paragraphs":["Chapter 2225.2: Where Has the World of Immortals Gone","I've reached the cusp of breaking through after a few monumental battles. I’m only a hair’s breadth from mid soul separation. Lu Yun quickly ran through various courses of action. What he needed most at the moment was a massive fight, one that preferably brought him pressure from someone evenly matched with him. This genteel and refined young man seemed to be a good opponent.","Battle was always the best path for growth. Those who survived the tempering of blood and fire became powerhouses.","BOOM!","A massive explosion sounded in the air as a golden immortal residence three hundred meters tall stood over Xia Houwan’s head. It had fully materialized. His eyes snapped open and an overwhelming aura blossomed from his body. Cultivators attacking him dropped out of the sky like dumplings plopping into a pot.","“How dare you scheme against this young master?? Have you tired of living?!” Xia Houwan waved his hand and spun the residence like a mountain. It bore down on the cultivators with domineering pressure.","“Run!” yelled the cultivators. They didn’t think that Xia Houwan would refine the residence so quickly! The power that he was bringing to bear through it could only be described as limitless.","PFFT!","As fast as they ran, many were still smashed to meat pies beneath the enormous structure.","“Hahahaha!!” Xia Houwan threw his head back with laughter to see cultivators who could kill him with one hand flee for their lives.","“Eh, fellow daoist, so we’re agreed. I’ll treat you to a tea tasting next time we meet!” Yu Mo spun on his heel without hesitation and left.","“As you say!” Lu Yun agreed, refraining from chasing Yu Mo since Xia Houwan had finished refining the immortal residence.","“Thank the heavens you blocked that guy, Brother Lu. Xia Houwan would be hard pressed to avoid disaster otherwise.” Yu Hen had also discovered Yu Mo’s might and inwardly rejoiced that they had Lu Yun with them. If not, Xia Houwan would be severely injured even if he managed to obtain the immortal residence.","“Was that guy really strong?” Xia Houwan blinked uncertainly.","“Strong enough to slap you to death with one palm strike!” Yu Hen laughed.","“C’mon, this place is about to collapse.” Lu Yun looked around their surroundings.","The Nine Radiance Residence had been preserved and evaded being devoured by the entity in the seed storage world because it’d become one with Sagittarii Hall. It’d come under the palace’s protection. Now that it’d emerged from the palace, that was the equivalent of withdrawing the hall’s core essence. The structure wouldn’t stand for much longer.","......","The enormous palace collapsed into rubble a dozen breaths after Lu Yun and the others left.","What a shame... the last evidence of the southern immortal emperor ever existing has now become dust in the records of history, Lu Yun sighed to himself.","While Xia Houwan was a prodigal, he was a loyal person who treasured his friendships. He was good to whoever was good to him. Thus, a clear current flowed from him to Lu Yun. Due to receiving the recognition of the Nine Radiance Residence and fully refining it, Xia Houwan’s strength increased several times over. He was almost on par with Yun Shuige, so the goodwill he generated was uncommonly powerful.","A green whirlpool of goodwill slowly took shape within the Seal of the Multitude. Lu Yun smiled faintly—he’d finally collected an incense stick of goodwill!","......","“Brother Yu, Duke Xia.” Lu Yun raised cupped fist salutes at the two after they left Sagittarii Hall. “I have some other things to attend to, so I am afraid I cannot accompany you further. But if you are ever in the mood, please visit Dusk City. I will personally welcome you as honored guests.”","Yu Hen and Xia Houwan looked at each other, then nodded in unison.","“It’s all thanks to Brother Lu that I secured this heaven-defying opportunity. I will speak to my grandfather about Yan Guichi.” Xia Houwan nodded emphatically.","“Ah yes, the Dao Academy is about to recruit a new batch of disciples. You must make sure that you do not miss it, Brother Lu. With your potential, you will receive significant attention after entering the Dao Academy,” Yu Hen suddenly recalled.","“The Great Xia Dao Academy? I’ll be there!” Lu Yun nodded emphatically. He highly yearned to be part of the Dao Academy—not because of the attention and resources he’d receive as a disciple, but because the name touched upon the memories at the bottom of his heart.","Strangely enough, he didn’t instinctively shy away from the reaction. There was an extensive library at the Dao Academy—he’d find what he wanted there.","Such as what had happened to the world of immortals.","After he took his leave of Yu Hen and Xia Houwen, a meaningful smile appeared on Lu Yun’s face.","“Who would’ve thought that I’d be a saint... BAH! I’m not a saint!” He shook his head furiously, abnormally resistant to the term. “Ai, I still have to collect goodwill where I can. It’s easy enough to make friends so long as I don’t run into ungrateful people.”","Whether it was Ling Chu and the others, or Yu Hen and Xia Houwan, Lu Yun had helped them because he wanted to collect goodwill. While it appeared from the surface that they didn’t give him anything in return, Lu Yun obtained what he wanted most after seemingly giving endlessly of himself.","Goodwill.","Although his original intentions were not pure, he still truly saved the lives of those he helped. If the other happened to be someone worth befriending, then he was happy to make new friends as well. After three thousand reincarnations, he knew a little bit of the human heart.","Despite Xia Houwan being a spoiled young master, his thoughts and actions were a hundred times better than hypocrites who mouthed pretty words.","......","Lu Yun found a relatively secluded spot roughly fifty kilometers from the ruins of Sagittarii Hall and casually set up a formation before setting down cross-legged. His nascent spirit focused inward into the sword pagoda.","The Tai Sui Immortal King had succumbed to his fate and no longer struggled. Yan Beifei, however, was unusually agitated.","“So what if you were once an immortal emperor of the world of immortals! You’re just someone who died! That still makes you a failure!” he roared as soon as he saw Lu Yun, attempting to instill an internal demon in the young man.","“You’re a devious little bastard.” Lu Yun wasn’t surprised that Yan Beifei knew his identity. Tai Sui had plainly said something to him, but he was far from being able to create an internal demon in Lu Yun’s heart.","Lu Yun was the disciple of the heavenly dao and his three thousand lifetimes just to use the seal of reincarnation to obscure his original memories. To him, everything had just been a realistic dream.","As for death... he did indeed die in some of the worlds and taste the bitterness of defeat. But in the first world, he broke through the shackles of immortal emperor and crushed even the rules of the northern emperor at the last possible second. He pierced through the final veil to enter a new territory.","Of course, he’d yet to fully experience that territory before the heavenly dao grabbed him for his second reincarnation. It had nothing to do with death or failure.","Lu Yun couldn’t be bothered to explain anything to Yan Beifei. A hand of white probed out of the void and grabbed the man’s body, hauling him up to his captor.","“The Yans’ resentment toward the Lus probably eclipses what the Lus feel toward the Yans, doesn’t it?” Frostiness threaded through the sword qi collecting in Lu Yun’s eyes. “After all, you Yans were just our slaves...”","“You!!” Fury boiled in Yan Beifei. Slaves of the Lu Clan... this was an eternal thorn in the Yan Clan side! Although Yan Guichi was now the noble Origin King of Great Xia, he came from the origins of a slave and was one who’d betrayed his masters!","A ponderous intent descended from the void when Yan Beifei lost his mental footing and barrelled into the depths of his nascent soul.","“AHHHH!!!” The man screamed with the agony of being turned inside out. He twisted and turned, trying to struggle free of the iron grip. The hand in the held him so firmly that he didn’t shift one bit no matter how he tried.","“Soul refinement...” Tai Sui shuddered and identified in a shaking voice.","Soul refinement was one of the most vicious arts in the three realms and six paths. It refined a cultivator’s nascent soul and ripped their memories out of their mind. Those who suffered this treatment saw their souls scattered to the four corners and never found salvation.","At the same time, the one who deployed this art needed to possess an uncommonly strong mind and heart. Otherwise, they were easily assimilated by their victim’s memories and formed a split personality.","Lu Yun’s mind was so resolute that not even immortal emperors could match him. The memories of an awakened cultivator affected him not at all. He stripped each thread of Yan Beifei’s memories out of his nascent soul, displaying them in front of him.","“The Celestial Realm Battlefront!”","He found what he was looking for! Yan Beifei had found Origination Mountain in a hazardous area from that world.","“It looks like I really need to make time to visit that area,” Lu Yun murmured to himself. He flipped through the memories related to the Origin Sect and set aside the others, uninterested.","Yan Beifei’s soul had been blown apart and no further vitality emanated from his body. With his death, Origination Mountain lacked a master and returned to being a towering mountain in the sword pagoda.","“It’s Origination Mountain... No wonder you wanted to deploy soul refinement on him...” Tai Sui murmured as he gazed upon the mountain.","Lu Yun slowly opened his eyes in the place of burial and breathed out a mouthful of putrid air.","“No matter how hard and no matter how directionless I was, I have a clue now. I’ll follow it until I find the world of immortals.” Lu Yun lowered his head.","Dao followed its matter of course. All he needed to do in this world was to follow the course of nature and do everything he wanted."]},{"number":2354,"title":"Chapter 2354: Chapter 2226.1: Vermilion Bird","paragraphs":["Chapter 2226.1: Vermilion Bird","A small knot in Lu Yun’s heart loosened after he refined Yan Beifei’s memories and learned where the man had obtained Origination Mountain. Everything proceeded naturally after that and he entered mid soul separation.","Once he set foot into this stage, the black shadow that was one with the sword pagoda turned silver. It was a few hints more solid and his image of heaven and earth also increased in power.","“Although I’m mid soul separation, I’m still unable to deploy the fourth stroke of the Nine Oscillations of the Heavenly Sword... I probably won’t be able to until I break through to combination stage,” Lu Yun mused.","The Nine Oscillations of the Heavenly Sword was the accumulation of nine strokes overlaid on top of each other. The first three were sufficient power for Lu Yun to destroy some of Great Xia’s empyrean immortals.","The gap between Great Xia’s empyrean immortals and those of the worlds of cultivation was similar to the difference between the dynasty’s cultivators and those from the worlds of cultivation. Immortals from the worlds remained primitive immortals if they didn’t move to Great Xia; they would never stand on the same footing as the dynasty’s immortals.","That was why Jadecliff never dared to leave Jade Ruins Realm. Once an empyrean immortal from a world of cultivation traveled to Great Xia, they became a rootless ant without backing.","However, there was also an insurmountable gap between cultivators and immortals. It was completely preposterous for a cultivator to kill an immortal in the worlds of cultivation. Even in Great Xia, such feats were manageable only by the most monstrous geniuses. A good portion of Great Xia cultivators would still be overpowered by empyrean immortals from worlds of cultivation.","In his current condition, Lu Yun would absolutely be a perverse genius if he was in Great Xia. Regular Great Xia empyrean immortals were no match for him. If he was able to deploy the fourth stroke of the Nine Oscillations of the Heavenly Sword, then he would be able to compete on equal terms against Lu Youya.","“I’m just mid soul separation right now and have many combat arts to practice. A sword technique like that Nine Oscillations of the Heavenly Sword consumes too many resources. I can only use it as a final ace up my sleeve.” Lu Yun formed a hand seal with both hands and summoned the green whirlpool from the Seal of the Multitude.","Not being a connate treasure, the seal wasn’t powerful when it came to offensive capabilities. Its main function was to collect goodwill from the people. Thus, Lu Yun never considered refining it for his image of heaven and earth. It was completely useless for that. Apart from its innate attack abilities, the attributes of the treasure were extremely important for an image of heaven and earth.","After the incense of goodwill that was the vortex of green floated upward, rays of iridescent light flashed through the air over his nascent soul and formed runes that contained the profound mysteries of heaven and earth. Runes corresponding to Petrification, the Connate Great Dao of the Five Elements, Eye of Nullification, Size Manipulation, Teleportation and Split Shadow circled around his nascent soul.","Lu Yun took a deep breath and sent the whirlpool into the rune for the Eye of Nullification. The other five runes made another circle in the air before returning to his nascent soul.","An incense stick worth of goodwill surged into the rune for the Eye of Nullification, sending rays of scintillating light flashing out of it. The presence of the heavenly dao suffused Lu Yun’s dantian as runes of heavenly dao gathered from all directions to meld into the rune.","“So goodwill itself doesn’t improve the combat art... It’s the summation of goodwill from the people that communicates with the heavenly dao. That in turn collects power from the heavenly dao to improve the combat art ...” Enlightenment dawned in Lu Yun’s eyes. “The goodwill of the people isn’t supposed to enhance my cultivation or the combat arts! It’s meant to help me draw closer to the heavenly dao and understand it.”","The combat arts of heavenly dao weren’t a result of ascension, but from the comprehension of heavenly dao. Goodwill from the multitude was the ladder with which to gain this understanding.","After the radiance flashed by, the Eye of Nullification rune fully transformed into something brighter than before. The combat art of heavenly dao—the Heavenly Eye!","It examined everything within five hundred meters down to the tiniest detail and nothing escaped its purview!","However, the mental strain posed by this art was rather profound. Lu Yun’s current level of cultivation could maintain it for a dozen breaths at most. And yet, a dozen breaths was sufficient for cultivators to do many things.","The rune for the combat art flickered a while longer before melding back into his nascent soul. Lu Yun heaved a long sigh as he stood up.","Goodwill still trickled toward him from various parts of the void. It might be the Vermilion Birds’ faith in him, or it might be lingering gratitude from cultivators in other parts of the valley. Regardless of the source, it slightly replenished the goodwill that he’d just exhausted.","“I still have three Dao Rune Pills and should be able to use those to reach combination stage. Sadly, I can’t take it in the formation array.” It was quite a pity as if he could break through to combination stage in the place of burial, he’d dominate the area and locate more treasures.","The rune of dao in the pill helped cultivators comprehend nature and reach the realm of becoming one with heaven and earth. When one reached that stage, one absorbed ambient qi at a faster pace as well.","However, Dao Rune Pills were too precious. Even just one of the pills was beyond the reach of ordinary cultivators. Everything within the formation array was isolated from heaven and earth. Dao Rune Pills were ineffective here; Lu Yun had to wait until he left.","He stood up and raised a ray of sword light beneath his feet, flying toward the ruins of Sagittarii Hall. With the Eye of Nullification being elevated to the Heavenly Eye, he wanted to see what was within the seed storage world beneath the palace.","He took a deep breath when he arrived at the ruins and opened his eyes with a flicker of lilac radiance. A void suffused with flames appeared in front of him, one that held a scarlet bird the size of a palm in its center. It drooped listlessly—feathers that should have been brilliantly resplendent were a shabby mess. Its eyes like black pearl were half closed as it weakly regarded Lu Yun.","“You’ve finally come,” A pleasing, yet uncommonly tired female voice echoed in his mind.","“You were waiting for me?” Lu Yun raised a brow and transmitted back in kind.","“I would say that to anyone who came.”","Lu Yun: ......","“But I didn’t think it would be you, immortal emperor of the north—the High Lord of the Northern Sky!” Joy traced the voice’s words.","“Neither did I think that the notable Vermilion Bird of the South would fall to these straits,” Lu Yun sighed.","The palm-sized bird in the void was the divine beast of the south—the Vermilion Bird.","“What happened that year? Why did you vanish the second you broke through, like you never existed in the first place ?” Confusion appeared in the beast’s voice as it regarded itself self-deprecatingly. “Do you know how overjoyed we were when we discovered that you’d broken through chaos immortal and become an existence like us? But you had us rejoice for nothing.”","“My master took me away.” Lu Yun shrugged helplessly.","“Your master?” asked a baffled Vermilion Bird.","“The heavenly dao,” the young man responded candidly.","An existence like the Vermilion Bird could absolutely understand the heavenly dao. Lu Yun felt no mental pressure as he faced the divine beast. The heavenly dao hadn’t said he was to keep the relationship a secret, so it didn’t matter if he told others.","Of course, most would think him a madman if he said that his master was the heavenly dao. No one would believe him as cultivators typically thought of the heavenly dao as an intangible, formless existence.","The disciple of the heavenly dao? What a joke!","As for the Vermilion Bird... The divine beast of the south was born of the rules of fire. It naturally understood the existence of the heavenly dao.","“I see.... I see. No wonder the five of us couldn’t calculate your origins when you first appeared. So you’re the disciple of the heavenly dao.” Having understood, the Vermilion Bird continued meaningfully, “This must be your true self. The northern immortal emperor in the world of immortals was your reincarnated self, wasn’t it?”","“Yes,” Lu Yun nodded, but then looked startled. “Five of you?”","“Our leader is the qilin. He wields the rules of the central earth,” Vermilion Bird explained.","Lu Yun stood in front of the ruins of Sagittarii Palace, having stopped the Heavenly Eye a long time ago. He communicated with the divine beast through mind alone. The Vermilion Bird was heavily injured and couldn’t leave that part of the void. It would vanish as soon as it did and be reincorporated into the rules, returning to its origins.","Prior to this, it was the one behind absorbing the nascent souls of Terra Demon and the five inauspicious immortal kings, as well as the core essence of the immortal treasures. It only wanted to recover from its injuries—the six immortal kings wouldn’t \\ be alive otherwise. They would’ve long been scattered to the four winds.","Vermilion Bird couldn’t be bothered to communicate with anyone if no one disturbed it. Lu Yun scanning it with the Heavenly Eye had awoken it out of slumber, which was why it sent out its consciousness to talk with the young man.","“What happened? Where has the world of immortals gone? What is this place?” Lu Yun asked after a long moment.","“The affairs of times past are very complicated,” Vermilion Bird responded with resignation. “Out of the five of us, only I was lucky enough to live. The other four died. It was a cataclysm of sorts—you’ll find out later.","“As for where the world of immortals has gone, I don’t know either. It was still there when I fell asleep. This place should be a special void formed after the palaces of the five immortal emperors smashed into each other.”","Lu Yun fell silent.","A cataclysm..."]},{"number":2355,"title":"Chapter 2355: Chapter 2226.2: Vermilion Bird","paragraphs":["Chapter 2226.2: Vermilion Bird","Lu Yun dearly hoped that the cataclysm that beset the world of immortals was different from the one of his subconscious. Although his memories were sealed, he retained his instincts and a sliver of subconscious.","He knew many things, such as the ghost zombies, vicious spirits, and... and the root of the world’s destruction. He also knew why he was here. The only thing he couldn’t recall was who he was and where he was from.","“Ai... I hope you can find where the world of immortals is now. It is vital to many things, and the three worlds and six paths cannot be without it.” Vermilion Bird blinked its beady black eyes and opened its mouth, sending a drop of golden blood essence through the void to Lu Yun. “You have an interesting little fellow with you. This drop of blood essence is a gift for it.” Tenderness filled its tone.","Lu Yun knew that the divine beast meant the Hadal Bird. Legend had it that the first bloom of Hadal Fire to ever exist originated from a drop of Vermilion Bird blood. When it landed in the Hadal Land, it absorbed hadal qi and became a flame. Thus, the fire spirit of the Hadal Flame possessed the Vermilion Bird bloodline.","This drop of blood essence was sufficient to enable the Hadal Bird to fully take form and break free of the shackles of its flame. It would become a real living being and the Hadal Flame would evolve into a heavenly fire.","Lu Yun carefully put the drop of blood essence away. Meanwhile, the Vermilion Bird’s aura faltered even more and its eyes like black pearls closed slightly. It no longer talked.","The young man fell silent before summoning a golden fruit and a tea leaf the size of a nail with a flip of his hand.","“The Hongmeng Fruit and Dao Enlightenment Tea!” The divine beast’s eyes opened again, this time with surprise. A flash of scarlet light brought both items to it.","“I owe you a favor.” The bird fell into deep slumber after swallowing both items.","“You are too polite, senior.” Lu Yun inclined his head and left, refraining from disturbing the divine beast further. So this place was the ruins of the combined five heavenly palaces of the world of immortals. No wonder there were so many treasures here.","Lu Yun sighed softly after learning of the truth. “This should be the territory around the southern palace... Let me go take a look at the northern palace.”","He briefly opened the Heavenly Eye to set a course and flew in the appropriate direction.","Sword light three hundred meters long broke through the air with unstoppable momentum, drawing piercing shrieks from vicious spirits when they saw it. Sword seals flashed through Lu Yun’s hands and split into rays of crimson splendor, swiftly cutting all of them down.","He sensed a familiar presence on the third day... the presence of the northern palace. It’d been nearly reduced to a vacant lot—there weren’t even ruins left. It’d suffered a more thorough level of destruction than the southern palace.","The disappearance of its emperor left it rudderless and unable to bring its full power to bear. Thus, it suffered the greatest damage.","“I always thought that the disappearance of the world of immortals had something to do with those vicious spirits. It seems like I was wrong,” Lu Yun took a deep breath.","The attrition wrought upon the five heavenly palaces plainly came from the barrage of an overwhelming treasure. The five palaces shared the same origins and were some of the strongest connate treasures born of the world of immortals. They’d clearly become one, but something had still blown them to pieces.","That source of trouble should be man made.","“But who...” Lu Yun was suddenly reminded of the severed body of the ten-winged chaos scaled-dragon falling from the sky. “Forget it, let’s not think too much about it.”","He brought his sword light down. There were the fewest cultivators here as the northern palace had suffered the most damage. Just a few hopefuls wandered through the area. “I hope it’s still here.”","Lu Yun opened the Heavenly Eye to scan the northern palace’s domain. There was less than four hundred kilometers of territory left after its destruction, so the Heavenly Eye easily took everything into view.","“There!” He brightened and sped in a certain direction. He’d left a treasure in the palace, meant to be used after he ascended beyond chaos immortal. Who would’ve thought that he’d never have the chance to refine it?","Only he and his empress knew of the treasure’s existence.","“Oh, it’s definitely still there!”","A ramshackle herb garden came into view. It should’ve nurtured countless immortal herbs and numerous specimens of the thirty-six earthly treasures. Sadly, it was in almost complete disrepair and its qi nearly completely dispersed.","However, Lu Yun knew that there was a modest seed storage space beneath the herb garden and that his treasure was quietly resting within.","Given that this was an herb garden, there were still plenty of immortal herb remnants within. Several cultivators scavenged through the meager pickings; an occasional shout of surprise sounded when someone discovered one or two herbs teetering on the edge of life.","Lu Yun knew that it was due to the treasure beneath the herb garden that there was anything to be found. Otherwise, the entire garden would be long dead.","“Hey, kid! Get over here!” a coarse voice blasted into Lu Yun’s ear. “Come here and dig nine meters down to see what kind of treasures are down there. There will be a reward for you if you do your job well!”","The speaker was a tribulation stage cultivator with a thick beard. His flabby cheeks shook as he gave loud commands to the young man.","“Eh?” Lu Yun looked at the cultivator with surprise. Dragons were found alongside snakes in Immortal Burial Valley and those from the worlds of cultivation had long witnessed for themselves the might of Great Xia cultivators. This man was obviously from a world of cultivation. Where did he get the courage to strut around like this?","“Acting tough, are you? Get digging!” A latter combination cultivator next to the man shouted at Lu Yun.","“Boss, we have news! There’s treasure nine hundred meters down!” A slim and small man with clunky features on his face scurried to their side with a shifty expression. He held a gray spirit beast in his arms.","“A Treasurehunter Rat?” Lu Yun blinked to see the spirit beast. Treasurehunter Rats were just first rank spirit beasts, but they were uncommonly sensitive to qi. They caught any ripple within fifty kilometers.","“Well? Hurry up and dig nine hundred meters down!” snapped the tribulation cultivator.","There were two dozen other cultivators here and they all looked at Lu Yun with pity. A soul separation cultivator was already doing very well to survive to this point without protection from a powerhouse. Unfortunately for the young man, he’d run into this streak of misfortune.","The tribulation cultivator was the strongest of them, so the other cultivators gave him a wide berth. Most of them were combination stage with a few soul separation cultivators forming teams with other combination cultivators.","A little fellow like Lu Yun showing up here? Who else would the tribulation cultivator pick on?","The Great Xia cultivators? They had all been transported elsewhere a day ago; not a single one remained in the place of burial. The remaining cultivators naturally respected whoever was the strongest.","Without the pressure of Great Xia cultivators, the heavyweights of the worlds of cultivation gleefully threw their weight around.","“Nine hundred meters below ground?” Purple light flashed through Lu Yun’s eyes as he looked at the relevant spot. “Oho, it’s an Origin Ginseng.”","Origin Ginseng was ranked number six on the list of earthly treasures and was the most likely one to become sentient and evolve into a monster spirit. A dao immortal ginseng that’d taken human form had been the caretaker of Lu Yun’s herb garden back in the day.","That one had likely perished and the one sleeping nine hundred meters below was one of its roots.","“Hurry up and get digging!!” roared the tribulation cultivator when the young man stood unmoving on the spot.","Lu Yun cocked his head and grasped in the direction of the earth, retrieving a plump baby that was fifty centimeters tall. Naked and bearing a jade-green sapling on its head, a dense fragrance spread in all directions. It was sucking on its thumb and its chest rose at an even pace as it slumbered.","“Squeak squeak!” The Treasurehunter Rat twisted with agitation when it saw the baby in Lu Yun’s hand.","“Definitely a good treasure alright... Hand it over, kid!” The tribulation cultivator was nearly drooling.","Sadness appeared in Lu Yun’s eyes when he saw that the baby ginseng in his hand resembled the garden’s old caretaker. He waved it into the sword pagoda.","“You! Court death!” The tribulation cultivator flew into a rage when he saw Lu Yun completely ignore him. Fingers splayed wide, he grabbed at Lu Yun’s collar.","Bam!","Lu Yun stomped on his face and sent him flying with cries of anguish.","“Did your parents not tell you that Immortal Burial Valley is very dangerous, that you should exercise caution in everything you do?” Lu Yun snorted and walked toward the tribulation cultivator’s clique.","“Are... you a Great Xia cultivator? No, they were all transported out of here a day ago. What are you still doing here?” The clique was made of ten people and the other tribulation cultivator within it shuddered when he looked at Lu Yun’s expression.","“This young master will spare your lives if you hand over everything you own.” Lu Yun probed the air with his right hand and summoned back the man he’d just kicked. He casually relieved the man of his storage rings, then threw him aside like a bag of trash."]},{"number":2356,"title":"Chapter 2356: Chapter 2227.1: No Mercy","paragraphs":["Chapter 2227.1: No Mercy","Since these people owned a Treasurehunter Rat, they must have picked up quite a few treasures already. It’d be one thing if they didn’t run afoul of him, but since they’d placed themselves in his way, then he wouldn’t let them off the hook so easily.","Yes, he was collecting goodwill, but he wasn’t a saint. He would kill and loot when he should!","“Don’t act too out of bounds, young man.” The second tribulation cultivator was a haggard old man, but his cultivation was stronger than the man with the flabby cheeks. He was latter tribulation and only needed to endure his final heavenly tribulation before he became an awakened cultivator. “Taking one step back means we will still be able to meet in good faith later on!”","“Good faith later on?” Lu Yun curled his lip. “I’m sure that none of you will ever want to see me again.”","He shifted in front of the elder and punched the old man in the stomach. The elder flushed beet red and coughed weakly. Another kick sent him flying and a storage ring into Lu Yun’s hand. The young man then flashed in quick succession and charged the other eight.","None of them escaped Lu Yun’s blows. Each suffered a hearty beating and was stripped naked, then thrown aside in a half dead state.","Who was Lu Yun? The greatest prodigal of Darklake Empire and a young man with an eccentric temper! It was only ever him pointing at the noses of other people—no one dared so much as raise their voice at him. It was already a show of mercy that he didn’t kill them on the spot!","He smiled with satisfaction at the struggling Treasurehunter Rat in his hands. He didn’t need one since he possessed the Heavenly Eye, but a vast family stood behind him. A spirit beast like the Treasurehunter Rat was a hot commodity no matter where it was.","He threw it into the sword pagoda.","“All of you have nothing to do with this. Scram!” he shouted arrogantly at the other cultivators.","None of them moved. Instead, they looked at Lu Yun with looks of greed. First it was the Origin Ginseng, then the Treasurehunter Rat... The young man must possess a storage treasure that could hold living beings! A treasure like that was at least immortal rank, and a very high immortal rank at that!","Lu Yun snorted when he saw the looks creep over their faces. A powerful aura exploded out of his body and sent them all flying before they could react.","Whoosh!","Crimson light flashed from his sword and decapitated a combination cultivator.","This time, the rest of the people ran without needing Lu Yun to say anything else. They didn’t dare linger on the scene any longer. Sure enough, the young man possessed many treasures, but he was also a harbinger of doom.","“Hmph, now I’m pissed enough to go on a killing spree.” Lu Yun curled his lip. “And why aren’t you getting out of here yet?”","He tilted his head and looked at the void next to him.","“You can see me?” A handsome young man in light blue robes walked out with surprise. He was the same cultivation level as Lu Yun, but the latter somehow sensed a terrifying wild beast crouched within the young man’s body.","“There’s nothing in this world that can hide from my eyes.” Lu Yun smirked arrogantly.","“Your eyes?” The handsome young man took a close look and smiled. “They are indeed fine eyes, I like them. How about you dig them out for me?”","His smile was warm and outgoing, his tone perfectly matching them. However, an inexplicable sense of evil framed his words.","“We’ll have to see first if you have what it takes!” Lu Yun brayed with laughter.","“Hahahaha!!” The young man suddenly struck, sending a massive longsword at Lu Yun with a flash of black radiance. “The heavens prosper if they bow at my feet, the heavens perish if they stand in my way!”","The young man whistled and directed rampaging qi out of the blade. It bloomed in the void like a black lotus.","Whoosh!","The blade qi twisted into a ray of black light and cut straight at Lu Yun.","Clang!","Lu Yun brought up Immortals Forbidden and rebuffed a blow, but not without suffering a nick as big as a grain of rice to the sword’s edge.","Immortals Forbidden was forged out of the essence of li fire metal—a king rank material for immortal weapons. Though he’d tempered it into a lower dao rank weapon instead of bringing it up to its full potential, it was unusually durable. That the young man had caused a flaw in it with one stroke was testament to his might.","Lu Yun narrowed his eyes and looked at the longsword in his opponent’s hand.","“A mere lower dao rank weapon is still intact after a blow from my Black Lotus... It looks like that flying sword is also made of supreme materials. I want it! This time, I’m taking your life!” the handsome young man shouted.","Hummm!","Blade qi nine meters wide and thirty meters long erupted in the void and came down on Lu Yun like a razor-sharp mountain. The young man didn’t dare hesitate—his opponent was too uncanny. He was just soul separation, but he was so strong that those like Yu Hen and Yan Beifei were absolutely no match for him.","The first stroke of the Nine Oscillations of the Heavenly Sword!","A jade-green immortal sword appeared in Lu Yun’s hand as he deployed Wood Reincarnation from the Reincarnation of the Five Elements. Wood Reincarnation propelled the first stroke of the Nine Oscillations of the Heavenly Sword!","Green light flashed through the air and bore down on the young man’s head. Another flaming red sword appeared in Lu Yun’s hand the next second—the second stroke of the Nine Oscillations of the Heavenly Sword!","The immortal sword in his hand crumbled away when the wheel of Fire Reincarnation formed. Fire and wood intersected—wood fed fire, so their power grew stronger!","“You...” The young man’s expression changed drastically. The blade qi that he’d just brought to bear was as if paper in the face of Wood Reincarnation. It was crushed within a split second. Two wheels of green and red arrived simultaneously, drawing an agonized shriek from him. “This is plainly a killing move! Why aren’t you like everyone else? Why are you using one of your ultimate moves in the first exchange??”","The young man possessed countless combat arts that he hadn’t had a chance to deploy. He needed time to prepare them even if he wanted to use them now, but Lu Yun’s two strokes of the Nine Oscillations of the Heavenly Sword didn’t leave him a chance to do anything!","He gnashed his teeth with fury. Didn’t experts open with probing moves and gain a better understanding of each other’s backgrounds before letting loose with their greatest techniques? Why wasn’t this guy following the playbook?","“AHHHHH!!” the young man roared and sent a black lotus out of his head. It was like darkness had descended upon the world and the entire void darkened. With his image of heaven and earth on the battlefield, the young man relaxed slightly. However, he paled the next second and spat out a mouthful of blood.","BOOM! BOOM!","Two tremendous explosions rang out when wheels of green and red smashed into the young man’s image. It shook so violently that the young man was greatly injured as well.","“I! Want! You! To! Suffer!” He snapped out, having never suffered such a setback in his life of smooth sailing.","However, a haze of red immediately enveloped him and a massive dragon of sword qi snarled, diving through the void with cutting sword qi around it. The young man’s defensive treasures didn’t impede it at all.","Pfft!","The third stroke of the Nine Oscillations of the Heavenly Sword, Eighteen Cerulean Sword Dragons!","The young man burst into a bloody mist and a black nascent soul broke through the air, protected by the black lotus. It vanished from sight.","“No matter who you are, you’re doomed! I am Cui Jiuyuan of Wuxi Mountain and will obliterate you no matter where you might run!” A harrowing scream echoed in Lu Yun’s ears.","“Wuxi Mountain, again?” He frowned. “What is that place? I think I vaguely recall it from my three thousand years of reincarnation, but not really. It must not have amounted to much during my era...”","Lu Yun wasn’t sure how long it’d been since his time in the world of immortals and the world vanishing.","“Forget it, one problem at a time. I’m going about my business as I should be doing.” He put Wuxi Mountain out of his mind—he’d already killed three of them anyhow. “A true world of water, hmm? How exciting!”","His fingers flicked through a strange hand seal as he vanished into thin air.","A speck of dust one hundred and fifty kilometers beneath the ruins of the northern palace contained an incomparably vast world. It was bigger than even Immortal Burial Valley. It’d once been the seed storage world of the northern emperor.","Five hundred thousand kilometers across, it was one of the smaller instances of its kind. What set it apart was the treasure it contained, one infinitely priceless even in the world of immortals—a world of true water!","The heart of this world was a ball of cerulean radiance. It hovered silently in the air, appearing completely ordinary. There were no ripples of energy from it, but it seemed like a vast world without end.","There were countless living beings within it, anything from tadpoles to massive beasts, from ants to immortals. There was even a complete three realms and six paths within it. Living beings cycled through reincarnation, seeking immortal dao and searching for immortality.","Everything in this world was based off of the dao of water. The rules of water were its only principles. Thus, it was no match for a real world despite possessing a complete three realms and six paths. At the same time, it truly contained the rules of a world.","Back in the day after Lu Yun obtained the treasure, he’d borrowed the laws of the world within to touch the cultivation realm beyond chaos immortal. However, he hadn’t been able to comprehend its laws and thus failed to truly refine the world of true water."]},{"number":2357,"title":"Chapter 2357: Chapter 2227.2: No Mercy","paragraphs":["Chapter 2227.2: No Mercy","Lu Yun swallowed gently as he looked at the fist-sized world of true water in front of him. Its aura was calm and measured, like it was a ball of water without any qi. Those who lacked a sufficient cultivation level weren’t even able to sense the world inside the treasure.","Although the young man had experienced all three thousand lifetimes, he recalled them in the form of dreams. He needed to comprehend them anew for himself. He cultivated the Nine Chapters of Dao now and was constantly baptized by dao. His cultivation grew at a rapid pace and he’d long gained the mindset of an empyrean immortal.","Hummm!","The dao character seat cushion that his nascent soul sat upon in his dantian suddenly released a ray of gray splendor. It flared out of his body and enveloped the cerulean world of true water.","“Hmm?” Surprised delight flashed through his eyes.","Slight ripples surged over the treasure in front of him and rays of illumination flowed out of it, becoming one with the gray haze emanating from the dao character.","A refreshing stream flowed out of the ball and gently nourished Lu Yun’s body. An extremely comfortable feeling flooded through his body and he lost himself in the sensation.","The fist-sized world of true water bloomed with cerulean radiance and cocooned him with it. With that, the treasure gradually shrank into a speck of dust that entered Lu Yun’s forehead.","Humm!","His dantian shook as the treasure appeared within it. The power of water gushed from it to become part of his core essence. His spirit root of dual elements suddenly saw the addition of a third—water!","Lu Yun’s spirit root was now wood, fire, and water. They sustained and countered each other in a never-ending cycle. His Hongmeng qi began circling at a faster pace as well. The power of water split into two—part of it was absorbed by the Builder Tree sapling in Lu Yun’s body and the other part melded with the Hongmeng qi.","Lu Yun’s cultivation surged forward without restraint and he arrived at peak soul separation.","“Builder Tree, world of true water...” Understanding dawned in Lu Yun’s mind. “The world of true water is a treasure on the same level as the Builder Tree. I still need to refine two more, one of earth and another of metal, before I can alter my spirit root into an empyrean spirit root of the five elements...”","Wood, fire, and water circulated in his outstretched hand. Black connate kui water gathered in his palm through the Connate Great Dao of the Five Elements. Just like the power of wood, Lu Yun could now utilize connate kui water of the north as he wished.","“My command over water and wood has reached perfection, I’ve yet to obtain metal and wood, but my mastery of connate fire is lacking...” After a quick comparison, Lu Yun discovered that wood and water dominated his spirit root. Fire should’ve been the strongest of the three, but it was actually on weaker footing.","“Do I need to find another fire attribute treasure to make my spirit root whole?” Only through comparison was there discovery. With the addition of water to his spirit root, Lu Yun noticed several things that he hadn’t before.","His nascent soul sat in the middle of his dantian with the Builder Tree, sword pagoda, and world of true water forming a triangle around it. At the same time, they were on even footing with Lu Yun’s nascent soul.","The Seal of the Multitude sat beneath the nascent soul like it was an offering table, lifting the nascent soul up high.","“Refining the world of true water has brought my cultivation to peak soul separation. All I need to do is exit Immortal Burial Valley and take a Dao Rune Pill. I’ll instantly break through to combination stage!”","He brimmed with confidence as while he hadn’t claimed the rules within the world of true water, his strength had undergone a fundamental shift.","“I wonder what the perverse geniuses of Great Xia are like. The young man who scared off Yan Guichi in Dark City, for example, is only a nascent soul cultivator...” While Lu Yun’s strength had bounded forward, he didn’t let it go to his head and think he was invincible. Even a reincarnated immortal emperor ran the chance of perishing before he fully grew into his strength.","He left the seed stage world with another hand seal, unable to refine it given his current level of strength. Since he couldn’t take it with him, he had to leave it here.","While he’d once owned it, that experience was just a dream. In other words, the High Lord of the Northern Sky was Lu Yun, but Lu Yun was not that august personage.","“I have to reach dao immortal first before I can take this space with me.” He turned and left without a glance back. The only evidence that the northern immortal emperor had ever existed was just this perfectly preserved seed storage world.","......","The number of cultivators in the place of burial had greatly decreased. With the departure of the Great Xia cultivators, it was nigh impossible for those from worlds of cultivation to survive in the face of the terrifying vicious spirits and countless unknown dangers. Thus, those with a thorough knowledge of their own limitations filtered out of Immortal Burial Valley.","“I’ve gotten enough here, I’ll leave the rest to those who are fortunate enough to happen upon these opportunities.” When Lu Yun scanned the area with the Heavenly Eye, he found many treasures still to be collected. There were even a few intact connate treasures that could be found, but he left them alone. All should proceed as they were meant to.","He’d lost the desire to remain after obtaining Yan Beifei’s memories. If it wasn’t for Sagittarii Hall raising his curiosity, he would’ve left long ago.","Since Origination Mountain had appeared in the Celestial Realm Battlefront, he wanted to pay it a visit as well. But with the rules of the heavenly book yet to settle back into place, the Jade Ruins Realm portion was still sealed shut.","There were only three days left until they returned, so Lu Yun made for the exit of the formation array. The second he walked through it, a dozen strong consciousnesses locked onto him and scanned him all over.","“You, open your storage ring for inspection,” said a nasally empyrean immortal dressed in black robes. He descended from the skies and landed in front of Lu Yun.","Great Xia cultivators had been transported back to the immortal dynasty through the rules of the heavenly book gathered here. That meant whoever walked out of the formation array was from a world of cultivation.","No matter how impressive their backgrounds were, they could not compare to Great Xia immortals. Thus, many from the dynasty stood guard here and seized the treasures from any cultivator who walked out.","Blood had been spilt on the ground and more than a few cultivators had been killed for their refusal to give up their fortunes.","“Are you looking to die?” Lu Yun hissed after understanding the situation at hand.","“What did you say?” The immortal blinked, seemingly not having heard Lu Yun clearly.","“I said, are you looking to die?” Uncontrollable killing intent rose in Lu Yun’s heart when he looked at the ground and the fresh blood stains. Countless cultivators had risked their lives in the place of burial and barely managed to reach beyond the fingertips of Great Xia cultivators to secure a fortuitous opportunity. They’d thought that they would soar to the heavens after leaving, but met their doom instead.","When they saw what was happening, numerous cultivators wanted to wait for the heavenly book to return to its place. It would be safe when immortals left Jade Ruins Realm. However, the land inside the formation array had become a sea of vicious spirits. Even though they knew how to kill the spirits, they could not kill them all.","“I am not a saint, so what do these things have to do with me? I, Lu Yun, am a cultivator of Jade Ruins Realm in this lifetime. I live as one of them and die as one of them. I can bully and kill them as I will, but if anyone else does so... Most of the dead are Jade Ruins cultivators...” Lu Yun took a deep breath, finally understanding why so many cultivators were gathered at the entrance. They would rather be slaughtered by the vicious spirits than walk out. They were fully aware of what was taking place on the other side.","He suddenly recalled that some people had tried to stop him before he exited, but he’d ignored them.","Whoosh!","Crimson splendor sparkled in his hand and a blazing sun rose to hover in the air.","“Any immortal not from Jade Ruins Realm who dare approaches within five hundred kilometers of the formation array will be shown no mercy! No mercy! No mercy!”","......","The young man’s shouts echoed over the land, drawing raised heads from the assembly. People’s eyes widened when they saw the wheel of piercing light that shone like a second sun. Cultivators hanging on for dear life at the entrance to the array also looked up. Peering blearily through the curtain of light, they saw a second sun as well.","“You!” gasped the immortal. However, he didn’t even have a chance to scream before the blazing sun descended and burned the latter empyrean immortal to a crisp.","“Kill!” Lu Yun howled at the sky, locking on to another immortal in black. A sword dragon twisted eighteen times in the void and transformed into nine crimson dragons, converging upon the immortal from nine different directions.","BOOM!","A muffled explosion rang out as the immortal slashed the closest dragon with his immortal sword.","Pfft!","Lu Yun’s Eighteen Cerulean Sword Dragons combined the second stroke of the Nine Oscillations of the Heavenly Sword. What could an empyrean immortal do against it?","The terrible force sent him flying while the three sword dragons behind him tore his body and immortal soul to pieces.","“How dare you, child!” Many Great Xia immortals were gathered at the entrance. The dynasty’s cultivators may have left, but they stayed here so they could glean what fat they could from the top. Who would’ve thought that they’d run into a character like Lu Yun?","Seven empyrean immortals joined hands and charged the impudent young man."]},{"number":2358,"title":"Chapter 2358: Chapter 2228.1: Return","paragraphs":["Chapter 2228.1: Return","The seven empyrean immortals were from Great Xia rather than bumpkins from worlds of cultivation. Their combined strength was sufficient to end worlds and shatter the heavens.","The void rumbled as seven rays of multicolored sword light shot toward Lu Yun from seven different directions. They pierced him through and shredded him to pieces.","He reappears in another direction and hacked one of the immortals into two.","“Kill!”","“Kill!” Two figures shot out of the formation array—one the color of blood and the other stark white. They screamed with overpowering killing intent as they rushed the remaining six empyrean immortals.","When they heard their young master’s roar, Bloodbath and Gui Xie extracted themselves with the fastest speed possible and joined the fray. Two rays of light replete with towering killing intent blasted into the two nearest immortals.","The Cosmic Flag had evolved into a paramount dao rank weapon in Gui Xie’s hands. Endless starlight gathered to him and condensed into something nearly tangible, corralling an empyrean immortal in front of him.","BAM!!","Gui Xie punched through the immortal and crushed his opponent’s immortal soul to pieces, leaving a trail of stark-white light in his wake. Everyone was caught off guard by how quickly he killed a Great Xia empyrean immortal!","A massive flag appeared in Bloodbath’s hands as well. It flared with a bloody light and cracked threateningly in the wind—it was a third rank immortal weapon. Bloody light surged and roiled, catching an empyrean immortal off guard and slicing him to pieces.","Immortals Forbidden burst with radiance and swiftly cut down another two empyrean immortals. Lu Yun’s strength had more than doubled after he refined the world of true water. He was also newly ascended to latter soul separation. Although the empyrean immortals were from Great Xia, they were just ordinary immortals at the end of the day. He didn’t need to expend much effort to kill them.","After Bloodbath and Gui Xie swiftly took out their first opponent, they attacked a third together. Another burst of radiance from Lu Yun’s sword took out a fourth.","The trio obliterated all seven empyrean immortals within the blink of an eye. Ponderous goodwill brewed in the void and surged into the Seal of the Multitude from all directions. There was gratitude to Lu Yun and also veneration for how a cultivator had killed empyrean immortals. All sorts of goodwill streamed to him.","“You go too far!” One of the empyrean immortals sitting at the entrance to the array opened their eyes. The one yelling at him was a female immortal that Lu Yun remembered. She was the one who’d warned him before he entered the array.","“Too far?” He regarded her with a cold look. “Do these immortals not go too far in using their cultivation as a club to bully and loot from cultivators?”","“The weak are food for the strong. Dying is only reasonable,” said a middle-aged man next to the female immortal.","“Then why have I gone too far?” Lu Yun sneered.","“Ah...” She had no response to that.","“Cultivators are as if ants, how can they compare to immortals?!” continued the man.","“Very well!” Lu Yun threw his head back with laughter. “So cultivators are as if ants and cannot compare to immortals! I’d like to see for myself today just who is an ant! You are the ants in my eyes.”","He raised Immortals Forbidden to the sky and commanded a burst of magnificent sword light three thousand meters tall.","“Any foreign immortal present within five hundred kilometers of the array after twenty minutes will be given no quarter! Any who can be found within Jade Ruins Realm after a day will be shown no mercy! Do you hear that, Terra Demon?”","“Understood!” came a ruthless answer in the void.","“That includes the three of you.” A cold light glinted in Lu Yun’s eyes as he looked at the three empyrean immortals.","“We three protect the formation array by the orders of the Human Emperor,” said the last of the three—a young man.","“The Human Emperor’s orders are not needed in Jade Ruins Realm,” Lu Yun snorted.","“Are you... do you want to rebel?!” glared the female immortal.","“You are not the judges of that,” Lu Yun curled his lip. “Gui Xie, escort the cultivators at the entrance out of the array. Forget about the others inside. It’s their destiny if they die there and their fate if they make it out.”","“Understood.” Gui Xie was finally witnessing his young master’s temper. The young man didn’t think about the consequences at all when he lost his temper!","“You...” The young empyrean immortal’s expression twisted, but he shuddered when he thought of the answering shout from the void earlier. That had been at least a golden immortal!","“Piss off,” Lu Yun commanded from the air.","Goodwill reared like waves and crashed upon him. He wielded Immortals Forbidden while the wind tugged at his hair and white robes. Three empyrean immortals standing at the head of two hundred of their kind stood in front of him.","Facing off two hundred empyrean immortals with the strength of one... The scene indelibly etched itself into countless cultivators’ minds.","“We will die before violating His Majesty’s command!” The female immortal set her jaw.","Instead of responding, Lu Yun waved a brazier into existence next to him. Half of an incense stick burned slowly in it, green smoke curling around the object.","The cultivators who’d been forced back into the formation array gaped when Gui Xie led them out. Another overwhelming burst of goodwill broke through the air and smashed into the Seal of Multitude.","Lu Yun didn’t care about this; he wasn’t undertaking these actions for goodwill this time. Someone needed to speak up on behalf of Jade Ruins Realm.","The Human Emperor of Great Xia? He’d never respected that man.","“Who is this young man? When did such a young powerhouse appear in our world??”","“What a pity that he hasn’t given enough thought to the consequences. He won’t live much longer after defying the Human Emperor...”","“It’s definitely a pity. Maybe he reached these heights because of certain opportunities he found inside.”","“But if it was me, I would never stand up to these immortals for the sake of these cultivators...”","Some found their footing and relaxed enough to carry conversations on the ground. Opinions varied about Lu Yun, but the young man hardly cared about what they thought.","I, Lu Yun, repay all my favors and enact vengeance for all slights! I follow my heart and do whatever I want, kill whoever I want! Would I truly be me if I was preoccupied by too many concerns?","All Lu Yun needed to do was to be himself. He was the heavenly dao.","When mind and heart were one, Lu Yun felt his cultivation take another step forward to combination stage. There was one final piece of paper left between he broke through.","Time passed until the stick of incense burned nearly all the way down. All of the immortals were still present, fixing glares of death on the young man. If they were scared off by a native in a world of cultivation, it would become an eternal internal demon and their cultivation would never take another step forward.","The humiliation would remain even if they eventually killed the young man with their bare hands.","“There’s one of him and two hundred of us. Let’s kill him together!” One of the empyrean immortals could no longer bear the atmosphere and unsheathed his weapon against Lu Yun. The brazier was the first casualty and shattered to pieces. The almost extinguished stick of incense also flew apart into dust.","His actions were a catalyst that caused all of the other immortals to bring out their treasures as well. They blasted Lu Yun with their strongest strength.","No one noticed a small ripple appear over the formation array. The three empyrean immortals here by the Human Emperor’s order vanished soundlessly into the ripple.","“Kill!” Undaunted, Lu Yun remained unmoving in the void. Gui Xie and Bloodbath respectively waved the Cosmic Flag and Asura Flag by his side. Fully unfurled, the two flags summoned bloody light and starlight to fill the void.","It was at this moment that the air abruptly froze. The two hundred immortals and even some true immortals hidden among them were as if flies caught in amber. Their attacks screeched to a halt and petered out.","A massive hand probed out of the void and pressed down on all of their heads.","Horrified and panic-stricken, some struggled and wanted to run. Others wanted to shriek with fear, but couldn’t find the words to. They could only watch the hand descend upon them.","That part of the void vanished along with the immortals, leaving a mass of trembling cultivators on the ground below. They stared blankly at the air, at where two hundred domineering immortals had just died without a trace. There weren’t even bone shards left of them.","“Young master, what do we do with these things?” Terra Demon appeared in the air with two hundred storage rings.","Lu Yun flicked a glance at them and chose five, then emptied out the rest.","“You guys can have them,” he sighed as he looked at the cultivators below. Most of them had made it out of the place of burial, but the immortals had robbed them of their findings.","Quite a few had been unwilling to accept this outcome and wanted to reenter the formation array after the immortals left. However, the current situation inside was that of teeming masses of vicious spirits. They would more than likely die if they tried again.","Lu Yun decided to distribute the contents of these rings among them partially because he didn’t think much of the treasures, pills, and spirit crystals inside. The storage rings he claimed contained immortal swords of fire, water, and wood attributes. Immortal swords were the best tool for him to deploy the Reincarnation of the Five Elements, but low level swords were destroyed as soon as they were used.","Thus, Lu Yun needed to prepare multiple low level immortal swords for future battle.","No one touched the largesse at first. But after a few intrepid cultivators took the first couple of items, the crowd no longer hesitated."]},{"number":2359,"title":"Chapter 2359: Chapter 2228.2: Return","paragraphs":["Chapter 2228.2: Return","Lu Yun relinquished his claim over those storage rings naturally in pursuit of goodwill and the human heart. Jade Ruins Realm was his first target. While the cultivators who emerged from the formation array subsequently lost their fortuitous opportunities, they would surely achieve great things in the future. Thus, this was the best opportunity to win them over.","However, he didn’t reveal his identity—remaining anonymous was better in this situation.","“Terra Demon.” Lu Yun ignored the developing mess of cultivators squabbling over treasure. With the two of them here, nothing serious would develop. While heated, the cultivators kept to taking what they needed.","“Young master!” Terra Demon bowed when he reached Lu Yun. He suddenly felt that the northern immortal emperor of yesteryear had returned.","That year, when he’d just taken his throne, the central immortal emperor sent a chaos immortal to the northern domain of the world of immortals. The chaos immortal was a terror through the land and caused endless suffering and misery.","The northern immortal emperor had flown into a rage and chased the chaos immortal through the world, immortal sword in hand and the Reincarnation Disk as his image of heaven and earth. He’d kept up such a dogged chase that there was no where the immortal could run to.","Eventually, the chaos immortal of long-standing reputation fled to the domain of the central immortal emperor. The latter had appeared to protect the immortal’s life, but Lu Yun killed the chaos immortal in front of the strongest of his colleagues. Not only that, but he refined the immortal’s soul alive.","“Keep a close eye on your dogs. If they run through my territory again, this emperor will beat even the master.” The northern immortal emperor drifted away with these words.","After that, his fame was known throughout the lands and his authority unquestionable. Lu Yun had shown hints of that bearing just moments ago—he knew that he shouldn’t undertake those actions, but did so regardless.","“Handle this and survey Jade Ruins Realm after a day has passed. Kill any outsider you come across, no matter who they are,” Lu Yun commanded coolly and then paused, “Remember anyone that you cannot defeat. We’ll come for them later, but leave the ones in Fallen Leaf City alone.”","He transmitted the last sentence, then brought the Tai Sui Immortal King out of the sword pagoda and threw him at Terra Demon.","“Understood!” Terra Demon shook when he saw the immortal soul. Although it was polluted by the vicious spirits, the core essence of the immortal soul was still there. This was incredible nutrition for Terra Demon in his current state!","He ignored Tai Sui’s piteous gaze and vanished with the immortal soul.","“Everyone, make the best of your lives. The Jade Ruins Realms belongs to Jade Ruins denizens.” Lu Yun left with Bloodbath and Gui Xie.","All immortals within five hundred kilometers had long been scared off—who dared remain? Given Terra Demon’s presence, they didn’t even dare linger in the world, but returned straight to Great Xia.","......","“Young master, Bloodbath and I will undergo our heavenly tribulations soon.” Gui Xie and Bloodbath paused when they were several hundred meters out from Dark City.","Tribulation stage cultivators underwent three heavenly tribulations, one storm tribulation, one lightning tribulation, and one thunder tribulation. Gui Xie had already weathered his storm tribulation. Being in the formation array all this time, Bloodbath had been isolated from his trial despite his cultivation reaching tribulation stage.","Gui Xie was now strong enough to undergo his lightning and thunder tribulations; the same went for Bloodbath.","Lu Yun nodded and took out two purple pills from his storage ring, tossing them at the two.","“Refine this pill after you reach awakened stage.”","Bloodbath and Gui Xie brightened—they were very familiar with the Dao Rune Pill. It was only available to the core of nobility even in Great Xia.","Yun Shuige was Marquis Skycloud’s youngest and most beloved son. It was quite a feat that the Yun Shuige possessed Dao Rune Pills—Yan Beifei hadn’t owned any. Just one of the pills was of pivotal importance to awakened cultivators. It would prove extremely useful at critical moments.","“Our greatest thanks to the young master!” Bloodbath and Gui Xie hesitated briefly before carefully putting their pill away. Two enormous surges of goodwill rose from their bodies and melded into the Seal of the Multitude.","What a pity that it didn’t form faith... but that’s not far off now. Lu Yun inclined his head at the two. “Go on, then.”","“Understood!” They raised cupped fists and vanished from sight.","......","Lu Yun swiftly returned to Dark City after Gui Xie and Bloodbath departed. Trepidation had draped around the city as everyone readied for war. Troops of cultivators wielding strength beyond the capabilities of a third rank world of cultivation patrolled throughout the capital.","Several massive armies gathered outside Dark City, poised to march into battle at any time.","All these years, the Lu Clan bided their time and concealed their strength in the shadows. Lu Tianling even raised many powerhouses that’d become local titans in other higher ranked cultivation empires. The Lu patriarch himself never dared truly show off his strength as Darklake Empire teemed with Origin Sect spies.","Lu Tianling had patiently borne his misfortunes in life, holding himself together even when his son and daughter-in-law were killed, when his foster son was crippled. He stalwartly endured it all because his grandson had been born.","If not for Lu Yun, the Lu patriarch would’ve lost his mind long ago and thrown caution to the wind. Instead, he pretended to have lost his morale so that Yan Guichi would relax his guard and only utilize the strength found in the world of cultivation. Otherwise, far more than previous levels of harassment would’ve arrived on his doorstep if he displayed anything unexpected.","The worlds of cultivation were protected by the heavenly book, after all. Although Yan Guichi was Great Xia nobility, he had to respect its rules. Punishment would swiftly descend if he violated them.","Yan Guichi held his reservations and didn’t wish for the situation to rage out of control, so he utilized his authority against Lu Tianling in ways that stayed within the bounds of the heavenly book.","With a temporary reprieve in the rules and open hostilities between the two sides, Lu Tianling thought nothing of his previous concerns and fully displayed his strength.","His current goal was as Lu Yun anticipated—the Lu patriarch sought to rule over Jade Ruins Realm as its only sovereign. Only then would he wield enough true power to face Yan Guichi.","Jade Ruins Realm was the only one out of Great Xia’s three thousand worlds of cultivation that lacked a ruler. Lu Tianling was going to take that seat.","......","“Grandfather, I’m back!” A dusty Lu Yun sought out Lu Tianling as soon as he returned home.","Wearing clean white robes, Lu Tianling was studying a map of Jade Ruins Realm in his study. He made the occasional mark on the diagram.","“You’ve come back?” Lu Tianling turned to his grandson and brightened. “Latter soul separation?”","“Just one step away from combination stage—I can break through at any time.” Lu Yun nodded.","“How is your comprehension of your cultivation stage?” Lu Tianling raised an eyebrow.","“I killed a few Great Xia immortals outside the place of burial,” the young man answered casually.","Lu Tianling shook as a piercing look shone out of his eyes. “Did you borrow the help of external objects?”","“Just destroyed a few immortal swords along the way,” Lu Yun chuckled.","“Very good! As expected of my grandson!” Lu Tianling laughed merrily. “I grow ever more curious about your master!”","“You’ll meet one day if there’s a chance to,” Lu Yun continued chuckling. His grandfather wouldn’t believe that his master was the heavenly dao if he said so now. “Ah, yes, I may have been tempering myself on my master’s orders, but I happened to come across something valuable.”","He flipped his hand over and revealed a red flame interspersed with gold—the Void Sacred Flame.","“This is...” Lu Tianling’s eyes fixed on the fire and he turned beet red. His true origin circulated furiously, almost exploding out of his body. The flaming halberd that’d become one with him also stirred to motion. It ardently desired the flame... No, it ardently desired what the flame contained.","“This is the Void Sacred Flame, third among the ranking of heavenly fires...” Lu Tianling forced down his agitating true origin. “No, there is more than that here...”","“Grandfather, this flame is for you.” Lu Yun grinned radiantly. “There’s something else beneath it that’s a connate treasure. I think second uncle lacks an image of heaven and earth, so please give it to him for me.”","Lu Yun handed over the Luminous Lotus Throne.","“Good, good, very good!” Lu Tianling was more than overjoyed!","His grandson had always been viewed as trash that could never be redeemed. But Lu Yun blazed with glory these days and easily killed empyrean immortals. He easily obtained even connate treasures. What more could the Lu patriarch want from life given a grandson like this??","Lu Tianling truly saw the hope for revenge in this moment. He’d planned to march into battle after the rules of the heavenly book returned in three days. But now, he called for a delay and entered seclusion.","The Void Sacred Flame contained the Crimson Emperor Chapter of Inception. It barrelled into his mind almost as soon as Lu Tianling received the flame. Thus, he had no choice but to focus on cultivation. After he gave the Luminous Lotus Throne to his foster son, the Lu patriarch entered a closed door cultivation that he would not emerge from until he succeeded or failed in death.","Likewise, Lu Xiaochi set everything aside and entered seclusion after asking Lu Yun for a few spirit crystals.","Darklake emperor Situ Wenxian didn’t know whether to laugh or cry. Weren’t they just about to hoist the banners of war and conquer the realm? Who would’ve thought that Lu Yun’s return would immediately change these plans?","But Lu Tianling’s disciple wasn’t an ungrateful sort. Darklake Empire boasted of its current achievements solely because of Lu Tianling. Once the patriarch and his foster son emerged from closed door cultivation, their strength would undoubtedly have leapt forward again."]},{"number":2360,"title":"Chapter 2360: Chapter 2229.1: Tenth Rank Cultivation Empire","paragraphs":["Chapter 2229.1: Tenth Rank Cultivation Empire","Darklake Empire was but an ordinary third rank cultivation empire at the end of the day. It would still be bullied by its peer, the Tianlong Empire, if not for Lu Tianling, to say nothing of becoming independent of Dark Orchid.","Lu Tianling had continuously deployed a secret art all this time to conceal Situ Wenxian’s cultivation level of latter combination stage. The Lu patriarch was as if a god to the emperor. Rather than simple respect between disciple and master, Situ Wenxian venerated his master to the point of placing all his faith in Lu Tianling.","......","The stirring Darklake Empire fully quieted down after Lu Yun’s return. The great armies that’d assembled returned to their posts, but no longer had to hide themselves.","Darklake powerhouses concealed in other higher ranked empires returned home with boundless resources. Their addition swelled a mere third rank empire’s strength to more than ten thousand times stronger than before.","Darklake’s previous requirement to join the army was foundation establishment. It was now nascent soul. Only those at this cultivation level could officially become part of the army.","Previously lofty individuals in Darklake Empire, nascent soul cultivators didn’t lose their status with the return of powerhouses from other empires. Being well established in Darklake, their knowledge of the land was much greater than the returnees’.","They were the talents needed to administer the nation.","When he laid his plans, Lu Tianling picked members of mid-rank Darklake families to nurture. Now that they returned with tremendous resources, their families’ stock rose as well. The once seven great families of Darklake were but a joke through the lens of modern times.","The Yuwen, Ouyang, and Ling Clans were no more. The Zhao and Yu Clan survived due to Zhao Chenguang and Yu Shuai, but they were relegated to the bottom of the hierarchy in the nation. As for the most mysterious Mo Clan... All traces that they’d ever existed had been erased from Darklake Empire. There was no one even in their business establishment of the Immortal Gathering.","......","Lu Yun released the baby Origin Ginseng, Treasurehunter Rat, and Hadal Bird in the seed storage formation of the family vaults. Thanks to Mu Ge, the formation had been enlarged to five hundred kilometers across. While she was an empyrean immortal, she was able to bring golden immortal strength to bear as her injuries had taken a turn for the better. She sat on the other side of the formation and ignored Lu Yun.","The little Origin Ginseng looked to be a child one year old and was learning how to walk. He was fully awake now and looked blankly at Lu Yun, but did not show fear.","“Ee umm ahhh.” The Origin Ginseng opened and shut its mouth, trying to say something but not knowing how to talk.","“Alright then, you’ll live here from now on and take care of the herb garden for me.” Lu Yun pointed at the massive spirit herb garden not too far away.","The child blinked and seemed to understand Lu Yun’s words. It tottered to the garden, completely at ease in the unfamiliar surroundings. This Origin Ginseng came from the roots of Lu Yun’s old garden caretaker, so it naturally felt close to the young man and wasn’t repelled by the human.","Several nascent souls hauling small hoes around the herb garden jumped with shock when they saw the Origin Ginseng. Lu Yun ignored them. His new caretaker was ranked number six on the listing of earthly treasures and innately knew how to take care of these grasses more than any human cultivator.","He turned his attention to the firmly restrained Treasurehunter Rat. It was less than half a meter tall, but its tail was a full meter long. It peered piteously up at the young man.","“You’ll follow me in the future and do whatever I tell you to do, or I’ll feed you to the bird.” An ominous Lu Yun pointed to the napping Hadal Bird that was the size of a palm.","While the Treasurehunter Rat was a beast, it was very well aware of human nature. It quickly bobbed its head up and down to indicate its willingness to follow the young man’s orders. Lu Yun tossed it into the sword pagoda. Treasurehunter Rats were greedy by nature. If it was allowed to roam freely in the garden, it’d wreak havoc in less than a day.","“Little birdie, you’re the luckiest out of everyone this time.” Lu Yun smiled faintly at the bleary-eyed Hadal Bird. Being a fire spirit, it was yet to become a real living being. Its mind was not yet fully developed, so it looked at Lu Yun with confusion as it didn't understand what he was saying.","The young man flipped his hand over, revealing the drop of Vermilion Bird blood essence that was the size of a fist.","The Hadal Bird’s eyes went wide.","Whoosh!","It beelined into a black line before Lu Yun could react and swallowed the blood essence. Chirping with joy, it circled around Lu Yun’s head and landed on his shoulder. It lifted a beak smaller than a pinky fingernail and intimately nuzzled the young man’s cheek.","After that, it wobbled back into the air and transformed into a black flame before returning to the Cauldron of Heaven and Earth. Lu Yun carefully placed the cauldron in the seed storage formation.","“You seemed to have brought out Vermilion Bird blood essence just now.” Mu Ge had appeared in front of Lu Yun at some point in time. Her tone was as cool as ever.","“I obtained it from Immortal Burial Valley,” Lu Yun nodded, not intending to hide anything from her.","“Ah, Immortal Burial Valley...” Mu Ge nodded, naturally having heard of the place. She returned to her seat and sat down cross-legged. The pale-gold dragon egg next to her brimmed with vitality.","......","Dewcloud Mountain was the largest mountain within the Darklake borders. It was like Fallen Leaf Mountain and the Barren Mountains, spanning nearly five thousand kilometers with a main peak towering above the clouds. It was one of the most idyllic spots in the nation.","Darklake’s greatest sect—Cloudraid Sword Sect—called the mountain home. There were a dozen nascent soul powerhouses in residence and it considered itself too mighty to bow its head to Darklake Empire. It didn’t consider itself a subject or offer tribute.","In the six months that the heavenly book’s rules were inactive, the sect sealed the mountain shut and turned a blind eye to all external affairs. On this day, a young man in white robes appeared outside the sect’s front doors.","“Cloudraid Sword Sect is sealed shut for three years and will not receive guests. Please depart, fellow daoist!” A foundation establishment disciple on duty called out to the young man.","Lu Yun ignored the guard and set foot into the mountain’s main peak. The enormous defensive formation stuttered for a split second when he entered it.","“Dewcloud Mountain eh? The pronunciation for the characters of your name are the same as mine.” Lu Yun’s lips curved upward. This mountain and him had a shared affinity.","“Who are you?! The sect has sealed off the mountain, so please depart with due haste!” The foundation establishment disciple was alarmed to find that he didn't know how Lu Yun had made it inside. He hastily rang the alarm bell at the front gates and set off bells throughout the entire main peak.","“What is it? Is someone attacking the sect?” A few golden core cultivators ran out of seclusion when they heard the alarm. But when they arrived at the front gates, they saw only the confused foundation establishment cultivator.","“What’s going on, Jing Ming? Why have you rung the bell?” frowned a man with a black beard.","“Someone came through the formation just now, but I don’t see any sign of them anymore,” the disciple quickly responded.","The man’s frown deepened when he failed to see any signs of damage to the formation.","“Jing Ming, have you been drinking?” A female golden core cultivator twitched her nose when she smelled the alcohol on the disciple’s clothes.","“I...” Jing Ming frantically shook his head, wanting to explain myself.","BOOM!","A terrifying ripple of qi erupted in the sky. With the main peak as its center, an enormous swirling vortex summoned all ambient qi within five thousand kilometers to itself.","“What’s going on?!” A host of nascent soul cultivators in closed door cultivation ran out of their meditation chambers to peer at the main peak.","A young man in white robes stood unmoving at the very top. His clothes flapped and hair danced in the wind. Intimidating quantities of powerful qi surged toward the young man.","“It’s him! The one I was just talking about!” Jing Ming immediately recognized Lu Yun; cultivators possessed keen vision and they weren’t far from the main peak.","Lu Yun had decided to take the Dao Rune Pill on the mountain’s peak and easily became one with heaven. He drew all of the qi within five thousand kilometers to his body. After fully refining the pill and dao rune inside, one had a chance of becoming one with heaven and sensing its ultimate truths, thereby absorbing energy from the surroundings.","A Dao Rune Pill absorbed energy from five thousand kilometers around it after the cultivator found success. This was a terrifying quantity as not even empyrean immortals could contain such a ponderous amount!","Lu Yun continuously took in qi and transmuted it to Hongmeng qi. Hongmeng qi circulated throughout his body without fail.","Rumble!","Thunder roared inside the young man’s body! Everyone within the sect held their breaths—even nascent soul experts. No one was able to fight Lu Yun for the energy he was absorbing, not for even a sliver. Such was the might of the Dao Rune Pill."]},{"number":2361,"title":"Chapter 2361: Chapter 2229.2: Tenth Rank Cultivation Empire","paragraphs":["Chapter 2229.2: Tenth Rank Cultivation Empire","No cultivator beneath awakened stage dared attempt the Dao Rune Pill. If they did so and their bodies proved insufficient to withstand the might of all qi within five thousand kilometers, they ended up ensuring their own demise.","Some cultivators took the pill only when they reached initial awakened stage and their consciousness transmuted to immortal consciousness. Only that level of mind could manage such a massive quantity of qi.","Lu Yun, however, was different from ordinary cultivators. He practiced the Nine Chapters of Dao and his body contained the much more sophisticated Hongmeng qi.","......","The Lu young master stood unmoving at the pinnacle of Dewcloud Peak. He seemed as if a bottomless hole, endlessly devouring energy.","Countless spirit herbs within the sect’s herb gardens withered at a speed visible to the naked eye. Sect disciples rushed around like headless chickens, unsure of what to do. However, no one dared disturb the cultivating stranger.","Such a level of powerhouse could destroy the entire sect with a casual backhand. There was nothing sect disciples could do even if they wished to take action. They couldn’t come within fifty kilometers of the stranger.","It took four hours before Lu Yun stopped. He was now peak initial combination stage and half a step away from mid combination stage. The Nine Chapters of Dao consumed incredible amounts of qi, which made breaking through very difficult. And yet, one Dao Rune Pill had helped him ascend nearly two cultivation levels. How terrifying was this pill??","Ambient energy slowly returned to its usual flow, leaving behind a strange tranquility in the void. Even the air seemed to be clearer.","“Combat art of the heavenly dao... Sword Manipulation?” Lu Yun carefully took stock of the changes in his body and was taken aback by his newest combat art. However, he brightened anew when the runes for the combat art flashed in front of his eyes.","Sword Manipulation differed from the other combat arts in that he didn’t need to actively deploy it. It was a passive combat art that operated at every second. In fact, it seemed more accurate to say that Lu Yun had gained a new instinct.","His speed when flying with swords would now be at least three times faster than before. Any sword technique he deployed would also be thirty times stronger. How fearsome was that?? One had to know that when powerhouses fought each other, a misstep of millimeters was sufficient to completely change the outcome.","“Is this a type of... passive halo?” Lu Yun felt that his new combat art was a bit of a pity. If it could actually form a halo for him to use on his side’s cultivators, he would be invincible!","His eyes darted around rapidly and focused on the Cloudraid Sword disciples beneath him.","“Senior...” A latter nascent soul cultivator quickly stepped forward with a bow when he saw that Lu Yun had completed his meditation.","“Cloudraid Sword Sect will fully submit to Darklake Empire within three days or face extermination down to the last chicken if a single person resists,” Lu Yun intoned coldly.","“Understood!” The sect leader quickly assented when he heard that Lu Yun came from Darklake.","The young man promptly disappeared, leaving behind shell-shocked sect disciples sighing with relief.","......","Three days passed in the blink of an eye. On the fourth day, the skies of Jade Ruins Realm trembled like something had been added to them. Those of higher ranked worlds of cultivation understood that this meant the rules of the heavenly book had returned. The formerly defenseless Jade Ruins Realm was thus protected again.","Regardless, all foreign immortals frantically departed the realm three days ago. Even some wandering through parts of the land other than Immortal Burial Valley were unwilling to stay.","An absolute force of slaughter with the battle strength of a golden immortal rampaged through all of the realm. He killed any foreign immortal he met, no matter who they were or what they were doing.","Lu Yun’s words had been disseminated through the land three days ago, but many were those who thought nothing of them. The Lu young master was a far cry from the Human Emperor and His Majesty’s unequivocal might. He commanded no respect from the visiting immortals.","A golden immortal in residence at the Barren Empire royal palace declared that he would investigate the young man’s identity and assign him to eternal purgatory. But less than ten breaths after he voiced those words, he was summarily executed by a mysterious person. He didn’t know who killed him, even at the moment of death.","The golden immortal’s murder turned all foreigners into timid mice. They ran out of the realm, but there were still a few unlucky bastards that encountered Terra Demon. Lu Yun had already given them a day’s grace to depart. Since the hour was past, his rule was in place.","Jade Ruins Realm underwent key changes when the rules of the heavenly book returned. Numerous cultivation empires vaulted from a low rank to a higher rank. Some of the higher ranked empires declined overnight and were smashed into ruins.","Immortal Burial Valley was the source of fortune and nightmares. Some ascended to the heavens with one step thanks to fortuitous opportunities, others lost their lives despite being unquestionable powerhouses.","Awakened cultivators from the three ninth rank cultivation empires also ventured in. Of them, Firmament Empire’s representatives were lost to the last. Even their wandering immortals died to a mysterious assailant.","Firmament Empire was thus removed from the list of ninth rank cultivation empires. It was replaced by the Dark Orchid Empire. Dark Orchid had vaulted to ninth rank in one leap! And yet, that seemed to be within certain people’s expectations.","What was most surprising was that another name was placed above the three ninth rank empires—Darklake Empire!","A tenth rank cultivation empire!","This was Jade Ruins’ first tenth rank empire in its entire history!","The entire world shifted when the heavenly book returned to its rightful place. Clouds and wind surged while auspicious radiance shone as far as the eye could see. The list of cultivation empires in its pages kept continuously rearranging itself.","Lu Yun stood on the roof of his house and looked up at the tranquil radiance in the sky, waves of emotion in his heart.","“I wonder what that heavenly book is... Is it a treasure? A rule? Or something like the heavenly dao...” He scratched his head.","Endless qi surged in the sky and gathered into massive spirit veins. They darted beneath Darklake’s various cities and sects, instantly turning it from an impoverished nation into one that rivaled an immortal realm.","Waves of qi brewed and reared in all directions. Darklake cultivators were highly agitated as they received the most benefits due to being the original inhabitants of the empire. According to the rules of the Jade Ruins Realm, the heavenly book bestowed resources relevant to a cultivation empire’s new rank whenever it ascended higher.","“Although Darklake has become a tenth rank cultivation empire, its foundations are still rather weak. Grandfather’s specially raised troops alone are insufficient to support the nation’s weight on their backs,” Lu Yun smacked his lips. “Terra Demon can do it, but it’d be a waste of his talents if I keep him here. Forget it, I’ll make plans after grandpa becomes the ruler of the realm.”","Terra Demon returned with another person by his side—more accurately, an empyrean immortal.","“Tai Sui greets Your Majesty!” The empyrean immortal fell to his knees as soon as he saw Lu Yun and repeatedly kowtowed on the ground.","“Oh?” Lu Yun first looked at the newcomer, then bestowed a strange expression on Terra Demon. “I didn’t think you’d use this method to extract his true spirit and help him take possession of another.”","“The young master is short on people.” A smile cracked Terra Demon’s remote expression. “While Tai Sui’s reputation is hardly worth speaking of, he is still the true spirit of an immortal king and possesses a lifetime’s worth of immortal king memories. He is the perfect workhorse for the young master’s needs.”","Although Terra Demon had devoured Tai Sui’s immortal king nascent soul to nourish his own body, he didn’t destroy Tai Sui’s true spirit. Rather, he retrieved it and sent it into another empyrean immortal’s nascent soul, helping the man take possession of another.","It was a release of sorts to Tai Sui since it meant he was no longer a vicious spirit. Anything was better than that.","When Yinghuo, Seven Kills, Greedy Wolf, and Army schemed against him, endless bloody light from the vicious spirits surged into Tai Sui. If it wasn’t for Vermilion Bird surreptitiously giving him a hand, the immortal king might not have retained his sentience. He would’ve devolved into a mindless spirit long ago.","“Tai Sui is willing to do whatever Your Majesty requires!” Tai Sui quickly declared.","He’d originally placed the northern immortal emperor under the central immortal emperor, but his reverence for Lu Yun knew no bounds after a chaos immortal was executed in front of the central immortal emperor.","“Young master, I planted a restriction in his true spirit. He won’t dare rebel,” Terra Demon chuckled.","“Well done,” Lu Yun snorted and handed a Hongmeng Fruit to Terra Demon. The man brightened as he was able to refine another fruit after repairing his nascent soul with Tai Sui’s. One fruit had been the limits of his abilities before when he was still injured, and much of its effects had gone to waste.","“Ah, yes, you should be on your way and look for a cultivator called Song Yi in Great Xia. Help him from the shadows to build a faction in the dynasty,” Lu Yun remarked.","Terra Demon stowed the fruit and nodded. “Young master, I am strong enough to kill arcane immortals now, so that Yan Guichi...”"]},{"number":2362,"title":"Chapter 2362: Chapter 2230.1: Sir Heaven","paragraphs":["Chapter 2230.1: Sir Heaven","“My grandfather will personally take care of Yan Guichi in the future,” Lu Yun shook his head. “He has to do it himself or it will be an eternal mental demon for him. The Human Emperor also showed me face that day, so I cannot make things difficult for him.”","That day, the Human Emperor recalled the three empyrean immortals standing guard at the formation array to avoid an awkward situation. Otherwise, Lu Yun would’ve made a direct enemy out of Great Xia if Terra Demon killed those three in the public eye.","With the young man’s personality, he would not stay his hand. Thus, the Human Emperor recalling his three subordinates at that time had been a concession. Lu Yun had no idea why the emperor had done so. As impressive as the Lu young master’s background or feats may be, he walked along unlit paths at night. No one knew of him and not even the Fengxian Immortal King had the ability to make the Human Emperor give way.","But since the august personage had done so, Lu Yun would not invite contempt upon himself to act as if he hadn’t benefitted massively from the situation.","Terra Demon departed Jade Ruins Realm and soundlessly entered Great Xia. Tai Sui remained behind to help Situ Wenxian oversee Darklake Empire. Lu Tianling and Lu Xiaochi remained in closed door cultivation, but the drums of war pounded.","......","The emergence of Immortal Burial Valley altered the political layout of the realm, resulting in frequent battles and skirmishes. What was unexpected this time was that war commenced from the Tianlong Empire side.","The Tianlong Empire was a solid third rank empire—their strongest were nascent soul experts. Cultivators of that level did not have the right to enter Immortal Burial Valley. Even soul separation cultivators easily died in the formation array if they were not protected by powerful heavyweights.","Thus, the arrival of Immortal Burial Valley barely had an effect on lower ranked empires.","This was borne out in practice when Tianlong Empire no longer sent representatives to the valley after losing a dozen nascent soul cultivators in the first foray. The fires of war burned for another reason.","Three hundred cultivators of unknown origin descended upon the empire the second day after the heavenly book returned. Dressed in blazing red armor, their arrival in the capital was very unexpected. Their strongest was soul projection and weakest latter nascent soul. They cut down the Tianlong royal family like they were chopping vegetables and casually exterminated some of the nation’s biggest clans.","They then occupied the empire’s land and began ravaging the nation of its riches.","These events were the catalyst that detonated Jade Ruins Realm like it was a powder keg. First to strike out was Tianlong Empire’s superior nation—fourth rank Skypine Empire.","Skypine was a premier fourth rank nation and several of its soul projection cultivators had been extraordinarily lucky to obtain a few treasures from Immortal Burial Valley. One of them was one of a forefather of Tianlong royalty.","How would he sit back upon hearing that his family had been exterminated? He immediately requested permission to root out the mysterious cultivators in fiery armor.","Skypine Empire was in fine fettle after counting its riches from Immortal Burial Valley. It naturally mobilized its troops upon hearing that one of its vassal nations had been attacked.","The three hundred-odd cultivators were completely unafraid and stood up to Skypine’s army of more than one hundred thousand strong. A great battle commenced, but neither side was able to cinch a decisive victory. As the conflict dragged on, nearby cultivation empires couldn’t stand to remain on the sidelines. Those with grudges against Skypine or those of its allies became embroiled in the struggle.","The campaign grew and grew until it became a vortex that devoured the entire realm.","......","“Lu Xuan and Wu Zhen have seriously done quite a thing,” Lu Yun chuckled ruefully when he read the report in his hand.","Wu Zhen was the patriarch of the Wu Clan of Tianlong Empire—they’d been exterminated after the Tianlong emperor suspected them for no good reason. He was the only survivor and revenge the only constant thought on his mind.","Under the commands of Lu Xuan and Wu Zhen, the Vermilion Birds used this opportunity to eliminate Tianlong royalty and ignite this war.","Lu Yun passed no judgment about their actions and gave them full jurisdiction over the Vermilion Birds. He didn’t care what they did so long as they grew from this conflict and didn’t betray him. The ensuing chaos and confusion from war was a perfect match for his plans.","The Vermilion Birds found success with every maneuver they took on the battlefield. They were only three hundred and sixty-five strong, but they were shockingly ferocious and dominated their engagements. They were not the least bit disadvantaged when they faced an army from a fifth rank cultivation empire.","Wu Zhen was very quick-witted—he was an ideal strategist. Despite the fighting, he hadn’t lost a single member of the Vermilion Birds thus far.","“Go on, fight and struggle to the death. The dross will be discarded in the fires of war and leave only the essence.” A small ring appeared in Lu Yun’s hand as he slowly closed his eyes and sank his mind into it. He wasn’t a saint, so what did he care about all this?","Humm!","His nascent soul left his body and entered a strange world. Qi of heaven and earth surged to form a new body, one that was a container for his nascent soul. It possessed the cultivation level of initial nascent soul and its true origin was run-of-the-mill. The internal energy within this body was identical to the true origin of any nascent soul cultivator at the bottom rung of a world of cultivation.","This was the Celestial Realm Battlefront, the mysterious place that enshrouded Great Xia and all of the three realms and six paths.","The Celestial Realm Battlefront was unbounded without end. It looked the same as the rest of the three realms and six paths—the only difference was that all cultivators, even immortals, who entered this place were reduced to initial nascent soul. At the same time, only those at nascent soul and above could enter.","No one knew where or what it was. Only those approved by the heavenly book and bestowed one of its rings could enter.","Of course, this task was determined by the various rulers of the outside worlds. Those from fourth rank cultivation empires and above gained the right to enter the battlefront. They could obtain rings from the heavenly book and distribute them to cultivators under their banner.","Great Xia royalty, and by extension the royalty of other cultivation empires, ruled over their domain instead of being fractured by other sects or factions primarily due to the heavenly book and the Celestial Realm Battlefront.","Lu Yun briefly took stock of his new condition and determined that what belonged to him—his nascent soul, sword pagoda, Builder Tree, world of true water, and Seal of the Multitude had been left in his primary body. None of it was in the battlefront with him.","The only thing he brought in was his true spirit.","The ring that’d sent him in was still on his finger. It could transport items out of the battlefront, but could not bring items in. It was the only thing that could communicate with the outside world while he resided here.","A shadow shrouded his heart after Lu Yun arrived in the Celestial Realm Battlefront. Compared to the vicious spirits, this was the true origin point of destruction for the world of immortal dao civilization. Life would start its march on the heavens from this locale.","However, an unknown power quickly suppressed these thoughts—the heavenly dao.","“Heavenly book, oh heavenly book, it looks like I’ve underestimated you. You are nowhere near as simple as a mere connate treasure.” Lu Yun looked toward the center of the battlefront, where a massive book thirty thousand meters tall reared. Anyone could see it, no matter where they stood in the world.","On one side of it was a stone tablet with the characters War Gods Ranking carved on top. The list of names that followed was the ranking for the Jade Ruins Realm.","First: Sword First","Second: Ying Kongkong","Third: Sui Wuye","Fourth: Ji Lin","Fifth: Sui Wuzhou","There were only names on the ranking—no introductions or explanations. The Jade Ruins portion of the Celestial Battlefront appeared rather deserted at the moment as there weren’t that many cultivators moving through it.","“If memory serves correctly, Ji Lin should’ve been number ten on the ranking. It looks like he gained quite a great deal from Immortal Burial Valley to soar to number four.”","Every cultivator possessed the same cultivation and similar quality of methods and Hongmeng qi in the Celestial Realm Battlefront. Even their consciousness and senses were the same. This arena tested control of true origin and understanding of heaven and earth.","Lu Yun flexed his new muscles, finding that he could utilize both the Eighteen Cerulean Sword Dragons and Nine Oscillations of the Heavenly Sword. However, he needed to condense sword qi anew. As for the heavenly dao combat arts... they were unusable here because they were derived from his cultivation method.","All other combat arts remained available.","“Shall I go challenge the War Gods Ranking and see how far up I can make it?” Lu Yun shifted his body, flinging himself through the air due to a lack of flying sword.","While war raged outside, there were still numerous cultivators in the battlefront. After all, the battles didn’t involve every single cultivator in the realm. When the young man arrived in front of the stone tablet at the center of the realm, he took a close look at it.","There were one thousand and eight total names on it, meaning that out of the entire Jade Ruins Realm, only one thousand and eight cultivators had the right to be listed on the tablet.","This included empyrean immortals.","Cultivators were measured in terms of hundreds of millions in a world of cultivation. To be the top one thousand meant being an earth-shaking genius. One also received rewards from the heavenly book if listed on the ranking. The higher the placement, the greater the rewards. They were so bountiful that they caused cultivators to throw all caution aside and aim for a position on the ranking."]},{"number":2363,"title":"Chapter 2363: Chapter 2230.2: Sir Heaven","paragraphs":["Chapter 2230.2: Sir Heaven","The closer one drew to the heavenly book, the more prosperous the Celestial Realm Battlefront became. When Lu Yun came within five thousand kilometers of the treasure, he saw numerous marketplaces and temporary villages. There were even some rudimentary cities in the surroundings.","Cultivators who did not find success in the outside world chose to stay in the battlefront and operate businesses to maintain their livelihoods outside.","The War Gods Ranking wasn’t the heart of the realm. The area roughly five hundred kilometers around the heavenly book was the true core. Newcomers first arrived inside the core, so Lu Yun didn’t spend much time traveling to the stone tablet.","“A newcomer?” When other cultivators saw an empty-handed young man dressed in plain white robes, they immediately knew him to be someone on their first trip to the Celestial Realm Battlefront. Only rookies were dressed like this.","Those who frequently entered the battlefront retained flying swords and treasures for use in the realm. The rest they put into their rings for transport out. Whatever they kept on their bodies was present the next time they entered, but whatever they sent through the rings could never enter this world again.","“Mmhmm.” Lu Yun nodded without saying anything else. It was indeed the first time he entered the battlefront after his three thousand lifetimes.","“Tsk tsk, little guy, are your elders this at ease to let you enter the realm for the first time like this?” cackled a man with a heavy beard.","“Oh?” Lu Yun raised an eyebrow.","“While we do not truly die in the battlefront, we do experience a feeling that is even more harrowing than death.” The man looked at Lu Yun with evil intentions.","“Is that so?” Lu Yun asked innocently.","“Enough, Tiger, don’t scare the child.” A curvaceous woman with alluring features rolled her eyes at the bearded man. “Child, you don’t seem that old given the looks of you. The human heart is malicious and brutal on the battlefield. You need to be careful.”","Someone this young who’d reached nascent soul or above was someone who possessed a bit of talent. But it was also proof that he lacked experience in the world. That would prove the most fatal in the Celestial Realm Battlefront.","“Thank you for your words of caution, big sis.” Lu Yun smiled radiantly.","“The realm isn’t too peaceful as of late,” grumbled Tiger. “Don’t go running around on your own. Hurry up and go home after you open your eyes a bit.”","“Why isn’t it too peaceful? Is it because of the war outside?” Lu Yun asked curiously. With his understanding of the battlefront, this place would never be described as peaceful.","“The war outside? Bah, what does that count for? Since when is there no war in the Jade Ruins Realm? It’s our own matter if we destroy our home!” snorted the beguiling woman, her tone taking on a hard edge.","Lu Yun frowned, seeming to understand something.","“A group of outsiders have come to the battlefront lately and kill whoever they see. Even Sword First and Ying Kongkong have died a few times at their hands,” sighed Tiger. “They seem to be immortals as their methods are completely beyond the scope of our abilities.”","“They’re so damn shameless,” another cultivator spat. “They’re no match for Sir Heaven in the outside world and got sent running for their lives, so they come to the Jade Ruins Celestial Realm Battlefront to stir up trouble.”","“Sir Heaven?” Lu Yun blinked. “Who is Sir Heaven?”","“You don’t even know Sir Heaven?” the woman stared incredulous at him. “If I hadn’t seen you transport in with the ring myself, I would think you’re also from another world. How do you not know Sir Heaven of the Jade Ruins Realm??”","“I really haven’t, who is he?” Lu Yun was truly curious as it had to take someone cocky to adopt such a title.","“Hmph, outsiders bullied those of our realm at the formation array of Immortal Burial Valley and stole our fortunes and opportunities. It was then that Sir Heaven stepped forward and sent them all crying for their mothers. He struck back for the Jade Ruins Realm and even set himself against the Human Emperor for us.” The woman explained with a cold snort and flicked a dismissive glance at Lu Yun, plainly finding the young man ungrateful.","“That’s right, who is the great personage if not our heaven to stick up for ants like us? I saw it with my own eyes how young he was—he’s definitely not more than twenty. Is it wrong to call such a marvelously talented, magnanimous young man our Sir Heaven??” Tiger gesticulated; he’d been present outside the formation array that day!","“Sir Heaven’s cries of ‘No Mercy’ were really something to hear!” someone piped up.","Sir Heaven!","“Sir Heaven said it well—Jade Ruins Realm belongs to Jade Ruins denizens. This part of the Celestial Realm Battlefront is ours as well!”","“Although war rages through our home, it is fine if it's our people against ourselves. But outsiders wanting to move against us? Never!” Nearby cultivators passionately added to the conversation, some rolling up their sleeves to take the fight to these outsiders.","Lu Yun rubbed his nose self-consciously. This Sir Heaven... was him. Who would’ve thought that a moment of righteous indignation would lead to this kind of effect?","“Little brother!” Tiger smacked Lu Yun on the shoulder. “It’s alright if you haven’t heard of Sir Heaven before, that just means you’re clueless. You seem to be a similar age to the noble gentleman. Being able to enter the battlefront means that your potential is extraordinary too. So you should look up to Sir Heaven as your goal and strive for getting better!”","“Um... alright.” Lu Yun subconsciously rubbed his nose again.","Whether it was Immortal Burial Valley or the Celestial Realm Battlefront, he’d slightly altered his appearance in both places. Thus, no one here recognized that he was the Sir Heaven they were lauding. Given their direct and effusive praise, even Lu Yun felt embarrassed despite his thick skin of three thousand lifetimes.","“Hahahaha, Sir Heaven? Don’t make me laugh!” Piercing laughter rang from the sky. “Your Sir Heaven is just a sanctimonious hypocrite. He was able to threaten the immortals only because he had some powerful treasures on him. If he’s so wonderful, why isn’t he listed on your War Gods Ranking?”","“Or is that Sir Heaven actually Sword First or Ying Kongkong?”","“Didn’t you kill Sword First with one stroke?”","“Number two on the list couldn’t even take one blow from me!”","“Hahahaha!!” Five youngsters dressed in the same robes roared with laughter from above.","“It’s you!” Tiger, the alluring woman, and other cultivators on the ground reacted with dismay.","“Indeed it is us,” sneered the only woman among them. “I’ll kill your Sir Heaven if he dares put a toe in the battlefront. Jade Ruins Realm may be yours, but the Jade Ruins battlefront is ours from now on!”","Another dozen figures appeared in the sky and stood behind the five youngsters.","“If there are any Jade Ruins cultivators to be found in your battlefront after a day, we will show you no mercy!”","“The Jade Ruins battlefront? How about the battlefronts of all other worlds! Any Jade Ruins cultivator who dares show their face in the Celestial Realm Battlefront will die!”","“No mercy!”","The crowd in the sky grew as several hundred outsiders gathered from all directions, shouting at the Jade Ruins cultivators beneath.","There were more than one hundred thousand people on the ground, all looking back at them with incredibly unpleasant expressions. They were being humiliated in their own home!","The atmosphere froze.","“Ah... can I ask something?” came a weak voice. “Um... which Great Xia faction are you guys from?”","“What, do you want to tell your Sir Heaven so he can take revenge?” snorted the woman.","“It doesn’t matter if we tell you!” A man with a remote expression declared proudly. “We answer to Marquis Skyglory of Great Xia!”","Marquis Skyglory... No wonder these people were so brazen. Gasps of shock rose from the crowd.","“Marquis Skyglory? I’ll remember that.” The young man nodded.","“You have one day to get out. If there are Jade Ruins cultivators left in the Celestial Realm Battlefront after a day, we will commence a slaughter the likes of which you’ve never seen!” The announcement roiled to all corners of the land. Marquis Skyglory’s cultivators stood in the air, watching the cultivators beneath as they would prancing clowns.","“Actually, you don’t have a chance to leave anymore even if you wish to. I won’t give you the time to run.” The young man who’d just spoken—Lu Yun—raised his head. “I’ll. Commence. The. Slaughter. Now!”","HUM!","A black sun slowly rose into the air."]},{"number":2364,"title":"Chapter 2364: Chapter 2231.1: Kill You All The Same","paragraphs":["Chapter 2231.1: Kill You All The Same","A black sun rose in the air, its faint rays blotting out the listless sun of the Celestial Realm Battlefront. Terrifying aura surged in all directions and any cultivator affected by it turned beet red.","Dressed in long white robes, Lu Yun slowly drifted up into the air and stood beneath the black sun. He looked coolly at the group of Great Xia cultivators dressed in black.","“That young man... is terrifying” The curvaceous woman stared dumbly at the young man, unable to connect him with the boy who’d just been smiling shyly.","“The hell, Sword First and Ying Kongkong have nothing on him! They’re not even a grasshopper in front of him...” Tiger swallowed hard.","Lu Yun turned out empty hands that were bare of treasures. “All of you will die today even if Marquis Skyglory comes himself,” he enunciated slowly.","“Listen to you talk!” sternly rebuked the youngsters at the lead of the Great Xia contingent. They could sense the terrifying aura from Lu Yun, but being Great Xia cultivators and answering to the banner of a marquis, they held their own pride.","“Kill them, leave not a single Jade Ruins cultivator alive!”","“Kill!” the youngsters ordered. Several hundred cultivators in black raised sword light in response and rushed toward the masses below.","No one was a fool—none of them were a match for the young man and his harrowing aura. They weren’t here to bash their brains against a rock, but to clear out the Jade Ruins cultivators below. Someone else would take care of the young man.","The cultivators in black were so fast that they swiftly cut through large swathes of Jade Ruins cultivators after landing. There was nothing that the latter could do in response.","“Die!” Lu Yun’s voice seemed to emanate from hell itself; it was empty and without emotion. The black sun over his head—the wheel of Water Reincarnation—burst with power. Vast water origin suffused the area and turned the air within fifty kilometers viscous and sticky.","Great Xia cultivators that’d been flashing through the crowd were firmly trapped by the power of water origin.","Lu Yun padded down from the sky.","“If I might borrow your sword.” He walked up to the alluring woman and beckoned with his right hand, summoning her flying sword. His display of sword light wasn’t particularly cutting. It seemed more like a picture of radiant, blossoming fireworks. The sword was delicate and exquisite, just like its owner.","While Lu Yun’s strokes didn’t contain killing intent, they landed precisely on every single Great Xia cultivator. All several hundred were dead within the blink of an eye, apart from the leaders in the air.","The wheel of black light slowly dissipated in the void, taking the viscosity with it and leaving behind five tongue-tied youngsters overhead.","“They’re... all dead, truly dead.” Lu Yun’s lips curved upward in an extraordinarily beautiful smile. “It’s your turn next.”","Humm!","A pillar of piercing light rose from the War Gods Ranking and shot for the horizon. Lu Yun’s figure flashed through the light before the stone tablet trembled. Sword First’s name was demoted from first place, replaced by a new name.","Sir Heaven.","Sir Heaven had been added to the War Gods Ranking as number one!","Jaws dropped at the sight, including Lu Yun’s.","It looks like the heavenly book accepts the title that the Jade Ruins cultivators have bestowed upon me. Lu Yun quickly understood the situation. One did not need to use a real name in the Celestial Realm Battlefront. When he entered the battlefront as Slaughterless eight thousand years ago, that had been a moniker as well.","Sword First... was also likely a fake name. However, the heavenly book accepting a title given by others was a rare occurrence indeed. The Jade Ruins battlefront stilled when everyone saw the name.","“Sir Heaven... he’s Sir Heaven!” The curvaceous woman gaped at Lu Yun, completely flabbergasted. She’d just considered him an ungrateful fool, but he was the legendary Sir Heaven?","“Sir Heaven, Sir Heaven is really here! We’re saved!” Cultivators all over the battlefront brightened.","“Sir Heaven!”","“Sir Heaven!” Momentary silence was shattered when shouts of joy echoed over the land. Countless cultivators screamed with all of their might.","......","Darklake Empire, Dark City, the Lu Clan.","Within the underground seed storage formation, green light flashed over Lu Yun’s cross-legged form. It formed a wheel of green light that faded into a tiny green vortex, one that disappeared into the Seal of the Multitude.","One incense stick of gratitude.","Preoccupied with incubating the dragon egg, Mu Ge opened her eyes with astonishment.","“Not only does that kid have the presence of order on him... but was that wheel of green light gratitude??” she murmured.","......","Hum hum hum hum hum...","Black light flashed past Lu Yun as a flying sword one meter long and emanating a black hue slowly coalesced in front of the young man. He subconsciously reached forward; it flew into his hand like it possessed its own consciousness. His mind and heart instantly became one with the weapon and thoroughly refined it.","Paramount dao rank weapon—Immortals Decline.","This was the heavenly book’s reward to him for entering the War Gods Ranking. With the immortal sword in hand, vast water origin gathered to him from all sides and formed a massive vortex around him. The cheers beneath him grew louder at the sight.","“You’re that Sir Heaven?” The Great Xia cultivators regarded Lu Yun with horror. They’d had some confidence in facing off against Lu Yun moments earlier, but all of it had turned to horror.","Sir Heaven!","He was the cultivator who cut down Great Xia empyrean immortals in the Jade Ruins Realm. The young man could truly be considered invincible in the Celestial Realm Battlefront!","“I said that all of you will die.” Lu Yun’s gaze was remote. The mentality forged through three thousand lifetimes was not easily ruffled. If I want you to die, then you must die. Not even an immortal emperor can save you.","Such was Lu Yun.","Hum hum hum hum hum.","Radiance swirled through Immortals Decline as Lu Yun brought a sword stroke down on the remaining youngsters.","BAM!","Golden brilliance flashed through the void and rebuffed his blow. A man in his thirties—dressed in golden armor and wielding a golden immortal sword—stood in the air.","“How dare you threaten those of Marquis Skycloud’s estate!” He snarled and took a stand in front of the youngsters.","“So I have, what can you do about it?” Lu Yun took a step back and brandished his word.","“Voluntarily confine yourself and come with me to answer for your crimes.” The man’s aura abruptly exploded with the boundless power of heaven and earth.","An immortal.","The man in golden armor was an immortal, and a very strong immortal.","“Kill him, grand overseer!” shouted the only woman out of the group. “He killed several hundred of our cultivators!”","“What an utter disgrace all of you are. You will enter closed door cultivation upon our return and will not set foot into Celestial Realm Battlefront for three years,” the man snorted.","“Understood...” The youngsters lowered their heads, not daring to defy the grand overseer of the marquis’ household.","“None of you will be going back,” Lu Yun said softly to the man. “I said they would die, so they will die.”","“I’d like to see just how they will die. You guys will go back first.” The man raised his sword with a burst of splendor and stabbed it at Lu Yun’s forehead.","Whoosh!","Lu Yun twisted his body and sent Immortals Decline exploding into a black dragon coiled in the sky. Rather than the Eighteen Cerulean Sword Dragons, it was another powerful sword technique—Coiled Dragon Strike.","The technique’s splendid sword light coalesced into a black dragon hovering in the sky. It pierced through countless planes and arrived in front of the youngsters about to leave.","Pfft pfft pfft pfft...","The massive dragon churned in the air, drawing agonized shrieks from the group. Their bodies were flayed alive by thousands of rays of sword light.","“They are dead now.” Lu Yun’s form reappeared when the dragon faded away. “Fully dead.”","“You... destroyed their true spirits!” The man knew things were dire when his sword struck empty air. He turned around to see the youngsters already dead to the sword light. True spirits that should’ve been protected by the heavenly book’s rules were obliterated by the sword light!","Someone who could destroy true spirits in the Celestial Realm Battlefront was an absolute genius in Great Xia.","“A perverse genius? I shall end you today!” The man flew into a rage. He howled, fully releasing his aura and directing endless power of heaven and earth at Lu Yun."]},{"number":2365,"title":"Chapter 2365: Chapter 2231.2: Kill You All The Same","paragraphs":["“I would be able to destroy you in the Celestial Realm Battlefront even if you were Marquis Skyglory himself, to say nothing of the fact that you’re not.” Lu Yun twisted his ray of sword light and became unquestionably keen, cutting straight through the vast power of heaven and earth hurtling at him. The magnificent and unbounded strength that could crush anything was sliced through by the layer of light around the young man!","“Kill!” the Lu young master roared.","“Kill!”","“Kill!”","“Kill!” The portentous word echoed in the void instead of fading away, ripping through the power of heaven and earth that the man summoned. He paled with dismay at the sight.","“Die!”?There was no emotion in Lu Yun’s eyes as overwhelming black sword light exploded from his hand. It shot for the man’s head without any bells and whistles.","Terror dawned on the man’s face and he frantically twisted and turned. However, he was as if an ant in the face of such colossal sword aura.","“You can’t kill me! I’m the grand overseer for Marquis Skyglory! You’ll pay a hefty price if you kill me!” the man screamed.","“I already said that I would kill Marquis Skyglory himself if he came!” Lu Yun was wholly unmoved. The domineering man in golden armor flew apart as dust beneath the black sword light. His true spirit was completely extinguished.","All was silent between heaven and earth. Lu Yun seemed to awaken something beyond the three thousand lifetimes in this moment.","......","“That kid sure has some guts.” Two men stood in a patch of unknown space in the Celestial Realm Battlefront. Their eyes pierced through the void and looked at a particular spot in the battlefront.","The speaker was dressed in long ivory robes and looked to be in his early twenties. Some amusement flitted across his aloof face.","The other wore clean white robes. Fingernails neatly clipped and features delicately shaped, a wan pallor filled his face. The look in his eyes was empty without any emotional ripples.","“Although Marquis Skyglory is a newly promoted marquis, his predisposition toward his own rivals that of Marquis Skyrule. He wouldn’t send his people to seize the Jade Ruins Celestial Realm Battlefront for the death of a golden immortal otherwise.” The young man in ivory robes chattered on and on while his companion remained quiet as always.","“White,” the young man in ivory robes suddenly paused. “The heavenly book has fashioned a new body for you in this place. Can you still not see?”","“No.”","“Can you hear?”","“No.”","“Touch?”","“No.”","“Taste...”","“No.”","“Then...”","“Only if there is another red spider lily here,” said the young man with empty eyes.","“Ai...” sighed his companion. “I really wonder what’s the point of living then. If it was me, I would’ve long deconstructed myself and reincarnated.”","“Perhaps...” White turned around and turned his blank eyes to the young man—Mo Qiyue. “Perhaps I am still this way after I deconstruct myself.”","Mo Qiyue blinked, then nodded. If even the heavenly book was powerless to change White’s condition in the battlefront, then reincarnating might not lead to a better ending after all.","“Good thing you have your consciousness. You wouldn’t be able to do anything without it,” Mo Qiyue mumbled. “I say, who do you think Sir Heaven is?” He looked curiously at the young man in the air.","“I don’t know.” White remained as taciturn as always.","“I thought that it’d be Lu Yun, but it looks like it’s not him.” Mo Qiyue smacked his lips. “Lu Yun would be too ridiculous if he really is Sir Heaven.”","“I rather think that Lu Yun is one step higher than Sir Heaven,” White responded calmly. “Lu Yun dares hit even the Origin King.”","“Um...” Mo Qiyue rubbed his nose. “I always thought Lu Tianling was behind that.”","“No.”","......","Great Xia, Marquis Skyglory’s manor.","Marquis Skyglory wore a golden crown and long golden robes. He looked to be a young man not yet in his thirties.","His rise was legendary in Great Xia. Hailed as a stunning genius in his youth, he’d slain true immortals as a combination cultivator. The feat took Great Xia by storm.","After six marquises fell in the battle at Jade Ruins Realm, their empty spots needed to be filled. Marquis Skyglory was one of them through widespread public acclaim. The heavenly book bestowed him the title of Skyglory, of which he fully lived up to. He was extraordinarily dazzling no matter where he was.","“Your Grace.” An immortal dressed in the robes of a servant frantically ran up to the marquis and fell on both knees.","“What is it?” Marquis Skyglory slightly lifted his eyelids.","“The grand overseer’s soul lamp has shattered.” The shaking immortal didn’t dare look at the marquis’ face.","“I see.” Skyglory waved a hand. “You are dismissed.","“The Jade Ruins Celestial Realm Battlefront?” The marquis closed his eyes. When he next opened them, they blazed with killing intent.","......","The Jade Ruins Celestial Realm Battlefront had gone completely mad. Countless cultivators charged through it, singing Sir Heaven’s praises. The Jade Ruins portion seethed with excitement.","Lu Yun slowly heaved a sigh. “I have awoken from my dreams, but the skills I gained from the battlefront still remain.”","He had to start over from the beginning after awakening in the outside world, everything from cultivation, dao methods, and even understanding of heavenly dao. But after entering the Celestial Realm Battlefront, he returned to being the invincible Lu Yun of his dreams.","One’s true spirit entered the battlefront—he’d journeyed through his three thousand lifetimes with his true spirit. Thus, all potential in his true spirit flared when his true spirit took shape in this world.","In his current condition, he was the same as the Lu Yun of his reincarnations.","“While the Celestial Realm Battlefront is one entity, it’s been fragmented into multiple planes. Each one is a massive treasure. If Marquis Skyglory wishes to claim Jade Ruins, I will knock out all of his teeth.” Lu Yun waved a hand and summoned his last opponent’s immortal armor, sword, and transportation ring.","“A third rank immortal sword? It’s good enough, but its materials do not measure up to the Immortals Decline that the heavenly book has given me.” Lu Yun shook his head after observing the man’s sword.","While Immortals Decline was only a paramount dao weapon like his Immortals Forbidden, the materials it was forged from were paramount rank with limitless potential. Lu Yun was master refiner, so it was possible for him to enhance Immortals Decline to the immortal rank.","He didn’t plan on leaving it in the Celestial Realm Battlefront. In the outside world, he needed paramount rank flying swords of the five elements to deploy the Reincarnation of the Five Elements. Immortals Decline was a water attribute flying sword.","A typical immortal rank sword was sufficient for the battlefront.","“Are you... Sir Heaven?” The curvaceous woman and Tiger approached Lu Yun with trepidation.","“Thank you for your sword.” Lu Yun returned the woman’s sword with a wave. “As for the title of Sir Heaven... I don’t know anything about that.”","Smiles crossed the faces of the other cultivators. This was indeed the Sir Heaven from the outside world that was the scourge of Great Xia Immortals!","The woman carefully received her sword and put it away. She had something to boast about to others now!","“Everyone, that Marquis Skyglory or whatever came to the Jade Ruins part of the battlefront and wantonly sought to throw us out of it. Are we going to stand for that?” Lu Yun suddenly called out to the cultivators on the ground.","His presence was warm and gentle, giving one the feeling of a refreshing spring breeze. Added to that him taking the field for Jade Ruins cultivators and killing hundreds of Great Xia cultivators... it made all of the Jade Ruins cultivators kindly disposed toward him.","The crowd quieted down, waiting to hear what the young man would say next.","“Does Sir Heaven mean...” The same thought flashed through many people’s minds.","“I will charge into Great Xia’s battlefront after three days and seek out Marquis Skyglory. I demand an explanation!” Lu Yun’s tone was calm while killing intent blazed in his eyes.","Sir Heaven of the Jade Ruins Realm was going to march on the Great Xia battlefront in three days! He required an explanation from Marquis Skyglory of Great Xia!","The news quickly spread through the immortal dynasty as a terrifying whirlwind, raising enormous commotion in Great Xia and its three thousand worlds of cultivation. Countless cultivators cursed Sir Heaven for having an inflated sense of self worth and daring to show disrespect to a Great Xia marquis. Did he have a death wish??","Even more were those who remained silent.","......","Lu Yun never cared about what others said or thought. He followed his heart and did whatever he wanted to. When it came to tasks he didn’t care for, not even his master was able to sway him otherwise.","The three days were to ensure he had adequate time to prepare. Crouching tigers and hidden dragons abounded in Great Xia. Anyone who could rise to the ranks of the dynasty’s marquis was no ordinary heaven-defying genius.","Lu Yun never underestimated the enemy. Just one paramount dao rank weapon and a third rank immortal weapon was insufficient to challenge a powerful marquis of the immortal dynasty.","If it was single combat in the Celestial Realm Battlefront, he wouldn’t fear even the Human Emperor. But if numerous high level immortals rushed him at the same time, he would find things impossible as well. After all, he was only initial nascent soul in this arena."]},{"number":2366,"title":"Chapter 2366: Chapter 2232: The Personal Motives of the Heavenly Dao","paragraphs":["Chapter 2232: The Personal Motives of the Heavenly Dao","Lu Yun spent the next three days inside the Celestial Realm Battlefront. He used the first two days exploring the various zones of danger and forbidden areas in the Jade Ruins portion. After gleaning numerous treasures from them, he spent the remaining day refining his gains.","After exploring the battlefront for endless years, cultivators had harvested much of its plunder. However, there were still a few heaven-defying treasures to be found in certain zones of danger and forbidden areas.","Lu Yun didn’t need those treasures, he just wanted some spirit herbs and ores.","Events within the Celestial Realm Battlefront immensely impacted the outside world. Wars that raged all throughout Jade Ruins Realm called for a truce during these three days. Anyone with the right to enter the battlefront surged into it.","After three days, nearly one hundred million cultivators stood in the Jade Ruins battlefront. Nearly every cultivator who could enter this world was present. It presented quite a magnificent feast for the senses when an entire world of cultivation’s worth of cultivators were gathered in one place.","“Does Sir Heaven really intend to bring the fight to Great Xia? He’s going to their battlefront to go against a marquis?” Countless cultivators conversed among themselves in the clearing before the heavenly book. A loud hubbub rose over the assembly.","“It’s not like you haven’t seen his strength for yourself. He easily killed hundreds of Great Xia cultivators with a flip of his hand—Great Xia cultivators! Any of them can be ranked in the top ten of the War Gods Ranking if they were in the Jade Ruins Realm!”","Only those who’d been present at Immortal Burial Valley spoke of Sir Heaven at first. Meanwhile, the heavenly book had recorded the events of three days past. Everyone who entered the Celestial Realm Battlefront could view them at their leisure.","It was the singular most sensational event in Jade Ruins battlefront history. Sir Heaven had declared his intentions in front of countless cultivators—there was no going back on his word!","Of course, Lu Yun didn’t intend to go back on his word either.","Rays of sword splendor shot through the air as he appeared in the center of the Jade Ruins battlefront on a flying sword. He was only a few kilometers from the heavenly book.","The one in this part of the battlefront was just a projection, as was the one in Great Xia. None of them were the true treasure and Lu Yun couldn’t be bothered to study what it was. It was either his master or senior brother’s work.","All cultivators were focused on the faint smear of green in midair. Lu Yun wore long green robes today and permitted his hair to flow freely in the breeze. He rather resembled his senior brother in certain aspects.","The young man swept a glance over the Jade Ruins cultivators. “Today, I will deliver a warning to Marquis Skyglory of Great Xia. Those who wish to watch the show can come with me. From today henceforth, whoever dares think of acting against Jade Ruins will have to pay the price in blood!”","His flying sword burst with radiance and carried him north.","The Celestial Realm Battlefront was a massive entity with each world’s battlefront enveloped by a projection of the heavenly book. The boundary of the book’s influence was the boundary of the world’s domain. The center of the Celestial Realm Battlefront was Great Xia. The battlefronts of other worlds circled around it like the stars feting the moon.","This universe was so endlessly vast that Great Xia was the core of only its own plane. There were more worlds like Great Xia than could be counted. Although each world of cultivation possessed nearly the same surface area of territory, Jade Ruins was so weak that some of its frontier had been occupied by other worlds of cultivation.","When Lu Yun shot in the direction of the Great Xia battlefront, the cultivators behind him hesitated. A few took to the air until roughly ten million followed the young man.","Ten million cultivators still raised an astounding presence that shook the world and shocked wherever they passed through.","The image of the heavenly book at the core of the Jade Ruins battlefront flickered, bursting with a ball of light that transported Lu Yun and the ten million cultivators to the edge of its territory.","Sunpoint Mountain!","It bordered the Jade Ruins and Dayuan battlefront, but since it fell within the purview of the Jade Ruins heavenly book’s projection, it belonged to Jade Ruins.","Occupying ten thousand kilometers across, the mountain was rich in resources, ores, and spirit veins. It’d been taken over by Dayuan and many cultivators were encamped on it, forbidding Jade Ruins cultivators from entering.","As expected, this was where Marquis Skyglory’s contingent waited for Lu Yun. With ten million cultivators behind the Lu young master, the massive entourage coalesced a massive influence around the young man.","Not only were cultivators within the Celestial Realm Battlefront keeping an eye on the proceedings, but so were all of the cultivators within Jade Ruins Realm paying close attention. Challenging a Great Xia marquis and actually drawing a response from such an august personage as a cultivator? This battle broke everyone’s understanding of how things were done. It was a furious roar from cultivators at the bottom toward Great Xia and all immortals in general!","Apart from Jade Ruins Realm, those of various other worlds of cultivation were aware of the matter and observed quietly. Just those from Jade Ruins alone numbered more than one hundred million. How overwhelming was gratitude from one hundred million gathered on one person?","Within Dark City, goodwill condensed into layers of halos around Lu Yun’s primary body. He looked incomparably august and dignified, like he was a god.","One incense stick of goodwill?","Not even Lu Yun knew how many sticks of incense he’d collected when the Seal of Multitude trembled and rang with a sonorous hum.","......","In an unknown place within the Celestial Realm Battlefront.","A person in white silently watched events unfold on Sunpoint Mountain. His were the generic features of life—neither man nor woman, neither young nor old. There were no emotions on his face; he was so detached that it seemed like he didn’t care about anything.","Everything of the world seemed to be encompassed by a single one of his thoughts.","The heavenly dao.","Sky stood next to the heavenly dao and worried, “With so much and such intense goodwill gathered on junior brother, his sealed memories will break free ahead of time.”","“Sky,” the heavenly dao answered him. His voice was completely average, but everything in existence would hear their own voice in his. “What happens when the heavenly dao develops its own motives?”","Sky blinked, a tiny ripple appearing in his eternally static emotional state. “The heavenly dao... its own motives?”","“Indeed,” the heavenly dao murmured. “The heavenly dao with its own motives. I never would’ve rejected him and would have taught him all the same if he appeared in front of me as he was. He would’ve become the heavenly dao of his world.”","Emotion traced his empty tone. “But if circumstances proceeded in such a manner, he would immediately leave and return home. In his eyes, our world has been destroyed and become a particle of dust in the nothing. No, we are not even dust. We are just a part of history.”","Sky shook, his expression finally changing.","“But I... I have my own thoughts and desires. I do not wish to be destroyed, I wish to continue protecting my world,” the heavenly dao continued. “So I added something in the mistress’ plans and made later generations think that I would not tolerate his presence if his memories were not sealed, that I would strike him down on the spot.","“I sealed his memories to have him temporarily relinquish his past and fully become part of this world. Once he formed karmic ties to this world, he would ultimately protect it.","“The mistress, Dao King, and God have died in the future. There is no sign of them in all of space and time. In this world's future, the vicious spirits do not evolve into ghost zombies because of their presence. Now that we have lost them, they will surely complete the evolution and the weakness that I left on the vicious spirits will be erased.","“When that comes, living spirits will be slaughtered and all life wither away. The heavens dao will be no more.","“The demise of the four divine beasts is just a sign. We will not even survive until the day that life marches on the heavens. We will scatter upon the wind before then.","“No, life no longer possesses that ability anymore. It will only be slowly destroyed with the heavenly dao.","“Those three dying in the future means a severing of their final ties to this world. Whatever happens to this world will not result in any change to the future.”","That was because the nothing was boundless without end, without concept and was completely objective. This world of immortal dao civilization had no direct ties to anything of future worlds. The only tie was that the mistress, Dao King, and God had brought the seeds of this world’s immortal dao to the future. But in that world, the master of immortal dao and its origins were Lu Yun and Qing Yu.","With the demise of the trio, the last tie between this world and the future world dissipated. Even if this world somehow survived, it would not affect the future world because Lu Yun had come.","The future was set in stone.","Lu Yun, however, was an unknown factor. He could save this world. But in his understanding, he felt nothing for this world that had already crumbled away. He would not stop devastation from taking place as he’d already experienced such an example before. When he traveled from the future to the great wilderness, not only did he not change the development of history, but he became part of it. No matter what he did, it all followed the progression of history.","That concept was thoroughly etched in his heart, so he would not interfere in anything after arriving in this world—it was meant to die.","Thus, the heavenly dao thought of a way to seal the young man’s memories and used the marks of three thousand lifetimes to facilitate him becoming part of this world. Only in that way would he form relationships and karmic ties to it.","Such had been the mistress’ thoughts as well."]},{"number":2367,"title":"Chapter 2367: Chapter 2233.1: Getting Married and Having Kids, Then Watch Long Aotian’s Hatching","paragraphs":["The mistress’ final plan was to borrow Motong’s hand to send Lu Yun to her home, paying her own life as the price. If this world of immortal dao civilization was preserved, then the worlds of the future would survive as well.","Lu Yun was always the most pivotal part of the plan. His mission was complete the moment he obtained the Seal of the Multitude—he could return to his original world at any time. Everything that happened after was the machinations of the heavenly dao to ensure that he would form an increasing amount of ties to this world.","He now had friends, family, and an undertaking that he was soon to complete. He was further lauded as Sir Heaven by the Jade Ruins Realm and beloved by many. Lu Yun had fully become part of this world and truly formed karmic ties and connections to it. Even if he left now, he would return to complete his enterprise.","An exceedingly humanized smile appeared on the heavenly dao’s face. He knew that if Lu Yun awoke at this moment and understood the cause and effect of everything, he still wouldn’t blame anyone. Such was the mistress, Dao King, and God’s personal motives.","They paid not only the price of their lives, but also all traces of their existence to pursue their desires. They were eternally erased from all time and space, never to exist again.","......","According to the original history of this world, its world of immortals would be destroyed by the will of the nothing after all beings marched on the heavens. But since it’d lost its three greatest powerhouses earlier than expected, it was destroyed ahead of time.","......","Goodwill from the people settled down over Lu Yun like a mantle. The shadow of a sword broke out of his forehead—the Sword of Heaven and Earth.","The sword shadow hidden in the sword pagoda was the sword shadow that sealed away his memories in the Origin Continent. It came from Yushi Moli and was one of Motong’s contingencies. She wanted Lu Yun to recreate the deceased Origin Continent.","She nursed the same thoughts as the heavenly dao and mistress at first—have Lu Yun lose himself in the Origin Continent and prevent its demise. However, the continent’s karmic ties to the world of immortals of the future ran too deep. If the continent existed, the future would never arrive.","Thus, the shadow of the Sword of Heaven and Earth could not keep Lu Yun’s memories under wraps. He naturally progressed to awakening, leaving Motong no choice but to activate the mistress’ plan.","However, she secretly hoped that Lu Yun would still revitalize the Origin Continent after he became the heavenly dao.","......","The sword pagoda that Lu Yun refined was the Sugato Sword. After he reincarnated to the world of immortals from Earth, the Sugato Sword forced him to grow methodically and protect Dusk Province.","Dusk Province...","The place he’d reincarnated to in this world of immortals was called Dark City. They shared the same first character. So it would seem that all karmic ties were long decided in advance.","Lu Yun opened his eyes in reality, sorrow and a lost look flashing through them.","“But... I don’t want to go,” he murmured. “I haven’t challenged Marquis Skyglory yet and won justice for the Jade Ruins cultivators.","“I haven’t seen Long Aotian hatch yet...","“I haven’t seen my disciple unlock all of the restrictions on the bamboo...","“I haven’t seen grandfather defeat Yan Guichi and take vengeance... I haven’t seen the family rule over everything beneath the heavens...","“I really don’t want to go.” Although Lu Yun held endless yearning and connections to his world, he had truly built relationships in this one as well. He really didn’t want to go before he finished everything.","Was he supposed to give up halfway and forgo everything in this world?","“Go home,” the heavenly dao said lowly as he approached the young man. “With the Seal of the Multitude, you can defeat the will of nothing and become the heavenly dao of your world.”","“But...” Lu Yun’s throat was dry. “Can’t I go home after I finish everything here?”","“You should know our plans by now,” the heavenly dao chuckled. “What we wish for you to do is not only to save your home, but also ours. The mistress, Dao King, and God have already fallen. Our connection with the future is severed and you can come back if you so wish.","“I hope that when you return, you can save this world. With the mistress, Dao King, and God having perished, no one can prevent the vicious spirits from evolving into the ghost zombies. They will destroy the world of immortals—you are its only hope.","“If you stay, what happened to you in the great wilderness will play out once more. You will become part of history and propel it forward, becoming someone like the great three.","“But that will not empower you to save this world. Everything you care about, your grandfather, friends, disciple... Everyone in the Jade Ruins Realm and all of the worlds will be devoured by the ghost zombies,” the heavenly dao said gently.","“I can... come back?” Lu Yun brightened. Three thousand reincarnations had enabled him to take root in this world. The experiences of his final lifetime crafted bonds that made him reluctant to bid farewell to where he was.","“You can.” A figure in white appeared in front of him—a young man in pristine white robes with a vacant gaze in his eyes. There was no expression on his face and he held a scarlet Hell Flower in his hands.",".","“Lu Yun, do you still not recognize me?” White tugged at the corners of his lips, attempting to form a smile. Sadly, his expression was so stiff that he failed.","“Wayfarer... Fuxi!” Lu Yun lit up. “Senior Fuxi?!”","“Yes, it’s me,” Fuxi nodded.","“Are... are you a being of this world?” Lu Yun’s expression froze.","“No,” Fuxi shook his head. “I merely employed the same method as before to come here. I left my senses at home while the core essence of my soul traveled to this world with a sliver of consciousness.”","The current Fuxi lacked sight, touch, taste, and hearing. Only a tidbit of scent remained to ensure that he could smell the fragrance of the flower in his hand.","“Qing Yu and the little fox sent me here.” Fuxi finally succeeded in displaying a rigid smile. “The world of immortals has entered the nothing and become one with the new world of immortals in the nothing. The realms of heaven, earth, and human support the nothing.","“Qing Yu and Tushan Miao have inherited your power of reincarnation and control the three realms. They are its masters. City Lord Ouyang Du has survived. The only person that world lacks is you.” Fuxi’s smile deepened until it was more natural. “I... brought the Sword of Chaos with me. This world did not have that to begin with.”","“Remember to come back after you go,” the heavenly dao sighed. “I really don’t want to die.”","“I will,” Lu Yun nodded emphatically. “I will come back and save everything here!”","I, Lu Yun, will be that saint!","If everyone in the world was so egotistic and self-serving, if no one was willing to step forward and save the world and its people...","Then that world might as well fall apart into nothing.","Good opposed evil, the two camps were clearly marked. Doing good deeds and upholding justice did not make one a saint.","“Simply speak to my five senses in the world of immortals if you wish to return. I will use the power of reincarnation to bridge space and time from this world to bring you back.”","Lu Yun vanished into thin air.","......","“He’s gone.” Seven boys and girls in Fallen Leaf City looked to the sky.","“He is the heir of the mistress, Dao King, and God. He will be back,” Zi Chen chuckled.","While the three were no longer, someone needed to fill their positions and the vacancy. Thus, seven souls were born to inherit the three’s mantle, but they were far less than their predecessors. All they could do was silently watch over everything and die alongside with this world.","“The goodwill of those from the Jade Ruins Realm and that of the entire worlds of cultivation finally tied him so closely to us that we are one and the same. He is part of this world and its factor of change.","“We have found salvation.”","......","Deep in the depths of Immortal Burial Valley, Vermilion Bird lifted her head with an expression of great relief. Only with Lu Yun’s departure was he freed from the karmic ties of this world. He was now independent of it and its factor of change. When Lu Yun returned, this world would see a glimmer of hope.","All peak powerhouses in this world of immortal dao looked to the sky, at where Lu Yun had left.","......","“I’ve finally... come back.” Lu Yun stood at the peak of the world of immortals. The world of immortals, hell, and the new world of immortals were connected to each other. They were the only world in the nothing.","The war between the city lords of nothing and Saviors was over. The cities of nothing had been completely eradicated from the nothing and horrific casualties inflicted upon their former rulers. The survivors transferred to immortal dao and entered the world of immortals for succor.","The legitimate Saviors were dead; those that remained were controlled by the will of nothing.","Lu Yun stood at the tallest peak in the world of immortals—Mount Xuanhuang—and looked into the nothing. The great tomb had fully manifested and bore down on the world of immortals with magnificent momentum. Countless Saviors and ghost zombies circled around it, looking lasciviously at its prey.","Qing Yu and the little fox brimmed with the power of reincarnation, protectively flanking the world of immortals.","Their expressions suddenly changed as they shot to their feet and looked behind them."]},{"number":2368,"title":"Chapter 2368: Chapter 2233.2(END): Getting Married and Having Kids, Then Watch Long Aotian’s Hatching","paragraphs":["“Lu Yun!!” Qing Yu shook and threw herself into Lu Yun’s arms, sobbing uncontrollably. The little fox was the same way as she clung to Lu Yun’s waist with a death grip.","Given how far the world of immortals had developed, no one knew how long he’d been gone this time. Lu Yun’s heart was breaking. The yearning that’d wrapped around his heart all this time unfurled with fervor and burst forth.","“I’m back... I’m back... I’m never leaving again!” he murmured. While he would inevitably return to that world of immortal dao civilization, he was bringing Qing Yu and Tushan Miao with him! He would never suffer the torment of being apart again.","“Just leave this tomb and the will of nothing it nurtures to me.” A cold sneer played on his lips.","The Seal of the Multitude became one with the world of immortals as soon as he returned. The adoration and faith that all living beings held toward the immortal dao draped around Lu Yun. Under the treasure’s influence, he became something akin to order. All of his immortal force, rules, and everything vanished—replaced by a hazy true me. However... his emotions, thoughts, and everything that was human and alive about him also receded at the same time.","According to the expected pattern, Lu Yun would now become selfless and without desire. Safeguarding this world would be his only duty. And yet, he held two people in his arms. They were his heart, soul, and entire world.","The receding emotions instantly returned because of Qing Yu and Tushan Miao—Lu Yun became a living being again.","“Congratulations!” A merry Hongjun flashed out of the air. “I once sought to become the heavenly dao so I could protect this world, but I failed in the end.”","Hongjun had striven to integrate with the rules and become the heavenly dao in the great wilderness. However, he failed at the last possible step because to become the heavenly dao was to lose his emotions and no longer care about the survival of living beings. He would conform with the natural flow of development and even facilitate the nothing to devour the world.","The heavenly dao of the other world protected its denizens and accepted Lu Yun due to the mistress, Dao King, and God affecting it. Their influence remained even after the three died, and Lu Yun’s motives remained due to the two in his arms.","“You have me now.” A smile floated onto the young man’s face. When he turned to the great tomb, a frosty glint exploded out of his eyes.","All of the powerhouses in the world of immortals rose to the air to regard the newly returned Lu Yun. The Darkness city lord’s lips trembled, but he didn’t say anything.","“Uncle.” Lu Yun smiled at the man; he answered in kind.","The world that Lu Yun had gone to and briefly been part of as Yushi Moli was the city lord’s history. Nothing about it had changed with Lu Yun’s intervention because the karmic tie and Lu Yun’s appearance was already set in stone.","The city lord took a deep breath and murmured, “Do you... do you blame me?”","“Not at all.” Lu Yun shook his head with a smile. “Everything happens for a reason.”","If it wasn’t for the city lords refining shards of the worlds in the nothing and turning the denizens into ghost zombies, the current immortal dao wouldn’t stand as strong as it did now.","The city lord heaved a sigh of relief.","“I’m going to take care of that thing now.” Three draconic shadows appeared in Lu Yun’s eyes. The Dragonquake Scripture!","The three dragons represented the mistress, Dao King, and God and were the summation of their great dao. These dragons were solely meant to eliminate the tomb in the nothing.","Lu Yun stood outside it, not intending to make his way inside. He immediately obliterated all Saviors and ghost zombies around the tomb when he flung a punch at it.","RUMBLE!","Fissures appeared in the void. To the nothing, these fissures were existence. A loud snarl echoed from the tomb as a creature with red fur walked out of it. It seemed to be a combined vicious spirit, ghost zombie, and akasha ghost.","“Mowang...” Lu Yun’s eyelid twitched when he saw the figure. He didn’t experience Yushi Moli’s life after he left, but he possessed the boy’s memories up to thirteen years old. There was certain affection there for this younger brother.","Ouyang Du’s lips trembled as well, deep sorrow shining in them.","“What a shame that you’re no longer Yushi Mowang. You’re just the will of nothing.” Lu Yun took a deep breath and activated the Dragonquake Scripture again.","Concentrated power of heaven and earth unleashed from his body. Reinforced by the Seal of the Multitude, the hazy gray dao character in his dantian released boundless splendor.","Lu Yun was the heavenly dao in this moment, a heavenly dao with emotions and desires.","“DIE!!” he roared and punched outward again. Endless strength blasted the ancient zombie.","It threw its head back with a howl but remained unmoving. The young man’s aura made it feel very uncomfortable. Waving its arms around, it shrieked with finality and charged Lu Yun and the world of immortals behind it.","Sneering, the Seal of the Multitude appeared in the young man’s hand. Lu Yun cocked his hand back like he was throwing a brick and threw it at the zombie.","Power from the heavenly dao coalesced around Lu Yun and bloomed with rays of light. Fear surfaced in the zombie’s eyes. The will of the nothing around it instantly weakened and began to disperse when the power of heavenly dao rushed it.","Sensing impending doom, the ancient zombie turned to run.","“Heavenly dao combat art... Petrification!” Lu Yun suddenly roared. The power of heavenly and earth circulated over him and focused in the form of the Petrification combat art, freezing the zombie.","No matter how it struggled, it could only howl and snarl impotently.","With that, the Seal of the Multitude transformed into a sword—the Sword of the Multitude.","Heavenly dao combat art... Sword Manipulation!","Under this combat art, the Sword of the Multitude flared with terrifying might. One ray of sword light split open the void and crushed it to pieces. It contained the will of the multitude and represented all life!","BOOM!","The ancient zombie and the ancient tomb behind it were slashed apart.","“The subjective affecting the objective?” Lu Yun howled. “One person’s subjectivity cannot affect all of objectivity, only the subjectivity of the multitude can move this vast and unbounded objectivity! DIE!!”","He levied another stroke and ripped the ancient zombie to pieces. It dissipated into the nothing. Lu Yun slashed again and again, filling the void with sword qi and eviscerating the nihil.","Control the nothing?","He changed his mind in this moment—he didn’t want to control the nothing, he wanted to end it!","Rumble!","The nothing collapsed beneath Lu Yun’s sword qi while the boundless will of the nothing keened. Lu Yun hacked it to pieces and threw it into the cycle of reincarnation. A magnificent expanse of the cosmos slowly rose around him. Dots of celestial splendor exuded vibrant vitality...","This was the night sky of the immortal dao, the night sky of life. It was clear skies after the storm.","“Is it over? Is it truly over?” The Darkness city lord, Weilan city lord, and others sobbed silently on their knees in the void. Had the nothing that’d tormented them for countless eons finally been destroyed?","“It’s not over.” A pale Lu Yun shook his head. “Existence follows the cycle of reincarnation and all things will eventually end... Today, I destroy the nothing and create a boundless world. There will come another day in which this world ends and returns to the nothing.","“This is the objective rhythm of things and cannot be averted.” He took a deep breath and smiled. “But there is no longer any influence from something like the will of the nothing.","“Additionally, I am the heavenly dao. All things have a chance of survival beneath the heavenly dao. Those who grasp this chance will break free of reincarnation and escape their fate.”","Radiant starlight scattered over his body as Lu Yun drifted to the ground. There was no special aura or presence about him; it was as if he was an ordinary being.","“Oh, right!” His expression changed drastically and his tone grew urgent, “There’s something important I’ve yet to do!”","“What is it??” Everyone around him grew alarmed.","“That bastard Marquis Skyglory pissed me off, I need to get back and beat his ass!” Lu Yun clenched his fists with a frosty glint in his eyes. “I’m no saint, whoever struts around in front of me will have it coming for him!”","The crowd: ......","Did this sound like what a damned heavenly dao should say?","“Wait” Lu Yun thought of something else and happily clasped Qing Yu and the little fox to him. “That’s not that urgent, he’s not going anywhere. We should go home and make some children first!","“I have a dragon egg over there and Long Aotian’s almost ready to hatch. My dearest wives, let’s go make some children and take them to play with Long Aotian!”","Qing Yu and Tushan Miao, the overseers of the immortal dao and sovereigns of reincarnation, blushed bright red amidst the strange gazes of the crowd.","“What are you two being so shy for? We’re old married couples already!” Lu Yun grumbled.","“What old married couples?! We never got married!!” Qing Yu berated him.","“Oh, eh, then let’s get married first and then make babies. Then we’ll all go see Long Aotian hatch!”","“What about Marquis Skyglory?” the little fox asked naively.","“Right, let’s beat the crap out of Marquis Skyglory first and then go watch Long Aotian hatch!”","Qing Yu smiled. “Whatever we do is fine so long as we get married first!”","The End.","etvolare's Thoughts","There we have it, this is the end of NECRO. This series started in 2020 and ended in 2023, making it quite the witness to the some very interesting times in the world.","NGL, it was damn painful there at the end. Thank you all for bearing witness to several breakdowns lol. It was quite a wild and fun ride for a very long time and I think the last chapter confirms what we knew all along -- the real MC was everyone but Lu Yun lol. I'm glad we had an actual ending and most of the plot twists properly addressed.","Regardless of how this ride was, it was most wonderful with all of you along for it. You kept me going and believe me, there's no way my sanity would've lasted this long without you guys. The banter, memes, and discussion were lovely and I really do hope to see you in my next series! (Spoiler: it's one of the biggest names in the scene and was always ranked top 3 all site.) It won't be long before it's released, so please feel free to check out my previous work Sovereign of the Three Realms (MC dies because of a fart) or follow my adventures in Taiwan before then!","cupped fist salute. etvo","PS. My next novel is Star Gate and the synopsis is as follows!","Traditional martial cultivation and a budding society of arcane abilities clash in modern Silver City. Are the tried and true paths better, or are flashy arts of overwhelming power the new world order?","Li Hao is dragged out of normality by a song and the death of his childhood friend. Thrown into a war between old and new, he must decide which path to walk. Little do others know that the young man with an easy smile is the textbook definition of playing a pig to eat the tiger. It’s not a matter of finding those who hurt him, but how much he’ll make them pay.","What will it be, qi or magic? But why do decisions always have to be black and white? Can’t he mix his own shade of gray?"]}]);
